insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 9, 'And when they returned from the tomb, they reported all these things to the Eleven and to all the others.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 10, 'It was Mary Magdalene, Joanna, Mary the mother of James, and the other women with them who told this to the apostles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 11, 'But their words seemed like nonsense to them, and they did not believe the women.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 12, 'Peter, however, got up and ran to the tomb. And after bending down and seeing only the linen cloths, he went away, wondering to himself what had happened.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 13, 'That same day two of them were going to a village called Emmaus, about seven miles from Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 14, 'They were talking with each other about everything that had happened.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 15, 'And as they talked and deliberated, Jesus Himself came up and walked along with them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 16, 'But their eyes were kept from recognizing Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 17, 'He asked them, “What are you discussing so intently as you walk along?” They stood still, with sadness on their faces.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 18, 'One of them, named Cleopas, asked Him, “Are You the only visitor to Jerusalem who does not know the things that have happened there in recent days?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 19, '“What things?” He asked. “The events involving Jesus of Nazareth,” they answered. “This man was a prophet, powerful in speech and action before God and all the people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 20, 'Our chief priests and rulers delivered Him up to the sentence of death, and they crucified Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 21, 'But we were hoping He was the One who would redeem Israel. And besides all this, it is the third day since these things took place.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 22, 'Furthermore, some of our women astounded us. They were at the tomb early this morning,'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 23, 'but they did not find His body. They came and told us they had seen a vision of angels, who said that Jesus was alive.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 24, 'Then some of our companions went to the tomb and found it just as the women had described. But Him they did not see.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 25, 'Then Jesus said to them, “O foolish ones, how slow are your hearts to believe all that the prophets have spoken!'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 26, 'Was it not necessary for the Christ to suffer these things and then to enter His glory?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 27, 'And beginning with Moses and all the Prophets, He explained to them what was written in all the Scriptures about Himself.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 28, 'As they approached the village where they were headed, He seemed to be going farther.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 29, 'But they pleaded with Him, “Stay with us, for it is nearly evening and the day is almost over.” So He went in to stay with them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 30, 'While He was reclining at the table with them, He took bread, spoke a blessing and broke it, and gave it to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 31, 'Then their eyes were opened and they recognized Jesus—and He disappeared from their sight.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 32, 'They asked each other, “Were not our hearts burning within us as He spoke with us on the road and opened the Scriptures to us?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 33, 'And they got up that very hour and returned to Jerusalem. There they found the Eleven and those with them, gathered together'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 34, 'and saying, “The Lord has indeed risen and has appeared to Simon!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 35, 'Then the two told what had happened on the road, and how they had recognized Jesus in the breaking of the bread.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 36, 'While they were describing these events, Jesus Himself stood among them and said, “Peace be with you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 37, 'But they were startled and frightened, thinking they had seen a spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 38, '“Why are you troubled,” Jesus asked, “and why do doubts arise in your hearts?'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 39, 'Look at My hands and My feet. It is I Myself. Touch Me and see—for a spirit does not have flesh and bones, as you see I have.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 40, 'And when He had said this, He showed them His hands and feet.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 41, 'While they were still in disbelief because of their joy and amazement, He asked them, “Do you have anything here to eat?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 42, 'So they gave Him a piece of broiled fish,'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 43, 'and He took it and ate it in front of them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 44, 'Jesus said to them, “These are the words I spoke to you while I was still with you: Everything must be fulfilled that is written about Me in the Law of Moses, the Prophets, and the Psalms.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 45, 'Then He opened their minds to understand the Scriptures.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 46, 'And He told them, “This is what is written: The Christ will suffer and rise from the dead on the third day,'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 47, 'and in His name repentance and forgiveness of sins will be proclaimed to all nations, beginning in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 48, 'You are witnesses of these things.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 49, 'And behold, I am sending the promise of My Father upon you. But remain in the city until you have been clothed with power from on high.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 50, 'When Jesus had led them out as far as Bethany, He lifted up His hands and blessed them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 51, 'While He was blessing them, He left them and was carried up into heaven.'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 52, 'And they worshiped Him and returned to Jerusalem with great joy,'),
  ('BSB', 'Luke', 42, 24, 53, 'praising God continually in the temple.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 1, 'In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was God.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 2, 'He was with God in the beginning.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 3, 'Through Him all things were made, and without Him nothing was made that has been made.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 4, 'In Him was life, and that life was the light of men.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 5, 'The Light shines in the darkness, and the darkness has not overcome it.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 6, 'There came a man who was sent from God. His name was John.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 7, 'He came as a witness to testify about the Light, so that through him everyone might believe.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 8, 'He himself was not the Light, but he came to testify about the Light.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 9, 'The true Light who gives light to every man was coming into the world.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 10, 'He was in the world, and though the world was made through Him, the world did not recognize Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 11, 'He came to His own, and His own did not receive Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 12, 'But to all who did receive Him, to those who believed in His name, He gave the right to become children of God—'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 13, 'children born not of blood, nor of the desire or will of man, but born of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 14, 'The Word became flesh and made His dwelling among us. We have seen His glory, the glory of the one and only Son from the Father, full of grace and truth.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 15, 'John testified concerning Him. He cried out, saying, “This is He of whom I said, ‘He who comes after me has surpassed me because He was before me.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 16, 'From His fullness we have all received grace upon grace.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 17, 'For the law was given through Moses; grace and truth came through Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 18, 'No one has ever seen God, but the one and only Son, who is Himself God and is at the Father’s side, has made Him known.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 19, 'And this was John’s testimony when the Jews of Jerusalem sent priests and Levites to ask him, “Who are you?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 20, 'He did not refuse to confess, but openly declared, “I am not the Christ.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 21, '“Then who are you?” they inquired. “Are you Elijah?” He said, “I am not.” “Are you the Prophet?” He answered, “No.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 22, 'So they said to him, “Who are you? We need an answer for those who sent us. What do you say about yourself?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 23, 'John replied in the words of Isaiah the prophet: “I am a voice of one calling in the wilderness, ‘Make straight the way for the Lord.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 24, 'Then the Pharisees who had been sent'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 25, 'asked him, “Why then do you baptize, if you are not the Christ, nor Elijah, nor the Prophet?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 26, '“I baptize with water,” John replied, “but among you stands One you do not know.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 27, 'He is the One who comes after me, the straps of whose sandals I am not worthy to untie.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 28, 'All this happened at Bethany beyond the Jordan, where John was baptizing.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 29, 'The next day John saw Jesus coming toward him and said, “Look, the Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the world!'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 30, 'This is He of whom I said, ‘A man who comes after me has surpassed me because He was before me.’'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 31, 'I myself did not know Him, but the reason I came baptizing with water was that He might be revealed to Israel.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 32, 'Then John testified, “I saw the Spirit descending from heaven like a dove and resting on Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 33, 'I myself did not know Him, but the One who sent me to baptize with water told me, ‘The man on whom you see the Spirit descend and rest is He who will baptize with the Holy Spirit.’'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 34, 'I have seen and testified that this is the Son of God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 35, 'The next day John was there again with two of his disciples.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 36, 'When he saw Jesus walking by, he said, “Look, the Lamb of God!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 37, 'And when the two disciples heard him say this, they followed Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 38, 'Jesus turned and saw them following. “What do you want?” He asked. They said to Him, “Rabbi” (which means Teacher), “where are You staying?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 39, '“Come and see,” He replied. So they went and saw where He was staying, and spent that day with Him. It was about the tenth hour.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 40, 'Andrew, Simon Peter’s brother, was one of the two who heard John’s testimony and followed Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 41, 'He first found his brother Simon and told him, “We have found the Messiah” (which is translated as Christ).'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 42, 'Andrew brought him to Jesus, who looked at him and said, “You are Simon son of John. You will be called Cephas” (which is translated as Peter).'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 43, 'The next day Jesus decided to set out for Galilee. Finding Philip, He told him, “Follow Me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 44, 'Now Philip was from Bethsaida, the same town as Andrew and Peter.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 45, 'Philip found Nathanael and told him, “We have found the One Moses wrote about in the Law, the One the prophets foretold—Jesus of Nazareth, the son of Joseph.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 46, '“Can anything good come from Nazareth?” Nathanael asked. “Come and see,” said Philip.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 47, 'When Jesus saw Nathanael approaching, He said of him, “Here is a true Israelite, in whom there is no deceit.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 48, '“How do You know me?” Nathanael asked. Jesus replied, “Before Philip called you, I saw you under the fig tree.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 49, '“Rabbi,” Nathanael answered, “You are the Son of God! You are the King of Israel!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 50, 'Jesus said to him, “Do you believe just because I told you I saw you under the fig tree? You will see greater things than these.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 1, 51, 'Then He declared, “Truly, truly, I tell you, you will all see heaven open and the angels of God ascending and descending on the Son of Man.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 1, 'On the third day a wedding took place at Cana in Galilee. Jesus’ mother was there,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 2, 'and Jesus and His disciples had also been invited to the wedding.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 3, 'When the wine ran out, Jesus’ mother said to Him, “They have no more wine.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 4, '“Woman, why does this concern us?” Jesus replied. “My hour has not yet come.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 5, 'His mother said to the servants, “Do whatever He tells you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 6, 'Now six stone water jars had been set there for the Jewish rites of purification. Each could hold from twenty to thirty gallons.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 7, 'Jesus told the servants, “Fill the jars with water.” So they filled them to the brim.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 8, '“Now draw some out,” He said, “and take it to the master of the banquet.” They did so,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 9, 'and the master of the banquet tasted the water that had been turned into wine. He did not know where it was from, but the servants who had drawn the water knew. Then he called the bridegroom aside'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 10, 'and said, “Everyone serves the fine wine first, and then the cheap wine after the guests are drunk. But you have saved the fine wine until now!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 11, 'Jesus performed this, the first of His signs, at Cana in Galilee. He thus revealed His glory, and His disciples believed in Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 12, 'After this, He went down to Capernaum with His mother and brothers and His disciples, and they stayed there a few days.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 13, 'When the Jewish Passover was near, Jesus went up to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 14, 'In the temple courts He found men selling cattle, sheep, and doves, and money changers seated at their tables.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 15, 'So He made a whip out of cords and drove all from the temple courts, both sheep and cattle. He poured out the coins of the money changers and overturned their tables.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 16, 'To those selling doves He said, “Get these out of here! How dare you turn My Father’s house into a marketplace!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 17, 'His disciples remembered that it is written: “Zeal for Your house will consume Me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 18, 'On account of this, the Jews demanded, “What sign can You show us to prove Your authority to do these things?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 19, 'Jesus answered, “Destroy this temple, and in three days I will raise it up again.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 20, '“This temple took forty-six years to build,” the Jews replied, “and You are going to raise it up in three days?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 21, 'But Jesus was speaking about the temple of His body.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 22, 'After He was raised from the dead, His disciples remembered that He had said this. Then they believed the Scripture and the word that Jesus had spoken.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 23, 'While He was in Jerusalem at the Passover Feast, many people saw the signs He was doing and believed in His name.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 24, 'But Jesus did not entrust Himself to them, for He knew them all.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 2, 25, 'He did not need any testimony about man, for He knew what was in a man.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 1, 'Now there was a man of the Pharisees named Nicodemus, a leader of the Jews.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 2, 'He came to Jesus at night and said, “Rabbi, we know that You are a teacher who has come from God. For no one could perform the signs You are doing if God were not with him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 3, 'Jesus replied, “Truly, truly, I tell you, no one can see the kingdom of God unless he is born again.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 4, '“How can a man be born when he is old?” Nicodemus asked. “Can he enter his mother’s womb a second time to be born?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 5, 'Jesus answered, “Truly, truly, I tell you, no one can enter the kingdom of God unless he is born of water and the Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 6, 'Flesh is born of flesh, but spirit is born of the Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 7, 'Do not be amazed that I said, ‘You must be born again.’'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 8, 'The wind blows where it wishes. You hear its sound, but you do not know where it comes from or where it is going. So it is with everyone born of the Spirit.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 9, '“How can this be?” Nicodemus asked.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 10, '“You are Israel’s teacher,” said Jesus, “and you do not understand these things?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 11, 'Truly, truly, I tell you, we speak of what we know, and we testify to what we have seen, and yet you people do not accept our testimony.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 12, 'If I have told you about earthly things and you do not believe, how will you believe if I tell you about heavenly things?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 13, 'No one has ascended into heaven except the One who descended from heaven—the Son of Man.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 14, 'Just as Moses lifted up the snake in the wilderness, so the Son of Man must be lifted up,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 15, 'that everyone who believes in Him may have eternal life.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 16, 'For God so loved the world that He gave His one and only Son, that everyone who believes in Him shall not perish but have eternal life.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 17, 'For God did not send His Son into the world to condemn the world, but to save the world through Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 18, 'Whoever believes in Him is not condemned, but whoever does not believe has already been condemned, because he has not believed in the name of God’s one and only Son.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 19, 'And this is the verdict: The Light has come into the world, but men loved the darkness rather than the Light because their deeds were evil.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 20, 'Everyone who does evil hates the Light, and does not come into the Light for fear that his deeds will be exposed.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 21, 'But whoever practices the truth comes into the Light, so that it may be seen clearly that what he has done has been accomplished in God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 22, 'After this, Jesus and His disciples went into the Judean countryside, where He spent some time with them and baptized.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 23, 'Now John was also baptizing at Aenon near Salim, because the water was plentiful there, and people kept coming to be baptized.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 24, '(For John had not yet been thrown into prison.)'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 25, 'Then a dispute arose between John’s disciples and a certain Jew over the issue of ceremonial washing.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 26, 'So John’s disciples came to him and said, “Look, Rabbi, the One who was with you beyond the Jordan, the One you testified about—He is baptizing, and everyone is going to Him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 27, 'John replied, “A man can receive only what is given him from heaven.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 28, 'You yourselves can testify that I said, ‘I am not the Christ, but am sent ahead of Him.’'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 29, 'The bride belongs to the bridegroom. The friend of the bridegroom stands and listens for him, and is overjoyed to hear the bridegroom’s voice. That joy is mine, and it is now complete.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 30, 'He must increase; I must decrease.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 31, 'The One who comes from above is above all. The one who is from the earth belongs to the earth and speaks as one from the earth. The One who comes from heaven is above all.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 32, 'He testifies to what He has seen and heard, yet no one accepts His testimony.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 33, 'Whoever accepts His testimony has certified that God is truthful.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 34, 'For the One whom God has sent speaks the words of God, for God gives the Spirit without limit.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 35, 'The Father loves the Son and has placed all things in His hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 3, 36, 'Whoever believes in the Son has eternal life. Whoever rejects the Son will not see life. Instead, the wrath of God remains on him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 1, 'When Jesus realized that the Pharisees were aware He was gaining and baptizing more disciples than John'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 2, '(although it was not Jesus who baptized, but His disciples),'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 3, 'He left Judea and returned to Galilee.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 4, 'Now He had to pass through Samaria.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 5, 'So He came to a town of Samaria called Sychar, near the plot of ground that Jacob had given to his son Joseph.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 6, 'Since Jacob’s well was there, Jesus, weary from His journey, sat down by the well. It was about the sixth hour.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 7, 'When a Samaritan woman came to draw water, Jesus said to her, “Give Me a drink.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 8, '(His disciples had gone into the town to buy food.)'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 9, '“You are a Jew,” said the woman. “How can You ask for a drink from me, a Samaritan woman?” (For Jews do not associate with Samaritans.)'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 10, 'Jesus answered, “If you knew the gift of God and who is asking you for a drink, you would have asked Him, and He would have given you living water.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 11, '“Sir,” the woman replied, “You have nothing to draw with and the well is deep. Where then will You get this living water?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 12, 'Are You greater than our father Jacob, who gave us this well and drank from it himself, as did his sons and his livestock?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 13, 'Jesus said to her, “Everyone who drinks this water will be thirsty again.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 14, 'But whoever drinks the water I give him will never thirst. Indeed, the water I give him will become in him a fount of water springing up to eternal life.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 15, 'The woman said to Him, “Sir, give me this water so that I will not get thirsty and have to keep coming here to draw water.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 16, 'Jesus told her, “Go, call your husband and come back.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 17, '“I have no husband,” the woman replied. Jesus said to her, “You are correct to say that you have no husband.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 18, 'In fact, you have had five husbands, and the man you now have is not your husband. You have spoken truthfully.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 19, '“Sir,” the woman said, “I see that You are a prophet.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 20, 'Our fathers worshiped on this mountain, but you Jews say that the place where one must worship is in Jerusalem.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 21, '“Believe Me, woman,” Jesus replied, “a time is coming when you will worship the Father neither on this mountain nor in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 22, 'You worship what you do not know; we worship what we do know, for salvation is from the Jews.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 23, 'But a time is coming and has now come when the true worshipers will worship the Father in spirit and in truth, for the Father is seeking such as these to worship Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 24, 'God is Spirit, and His worshipers must worship Him in spirit and in truth.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 25, 'The woman said, “I know that Messiah” (called Christ) “is coming. When He comes, He will explain everything to us.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 26, 'Jesus answered, “I who speak to you am He.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 27, 'Just then His disciples returned and were surprised that He was speaking with a woman. But no one asked Him, “What do You want from her?” or “Why are You talking with her?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 28, 'Then the woman left her water jar, went back into the town, and said to the people,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 29, '“Come, see a man who told me everything I ever did. Could this be the Christ?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 30, 'So they left the town and made their way toward Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 31, 'Meanwhile the disciples urged Him, “Rabbi, eat something.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 32, 'But He told them, “I have food to eat that you know nothing about.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 33, 'So the disciples asked one another, “Could someone have brought Him food?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 34, 'Jesus explained, “My food is to do the will of Him who sent Me and to finish His work.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 35, 'Do you not say, ‘There are still four months until the harvest’? I tell you, lift up your eyes and look at the fields, for they are ripe for harvest.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 36, 'Already the reaper draws his wages and gathers a crop for eternal life, so that the sower and the reaper may rejoice together.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 37, 'For in this case the saying ‘One sows and another reaps’ is true.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 38, 'I sent you to reap what you have not worked for; others have done the hard work, and now you have taken up their labor.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 39, 'Many of the Samaritans from that town believed in Jesus because of the woman’s testimony, “He told me everything I ever did.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 40, 'So when the Samaritans came to Him, they asked Him to stay with them, and He stayed two days.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 41, 'And many more believed because of His message.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 42, 'They said to the woman, “We now believe not only because of your words; we have heard for ourselves, and we know that this man truly is the Savior of the world.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 43, 'After two days, Jesus left for Galilee.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 44, 'Now He Himself had testified that a prophet has no honor in his own hometown.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 45, 'Yet when He arrived, the Galileans welcomed Him. They had seen all the great things He had done in Jerusalem at the feast, for they had gone there as well.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 46, 'So once again He came to Cana in Galilee, where He had turned the water into wine. And there was a royal official whose son lay sick at Capernaum.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 47, 'When he heard that Jesus had come from Judea to Galilee, he went and begged Him to come down and heal his son, who was about to die.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 48, 'Jesus said to him, “Unless you people see signs and wonders, you will never believe.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 49, '“Sir,” the official said, “come down before my child dies.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 50, '“Go,” said Jesus. “Your son will live.” The man took Jesus at His word and departed.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 51, 'And while he was still on the way, his servants met him with the news that his boy was alive.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 52, 'So he inquired as to the hour when his son had recovered, and they told him, “The fever left him yesterday at the seventh hour.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 53, 'Then the father realized that this was the very hour in which Jesus had told him, “Your son will live.” And he and all his household believed.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 4, 54, 'This was now the second sign that Jesus performed after coming from Judea into Galilee.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 1, 'Some time later there was a feast of the Jews, and Jesus went up to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 2, 'Now there is in Jerusalem near the Sheep Gate a pool with five covered colonnades, which in Hebrew is called Bethesda.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 3, 'On these walkways lay a great number of the sick, the blind, the lame, and the paralyzed.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 4, ''),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 5, 'One man there had been an invalid for thirty-eight years.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 6, 'When Jesus saw him lying there and realized that he had spent a long time in this condition, He asked him, “Do you want to get well?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 7, '“Sir,” the invalid replied, “I have no one to help me into the pool when the water is stirred. While I am on my way, someone else goes in before me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 8, 'Then Jesus told him, “Get up, pick up your mat, and walk.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 9, 'Immediately the man was made well, and he picked up his mat and began to walk. Now this happened on the Sabbath day,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 10, 'so the Jews said to the man who had been healed, “This is the Sabbath! It is unlawful for you to carry your mat.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 11, 'But he answered, “The man who made me well told me, ‘Pick up your mat and walk.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 12, '“Who is this man who told you to pick it up and walk?” they asked.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 13, 'But the man who was healed did not know who it was, for Jesus had slipped away while the crowd was there.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 14, 'Afterward, Jesus found the man at the temple and said to him, “See, you have been made well. Stop sinning, or something worse may happen to you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 15, 'And the man went away and told the Jews that it was Jesus who had made him well.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 16, 'Now because Jesus was doing these things on the Sabbath, the Jews began to persecute Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 17, 'But Jesus answered them, “To this very day My Father is at His work, and I too am working.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 18, 'Because of this, the Jews tried all the harder to kill Him. Not only was He breaking the Sabbath, but He was even calling God His own Father, making Himself equal with God.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 19, 'So Jesus replied, “Truly, truly, I tell you, the Son can do nothing by Himself, unless He sees the Father doing it. For whatever the Father does, the Son also does.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 20, 'The Father loves the Son and shows Him all He does. And to your amazement, He will show Him even greater works than these.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 21, 'For just as the Father raises the dead and gives them life, so also the Son gives life to whom He wishes.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 22, 'Furthermore, the Father judges no one, but has assigned all judgment to the Son,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 23, 'so that all may honor the Son just as they honor the Father. Whoever does not honor the Son does not honor the Father who sent Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 24, 'Truly, truly, I tell you, whoever hears My word and believes Him who sent Me has eternal life and will not come under judgment. Indeed, he has crossed over from death to life.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 25, 'Truly, truly, I tell you, the hour is coming and has now come when the dead will hear the voice of the Son of God, and those who hear will live.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 26, 'For as the Father has life in Himself, so also He has granted the Son to have life in Himself.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 27, 'And He has given Him authority to execute judgment, because He is the Son of Man.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 28, 'Do not be amazed at this, for the hour is coming when all who are in their graves will hear His voice'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 29, 'and come out—those who have done good to the resurrection of life, and those who have done evil to the resurrection of judgment.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 30, 'I can do nothing by Myself; I judge only as I hear. And My judgment is just, because I do not seek My own will, but the will of Him who sent Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 31, 'If I testify about Myself, My testimony is not valid.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 32, 'There is another who testifies about Me, and I know that His testimony about Me is valid.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 33, 'You have sent to John, and he has testified to the truth.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 34, 'Even though I do not accept human testimony, I say these things so that you may be saved.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 35, 'John was a lamp that burned and gave light, and you were willing for a season to bask in his light.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 36, 'But I have testimony more substantial than that of John. For the works that the Father has given Me to accomplish—the very works I am doing—testify about Me that the Father has sent Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 37, 'And the Father who sent Me has Himself testified about Me. You have never heard His voice nor seen His form,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 38, 'nor does His word abide in you, because you do not believe the One He sent.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 39, 'You pore over the Scriptures because you presume that by them you possess eternal life. These are the very words that testify about Me,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 40, 'yet you refuse to come to Me to have life.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 41, 'I do not accept glory from men,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 42, 'but I know you, that you do not have the love of God within you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 43, 'I have come in My Father’s name, and you have not received Me; but if someone else comes in his own name, you will receive him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 44, 'How can you believe if you accept glory from one another, yet do not seek the glory that comes from the only God?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 45, 'Do not think that I will accuse you before the Father. Your accuser is Moses, in whom you have put your hope.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 46, 'If you had believed Moses, you would believe Me, because he wrote about Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 5, 47, 'But since you do not believe what he wrote, how will you believe what I say?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 1, 'After this, Jesus crossed to the other side of the Sea of Galilee (that is, the Sea of Tiberias).'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 2, 'A large crowd followed Him because they saw the signs He was performing on the sick.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 3, 'Then Jesus went up on the mountain and sat down with His disciples.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 4, 'Now the Jewish Feast of the Passover was near.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 5, 'When Jesus looked up and saw a large crowd coming toward Him, He said to Philip, “Where can we buy bread for these people to eat?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 6, 'But He was asking this to test him, for He knew what He was about to do.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 7, 'Philip answered, “Two hundred denarii would not buy enough bread for each of them to have a small piece.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 8, 'One of His disciples, Andrew, Simon Peter’s brother, said to Him,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 9, '“Here is a boy with five barley loaves and two small fish. But what difference will these make among so many?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 10, '“Have the people sit down,” Jesus said. Now there was plenty of grass in that place, so the men sat down, about five thousand of them.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 11, 'Then Jesus took the loaves and the fish, gave thanks, and distributed to those who were seated as much as they wanted.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 12, 'And when everyone was full, He said to His disciples, “Gather the pieces that are left over, so that nothing will be wasted.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 13, 'So they collected them and filled twelve baskets with the pieces of the five barley loaves left over by those who had eaten.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 14, 'When the people saw the sign that Jesus had performed, they began to say, “Truly this is the Prophet who is to come into the world.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 15, 'Then Jesus, realizing that they were about to come and make Him king by force, withdrew again to a mountain by Himself.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 16, 'When evening came, His disciples went down to the sea,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 17, 'got into a boat, and started across the sea to Capernaum. It was already dark, and Jesus had not yet gone out to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 18, 'A strong wind was blowing, and the sea grew agitated.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 19, 'When they had rowed about three or four miles, they saw Jesus approaching the boat, walking on the sea—and they were terrified.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 20, 'But Jesus spoke up: “It is I; do not be afraid.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 21, 'Then they were willing to take Him into the boat, and at once the boat reached the shore where they were heading.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 22, 'The next day, the crowd that had remained on the other side of the sea realized that only one boat had been there, and that Jesus had not boarded it with His disciples, but they had gone away alone.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 23, 'However, some boats from Tiberias landed near the place where the people had eaten the bread after the Lord had given thanks.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 24, 'So when the crowd saw that neither Jesus nor His disciples were there, they got into the boats and went to Capernaum to look for Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 25, 'When they found Him on the other side of the sea, they asked Him, “Rabbi, when did You get here?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 26, 'Jesus replied, “Truly, truly, I tell you, it is not because you saw these signs that you are looking for Me, but because you ate the loaves and had your fill.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 27, 'Do not work for food that perishes, but for food that endures to eternal life, which the Son of Man will give you. For on Him God the Father has placed His seal of approval.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 28, 'Then they inquired, “What must we do to perform the works of God?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 29, 'Jesus replied, “The work of God is this: to believe in the One He has sent.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 30, 'So they asked Him, “What sign then will You perform, so that we may see it and believe You? What will You do?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 31, 'Our fathers ate the manna in the wilderness, as it is written: ‘He gave them bread from heaven to eat.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 32, 'Jesus said to them, “Truly, truly, I tell you, it was not Moses who gave you the bread from heaven, but it is My Father who gives you the true bread from heaven.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 33, 'For the bread of God is He who comes down from heaven and gives life to the world.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 34, '“Sir,” they said, “give us this bread at all times.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 35, 'Jesus answered, “I am the bread of life. Whoever comes to Me will never hunger, and whoever believes in Me will never thirst.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 36, 'But as I stated, you have seen Me and still you do not believe.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 37, 'Everyone the Father gives Me will come to Me, and the one who comes to Me I will never drive away.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 38, 'For I have come down from heaven, not to do My own will, but to do the will of Him who sent Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 39, 'And this is the will of Him who sent Me, that I shall lose none of those He has given Me, but raise them up at the last day.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 40, 'For it is My Father’s will that everyone who looks to the Son and believes in Him shall have eternal life, and I will raise him up at the last day.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 41, 'At this, the Jews began to grumble about Jesus because He had said, “I am the bread that came down from heaven.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 42, 'They were asking, “Is this not Jesus, the son of Joseph, whose father and mother we know? How then can He say, ‘I have come down from heaven?’”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 43, '“Stop grumbling among yourselves,” Jesus replied.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 44, '“No one can come to Me unless the Father who sent Me draws him, and I will raise him up at the last day.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 45, 'It is written in the Prophets: ‘And they will all be taught by God.’ Everyone who has heard the Father and learned from Him comes to Me—'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 46, 'not that anyone has seen the Father except the One who is from God; only He has seen the Father.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 47, 'Truly, truly, I tell you, he who believes has eternal life.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 48, 'I am the bread of life.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 49, 'Your fathers ate the manna in the wilderness, yet they died.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 50, 'This is the bread that comes down from heaven, so that anyone may eat of it and not die.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 51, 'I am the living bread that came down from heaven. If anyone eats of this bread, he will live forever. And this bread, which I will give for the life of the world, is My flesh.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 52, 'At this, the Jews began to argue among themselves, “How can this man give us His flesh to eat?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 53, 'So Jesus said to them, “Truly, truly, I tell you, unless you eat the flesh and drink the blood of the Son of Man, you have no life in you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 54, 'Whoever eats My flesh and drinks My blood has eternal life, and I will raise him up at the last day.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 55, 'For My flesh is real food, and My blood is real drink.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 56, 'Whoever eats My flesh and drinks My blood remains in Me, and I in him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 57, 'Just as the living Father sent Me and I live because of the Father, so also the one who feeds on Me will live because of Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 58, 'This is the bread that came down from heaven. Unlike your fathers, who ate the manna and died, the one who eats this bread will live forever.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 59, 'Jesus said this while teaching in the synagogue in Capernaum.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 60, 'On hearing it, many of His disciples said, “This is a difficult teaching. Who can accept it?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 61, 'Aware that His disciples were grumbling about this teaching, Jesus asked them, “Does this offend you?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 62, 'Then what will happen if you see the Son of Man ascend to where He was before?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 63, 'The Spirit gives life; the flesh profits nothing. The words I have spoken to you are spirit and they are life.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 64, 'However, there are some of you who do not believe.” (For Jesus had known from the beginning which of them did not believe and who would betray Him.)'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 65, 'Then Jesus said, “This is why I told you that no one can come to Me unless the Father has granted it to him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 66, 'From that time on many of His disciples turned back and no longer walked with Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 67, 'So Jesus asked the Twelve, “Do you want to leave too?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 68, 'Simon Peter replied, “Lord, to whom would we go? You have the words of eternal life.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 69, 'We believe and know that You are the Holy One of God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 70, 'Jesus answered them, “Have I not chosen you, the Twelve? Yet one of you is a devil!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 6, 71, 'He was speaking about Judas, the son of Simon Iscariot. For although Judas was one of the Twelve, he was later to betray Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 1, 'After this, Jesus traveled throughout Galilee. He did not want to travel in Judea, because the Jews there were trying to kill Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 2, 'However, the Jewish Feast of Tabernacles was near.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 3, 'So Jesus’ brothers said to Him, “Leave here and go to Judea, so that Your disciples there may see the works You are doing.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 4, 'For no one who wants to be known publicly acts in secret. Since You are doing these things, show Yourself to the world.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 5, 'For even His own brothers did not believe in Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 6, 'Therefore Jesus told them, “Although your time is always at hand, My time has not yet come.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 7, 'The world cannot hate you, but it hates Me, because I testify that its works are evil.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 8, 'Go up to the feast on your own. I am not going up to this feast, because My time has not yet come.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 9, 'Having said this, Jesus remained in Galilee.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 10, 'But after His brothers had gone up to the feast, He also went—not publicly, but in secret.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 11, 'So the Jews were looking for Him at the feast and asking, “Where is He?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 12, 'Many in the crowds were whispering about Him. Some said, “He is a good man.” But others replied, “No, He deceives the people.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 13, 'Yet no one would speak publicly about Him for fear of the Jews.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 14, 'About halfway through the feast, Jesus went up to the temple courts and began to teach.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 15, 'The Jews were amazed and asked, “How did this man attain such learning without having studied?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 16, '“My teaching is not My own,” Jesus replied. “It comes from Him who sent Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 17, 'If anyone desires to do His will, he will know whether My teaching is from God or whether I speak on My own.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 18, 'He who speaks on his own authority seeks his own glory, but He who seeks the glory of the One who sent Him is a man of truth; in Him there is no falsehood.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 19, 'Has not Moses given you the law? Yet not one of you keeps it. Why are you trying to kill Me?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 20, '“You have a demon,” the crowd replied. “Who is trying to kill You?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 21, 'Jesus answered them, “I did one miracle, and you are all amazed.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 22, 'But because Moses gave you circumcision, you circumcise a boy on the Sabbath (not that it is from Moses, but from the patriarchs.)'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 23, 'If a boy can be circumcised on the Sabbath so that the law of Moses will not be broken, why are you angry with Me for making the whole man well on the Sabbath?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 24, 'Stop judging by outward appearances, and start judging justly.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 25, 'Then some of the people of Jerusalem began to say, “Isn’t this the man they are trying to kill?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 26, 'Yet here He is, speaking publicly, and they are not saying anything to Him. Have the rulers truly recognized that this is the Christ?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 27, 'But we know where this man is from. When the Christ comes, no one will know where He is from.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 28, 'Then Jesus, still teaching in the temple courts, cried out, “You know Me, and you know where I am from. I have not come of My own accord, but He who sent Me is true. You do not know Him,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 29, 'but I know Him, because I am from Him and He sent Me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 30, 'So they tried to seize Him, but no one laid a hand on Him, because His hour had not yet come.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 31, 'Many in the crowd, however, believed in Him and said, “When the Christ comes, will He perform more signs than this man?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 32, 'When the Pharisees heard the crowd whispering these things about Jesus, they and the chief priests sent officers to arrest Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 33, 'So Jesus said, “I am with you only a little while longer, and then I am going to the One who sent Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 34, 'You will look for Me, but you will not find Me; and where I am, you cannot come.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 35, 'At this, the Jews said to one another, “Where does He intend to go that we will not find Him? Will He go where the Jews are dispersed among the Greeks, and teach the Greeks?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 36, 'What does He mean by saying, ‘You will look for Me, but you will not find Me,’ and, ‘Where I am, you cannot come’?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 37, 'On the last and greatest day of the feast, Jesus stood up and called out in a loud voice, “If anyone is thirsty, let him come to Me and drink.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 38, 'Whoever believes in Me, as the Scripture has said: ‘Streams of living water will flow from within him.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 39, 'He was speaking about the Spirit, whom those who believed in Him were later to receive. For the Spirit had not yet been given, because Jesus had not yet been glorified.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 40, 'On hearing these words, some of the people said, “This is truly the Prophet.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 41, 'Others declared, “This is the Christ.” But still others asked, “How can the Christ come from Galilee?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 42, 'Doesn’t the Scripture say that the Christ will come from the line of David and from Bethlehem, the village where David lived?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 43, 'So there was division in the crowd because of Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 44, 'Some of them wanted to seize Him, but no one laid a hand on Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 45, 'Then the officers returned to the chief priests and Pharisees, who asked them, “Why didn’t you bring Him in?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 46, '“Never has anyone spoken like this man!” the officers answered.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 47, '“Have you also been deceived?” replied the Pharisees.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 48, '“Have any of the rulers or Pharisees believed in Him?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 49, 'But this crowd that does not know the law, they are under a curse.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 50, 'Nicodemus, who had gone to Jesus earlier and who himself was one of them, asked,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 51, '“Does our law convict a man without first hearing from him to determine what he has done?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 52, '“Aren’t you also from Galilee?” they replied. “Look into it, and you will see that no prophet comes out of Galilee.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 7, 53, 'Then each went to his own home.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 1, 'But Jesus went to the Mount of Olives.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 2, 'Early in the morning He went back into the temple courts. All the people came to Him, and He sat down to teach them.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 3, 'The scribes and Pharisees, however, brought to Him a woman caught in adultery. They made her stand before them'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 4, 'and said, “Teacher, this woman was caught in the act of adultery.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 5, 'In the Law Moses commanded us to stone such a woman. So what do You say?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 6, 'They said this to test Him, in order to have a basis for accusing Him. But Jesus bent down and began to write on the ground with His finger.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 7, 'When they continued to question Him, He straightened up and said to them, “Let him who is without sin among you be the first to cast a stone at her.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 8, 'And again He bent down and wrote on the ground.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 9, 'When they heard this, they began to go away one by one, beginning with the older ones, until only Jesus was left, with the woman standing there.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 10, 'Then Jesus straightened up and asked her, “Woman, where are your accusers? Has no one condemned you?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 11, '“No one, Lord,” she answered. “Then neither do I condemn you,” Jesus declared. “Now go and sin no more.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 12, 'Once again, Jesus spoke to the people and said, “I am the light of the world. Whoever follows Me will never walk in the darkness, but will have the light of life.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 13, 'So the Pharisees said to Him, “You are testifying about Yourself; Your testimony is not valid.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 14, 'Jesus replied, “Even if I testify about Myself, My testimony is valid, because I know where I came from and where I am going. But you do not know where I came from or where I am going.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 15, 'You judge according to the flesh; I judge no one.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 16, 'But even if I do judge, My judgment is true, because I am not alone; I am with the Father who sent Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 17, 'Even in your own Law it is written that the testimony of two men is valid.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 18, 'I am One who testifies about Myself, and the Father, who sent Me, also testifies about Me.”');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 19, '“Where is Your Father?” they asked Him. “You do not know Me or My Father,” Jesus answered. “If you knew Me, you would know My Father as well.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 20, 'He spoke these words while teaching in the temple courts, near the treasury. Yet no one seized Him, because His hour had not yet come.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 21, 'Again He said to them, “I am going away, and you will look for Me, but you will die in your sin. Where I am going, you cannot come.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 22, 'So the Jews began to ask, “Will He kill Himself, since He says, ‘Where I am going, you cannot come’?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 23, 'Then He told them, “You are from below; I am from above. You are of this world; I am not of this world.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 24, 'That is why I told you that you would die in your sins. For unless you believe that I am He, you will die in your sins.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 25, '“Who are You?” they asked. “Just what I have been telling you from the beginning,” Jesus replied.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 26, '“I have much to say about you and much to judge. But the One who sent Me is truthful, and what I have heard from Him, I tell the world.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 27, 'They did not understand that He was telling them about the Father.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 28, 'So Jesus said, “When you have lifted up the Son of Man, then you will know that I am He, and that I do nothing on My own, but speak exactly what the Father has taught Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 29, 'He who sent Me is with Me. He has not left Me alone, because I always do what pleases Him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 30, 'As Jesus spoke these things, many believed in Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 31, 'So He said to the Jews who had believed Him, “If you continue in My word, you are truly My disciples.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 32, 'Then you will know the truth, and the truth will set you free.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 33, '“We are Abraham’s descendants,” they answered. “We have never been slaves to anyone. How can You say we will be set free?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 34, 'Jesus replied, “Truly, truly, I tell you, everyone who sins is a slave to sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 35, 'A slave is not a permanent member of the family, but a son belongs to it forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 36, 'So if the Son sets you free, you will be free indeed.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 37, 'I know you are Abraham’s descendants, but you are trying to kill Me because My word has no place within you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 38, 'I speak of what I have seen in the presence of the Father, and you do what you have heard from your father.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 39, '“Abraham is our father,” they replied. “If you were children of Abraham,” said Jesus, “you would do the works of Abraham.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 40, 'But now you are trying to kill Me, a man who has told you the truth that I heard from God. Abraham never did such a thing.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 41, 'You are doing the works of your father.” “We are not illegitimate children,” they declared. “Our only Father is God Himself.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 42, 'Jesus said to them, “If God were your Father, you would love Me, for I have come here from God. I have not come on My own, but He sent Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 43, 'Why do you not understand what I am saying? It is because you are unable to accept My message.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 44, 'You belong to your father, the devil, and you want to carry out his desires. He was a murderer from the beginning, refusing to uphold the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he lies, he speaks his native language, because he is a liar and the father of lies.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 45, 'But because I speak the truth, you do not believe Me!'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 46, 'Which of you can prove Me guilty of sin? If I speak the truth, why do you not believe Me?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 47, 'Whoever belongs to God hears the words of God. The reason you do not hear is that you do not belong to God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 48, 'The Jews answered Him, “Are we not right to say that You are a Samaritan and You have a demon?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 49, '“I do not have a demon,” Jesus replied, “but I honor My Father, and you dishonor Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 50, 'I do not seek My own glory. There is One who seeks it, and He is the Judge.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 51, 'Truly, truly, I tell you, if anyone keeps My word, he will never see death.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 52, '“Now we know that You have a demon!” declared the Jews. “Abraham died, and so did the prophets, yet You say that anyone who keeps Your word will never taste death.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 53, 'Are You greater than our father Abraham? He died, as did the prophets. Who do You claim to be?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 54, 'Jesus answered, “If I glorify Myself, My glory means nothing. The One who glorifies Me is My Father, of whom you say ‘He is our God.’'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 55, 'You do not know Him, but I know Him. If I said I did not know Him, I would be a liar like you. But I do know Him, and I keep His word.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 56, 'Your father Abraham rejoiced that he would see My day. He saw it and was glad.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 57, 'Then the Jews said to Him, “You are not yet fifty years old, and You have seen Abraham?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 58, '“Truly, truly, I tell you,” Jesus declared, “before Abraham was born, I am!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 8, 59, 'At this, they picked up stones to throw at Him. But Jesus was hidden and went out of the temple area.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 1, 'Now as Jesus was passing by, He saw a man blind from birth,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 2, 'and His disciples asked Him, “Rabbi, who sinned, this man or his parents, that he was born blind?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 3, 'Jesus answered, “Neither this man nor his parents sinned, but this happened so that the works of God would be displayed in him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 4, 'While it is daytime, we must do the works of Him who sent Me. Night is coming, when no one can work.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 5, 'While I am in the world, I am the light of the world.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 6, 'When Jesus had said this, He spit on the ground, made some mud, and applied it to the man’s eyes.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 7, 'Then He told him, “Go, wash in the Pool of Siloam” (which means “Sent”). So the man went and washed, and came back seeing.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 8, 'At this, his neighbors and those who had formerly seen him begging began to ask, “Isn’t this the man who used to sit and beg?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 9, 'Some claimed that he was, but others said, “No, he just looks like him.” But the man kept saying, “I am the one.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 10, '“How then were your eyes opened?” they asked.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 11, 'He answered, “The man they call Jesus made some mud and anointed my eyes, and He told me to go to Siloam and wash. So I went and washed and received my sight.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 12, '“Where is He?” they asked. “I do not know,” he answered.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 13, 'They brought to the Pharisees the man who had been blind.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 14, 'Now the day on which Jesus had made the mud and opened his eyes was a Sabbath.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 15, 'So the Pharisees also asked him how he had received his sight. The man answered, “He put mud on my eyes, and I washed, and now I can see.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 16, 'Because of this, some of the Pharisees said, “This man is not from God, for He does not keep the Sabbath.” But others said, “How can a sinful man perform such signs?” And there was division among them.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 17, 'So once again they asked the man who had been blind, “What do you say about Him, since it was your eyes He opened?” “He is a prophet,” the man replied.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 18, 'The Jews still did not believe that the man had been blind and had received his sight until they summoned his parents'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 19, 'and asked, “Is this your son, the one you say was born blind? So how is it that he can now see?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 20, 'His parents answered, “We know he is our son, and we know he was born blind.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 21, 'But how he can now see or who opened his eyes, we do not know. Ask him. He is old enough to speak for himself.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 22, 'His parents said this because they were afraid of the Jews. For the Jews had already determined that anyone who confessed Jesus as the Christ would be put out of the synagogue.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 23, 'That was why his parents said, “He is old enough. Ask him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 24, 'So a second time they called for the man who had been blind and said, “Give glory to God! We know that this man is a sinner.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 25, 'He answered, “Whether He is a sinner I do not know. There is one thing I do know: I was blind, but now I see!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 26, '“What did He do to you?” they asked. “How did He open your eyes?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 27, 'He replied, “I already told you, and you did not listen. Why do you want to hear it again? Do you also want to become His disciples?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 28, 'Then they heaped insults on him and said, “You are His disciple; we are disciples of Moses.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 29, 'We know that God spoke to Moses, but we do not know where this man is from.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 30, '“That is remarkable indeed!” the man said. “You do not know where He is from, and yet He opened my eyes.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 31, 'We know that God does not listen to sinners, but He does listen to the one who worships Him and does His will.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 32, 'Never before has anyone heard of opening the eyes of a man born blind.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 33, 'If this man were not from God, He could do no such thing.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 34, 'They replied, “You were born in utter sin, and you are instructing us?” And they threw him out.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 35, 'When Jesus heard that they had thrown him out, He found the man and said, “Do you believe in the Son of Man?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 36, '“Who is He, Sir?” he replied. “Tell me so that I may believe in Him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 37, '“You have already seen Him,” Jesus answered. “He is the One speaking with you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 38, '“Lord, I believe,” he said. And he worshiped Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 39, 'Then Jesus declared, “For judgment I have come into this world, so that the blind may see and those who see may become blind.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 40, 'Some of the Pharisees who were with Him heard this, and they asked Him, “Are we blind too?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 9, 41, '“If you were blind,” Jesus replied, “you would not be guilty of sin. But since you claim you can see, your guilt remains.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 1, '“Truly, truly, I tell you, whoever does not enter the sheepfold by the gate, but climbs in some other way, is a thief and a robber.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 2, 'But the one who enters by the gate is the shepherd of the sheep.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 3, 'The gatekeeper opens the gate for him, and the sheep listen for his voice. He calls his own sheep by name and leads them out.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 4, 'When he has brought out all his own, he goes on ahead of them, and his sheep follow him because they know his voice.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 5, 'But they will never follow a stranger; in fact, they will flee from him because they do not recognize his voice.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 6, 'Jesus spoke to them using this illustration, but they did not understand what He was telling them.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 7, 'So He said to them again, “Truly, truly, I tell you, I am the gate for the sheep.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 8, 'All who came before Me were thieves and robbers, but the sheep did not listen to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 9, 'I am the gate. If anyone enters through Me, he will be saved. He will come in and go out and find pasture.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 10, 'The thief comes only to steal and kill and destroy. I have come that they may have life, and have it in all its fullness.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 11, 'I am the good shepherd. The good shepherd lays down His life for the sheep.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 12, 'The hired hand is not the shepherd, and the sheep are not his own. When he sees the wolf coming, he abandons the sheep and runs away. Then the wolf pounces on them and scatters the flock.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 13, 'The man runs away because he is a hired servant and is unconcerned for the sheep.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 14, 'I am the good shepherd. I know My sheep and My sheep know Me,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 15, 'just as the Father knows Me and I know the Father. And I lay down My life for the sheep.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 16, 'I have other sheep that are not of this fold. I must bring them in as well, and they will listen to My voice. Then there will be one flock and one shepherd.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 17, 'The reason the Father loves Me is that I lay down My life in order to take it up again.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 18, 'No one takes it from Me, but I lay it down of My own accord. I have authority to lay it down and authority to take it up again. This charge I have received from My Father.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 19, 'Again there was division among the Jews because of Jesus’ message.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 20, 'Many of them said, “He is demon-possessed and insane. Why would you listen to Him?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 21, 'But others replied, “These are not the words of a man possessed by a demon. Can a demon open the eyes of the blind?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 22, 'At that time the Feast of Dedication took place in Jerusalem. It was winter,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 23, 'and Jesus was walking in the temple courts in Solomon’s Colonnade.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 24, 'So the Jews gathered around Him and demanded, “How long will You keep us in suspense? If You are the Christ, tell us plainly.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 25, '“I already told you,” Jesus replied, “but you did not believe. The works I do in My Father’s name testify on My behalf.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 26, 'But because you are not My sheep, you refuse to believe.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 27, 'My sheep listen to My voice; I know them, and they follow Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 28, 'I give them eternal life, and they will never perish. No one can snatch them out of My hand.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 29, 'My Father who has given them to Me is greater than all. No one can snatch them out of My Father’s hand.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 30, 'I and the Father are one.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 31, 'At this, the Jews again picked up stones to stone Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 32, 'But Jesus responded, “I have shown you many good works from the Father. For which of these do you stone Me?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 33, '“We are not stoning You for any good work,” said the Jews, “but for blasphemy, because You, who are a man, declare Yourself to be God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 34, 'Jesus replied, “Is it not written in your Law: ‘I have said you are gods’?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 35, 'If he called them gods to whom the word of God came—and the Scripture cannot be broken—'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 36, 'then what about the One whom the Father sanctified and sent into the world? How then can you accuse Me of blasphemy for stating that I am the Son of God?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 37, 'If I am not doing the works of My Father, then do not believe Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 38, 'But if I am doing them, even though you do not believe Me, believe the works themselves, so that you may know and understand that the Father is in Me, and I am in the Father.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 39, 'At this, they tried again to seize Him, but He escaped their grasp.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 40, 'Then Jesus went back across the Jordan to the place where John had first been baptizing, and He stayed there.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 41, 'Many came to Him and said, “Although John never performed a sign, everything he said about this man was true.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 10, 42, 'And many in that place believed in Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 1, 'At this time a man named Lazarus was sick. He lived in Bethany, the village of Mary and her sister Martha.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 2, '(Mary, whose brother Lazarus was sick, was to anoint the Lord with perfume and wipe His feet with her hair.)'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 3, 'So the sisters sent word to Jesus, “Lord, the one You love is sick.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 4, 'When Jesus heard this, He said, “This sickness will not end in death. No, it is for the glory of God, so that the Son of God may be glorified through it.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 5, 'Now Jesus loved Martha and her sister and Lazarus.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 6, 'So on hearing that Lazarus was sick, He stayed where He was for two days,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 7, 'and then He said to the disciples, “Let us go back to Judea.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 8, '“Rabbi,” they replied, “the Jews just tried to stone You, and You are going back there?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 9, 'Jesus answered, “Are there not twelve hours of daylight? If anyone walks in the daytime, he will not stumble, because he sees by the light of this world.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 10, 'But if anyone walks at night, he will stumble, because he has no light.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 11, 'After He had said this, He told them, “Our friend Lazarus has fallen asleep, but I am going there to wake him up.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 12, 'His disciples replied, “Lord, if he is sleeping, he will get better.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 13, 'They thought that Jesus was talking about actual sleep, but He was speaking about the death of Lazarus.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 14, 'So Jesus told them plainly, “Lazarus is dead,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 15, 'and for your sake I am glad I was not there, so that you may believe. But let us go to him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 16, 'Then Thomas called Didymus said to his fellow disciples, “Let us also go, so that we may die with Him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 17, 'When Jesus arrived, He found that Lazarus had already spent four days in the tomb.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 18, 'Now Bethany was near Jerusalem, a little less than two miles away,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 19, 'and many of the Jews had come to Martha and Mary to console them in the loss of their brother.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 20, 'So when Martha heard that Jesus was coming, she went out to meet Him; but Mary stayed at home.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 21, 'Martha said to Jesus, “Lord, if You had been here, my brother would not have died.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 22, 'But even now I know that God will give You whatever You ask of Him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 23, '“Your brother will rise again,” Jesus told her.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 24, 'Martha replied, “I know that he will rise again in the resurrection at the last day.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 25, 'Jesus said to her, “I am the resurrection and the life. Whoever believes in Me will live, even though he dies.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 26, 'And everyone who lives and believes in Me will never die. Do you believe this?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 27, '“Yes, Lord,” she answered, “I believe that You are the Christ, the Son of God, who was to come into the world.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 28, 'After Martha had said this, she went back and called her sister Mary aside to tell her, “The Teacher is here and is asking for you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 29, 'And when Mary heard this, she got up quickly and went to Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 30, 'Now Jesus had not yet entered the village, but was still at the place where Martha had met Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 31, 'When the Jews who were in the house consoling Mary saw how quickly she got up and went out, they followed her, supposing she was going to the tomb to mourn there.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 32, 'When Mary came to Jesus and saw Him, she fell at His feet and said, “Lord, if You had been here, my brother would not have died.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 33, 'When Jesus saw her weeping, and the Jews who had come with her also weeping, He was deeply moved in spirit and troubled.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 34, '“Where have you put him?” He asked. “Come and see, Lord,” they answered.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 35, 'Jesus wept.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 36, 'Then the Jews said, “See how He loved him!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 37, 'But some of them asked, “Could not this man who opened the eyes of the blind also have kept Lazarus from dying?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 38, 'Jesus, once again deeply moved, came to the tomb. It was a cave with a stone laid across the entrance.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 39, '“Take away the stone,” Jesus said. “Lord, by now he stinks,” said Martha, the sister of the dead man. “It has already been four days.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 40, 'Jesus replied, “Did I not tell you that if you believed, you would see the glory of God?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 41, 'So they took away the stone. Then Jesus lifted His eyes upward and said, “Father, I thank You that You have heard Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 42, 'I knew that You always hear Me, but I say this for the benefit of the people standing here, so they may believe that You sent Me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 43, 'After Jesus had said this, He called out in a loud voice, “Lazarus, come out!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 44, 'The man who had been dead came out with his hands and feet bound in strips of linen, and his face wrapped in a cloth. “Unwrap him and let him go,” Jesus told them.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 45, 'Therefore many of the Jews who had come to Mary, and had seen what Jesus did, believed in Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 46, 'But some of them went to the Pharisees and told them what Jesus had done.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 47, 'Then the chief priests and Pharisees convened the Sanhedrin and said, “What are we to do? This man is performing many signs.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 48, 'If we let Him go on like this, everyone will believe in Him, and then the Romans will come and take away both our place and our nation.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 49, 'But one of them, named Caiaphas, who was high priest that year, said to them, “You know nothing at all!'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 50, 'You do not realize that it is better for you that one man die for the people than that the whole nation perish.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 51, 'Caiaphas did not say this on his own. Instead, as high priest that year, he was prophesying that Jesus would die for the nation,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 52, 'and not only for the nation, but also for the scattered children of God, to gather them together into one.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 53, 'So from that day on they plotted to kill Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 54, 'As a result, Jesus no longer went about publicly among the Jews, but He withdrew to a town called Ephraim in an area near the wilderness. And He stayed there with the disciples.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 55, 'Now the Jewish Passover was near, and many people went up from the country to Jerusalem to purify themselves before the Passover.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 56, 'They kept looking for Jesus and asking one another as they stood in the temple courts, “What do you think? Will He come to the feast at all?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 11, 57, 'But the chief priests and Pharisees had given orders that anyone who knew where He was must report it, so that they could arrest Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 1, 'Six days before the Passover, Jesus came to Bethany, the hometown of Lazarus, whom He had raised from the dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 2, 'So they hosted a dinner for Jesus there. Martha served, and Lazarus was among those reclining at the table with Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 3, 'Then Mary took about a pint of expensive perfume, made of pure nard, and she anointed Jesus’ feet and wiped them with her hair. And the house was filled with the fragrance of the perfume.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 4, 'But one of His disciples, Judas Iscariot, who was going to betray Him, asked,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 5, '“Why wasn’t this perfume sold for three hundred denarii and the money given to the poor?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 6, 'Judas did not say this because he cared about the poor, but because he was a thief. As keeper of the money bag, he used to take from what was put into it.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 7, '“Leave her alone,” Jesus replied. “She has kept this perfume in preparation for the day of My burial.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 8, 'The poor you will always have with you, but you will not always have Me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 9, 'Meanwhile a large crowd of Jews learned that Jesus was there. And they came not only because of Him, but also to see Lazarus, whom He had raised from the dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 10, 'So the chief priests made plans to kill Lazarus as well,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 11, 'for on account of him many of the Jews were deserting them and believing in Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 12, 'The next day the great crowd that had come to the feast heard that Jesus was coming to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 13, 'They took palm branches and went out to meet Him, shouting: “Hosanna!” “Blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord!” “Blessed is the King of Israel!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 14, 'Finding a young donkey, Jesus sat on it, as it is written:'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 15, '“Do not be afraid, O Daughter of Zion. See, your King is coming, seated on the colt of a donkey.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 16, 'At first His disciples did not understand these things, but after Jesus was glorified they remembered what had been done to Him, and they realized that these very things had also been written about Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 17, 'Meanwhile, many people continued to testify that they had been with Jesus when He called Lazarus from the tomb and raised him from the dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 18, 'That is also why the crowd went out to meet Him, because they heard that He had performed this sign.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 19, 'Then the Pharisees said to one another, “You can see that this is doing you no good. Look how the whole world has gone after Him!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 20, 'Now there were some Greeks among those who went up to worship at the feast.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 21, 'They came to Philip, who was from Bethsaida in Galilee, and requested of him, “Sir, we want to see Jesus.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 22, 'Philip relayed this appeal to Andrew, and both of them went and told Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 23, 'But Jesus replied, “The hour has come for the Son of Man to be glorified.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 24, 'Truly, truly, I tell you, unless a kernel of wheat falls to the ground and dies, it remains only a seed; but if it dies, it bears much fruit.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 25, 'Whoever loves his life will lose it, but whoever hates his life in this world will keep it for eternal life.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 26, 'If anyone serves Me, he must follow Me; and where I am, My servant will be as well. If anyone serves Me, the Father will honor him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 27, 'Now My soul is troubled, and what shall I say? ‘Father, save Me from this hour’? No, it is for this purpose that I have come to this hour.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 28, 'Father, glorify Your name!” Then a voice came from heaven: “I have glorified it, and I will glorify it again.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 29, 'The crowd standing there heard it and said that it had thundered. Others said that an angel had spoken to Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 30, 'In response, Jesus said, “This voice was not for My benefit, but yours.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 31, 'Now judgment is upon this world; now the prince of this world will be cast out.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 32, 'And I, when I am lifted up from the earth, will draw everyone to Myself.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 33, 'He said this to indicate the kind of death He was going to die.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 34, 'The crowd replied, “We have heard from the Law that the Christ will remain forever. So how can You say that the Son of Man must be lifted up? Who is this Son of Man?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 35, 'Then Jesus told them, “For a little while longer, the Light will be among you. Walk while you have the Light, so that darkness will not overtake you. The one who walks in the darkness does not know where he is going.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 36, 'While you have the Light, believe in the Light, so that you may become sons of light.” After Jesus had spoken these things, He went away and was hidden from them.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 37, 'Although Jesus had performed so many signs in their presence, they still did not believe in Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 38, 'This was to fulfill the word of Isaiah the prophet: “Lord, who has believed our message? And to whom has the arm of the Lord been revealed?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 39, 'For this reason they were unable to believe. For again, Isaiah says:'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 40, '“He has blinded their eyes and hardened their hearts, so that they cannot see with their eyes, and understand with their hearts, and turn, and I would heal them.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 41, 'Isaiah said these things because he saw Jesus’ glory and spoke about Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 42, 'Nevertheless, many of the leaders believed in Him; but because of the Pharisees they did not confess Him, for fear that they would be put out of the synagogue.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 43, 'For they loved praise from men more than praise from God.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 44, 'Then Jesus cried out, “Whoever believes in Me does not believe in Me alone, but in the One who sent Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 45, 'And whoever sees Me sees the One who sent Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 46, 'I have come into the world as a light, so that no one who believes in Me should remain in darkness.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 47, 'As for anyone who hears My words and does not keep them, I do not judge him. For I have not come to judge the world, but to save the world.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 48, 'There is a judge for the one who rejects Me and does not receive My words: The word that I have spoken will judge him on the last day.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 49, 'I have not spoken on My own, but the Father who sent Me has commanded Me what to say and how to say it.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 12, 50, 'And I know that His command leads to eternal life. So I speak exactly what the Father has told Me to say.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 1, 'It was now just before the Passover Feast, and Jesus knew that His hour had come to leave this world and return to the Father. Having loved His own who were in the world, He loved them to the very end.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 2, 'The evening meal was underway, and the devil had already put into the heart of Judas, the son of Simon Iscariot, to betray Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 3, 'Jesus knew that the Father had delivered all things into His hands, and that He had come from God and was returning to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 4, 'So He got up from the supper, laid aside His outer garments, and wrapped a towel around His waist.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 5, 'After that, He poured water into a basin and began to wash the disciples’ feet and dry them with the towel that was around Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 6, 'He came to Simon Peter, who asked Him, “Lord, are You going to wash my feet?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 7, 'Jesus replied, “You do not realize now what I am doing, but later you will understand.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 8, '“Never shall You wash my feet!” Peter told Him. Jesus answered, “Unless I wash you, you have no part with Me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 9, '“Then, Lord,” Simon Peter replied, “not only my feet, but my hands and my head as well!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 10, 'Jesus told him, “Whoever has already bathed needs only to wash his feet, and he will be completely clean. And you are clean, though not all of you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 11, 'For He knew who would betray Him. That is why He said, “Not all of you are clean.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 12, 'When Jesus had washed their feet and put on His outer garments, He reclined with them again and asked, “Do you know what I have done for you?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 13, 'You call Me Teacher and Lord, and rightly so, because I am.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 14, 'So if I, your Lord and Teacher, have washed your feet, you also should wash one another’s feet.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 15, 'I have set you an example so that you should do as I have done for you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 16, 'Truly, truly, I tell you, no servant is greater than his master, nor is a messenger greater than the one who sent him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 17, 'If you know these things, you will be blessed if you do them.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 18, 'I am not speaking about all of you; I know whom I have chosen. But this is to fulfill the Scripture: ‘The one who shares My bread has lifted up his heel against Me.’'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 19, 'I am telling you now before it happens, so that when it comes to pass, you will believe that I am He.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 20, 'Truly, truly, I tell you, whoever receives the one I send receives Me, and whoever receives Me receives the One who sent Me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 21, 'After Jesus had said this, He became troubled in spirit and testified, “Truly, truly, I tell you, one of you will betray Me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 22, 'The disciples looked at one another, perplexed as to which of them He meant.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 23, 'One of His disciples, the one whom Jesus loved, was reclining at His side.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 24, 'So Simon Peter motioned to him to ask Jesus which one He was talking about.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 25, 'Leaning back against Jesus, he asked, “Lord, who is it?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 26, 'Jesus answered, “It is the one to whom I give this morsel after I have dipped it.” Then He dipped the morsel and gave it to Judas son of Simon Iscariot.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 27, 'And when Judas had taken the morsel, Satan entered into him. Then Jesus said to Judas, “What you are about to do, do quickly.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 28, 'But no one at the table knew why Jesus had said this to him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 29, 'Since Judas kept the money bag, some thought that Jesus was telling him to buy what was needed for the feast, or to give something to the poor.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 30, 'As soon as he had received the morsel, Judas went out into the night.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 31, 'When Judas had gone out, Jesus said, “Now the Son of Man is glorified, and God is glorified in Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 32, 'If God is glorified in Him, God will also glorify the Son in Himself—and will glorify Him at once.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 33, 'Little children, I am with you only a little while longer. You will look for Me, and as I said to the Jews, so now I say to you: ‘Where I am going, you cannot come.’'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 34, 'A new commandment I give you: Love one another. As I have loved you, so you also must love one another.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 35, 'By this everyone will know that you are My disciples, if you love one another.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 36, '“Lord, where are You going?” Simon Peter asked. Jesus answered, “Where I am going, you cannot follow Me now, but you will follow later.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 37, '“Lord,” said Peter, “why can’t I follow You now? I will lay down my life for You.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 13, 38, '“Will you lay down your life for Me?” Jesus replied. “Truly, truly, I tell you, before the rooster crows, you will deny Me three times.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 1, '“Do not let your hearts be troubled. You believe in God; believe in Me as well.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 2, 'In My Father’s house are many rooms. If it were not so, would I have told you that I am going there to prepare a place for you?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 3, 'And if I go and prepare a place for you, I will come back and welcome you into My presence, so that you also may be where I am.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 4, 'You know the way to the place where I am going.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 5, '“Lord,” said Thomas, “we do not know where You are going, so how can we know the way?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 6, 'Jesus answered, “I am the way and the truth and the life. No one comes to the Father except through Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 7, 'If you had known Me, you would know My Father as well. From now on you do know Him and have seen Him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 8, 'Philip said to Him, “Lord, show us the Father, and that will be enough for us.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 9, 'Jesus replied, “Philip, I have been with you all this time, and still you do not know Me? Anyone who has seen Me has seen the Father. How can you say, ‘Show us the Father’?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 10, 'Do you not believe that I am in the Father and the Father is in Me? The words I say to you, I do not speak on My own. Instead, it is the Father dwelling in Me, performing His works.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 11, 'Believe Me that I am in the Father and the Father is in Me—or at least believe on account of the works themselves.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 12, 'Truly, truly, I tell you, whoever believes in Me will also do the works that I am doing. He will do even greater things than these, because I am going to the Father.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 13, 'And I will do whatever you ask in My name, so that the Father may be glorified in the Son.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 14, 'If you ask Me for anything in My name, I will do it.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 15, 'If you love Me, you will keep My commandments.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 16, 'And I will ask the Father, and He will give you another Advocate to be with you forever—'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 17, 'the Spirit of truth. The world cannot receive Him, because it neither sees Him nor knows Him. But you do know Him, for He abides with you and will be in you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 18, 'I will not leave you as orphans; I will come to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 19, 'In a little while the world will see Me no more, but you will see Me. Because I live, you also will live.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 20, 'On that day you will know that I am in My Father, and you are in Me, and I am in you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 21, 'Whoever has My commandments and keeps them is the one who loves Me. The one who loves Me will be loved by My Father, and I will love him and reveal Myself to him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 22, 'Judas (not Iscariot) asked Him, “Lord, why are You going to reveal Yourself to us and not to the world?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 23, 'Jesus replied, “If anyone loves Me, he will keep My word. My Father will love him, and We will come to him and make Our home with him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 24, 'Whoever does not love Me does not keep My words. The word that you hear is not My own, but it is from the Father who sent Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 25, 'All this I have spoken to you while I am still with you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 26, 'But the Advocate, the Holy Spirit, whom the Father will send in My name, will teach you all things and will remind you of everything I have told you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 27, 'Peace I leave with you; My peace I give to you. I do not give to you as the world gives. Do not let your hearts be troubled; do not be afraid.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 28, 'You heard Me say, ‘I am going away, and I am coming back to you.’ If you loved Me, you would rejoice that I am going to the Father, because the Father is greater than I.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 29, 'And now I have told you before it happens, so that when it does happen, you will believe.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 30, 'I will not speak with you much longer, for the prince of this world is coming, and he has no claim on Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 14, 31, 'But I do exactly what the Father has commanded Me, so that the world may know that I love the Father. Get up! Let us go on from here.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 1, '“I am the true vine, and My Father is the keeper of the vineyard.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 2, 'He cuts off every branch in Me that bears no fruit, and every branch that does bear fruit, He prunes to make it even more fruitful.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 3, 'You are already clean because of the word I have spoken to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 4, 'Remain in Me, and I will remain in you. Just as no branch can bear fruit by itself unless it remains in the vine, neither can you bear fruit unless you remain in Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 5, 'I am the vine and you are the branches. The one who remains in Me, and I in him, will bear much fruit. For apart from Me you can do nothing.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 6, 'If anyone does not remain in Me, he is like a branch that is thrown away and withers. Such branches are gathered up, thrown into the fire, and burned.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 7, 'If you remain in Me and My words remain in you, ask whatever you wish, and it will be done for you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 8, 'This is to My Father’s glory, that you bear much fruit, proving yourselves to be My disciples.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 9, 'As the Father has loved Me, so have I loved you. Remain in My love.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 10, 'If you keep My commandments, you will remain in My love, just as I have kept My Father’s commandments and remain in His love.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 11, 'I have told you these things so that My joy may be in you and your joy may be complete.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 12, 'This is My commandment, that you love one another as I have loved you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 13, 'Greater love has no one than this, that he lay down his life for his friends.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 14, 'You are My friends if you do what I command you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 15, 'No longer do I call you servants, for a servant does not understand what his master is doing. But I have called you friends, because everything I have learned from My Father I have made known to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 16, 'You did not choose Me, but I chose you. And I appointed you to go and bear fruit—fruit that will remain—so that whatever you ask the Father in My name, He will give you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 17, 'This is My command to you: Love one another.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 18, 'If the world hates you, understand that it hated Me first.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 19, 'If you were of the world, it would love you as its own. Instead, the world hates you, because you are not of the world, but I have chosen you out of the world.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 20, 'Remember the word that I spoke to you: ‘No servant is greater than his master.’ If they persecuted Me, they will persecute you as well; if they kept My word, they will keep yours as well.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 21, 'But they will treat you like this because of My name, since they do not know the One who sent Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 22, 'If I had not come and spoken to them, they would not be guilty of sin. Now, however, they have no excuse for their sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 23, 'Whoever hates Me hates My Father as well.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 24, 'If I had not done among them the works that no one else did, they would not be guilty of sin; but now they have seen and hated both Me and My Father.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 25, 'But this is to fulfill what is written in their Law: ‘They hated Me without reason.’'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 26, 'When the Advocate comes, whom I will send to you from the Father—the Spirit of truth who proceeds from the Father—He will testify about Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 15, 27, 'And you also must testify, because you have been with Me from the beginning.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 1, '“I have told you these things so that you will not fall away.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 2, 'They will put you out of the synagogues. In fact, a time is coming when anyone who kills you will think he is offering a service to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 3, 'They will do these things because they have not known the Father or Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 4, 'But I have told you these things so that when their hour comes, you will remember that I told you about them. I did not tell you these things from the beginning, because I was with you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 5, 'Now, however, I am going to Him who sent Me; yet none of you asks Me, ‘Where are You going?’'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 6, 'Instead, your hearts are filled with sorrow because I have told you these things.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 7, 'But I tell you the truth, it is for your benefit that I am going away. Unless I go away, the Advocate will not come to you; but if I go, I will send Him to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 8, 'And when He comes, He will convict the world in regard to sin and righteousness and judgment:'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 9, 'in regard to sin, because they do not believe in Me;'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 10, 'in regard to righteousness, because I am going to the Father and you will no longer see Me;'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 11, 'and in regard to judgment, because the prince of this world has been condemned.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 12, 'I still have much to tell you, but you cannot yet bear to hear it.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 13, 'However, when the Spirit of truth comes, He will guide you into all truth. For He will not speak on His own, but He will speak what He hears, and He will declare to you what is to come.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 14, 'He will glorify Me by taking from what is Mine and disclosing it to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 15, 'Everything that belongs to the Father is Mine. That is why I said that the Spirit will take from what is Mine and disclose it to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 16, 'In a little while you will see Me no more, and then after a little while you will see Me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 17, 'Then some of His disciples asked one another, “Why is He telling us, ‘In a little while you will not see Me, and then after a little while you will see Me’ and ‘Because I am going to the Father’?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 18, 'They kept asking, “Why is He saying, ‘a little while’? We do not understand what He is saying.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 19, 'Aware that they wanted to question Him, Jesus said to them, “Are you asking one another why I said, ‘In a little while you will not see Me, and then after a little while you will see Me’?'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 20, 'Truly, truly, I tell you, you will weep and wail while the world rejoices. You will grieve, but your grief will turn to joy.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 21, 'A woman has pain in childbirth because her time has come; but when she brings forth her child, she forgets her anguish because of her joy that a child has been born into the world.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 22, 'So also you have sorrow now, but I will see you again and your hearts will rejoice, and no one will take away your joy.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 23, 'In that day you will no longer ask Me anything. Truly, truly, I tell you, whatever you ask the Father in My name, He will give you.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 24, 'Until now you have not asked for anything in My name. Ask and you will receive, so that your joy may be complete.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 25, 'I have spoken these things to you in figures of speech. An hour is coming when I will no longer speak to you this way, but will tell you plainly about the Father.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 26, 'In that day you will ask in My name. I am not saying that I will ask the Father on your behalf.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 27, 'For the Father Himself loves you, because you have loved Me and have believed that I came from God.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 28, 'I came from the Father and entered the world. In turn, I will leave the world and go to the Father.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 29, 'His disciples said, “See, now You are speaking plainly and without figures of speech.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 30, 'Now we understand that You know all things and that You have no need for anyone to question You. Because of this, we believe that You came from God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 31, '“Do you finally believe?” Jesus replied.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 32, '“Look, an hour is coming and has already come when you will be scattered, each to his own home, and you will leave Me all alone. Yet I am not alone, because the Father is with Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 16, 33, 'I have told you these things so that in Me you may have peace. In the world you will have tribulation. But take courage; I have overcome the world!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 1, 'When Jesus had spoken these things, He lifted up His eyes to heaven and said, “Father, the hour has come. Glorify Your Son, that Your Son may glorify You.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 2, 'For You granted Him authority over all people, so that He may give eternal life to all those You have given Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 3, 'Now this is eternal life, that they may know You, the only true God, and Jesus Christ, whom You have sent.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 4, 'I have glorified You on earth by accomplishing the work You gave Me to do.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 5, 'And now, Father, glorify Me in Your presence with the glory I had with You before the world existed.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 6, 'I have revealed Your name to those You have given Me out of the world. They were Yours; You gave them to Me, and they have kept Your word.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 7, 'Now they know that everything You have given Me comes from You.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 8, 'For I have given them the words You gave Me, and they have received them. They knew with certainty that I came from You, and they believed that You sent Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 9, 'I ask on their behalf. I do not ask on behalf of the world, but on behalf of those You have given Me; for they are Yours.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 10, 'All I have is Yours, and all You have is Mine; and in them I have been glorified.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 11, 'I will no longer be in the world, but they are in the world, and I am coming to You. Holy Father, protect them by Your name, the name You gave Me, so that they may be one as We are one.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 12, 'While I was with them, I protected and preserved them by Your name, the name You gave Me. Not one of them has been lost, except the son of destruction, so that the Scripture would be fulfilled.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 13, 'But now I am coming to You; and I am saying these things while I am in the world, so that they may have My joy fulfilled within them.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 14, 'I have given them Your word and the world has hated them; for they are not of the world, just as I am not of the world.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 15, 'I am not asking that You take them out of the world, but that You keep them from the evil one.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 16, 'They are not of the world, just as I am not of the world.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 17, 'Sanctify them by the truth; Your word is truth.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 18, 'As You sent Me into the world, I have also sent them into the world.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 19, 'For them I sanctify Myself, so that they too may be sanctified by the truth.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 20, 'I am not asking on behalf of them alone, but also on behalf of those who will believe in Me through their message,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 21, 'that all of them may be one, as You, Father, are in Me, and I am in You. May they also be in Us, so that the world may believe that You sent Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 22, 'I have given them the glory You gave Me, so that they may be one as We are one—'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 23, 'I in them and You in Me—that they may be perfectly united, so that the world may know that You sent Me and have loved them just as You have loved Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 24, 'Father, I want those You have given Me to be with Me where I am, that they may see the glory You gave Me because You loved Me before the foundation of the world.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 25, 'Righteous Father, although the world has not known You, I know You, and they know that You sent Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 17, 26, 'And I have made Your name known to them and will continue to make it known, so that the love You have for Me may be in them, and I in them.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 1, 'After Jesus had spoken these words, He went out with His disciples across the Kidron Valley, where they entered a garden.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 2, 'Now Judas His betrayer also knew the place, because Jesus had often met there with His disciples.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 3, 'So Judas brought a band of soldiers and officers from the chief priests and Pharisees. They arrived at the garden carrying lanterns, torches, and weapons.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 4, 'Jesus, knowing all that was coming upon Him, stepped forward and asked them, “Whom are you seeking?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 5, '“Jesus of Nazareth,” they answered. Jesus said, “I am He.” And Judas His betrayer was standing there with them.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 6, 'When Jesus said, “I am He,” they drew back and fell to the ground.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 7, 'So He asked them again, “Whom are you seeking?” “Jesus of Nazareth,” they answered.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 8, '“I told you that I am He,” Jesus replied. “So if you are looking for Me, let these men go.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 9, 'This was to fulfill the word He had spoken: “I have not lost one of those You have given Me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 10, 'Then Simon Peter drew his sword and struck the servant of the high priest, cutting off his right ear. The servant’s name was Malchus.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 11, '“Put your sword back in its sheath!” Jesus said to Peter. “Shall I not drink the cup the Father has given Me?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 12, 'Then the band of soldiers, with its commander and the officers of the Jews, arrested Jesus and bound Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 13, 'They brought Him first to Annas, who was the father-in-law of Caiaphas, the high priest that year.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 14, 'Caiaphas was the one who had advised the Jews that it would be better if one man died for the people.');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 15, 'Now Simon Peter and another disciple were following Jesus. Since that disciple was known to the high priest, he also went with Jesus into the courtyard of the high priest.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 16, 'But Peter stood outside at the door. Then the disciple who was known to the high priest went out and spoke to the doorkeeper, and brought Peter in.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 17, 'At this, the servant girl watching the door said to Peter, “Aren’t you also one of this man’s disciples?” “I am not,” he answered.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 18, 'Because it was cold, the servants and officers were standing around a charcoal fire they had made to keep warm. And Peter was also standing with them, warming himself.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 19, 'Meanwhile, the high priest questioned Jesus about His disciples and His teaching.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 20, '“I have spoken openly to the world,” Jesus answered. “I always taught in the synagogues and at the temple, where all the Jews come together. I said nothing in secret.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 21, 'Why are you asking Me? Ask those who heard My message. Surely they know what I said.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 22, 'When Jesus had said this, one of the officers standing nearby slapped Him in the face and said, “Is this how You answer the high priest?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 23, 'Jesus replied, “If I said something wrong, testify as to what was wrong. But if I spoke correctly, why did you strike Me?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 24, 'Then Annas sent Him, still bound, to Caiaphas the high priest.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 25, 'Simon Peter was still standing and warming himself. So they asked him, “Aren’t you also one of His disciples?” He denied it and said, “I am not.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 26, 'One of the high priest’s servants, a relative of the man whose ear Peter had cut off, asked, “Didn’t I see you with Him in the garden?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 27, 'Peter denied it once more, and immediately a rooster crowed.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 28, 'Then they led Jesus away from Caiaphas into the Praetorium. By now it was early morning, and the Jews did not enter the Praetorium, to avoid being defiled and unable to eat the Passover.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 29, 'So Pilate went out to them and asked, “What accusation are you bringing against this man?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 30, '“If He were not a criminal,” they replied, “we would not have handed Him over to you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 31, '“You take Him and judge Him by your own law,” Pilate told them. “We are not permitted to execute anyone,” the Jews replied.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 32, 'This was to fulfill the word that Jesus had spoken to indicate the kind of death He was going to die.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 33, 'Pilate went back into the Praetorium, summoned Jesus, and asked Him, “Are You the King of the Jews?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 34, '“Are you saying this on your own,” Jesus asked, “or did others tell you about Me?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 35, '“Am I a Jew?” Pilate replied. “Your own people and chief priests handed You over to me. What have You done?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 36, 'Jesus answered, “My kingdom is not of this world; if it were, My servants would fight to prevent My arrest by the Jews. But now My kingdom is not of this realm.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 37, '“Then You are a king!” Pilate said. “You say that I am a king,” Jesus answered. “For this reason I was born and have come into the world, to testify to the truth. Everyone who belongs to the truth listens to My voice.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 38, '“What is truth?” Pilate asked. And having said this, he went out again to the Jews and told them, “I find no basis for a charge against Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 39, 'But it is your custom that I release to you one prisoner at the Passover. So then, do you want me to release to you the King of the Jews?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 18, 40, '“Not this man,” they shouted, “but Barabbas!” (Now Barabbas was an insurrectionist.)'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 1, 'Then Pilate took Jesus and had Him flogged.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 2, 'The soldiers twisted together a crown of thorns, set it on His head, and dressed Him in a purple robe.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 3, 'And they went up to Him again and again, saying, “Hail, King of the Jews!” and slapping Him in the face.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 4, 'Once again Pilate came out and said to the Jews, “Look, I am bringing Him out to you to let you know that I find no basis for a charge against Him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 5, 'When Jesus came out wearing the crown of thorns and the purple robe, Pilate said to them, “Here is the man!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 6, 'As soon as the chief priests and officers saw Him, they shouted, “Crucify Him! Crucify Him!” “You take Him and crucify Him,” Pilate replied, “for I find no basis for a charge against Him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 7, '“We have a law,” answered the Jews, “and according to that law He must die, because He declared Himself to be the Son of God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 8, 'When Pilate heard this statement, he was even more afraid,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 9, 'and he went back into the Praetorium. “Where are You from?” he asked. But Jesus gave no answer.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 10, 'So Pilate said to Him, “Do You refuse to speak to me? Do You not know that I have authority to release You and authority to crucify You?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 11, 'Jesus answered, “You would have no authority over Me if it were not given to you from above. Therefore the one who handed Me over to you is guilty of greater sin.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 12, 'From then on, Pilate tried to release Him, but the Jews kept shouting, “If you release this man, you are no friend of Caesar. Anyone who declares himself a king is defying Caesar.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 13, 'When Pilate heard these words, he brought Jesus out and sat on the judgment seat at a place called the Stone Pavement, which in Hebrew is Gabbatha.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 14, 'It was the day of Preparation for the Passover, about the sixth hour. And Pilate said to the Jews, “Here is your King!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 15, 'At this, they shouted, “Away with Him! Away with Him! Crucify Him!” “Shall I crucify your King?” Pilate asked. “We have no king but Caesar,” replied the chief priests.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 16, 'Then Pilate handed Jesus over to be crucified, and the soldiers took Him away.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 17, 'Carrying His own cross, He went out to The Place of the Skull, which in Hebrew is called Golgotha.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 18, 'There they crucified Him, and with Him two others, one on each side, with Jesus in the middle.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 19, 'Pilate also had a notice posted on the cross. It read: JESUS OF NAZARETH, THE KING OF THE JEWS.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 20, 'Many of the Jews read this sign, because the place where Jesus was crucified was near the city, and it was written in Hebrew, Latin, and Greek.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 21, 'So the chief priests of the Jews said to Pilate, “Do not write, ‘The King of the Jews,’ but only that He said, ‘I am the King of the Jews.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 22, 'Pilate answered, “What I have written, I have written.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 23, 'When the soldiers had crucified Jesus, they divided His garments into four parts, one for each soldier, with the tunic remaining. It was seamless, woven in one piece from top to bottom.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 24, 'So they said to one another, “Let us not tear it. Instead, let us cast lots to see who will get it.” This was to fulfill the Scripture: “They divided My garments among them, and cast lots for My clothing.” So that is what the soldiers did.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 25, 'Near the cross of Jesus stood His mother and her sister, as well as Mary the wife of Clopas and Mary Magdalene.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 26, 'When Jesus saw His mother and the disciple whom He loved standing nearby, He said to His mother, “Woman, here is your son.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 27, 'Then He said to the disciple, “Here is your mother.” So from that hour, this disciple took her into his home.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 28, 'After this, knowing that everything had now been accomplished, and to fulfill the Scripture, Jesus said, “I am thirsty.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 29, 'A jar of sour wine was sitting there. So they soaked a sponge in the wine, put it on a stalk of hyssop, and lifted it to His mouth.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 30, 'When Jesus had received the sour wine, He said, “It is finished.” And bowing His head, He yielded up His spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 31, 'It was the day of Preparation, and the next day was a High Sabbath. In order that the bodies would not remain on the cross during the Sabbath, the Jews asked Pilate to have the legs broken and the bodies removed.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 32, 'So the soldiers came and broke the legs of the first man who had been crucified with Jesus, and those of the other.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 33, 'But when they came to Jesus and saw that He was already dead, they did not break His legs.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 34, 'Instead, one of the soldiers pierced His side with a spear, and immediately blood and water flowed out.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 35, 'The one who saw it has testified to this, and his testimony is true. He knows that he is telling the truth, so that you also may believe.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 36, 'Now these things happened so that the Scripture would be fulfilled: “Not one of His bones will be broken.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 37, 'And, as another Scripture says: “They will look on the One they have pierced.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 38, 'Afterward, Joseph of Arimathea, who was a disciple of Jesus (but secretly for fear of the Jews), asked Pilate to let him remove the body of Jesus. Pilate gave him permission, so he came and removed His body.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 39, 'Nicodemus, who had previously come to Jesus at night, also brought a mixture of myrrh and aloes, about seventy-five pounds.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 40, 'So they took the body of Jesus and wrapped it in linen cloths with the spices, according to the Jewish burial custom.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 41, 'Now there was a garden in the place where Jesus was crucified, and in the garden a new tomb in which no one had yet been laid.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 19, 42, 'And because it was the Jewish day of Preparation and the tomb was nearby, they placed Jesus there.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 1, 'Early on the first day of the week, while it was still dark, Mary Magdalene went to the tomb and saw that the stone had been removed from the entrance.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 2, 'So she came running to Simon Peter and the other disciple, the one whom Jesus loved. “They have taken the Lord out of the tomb,” she said, “and we do not know where they have put Him!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 3, 'Then Peter and the other disciple set out for the tomb.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 4, 'The two were running together, but the other disciple outran Peter and reached the tomb first.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 5, 'He bent down and looked in at the linen cloths lying there, but he did not go in.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 6, 'Simon Peter arrived just after him. He entered the tomb and saw the linen cloths lying there.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 7, 'The cloth that had been around Jesus’ head was rolled up, lying separate from the linen cloths.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 8, 'Then the other disciple, who had reached the tomb first, also went in. And he saw and believed.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 9, 'For they still did not understand from the Scripture that Jesus had to rise from the dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 10, 'Then the disciples returned to their homes.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 11, 'But Mary stood outside the tomb weeping. And as she wept, she bent down to look into the tomb,'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 12, 'and she saw two angels in white sitting where the body of Jesus had lain, one at the head and the other at the feet.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 13, '“Woman, why are you weeping?” they asked. “Because they have taken my Lord away,” she said, “and I do not know where they have put Him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 14, 'When she had said this, she turned around and saw Jesus standing there; but she did not recognize that it was Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 15, '“Woman, why are you weeping?” Jesus asked. “Whom are you seeking?” Thinking He was the gardener, she said, “Sir, if you have carried Him off, tell me where you have put Him, and I will get Him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 16, 'Jesus said to her, “Mary.” She turned and said to Him in Hebrew, “Rabboni!” (which means “Teacher”).'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 17, '“Do not cling to Me,” Jesus said, “for I have not yet ascended to the Father. But go and tell My brothers, ‘I am ascending to My Father and your Father, to My God and your God.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 18, 'Mary Magdalene went and announced to the disciples, “I have seen the Lord!” And she told them what He had said to her.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 19, 'It was the first day of the week, and that very evening, while the disciples were together with the doors locked for fear of the Jews, Jesus came and stood among them. “Peace be with you!” He said to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 20, 'After He had said this, He showed them His hands and His side. The disciples rejoiced when they saw the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 21, 'Again Jesus said to them, “Peace be with you. As the Father has sent Me, so also I am sending you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 22, 'When He had said this, He breathed on them and said, “Receive the Holy Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 23, 'If you forgive anyone his sins, they are forgiven; if you withhold forgiveness from anyone, it is withheld.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 24, 'Now Thomas called Didymus, one of the Twelve, was not with the disciples when Jesus came.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 25, 'So the other disciples told him, “We have seen the Lord!” But he replied, “Unless I see the nail marks in His hands, and put my finger where the nails have been, and put my hand into His side, I will never believe.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 26, 'Eight days later, His disciples were once again inside with the doors locked, and Thomas was with them. Jesus came and stood among them and said, “Peace be with you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 27, 'Then Jesus said to Thomas, “Put your finger here and look at My hands. Reach out your hand and put it into My side. Stop doubting and believe.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 28, 'Thomas replied, “My Lord and my God!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 29, 'Jesus said to him, “Because you have seen Me, you have believed; blessed are those who have not seen and yet have believed.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 30, 'Jesus performed many other signs in the presence of His disciples, which are not written in this book.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 20, 31, 'But these are written so that you may believe that Jesus is the Christ, the Son of God, and that by believing you may have life in His name.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 1, 'Later, by the Sea of Tiberias, Jesus again revealed Himself to the disciples. He made Himself known in this way:'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 2, 'Simon Peter, Thomas called Didymus, Nathanael from Cana in Galilee, the sons of Zebedee, and two other disciples were together.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 3, 'Simon Peter told them, “I am going fishing.” “We will go with you,” they said. So they went out and got into the boat, but caught nothing that night.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 4, 'Early in the morning, Jesus stood on the shore, but the disciples did not recognize that it was Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 5, 'So He called out to them, “Children, do you have any fish?” “No,” they answered.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 6, 'He told them, “Cast the net on the right side of the boat, and you will find some.” So they cast it there, and they were unable to haul it in because of the great number of fish.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 7, 'Then the disciple whom Jesus loved said to Peter, “It is the Lord!” As soon as Simon Peter heard that it was the Lord, he put on his outer garment (for he had removed it) and jumped into the sea.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 8, 'The other disciples came ashore in the boat. They dragged in the net full of fish, for they were not far from land, only about a hundred yards.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 9, 'When they landed, they saw a charcoal fire there with fish on it, and some bread.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 10, 'Jesus told them, “Bring some of the fish you have just caught.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 11, 'So Simon Peter went aboard and dragged the net ashore. It was full of large fish, 153, but even with so many, the net was not torn.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 12, '“Come, have breakfast,” Jesus said to them. None of the disciples dared to ask Him, “Who are You?” They knew it was the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 13, 'Jesus came and took the bread and gave it to them, and He did the same with the fish.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 14, 'This was now the third time that Jesus appeared to the disciples after He was raised from the dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 15, 'When they had finished eating, Jesus asked Simon Peter, “Simon son of John, do you love Me more than these?” “Yes, Lord,” he answered, “You know I love You.” Jesus replied, “Feed My lambs.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 16, 'Jesus asked a second time, “Simon son of John, do you love Me?” “Yes, Lord,” he answered, “You know I love You.” Jesus told him, “Shepherd My sheep.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 17, 'Jesus asked a third time, “Simon son of John, do you love Me?” Peter was deeply hurt that Jesus had asked him a third time, “Do you love Me?” “Lord, You know all things,” he replied. “You know I love You.” Jesus said to him, “Feed My sheep.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 18, 'Truly, truly, I tell you, when you were young, you dressed yourself and walked where you wanted; but when you are old, you will stretch out your hands, and someone else will dress you and lead you where you do not want to go.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 19, 'Jesus said this to indicate the kind of death by which Peter would glorify God. And after He had said this, He told him, “Follow Me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 20, 'Peter turned and saw the disciple whom Jesus loved following them. He was the one who had leaned back against Jesus at the supper to ask, “Lord, who is going to betray You?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 21, 'When Peter saw him, he asked, “Lord, what about him?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 22, 'Jesus answered, “If I want him to remain until I return, what is that to you? You follow Me!”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 23, 'Because of this, the rumor spread among the brothers that this disciple would not die. However, Jesus did not say that he would not die, but only, “If I want him to remain until I return, what is that to you?”'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 24, 'This is the disciple who testifies to these things and who has written them down. And we know that his testimony is true.'),
  ('BSB', 'John', 43, 21, 25, 'There are many more things that Jesus did. If all of them were written down, I suppose that not even the world itself would have space for the books that would be written.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 1, 'In my first book, O Theophilus, I wrote about all that Jesus began to do and to teach,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 2, 'until the day He was taken up to heaven, after giving instructions through the Holy Spirit to the apostles He had chosen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 3, 'After His suffering, He presented Himself to them with many convincing proofs that He was alive. He appeared to them over a span of forty days and spoke about the kingdom of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 4, 'And while they were gathered together, He commanded them: “Do not leave Jerusalem, but wait for the gift the Father promised, which you have heard Me discuss.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 5, 'For John baptized with water, but in a few days you will be baptized with the Holy Spirit.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 6, 'So when they came together, they asked Him, “Lord, will You at this time restore the kingdom to Israel?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 7, 'Jesus replied, “It is not for you to know times or seasons that the Father has fixed by His own authority.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 8, 'But you will receive power when the Holy Spirit comes upon you, and you will be My witnesses in Jerusalem, and in all Judea and Samaria, and to the ends of the earth.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 9, 'After He had said this, they watched as He was taken up, and a cloud hid Him from their sight.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 10, 'They were looking intently into the sky as He was going, when suddenly two men dressed in white stood beside them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 11, '“Men of Galilee,” they said, “why do you stand here looking into the sky? This same Jesus, who has been taken from you into heaven, will come back in the same way you have seen Him go into heaven.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 12, 'Then they returned to Jerusalem from the Mount of Olives, which is near the city, a Sabbath day’s journey away.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 13, 'When they arrived, they went to the upper room where they were staying: Peter and John, James and Andrew, Philip and Thomas, Bartholomew and Matthew, James son of Alphaeus, Simon the Zealot, and Judas son of James.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 14, 'With one accord they all continued in prayer, along with the women and Mary the mother of Jesus, and with His brothers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 15, 'In those days Peter stood up among the brothers (a gathering of about a hundred and twenty) and said,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 16, '“Brothers, the Scripture had to be fulfilled which the Holy Spirit foretold through the mouth of David concerning Judas, who became a guide for those who arrested Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 17, 'He was one of our number and shared in this ministry.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 18, '(Now with the reward for his wickedness Judas bought a field; there he fell headlong and burst open in the middle, and all his intestines spilled out.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 19, 'This became known to all who lived in Jerusalem, so they called that field in their own language Akeldama, that is, Field of Blood.)'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 20, '“For it is written in the book of Psalms: ‘May his place be deserted; let there be no one to dwell in it,’ and, ‘May another take his position.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 21, 'Therefore it is necessary to choose one of the men who have accompanied us the whole time the Lord Jesus went in and out among us,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 22, 'beginning from John’s baptism until the day Jesus was taken up from us. For one of these must become a witness with us of His resurrection.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 23, 'So they proposed two men: Joseph called Barsabbas (also known as Justus) and Matthias.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 24, 'And they prayed, “Lord, You know everyone’s heart. Show us which of these two You have chosen'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 25, 'to take up this ministry and apostleship, which Judas abandoned to go to his rightful place.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 1, 26, 'Then they cast lots, and the lot fell to Matthias; so he was added to the eleven apostles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 1, 'When the day of Pentecost came, they were all together in one place.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 2, 'Suddenly a sound like a mighty rushing wind came from heaven and filled the whole house where they were sitting.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 3, 'They saw tongues like flames of fire that separated and came to rest on each of them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 4, 'And they were all filled with the Holy Spirit and began to speak in other tongues as the Spirit enabled them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 5, 'Now there were dwelling in Jerusalem God-fearing Jews from every nation under heaven.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 6, 'And when this sound rang out, a crowd came together in bewilderment, because each one heard them speaking his own language.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 7, 'Astounded and amazed, they asked, “Are not all these men who are speaking Galileans?'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 8, 'How is it then that each of us hears them in his own native language?'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 9, 'Parthians, Medes, and Elamites; residents of Mesopotamia, Judea and Cappadocia, Pontus and Asia,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 10, 'Phrygia and Pamphylia, Egypt and the parts of Libya near Cyrene; visitors from Rome,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 11, 'both Jews and converts to Judaism; Cretans and Arabs—we hear them declaring the wonders of God in our own tongues!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 12, 'Astounded and perplexed, they asked one another, “What does this mean?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 13, 'But others mocked them and said, “They are drunk on new wine!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 14, 'Then Peter stood up with the Eleven, lifted up his voice, and addressed the crowd: “Men of Judea and all who dwell in Jerusalem, let this be known to you, and listen carefully to my words.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 15, 'These men are not drunk, as you suppose. It is only the third hour of the day!'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 16, 'No, this is what was spoken by the prophet Joel:'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 17, '‘In the last days, God says, I will pour out My Spirit on all people. Your sons and daughters will prophesy, your young men will see visions, your old men will dream dreams.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 18, 'Even on My menservants and maidservants I will pour out My Spirit in those days, and they will prophesy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 19, 'I will show wonders in the heavens above and signs on the earth below, blood and fire and billows of smoke.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 20, 'The sun will be turned to darkness, and the moon to blood, before the coming of the great and glorious Day of the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 21, 'And everyone who calls on the name of the Lord will be saved.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 22, 'Men of Israel, listen to this message: Jesus of Nazareth was a man certified by God to you by miracles, wonders, and signs, which God did among you through Him, as you yourselves know.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 23, 'He was delivered up by God’s set plan and foreknowledge, and you, by the hands of the lawless, put Him to death by nailing Him to the cross.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 24, 'But God raised Him from the dead, releasing Him from the agony of death, because it was impossible for Him to be held in its clutches.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 25, 'David says about Him: ‘I saw the Lord always before me; because He is at my right hand, I will not be shaken.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 26, 'Therefore my heart is glad and my tongue rejoices; my body also will dwell in hope,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 27, 'because You will not abandon my soul to Hades, nor will You let Your Holy One see decay.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 28, 'You have made known to me the paths of life; You will fill me with joy in Your presence.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 29, 'Brothers, I can tell you with confidence that the patriarch David died and was buried, and his tomb is with us to this day.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 30, 'But he was a prophet and knew that God had promised him on oath that He would place one of his descendants on his throne.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 31, 'Foreseeing this, David spoke about the resurrection of the Christ, that He was not abandoned to Hades, nor did His body see decay.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 32, 'God has raised this Jesus to life, to which we are all witnesses.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 33, 'Exalted, then, to the right hand of God, He has received from the Father the promised Holy Spirit and has poured out what you now see and hear.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 34, 'For David did not ascend into heaven, but he himself says: ‘The Lord said to my Lord, “Sit at My right hand'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 35, 'until I make Your enemies a footstool for Your feet.”’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 36, 'Therefore let all Israel know with certainty that God has made this Jesus, whom you crucified, both Lord and Christ!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 37, 'When the people heard this, they were cut to the heart and asked Peter and the other apostles, “Brothers, what shall we do?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 38, 'Peter replied, “Repent and be baptized, every one of you, in the name of Jesus Christ for the forgiveness of your sins, and you will receive the gift of the Holy Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 39, 'This promise belongs to you and your children and to all who are far off—to all whom the Lord our God will call to Himself.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 40, 'With many other words he testified, and he urged them, “Be saved from this corrupt generation.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 41, 'Those who embraced his message were baptized, and about three thousand were added to the believers that day.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 42, 'They devoted themselves to the apostles’ teaching and to the fellowship, to the breaking of bread and to prayer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 43, 'A sense of awe came over everyone, and the apostles performed many wonders and signs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 44, 'All the believers were together and had everything in common.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 45, 'Selling their possessions and goods, they shared with anyone who was in need.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 46, 'With one accord they continued to meet daily in the temple courts and to break bread from house to house, sharing their meals with gladness and sincerity of heart,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 2, 47, 'praising God and enjoying the favor of all the people. And the Lord added to their number daily those who were being saved.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 1, 'One afternoon Peter and John were going up to the temple at the hour of prayer, the ninth hour.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 2, 'And a man who was lame from birth was being carried to the temple gate called Beautiful, where he was put every day to beg from those entering the temple courts.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 3, 'When he saw Peter and John about to enter, he asked them for money.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 4, 'Peter looked directly at him, as did John. “Look at us!” said Peter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 5, 'So the man gave them his attention, expecting to receive something from them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 6, 'But Peter said, “Silver or gold I do not have, but what I have I give you: In the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, get up and walk!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 7, 'Taking him by the right hand, Peter helped him up, and at once the man’s feet and ankles were made strong.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 8, 'He sprang to his feet and began to walk. Then he went with them into the temple courts, walking and leaping and praising God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 9, 'When all the people saw him walking and praising God,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 10, 'they recognized him as the man who used to sit begging at the Beautiful Gate of the temple, and they were filled with wonder and amazement at what had happened to him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 11, 'While the man clung to Peter and John, all the people were astonished and ran to them in the walkway called Solomon’s Colonnade.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 12, 'And when Peter saw this, he addressed the people: “Men of Israel, why are you surprised by this? Why do you stare at us as if by our own power or godliness we had made this man walk?'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 13, 'The God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, the God of our fathers, has glorified His servant Jesus. You handed Him over and rejected Him before Pilate, even though he had decided to release Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 14, 'You rejected the Holy and Righteous One and asked that a murderer be released to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 15, 'You killed the Author of life, but God raised Him from the dead, and we are witnesses of the fact.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 16, 'By faith in the name of Jesus, this man whom you see and know has been made strong. It is Jesus’ name and the faith that comes through Him that has given him this complete healing in your presence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 17, 'And now, brothers, I know that you acted in ignorance, as did your leaders.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 18, 'But in this way God has fulfilled what He foretold through all the prophets, saying that His Christ would suffer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 19, 'Repent, then, and turn back, so that your sins may be wiped away,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 20, 'that times of refreshing may come from the presence of the Lord, and that He may send Jesus, the Christ, who has been appointed for you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 21, 'Heaven must take Him in until the time comes for the restoration of all things, which God announced long ago through His holy prophets.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 22, 'For Moses said, ‘The Lord your God will raise up for you a prophet like me from among your brothers. You must listen to Him in everything He tells you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 23, 'Everyone who does not listen to Him will be completely cut off from among his people.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 24, 'Indeed, all the prophets from Samuel on, as many as have spoken, have proclaimed these days.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 25, 'And you are sons of the prophets and of the covenant God made with your fathers when He said to Abraham, ‘Through your offspring all the families of the earth will be blessed.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 3, 26, 'When God raised up His Servant, He sent Him first to you to bless you by turning each of you from your wicked ways.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 1, 'While Peter and John were speaking to the people, the priests and the captain of the temple guard and the Sadducees came up to them,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 2, 'greatly disturbed that they were teaching the people and proclaiming in Jesus the resurrection of the dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 3, 'They seized Peter and John, and because it was evening, they put them in custody until the next day.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 4, 'But many who heard the message believed, and the number of men grew to about five thousand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 5, 'The next day the rulers, elders, and scribes assembled in Jerusalem,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 6, 'along with Annas the high priest, Caiaphas, John, Alexander, and many others from the high priest’s family.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 7, 'They had Peter and John brought in and began to question them: “By what power or what name did you do this?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 8, 'Then Peter, filled with the Holy Spirit, said to them, “Rulers and elders of the people!'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 9, 'If we are being examined today about a kind service to a man who was lame, to determine how he was healed,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 10, 'then let this be known to all of you and to all the people of Israel: It is by the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, whom you crucified but whom God raised from the dead, that this man stands before you healed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 11, 'This Jesus is ‘the stone you builders rejected, which has become the cornerstone.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 12, 'Salvation exists in no one else, for there is no other name under heaven given to men by which we must be saved.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 13, 'When they saw the boldness of Peter and John and realized that they were unschooled, ordinary men, they marveled and took note that these men had been with Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 14, 'And seeing the man who had been healed standing there with them, they had nothing to say in response.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 15, 'So they ordered them to leave the Sanhedrin and then conferred together.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 16, '“What shall we do with these men?” they asked. “It is clear to everyone living in Jerusalem that a remarkable miracle has occurred through them, and we cannot deny it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 17, 'But to keep this message from spreading any further among the people, we must warn them not to speak to anyone in this name.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 18, 'Then they called them in again and commanded them not to speak or teach at all in the name of Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 19, 'But Peter and John replied, “Judge for yourselves whether it is right in God’s sight to listen to you rather than God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 20, 'For we cannot stop speaking about what we have seen and heard.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 21, 'After further threats they let them go. They could not find a way to punish them, because all the people were glorifying God for what had happened.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 22, 'For the man who was miraculously healed was over forty years old.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 23, 'On their release, Peter and John returned to their own people and reported everything that the chief priests and elders had said to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 24, 'When the believers heard this, they lifted up their voices to God with one accord. “Sovereign Lord,” they said, “You made the heaven and the earth and the sea and everything in them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 25, 'You spoke by the Holy Spirit through the mouth of Your servant, our father David: ‘Why do the nations rage and the peoples plot in vain?'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 26, 'The kings of the earth take their stand and the rulers gather together against the Lord and against His Anointed One.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 27, 'In fact, this is the very city where Herod and Pontius Pilate conspired with the Gentiles and the people of Israel against Your holy servant Jesus, whom You anointed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 28, 'They carried out what Your hand and will had decided beforehand would happen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 29, 'And now, Lord, consider their threats, and enable Your servants to speak Your word with complete boldness,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 30, 'as You stretch out Your hand to heal and perform signs and wonders through the name of Your holy servant Jesus.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 31, 'After they had prayed, their meeting place was shaken, and they were all filled with the Holy Spirit and spoke the word of God boldly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 32, 'The multitude of believers was one in heart and soul. No one claimed that any of his possessions was his own, but they shared everything they owned.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 33, 'With great power the apostles continued to give their testimony about the resurrection of the Lord Jesus. And abundant grace was upon them all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 34, 'There were no needy ones among them, because those who owned lands or houses would sell their property, bring the proceeds from the sales,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 35, 'and lay them at the apostles’ feet for distribution to anyone as he had need.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 36, 'Joseph, a Levite from Cyprus, whom the apostles called Barnabas (meaning Son of Encouragement),'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 4, 37, 'sold a field he owned, brought the money, and laid it at the apostles’ feet.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 1, 'Now a man named Ananias, together with his wife Sapphira, also sold a piece of property.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 2, 'With his wife’s full knowledge, he kept back some of the proceeds for himself, but brought a portion and laid it at the apostles’ feet.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 3, 'Then Peter said, “Ananias, how is it that Satan has filled your heart to lie to the Holy Spirit and withhold some of the proceeds from the land?'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 4, 'Did it not belong to you before it was sold? And after it was sold, was it not at your disposal? How could you conceive such a deed in your heart? You have not lied to men, but to God!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 5, 'On hearing these words, Ananias fell down and died. And great fear came over all who heard what had happened.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 6, 'Then the young men stepped forward, wrapped up his body, and carried him out and buried him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 7, 'About three hours later his wife also came in, unaware of what had happened.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 8, '“Tell me,” said Peter, “is this the price you and your husband got for the land?” “Yes,” she answered, “that is the price.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 9, '“How could you agree to test the Spirit of the Lord?” Peter replied. “Look, the feet of the men who buried your husband are at the door, and they will carry you out also.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 10, 'At that instant she fell down at his feet and died. Then the young men came in and, finding her dead, carried her out and buried her beside her husband.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 11, 'And great fear came over the whole church and all who heard about these events.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 12, 'The apostles performed many signs and wonders among the people, and with one accord the believers gathered together in Solomon’s Colonnade.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 13, 'Although the people regarded them highly, no one else dared to join them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 14, 'Yet more and more believers were brought to the Lord—large numbers of both men and women.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 15, 'As a result, people brought the sick into the streets and laid them on cots and mats, so that at least Peter’s shadow might fall on some of them as he passed by.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 16, 'Crowds also gathered from the towns around Jerusalem, bringing the sick and those tormented by unclean spirits, and all of them were healed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 17, 'Then the high priest and all his associates, who belonged to the party of the Sadducees, were filled with jealousy. They went out'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 18, 'and arrested the apostles and put them in the public jail.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 19, 'But during the night an angel of the Lord opened the doors of the jail and brought them out, saying,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 20, '“Go, stand in the temple courts and tell the people the full message of this new life.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 21, 'At daybreak the apostles entered the temple courts as they had been told and began to teach the people. When the high priest and his associates arrived, they convened the Sanhedrin—the full assembly of the elders of Israel—and sent to the jail for the apostles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 22, 'But on arriving at the jail, the officers did not find them there. So they returned with the report:'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 23, '“We found the jail securely locked, with the guards posted at the doors; but when we opened them, we found no one inside.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 24, 'When the captain of the temple guard and the chief priests heard this account, they were perplexed as to what was happening.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 25, 'Then someone came in and announced, “Look, the men you put in jail are standing in the temple courts teaching the people!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 26, 'At that point, the captain went with the officers and brought the apostles—but not by force, for fear the people would stone them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 27, 'They brought them in and made them stand before the Sanhedrin, where the high priest interrogated them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 28, '“We gave you strict orders not to teach in this name,” he said. “Yet you have filled Jerusalem with your teaching and are determined to make us responsible for this man’s blood.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 29, 'But Peter and the other apostles replied, “We must obey God rather than men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 30, 'The God of our fathers raised up Jesus, whom you had killed by hanging Him on a tree.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 31, 'God exalted Him to His right hand as Prince and Savior, in order to grant repentance and forgiveness of sins to Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 32, 'We are witnesses of these things, and so is the Holy Spirit, whom God has given to those who obey Him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 33, 'When the Council members heard this, they were enraged, and they resolved to put the apostles to death.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 34, 'But a Pharisee named Gamaliel, a teacher of the law who was honored by all the people, stood up in the Sanhedrin and ordered that the men be put outside for a short time.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 35, '“Men of Israel,” he said, “consider carefully what you are about to do to these men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 36, 'Some time ago Theudas rose up, claiming to be somebody, and about four hundred men joined him. He was killed, all his followers were dispersed, and it all came to nothing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 37, 'After him, Judas the Galilean appeared in the days of the census and drew away people after him. He too perished, and all his followers were scattered.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 38, 'So in the present case I advise you: Leave these men alone. Let them go! For if their purpose or endeavor is of human origin, it will fail.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 39, 'But if it is from God, you will not be able to stop them. You may even find yourselves fighting against God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 40, 'At this, they yielded to Gamaliel. They called the apostles in and had them flogged. Then they ordered them not to speak in the name of Jesus, and released them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 41, 'The apostles left the Sanhedrin, rejoicing that they had been counted worthy of suffering disgrace for the Name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 5, 42, 'Every day, in the temple courts and from house to house, they did not stop teaching and proclaiming the good news that Jesus is the Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 6, 1, 'In those days when the disciples were increasing in number, the Grecian Jews among them began to grumble against the Hebraic Jews because their widows were being overlooked in the daily distribution of food.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 6, 2, 'So the Twelve summoned all the disciples and said, “It is unacceptable for us to neglect the word of God in order to wait on tables.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 6, 3, 'Therefore, brothers, select from among you seven men confirmed to be full of the Spirit and wisdom. We will appoint this responsibility to them'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 6, 4, 'and will devote ourselves to prayer and to the ministry of the word.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 6, 5, 'This proposal pleased the whole group. They chose Stephen, a man full of faith and of the Holy Spirit, as well as Philip, Prochorus, Nicanor, Timon, Parmenas, and Nicolas from Antioch, a convert to Judaism.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 6, 6, 'They presented these seven to the apostles, who prayed and laid their hands on them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 6, 7, 'So the word of God continued to spread. The number of disciples in Jerusalem grew rapidly, and a great number of priests became obedient to the faith.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 6, 8, 'Now Stephen, who was full of grace and power, was performing great wonders and signs among the people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 6, 9, 'But resistance arose from what was called the Synagogue of the Freedmen, including Cyrenians, Alexandrians, and men from the provinces of Cilicia and Asia. They began to argue with Stephen,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 6, 10, 'but they could not stand up to his wisdom or the Spirit by whom he spoke.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 6, 11, 'Then they prompted some men to say, “We heard Stephen speak words of blasphemy against Moses and against God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 6, 12, 'So they stirred up the people, elders, and scribes and confronted Stephen. They seized him and brought him before the Sanhedrin,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 6, 13, 'where they presented false witnesses who said, “This man never stops speaking against this holy place and against the law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 6, 14, 'For we have heard him say that Jesus of Nazareth will destroy this place and change the customs that Moses handed down to us.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 6, 15, 'All who were sitting in the Sanhedrin looked intently at Stephen, and they saw that his face was like the face of an angel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 1, 'Then the high priest asked Stephen, “Are these charges true?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 2, 'And Stephen declared: “Brothers and fathers, listen to me! The God of glory appeared to our father Abraham while he was still in Mesopotamia, before he lived in Haran,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 3, 'and told him, ‘Leave your country and your kindred and go to the land I will show you.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 4, 'So Abraham left the land of the Chaldeans and settled in Haran. After his father died, God brought him out of that place and into this land where you are now living.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 5, 'He gave him no inheritance here, not even a foot of ground. But God promised to give possession of the land to Abraham and his descendants, even though he did not yet have a child.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 6, 'God told him that his descendants would be foreigners in a strange land, and that they would be enslaved and mistreated four hundred years.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 7, '‘But I will punish the nation that enslaves them,’ God said, ‘and afterward they will come forth and worship Me in this place.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 8, 'Then God gave Abraham the covenant of circumcision, and Abraham became the father of Isaac and circumcised him on the eighth day. And Isaac became the father of Jacob, and Jacob of the twelve patriarchs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 9, 'Because the patriarchs were jealous of Joseph, they sold him as a slave into Egypt. But God was with him'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 10, 'and rescued him from all his troubles. He granted Joseph favor and wisdom in the sight of Pharaoh king of Egypt, who appointed him ruler over Egypt and all his household.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 11, 'Then famine and great suffering swept across Egypt and Canaan, and our fathers could not find food.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 12, 'When Jacob heard that there was grain in Egypt, he sent our fathers on their first visit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 13, 'On their second visit, Joseph revealed his identity to his brothers, and his family became known to Pharaoh.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 14, 'Then Joseph sent for his father Jacob and all his relatives, seventy-five in all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 15, 'So Jacob went down to Egypt, where he and our fathers died.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 16, 'Their bones were carried back to Shechem and placed in the tomb that Abraham had bought from the sons of Hamor at Shechem for a price he paid in silver.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 17, 'As the time drew near for God to fulfill His promise to Abraham, our people in Egypt increased greatly in number.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 18, 'Then another king, who knew nothing of Joseph, arose over Egypt.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 19, 'He exploited our people and oppressed our fathers, forcing them to abandon their infants so they would die.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 20, 'At that time Moses was born, and he was beautiful in the sight of God. For three months he was nurtured in his father’s house.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 21, 'When he was set outside, Pharaoh’s daughter took him and brought him up as her own son.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 22, 'So Moses was educated in all the wisdom of the Egyptians and was powerful in speech and action.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 23, 'When Moses was forty years old, he decided to visit his brothers, the children of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 24, 'And when he saw one of them being mistreated, Moses went to his defense and avenged him by striking down the Egyptian who was oppressing him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 25, 'He assumed his brothers would understand that God was using him to deliver them, but they did not.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 26, 'The next day he came upon two Israelites who were fighting, and he tried to reconcile them, saying, ‘Men, you are brothers. Why are you mistreating each other?’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 27, 'But the man who was abusing his neighbor pushed Moses aside and said, ‘Who made you ruler and judge over us?'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 28, 'Do you want to kill me as you killed the Egyptian yesterday?’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 29, 'At this remark, Moses fled to the land of Midian, where he lived as a foreigner and had two sons.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 30, 'After forty years had passed, an angel appeared to Moses in the flames of a burning bush in the desert near Mount Sinai.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 31, 'When Moses saw it, he marveled at the sight. As he approached to look more closely, the voice of the Lord came to him:'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 32, '‘I am the God of your fathers, the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.’ Moses trembled with fear and did not dare to look.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 33, 'Then the Lord said to him, ‘Take off your sandals, for the place where you are standing is holy ground.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 34, 'I have indeed seen the oppression of My people in Egypt. I have heard their groaning and have come down to deliver them. Now come, I will send you back to Egypt.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 35, 'This Moses, whom they had rejected with the words, ‘Who made you ruler and judge?’ is the one whom God sent to be their ruler and redeemer through the angel who appeared to him in the bush.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 36, 'He led them out and performed wonders and signs in the land of Egypt, at the Red Sea, and for forty years in the wilderness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 37, 'This is the same Moses who told the Israelites, ‘God will raise up for you a prophet like me from among your brothers.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 38, 'He was in the assembly in the wilderness with the angel who spoke to him on Mount Sinai, and with our fathers. And he received living words to pass on to us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 39, 'But our fathers refused to obey him. Instead, they rejected him and in their hearts turned back to Egypt.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 40, 'They said to Aaron, ‘Make us gods who will go before us! As for this Moses who led us out of the land of Egypt, we do not know what has happened to him.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 41, 'At that time they made a calf and offered a sacrifice to the idol, rejoicing in the works of their hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 42, 'But God turned away from them and gave them over to the worship of the host of heaven, as it is written in the book of the prophets: ‘Did you bring Me sacrifices and offerings forty years in the wilderness, O house of Israel?'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 43, 'You have taken along the tabernacle of Molech and the star of your god Rephan, the idols you made to worship. Therefore I will send you into exile beyond Babylon.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 44, 'Our fathers had the tabernacle of the Testimony with them in the wilderness. It was constructed exactly as God had directed Moses, according to the pattern he had seen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 45, 'And our fathers who received it brought it in with Joshua when they dispossessed the nations God drove out before them. It remained until the time of David,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 46, 'who found favor in the sight of God and asked to provide a dwelling place for the God of Jacob.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 47, 'But it was Solomon who built the house for Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 48, 'However, the Most High does not dwell in houses made by human hands. As the prophet says:'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 49, '‘Heaven is My throne and the earth is My footstool. What kind of house will you build for Me, says the Lord, or where will My place of repose be?'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 50, 'Has not My hand made all these things?’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 51, 'You stiff-necked people with uncircumcised hearts and ears! You always resist the Holy Spirit, just as your fathers did.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 52, 'Which of the prophets did your fathers fail to persecute? They even killed those who foretold the coming of the Righteous One. And now you are His betrayers and murderers—'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 53, 'you who received the law ordained by angels, yet have not kept it.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 54, 'On hearing this, the members of the Sanhedrin were enraged, and they gnashed their teeth at him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 55, 'But Stephen, full of the Holy Spirit, looked intently into heaven and saw the glory of God and Jesus standing at the right hand of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 56, '“Look,” he said, “I see heaven open and the Son of Man standing at the right hand of God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 57, 'At this they covered their ears, cried out in a loud voice, and rushed together at him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 58, 'They dragged him out of the city and began to stone him. Meanwhile the witnesses laid their garments at the feet of a young man named Saul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 59, 'While they were stoning him, Stephen appealed, “Lord Jesus, receive my spirit.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 7, 60, 'Falling on his knees, he cried out in a loud voice, “Lord, do not hold this sin against them.” And when he had said this, he fell asleep.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 1, 'And Saul was there, giving approval to Stephen’s death. On that day a great persecution broke out against the church in Jerusalem, and all except the apostles were scattered throughout Judea and Samaria.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 2, 'God-fearing men buried Stephen and mourned deeply over him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 3, 'But Saul began to destroy the church. Going from house to house, he dragged off men and women and put them in prison.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 4, 'Those who had been scattered preached the word wherever they went.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 5, 'Philip went down to a city in Samaria and proclaimed the Christ to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 6, 'The crowds gave their undivided attention to Philip’s message and to the signs they saw him perform.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 7, 'With loud shrieks, unclean spirits came out of many who were possessed, and many of the paralyzed and lame were healed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 8, 'So there was great joy in that city.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 9, 'Prior to that time, a man named Simon had practiced sorcery in the city and astounded the people of Samaria. He claimed to be someone great,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 10, 'and all the people, from the least to the greatest, heeded his words and said, “This man is the divine power called the Great Power.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 11, 'They paid close attention to him because he had astounded them for a long time with his sorcery.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 12, 'But when they believed Philip as he preached the gospel of the kingdom of God and the name of Jesus Christ, they were baptized, both men and women.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 13, 'Even Simon himself believed and was baptized. He followed Philip closely and was astounded by the great signs and miracles he observed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 14, 'When the apostles in Jerusalem heard that Samaria had received the word of God, they sent Peter and John to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 15, 'On their arrival, they prayed for them to receive the Holy Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 16, 'For the Holy Spirit had not yet fallen upon any of them; they had simply been baptized into the name of the Lord Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 17, 'Then Peter and John laid their hands on them, and they received the Holy Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 18, 'When Simon saw that the Spirit was given through the laying on of the apostles’ hands, he offered them money.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 19, '“Give me this power as well,” he said, “so that everyone on whom I lay my hands may receive the Holy Spirit.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 20, 'But Peter replied, “May your silver perish with you, because you thought you could buy the gift of God with money!'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 21, 'You have no part or share in our ministry, because your heart is not right before God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 22, 'Repent, therefore, of your wickedness, and pray to the Lord. Perhaps He will forgive you for the intent of your heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 23, 'For I see that you are poisoned by bitterness and captive to iniquity.”');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 24, 'Then Simon answered, “Pray to the Lord for me, so that nothing you have said may happen to me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 25, 'And after Peter and John had testified and spoken the word of the Lord, they returned to Jerusalem, preaching the gospel in many of the Samaritan villages.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 26, 'Now an angel of the Lord said to Philip, “Get up and go south to the desert road that goes down from Jerusalem to Gaza.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 27, 'So he started out, and on his way he met an Ethiopian eunuch, a court official in charge of the entire treasury of Candace, queen of the Ethiopians. He had gone to Jerusalem to worship,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 28, 'and on his return was sitting in his chariot reading Isaiah the prophet.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 29, 'The Spirit said to Philip, “Go over to that chariot and stay by it.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 30, 'So Philip ran up and heard the man reading Isaiah the prophet. “Do you understand what you are reading?” Philip asked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 31, '“How can I,” he said, “unless someone guides me?” And he invited Philip to come up and sit with him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 32, 'The eunuch was reading this passage of Scripture: “He was led like a sheep to the slaughter, and as a lamb before the shearer is silent, so He did not open His mouth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 33, 'In His humiliation He was deprived of justice. Who can recount His descendants? For His life was removed from the earth.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 34, '“Tell me,” said the eunuch, “who is the prophet talking about, himself or someone else?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 35, 'Then Philip began with this very Scripture and told him the good news about Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 36, 'As they traveled along the road and came to some water, the eunuch said, “Look, here is water! What is there to prevent me from being baptized?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 37, ''),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 38, 'And he gave orders to stop the chariot. Then both Philip and the eunuch went down into the water, and Philip baptized him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 39, 'When they came up out of the water, the Spirit of the Lord carried Philip away, and the eunuch saw him no more, but went on his way rejoicing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 8, 40, 'But Philip appeared at Azotus and traveled through that region, preaching the gospel in all the towns until he came to Caesarea.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 1, 'Meanwhile, Saul was still breathing out murderous threats against the disciples of the Lord. He approached the high priest'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 2, 'and requested letters to the synagogues in Damascus, so that if he found any men or women belonging to the Way, he could bring them as prisoners to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 3, 'As Saul drew near to Damascus on his journey, suddenly a light from heaven flashed around him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 4, 'He fell to the ground and heard a voice say to him, “Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 5, '“Who are You, Lord?” Saul asked. “I am Jesus, whom you are persecuting,” He replied.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 6, '“Now get up and go into the city, and you will be told what you must do.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 7, 'The men traveling with Saul stood there speechless. They heard the voice but did not see anyone.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 8, 'Saul got up from the ground, but when he opened his eyes he could not see a thing. So they led him by the hand into Damascus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 9, 'For three days he was without sight, and he did not eat or drink anything.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 10, 'In Damascus there was a disciple named Ananias. The Lord spoke to him in a vision, “Ananias!” “Here I am, Lord,” he answered.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 11, '“Get up!” the Lord told him. “Go to the house of Judas on Straight Street and ask for a man from Tarsus named Saul, for he is praying.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 12, 'In a vision he has seen a man named Ananias come and place his hands on him to restore his sight.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 13, 'But Ananias answered, “Lord, many people have told me about this man and all the harm he has done to Your saints in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 14, 'And now he is here with authority from the chief priests to arrest all who call on Your name.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 15, '“Go!” said the Lord. “This man is My chosen instrument to carry My name before the Gentiles and their kings, and before the people of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 16, 'I will show him how much he must suffer for My name.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 17, 'So Ananias went to the house, and when he arrived, he placed his hands on Saul. “Brother Saul,” he said, “the Lord Jesus, who appeared to you on the road as you were coming here, has sent me so that you may see again and be filled with the Holy Spirit.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 18, 'At that instant, something like scales fell from Saul’s eyes, and his sight was restored. He got up and was baptized,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 19, 'and after taking some food, he regained his strength. And he spent several days with the disciples in Damascus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 20, 'Saul promptly began to proclaim Jesus in the synagogues, declaring, “He is the Son of God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 21, 'All who heard him were astounded and asked, “Isn’t this the man who wreaked havoc in Jerusalem on those who call on this name? And hasn’t he come here to take them as prisoners to the chief priests?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 22, 'But Saul was empowered all the more, and he confounded the Jews living in Damascus by proving that Jesus is the Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 23, 'After many days had passed, the Jews conspired to kill him,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 24, 'but Saul learned of their plot. Day and night they watched the city gates in order to kill him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 25, 'One night, however, his disciples took him and lowered him in a basket through a window in the wall.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 26, 'When Saul arrived in Jerusalem, he tried to join the disciples, but they were all afraid of him, not believing that he was a disciple.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 27, 'Then Barnabas brought him to the apostles and described how Saul had seen the Lord, who spoke to him on the road to Damascus, and how Saul had spoken boldly in that city in the name of Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 28, 'So Saul stayed with them, moving about freely in Jerusalem and speaking boldly in the name of the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 29, 'He talked and debated with the Grecian Jews, but they tried to kill him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 30, 'When the brothers learned of this, they took him down to Caesarea and sent him off to Tarsus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 31, 'Then the church throughout Judea, Galilee, and Samaria experienced a time of peace. It grew in strength and numbers, living in the fear of the Lord and the encouragement of the Holy Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 32, 'As Peter traveled throughout the area, he went to visit the saints in Lydda.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 33, 'There he found a man named Aeneas, who had been paralyzed and bedridden for eight years.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 34, '“Aeneas,” Peter said to him, “Jesus Christ heals you! Get up and put away your mat.” Immediately Aeneas got up,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 35, 'and all who lived in Lydda and Sharon saw him and turned to the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 36, 'In Joppa there was a disciple named Tabitha (which is translated as Dorcas), who was always occupied with works of kindness and charity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 37, 'At that time, however, she became sick and died, and her body was washed and placed in an upper room.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 38, 'Since Lydda was near Joppa, the disciples heard that Peter was there and sent two men to urge him, “Come to us without delay.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 39, 'So Peter got up and went with them. On his arrival, they took him to the upper room. All the widows stood around him, weeping and showing him the tunics and other clothing that Dorcas had made while she was still with them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 40, 'Then Peter sent them all out of the room. He knelt down and prayed, and turning toward her body, he said, “Tabitha, get up!” She opened her eyes, and seeing Peter, she sat up.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 41, 'Peter took her by the hand and helped her up. Then he called the saints and widows and presented her to them alive.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 42, 'This became known all over Joppa, and many people believed in the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 9, 43, 'And Peter stayed for several days in Joppa with a tanner named Simon.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 1, 'At Caesarea there was a man named Cornelius, a centurion in what was called the Italian Regiment.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 2, 'He and all his household were devout and God-fearing. He gave generously to the people and prayed to God regularly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 3, 'One day at about the ninth hour, he had a clear vision of an angel of God who came to him and said, “Cornelius!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 4, 'Cornelius stared at him in fear and asked, “What is it, Lord?” The angel answered, “Your prayers and gifts to the poor have ascended as a memorial offering before God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 5, 'Now send men to Joppa to call for a man named Simon who is called Peter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 6, 'He is staying with Simon the tanner, whose house is by the sea.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 7, 'When the angel who spoke to him had gone, Cornelius called two of his servants and a devout soldier from among his attendants.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 8, 'He explained what had happened and sent them to Joppa.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 9, 'The next day at about the sixth hour, as the men were approaching the city on their journey, Peter went up on the roof to pray.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 10, 'He became hungry and wanted something to eat, but while the meal was being prepared, he fell into a trance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 11, 'He saw heaven open and something like a large sheet being let down to earth by its four corners.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 12, 'It contained all kinds of four-footed animals and reptiles of the earth, as well as birds of the air.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 13, 'Then a voice said to him: “Get up, Peter, kill and eat!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 14, '“No, Lord!” Peter answered. “I have never eaten anything impure or unclean.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 15, 'The voice spoke to him a second time: “Do not call anything impure that God has made clean.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 16, 'This happened three times, and all at once the sheet was taken back up into heaven.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 17, 'While Peter was puzzling over the meaning of the vision, the men sent by Cornelius found Simon’s house and approached the gate.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 18, 'They called out to ask if Simon called Peter was staying there.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 19, 'As Peter continued to reflect on the vision, the Spirit said to him, “Behold, three men are looking for you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 20, 'So get up! Go downstairs and accompany them without hesitation, because I have sent them.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 21, 'So Peter went down to the men and said, “Here am I, the one you are looking for. Why have you come?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 22, '“Cornelius the centurion has sent us,” they said. “He is a righteous and God-fearing man with a good reputation among the whole Jewish nation. A holy angel instructed him to request your presence in his home so he could hear a message from you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 23, 'So Peter invited them in as his guests. And the next day he got ready and went with them, accompanied by some of the brothers from Joppa.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 24, 'The following day he arrived in Caesarea, where Cornelius was expecting them and had called together his relatives and close friends.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 25, 'As Peter was about to enter, Cornelius met him and fell at his feet to worship him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 26, 'But Peter helped him up. “Stand up,” he said, “I am only a man myself.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 27, 'As Peter talked with him, he went inside and found many people gathered together.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 28, 'He said to them, “You know how unlawful it is for a Jew to associate with a foreigner or visit him. But God has shown me that I should not call any man impure or unclean.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 29, 'So when I was invited, I came without objection. I ask, then, why have you sent for me?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 30, 'Cornelius answered: “Four days ago I was in my house praying at this, the ninth hour. Suddenly a man in radiant clothing stood before me'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 31, 'and said, ‘Cornelius, your prayer has been heard, and your gifts to the poor have been remembered before God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 32, 'Therefore send to Joppa for Simon, who is called Peter. He is a guest in the home of Simon the tanner, by the sea.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 33, 'So I sent for you immediately, and you were kind enough to come. Now then, we are all here in the presence of God to listen to everything the Lord has instructed you to tell us.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 34, 'Then Peter began to speak: “I now truly understand that God does not show favoritism,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 35, 'but welcomes those from every nation who fear Him and do what is right.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 36, 'He has sent this message to the people of Israel, proclaiming the gospel of peace through Jesus Christ, who is Lord of all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 37, 'You yourselves know what has happened throughout Judea, beginning in Galilee with the baptism that John proclaimed:'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 38, 'how God anointed Jesus of Nazareth with the Holy Spirit and with power, and how Jesus went around doing good and healing all who were oppressed by the devil, because God was with Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 39, 'We are witnesses of all that He did, both in the land of the Jews and in Jerusalem. And although they put Him to death by hanging Him on a tree,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 40, 'God raised Him up on the third day and caused Him to be seen—'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 41, 'not by all the people, but by the witnesses God had chosen beforehand, by us who ate and drank with Him after He rose from the dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 42, 'And He commanded us to preach to the people and to testify that He is the One appointed by God to judge the living and the dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 43, 'All the prophets testify about Him that everyone who believes in Him receives forgiveness of sins through His name.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 44, 'While Peter was still speaking these words, the Holy Spirit fell upon all who heard his message.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 45, 'All the circumcised believers who had accompanied Peter were astounded that the gift of the Holy Spirit had been poured out even on the Gentiles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 46, 'For they heard them speaking in tongues and exalting God. Then Peter said,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 47, '“Can anyone withhold the water to baptize these people? They have received the Holy Spirit just as we have!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 10, 48, 'So he ordered that they be baptized in the name of Jesus Christ. Then they asked him to stay for a few days.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 1, 'The apostles and brothers throughout Judea soon heard that the Gentiles also had received the word of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 2, 'So when Peter went up to Jerusalem, the circumcised believers took issue with him'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 3, 'and said, “You visited uncircumcised men and ate with them.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 4, 'But Peter began and explained to them the whole sequence of events:'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 5, '“I was in the city of Joppa praying, and in a trance I saw a vision of something like a large sheet being let down from heaven by its four corners, and it came right down to me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 6, 'I looked at it closely and saw four-footed animals of the earth, wild beasts, reptiles, and birds of the air.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 7, 'Then I heard a voice saying to me, ‘Get up, Peter, kill and eat.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 8, '‘No, Lord,’ I said, ‘for nothing impure or unclean has ever entered my mouth.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 9, 'But the voice spoke from heaven a second time, ‘Do not call anything impure that God has made clean.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 10, 'This happened three times, and everything was drawn back up into heaven.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 11, 'Just then three men sent to me from Caesarea stopped at the house where I was staying.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 12, 'The Spirit told me to accompany them without hesitation. These six brothers also went with me, and we entered the man’s home.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 13, 'He told us how he had seen an angel standing in his house and saying, ‘Send to Joppa for Simon who is called Peter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 14, 'He will convey to you a message by which you and all your household will be saved.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 15, 'As I began to speak, the Holy Spirit fell upon them, just as He had fallen upon us at the beginning.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 16, 'Then I remembered the word of the Lord, as He used to say, ‘John baptized with water, but you will be baptized with the Holy Spirit.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 17, 'So if God gave them the same gift He gave us who believed in the Lord Jesus Christ, who was I to hinder the work of God?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 18, 'When they heard this, their objections were put to rest, and they glorified God, saying, “So then, God has granted even the Gentiles repentance unto life.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 19, 'Meanwhile those scattered by the persecution that began with Stephen traveled as far as Phoenicia, Cyprus, and Antioch, speaking the message only to Jews.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 20, 'But some of them, men from Cyprus and Cyrene, went to Antioch and began speaking to the Greeks as well, proclaiming the good news about the Lord Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 21, 'The hand of the Lord was with them, and a great number of people believed and turned to the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 22, 'When news of this reached the ears of the church in Jerusalem, they sent Barnabas to Antioch.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 23, 'When he arrived and saw the grace of God, he rejoiced and encouraged them all to abide in the Lord with all their hearts.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 24, 'Barnabas was a good man, full of the Holy Spirit and faith, and a great number of people were brought to the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 25, 'Then Barnabas went to Tarsus to look for Saul,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 26, 'and when he found him, he brought him back to Antioch. So for a full year they met together with the church and taught large numbers of people. The disciples were first called Christians at Antioch.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 27, 'In those days some prophets came down from Jerusalem to Antioch.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 28, 'One of them named Agabus stood up and predicted through the Spirit that a great famine would sweep across the whole world. (This happened under Claudius.)'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 29, 'So the disciples, each according to his ability, decided to send relief to the brothers living in Judea.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 11, 30, 'This they did, sending their gifts to the elders with Barnabas and Saul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 1, 'About that time, King Herod reached out to harm some who belonged to the church.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 2, 'He had James, the brother of John, put to death with the sword.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 3, 'And seeing that this pleased the Jews, Herod proceeded to seize Peter during the Feast of Unleavened Bread.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 4, 'He arrested him and put him in prison, handing him over to be guarded by four squads of four soldiers each. Herod intended to bring him out to the people after the Passover.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 5, 'So Peter was kept in prison, but the church was fervently praying to God for him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 6, 'On the night before Herod was to bring him to trial, Peter was sleeping between two soldiers, bound with two chains, with sentries standing guard at the entrance to the prison.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 7, 'Suddenly an angel of the Lord appeared and a light shone in the cell. He tapped Peter on the side and woke him up, saying, “Get up quickly.” And the chains fell off his wrists.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 8, '“Get dressed and put on your sandals,” said the angel. Peter did so, and the angel told him, “Wrap your cloak around you and follow me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 9, 'So Peter followed him out, but he was unaware that what the angel was doing was real. He thought he was only seeing a vision.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 10, 'They passed the first and second guards and came to the iron gate leading to the city, which opened for them by itself. When they had gone outside and walked the length of one block, the angel suddenly left him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 11, 'Then Peter came to himself and said, “Now I know for sure that the Lord has sent His angel and rescued me from Herod’s grasp and from everything the Jewish people were anticipating.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 12, 'And when he had realized this, he went to the house of Mary the mother of John, also called Mark, where many people had gathered together and were praying.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 13, 'He knocked at the outer gate, and a servant girl named Rhoda came to answer it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 14, 'When she recognized Peter’s voice, she was so overjoyed that she forgot to open the gate, but ran inside and announced, “Peter is standing at the gate!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 15, '“You are out of your mind,” they told her. But when she kept insisting it was so, they said, “It must be his angel.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 16, 'But Peter kept on knocking, and when they opened the door and saw him, they were astounded.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 17, 'Peter motioned with his hand for silence, and he described how the Lord had brought him out of the prison. “Send word to James and to the brothers,” he said, and he left for another place.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 18, 'At daybreak there was no small commotion among the soldiers as to what had become of Peter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 19, 'After Herod had searched for him unsuccessfully, he examined the guards and ordered that they be executed. Then he went down from Judea to Caesarea and spent some time there.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 20, 'Now Herod was in a furious dispute with the people of Tyre and Sidon, and they convened before him. Having secured the support of Blastus, the king’s chamberlain, they asked for peace, because their region depended on the king’s country for food.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 21, 'On the appointed day, Herod donned his royal robes, sat on his throne, and addressed the people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 22, 'And they began to shout, “This is the voice of a god, not a man!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 23, 'Immediately, because Herod did not give glory to God, an angel of the Lord struck him down, and he was eaten by worms and died.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 24, 'But the word of God continued to spread and multiply.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 12, 25, 'When Barnabas and Saul had fulfilled their mission to Jerusalem, they returned, bringing with them John, also called Mark.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 1, 'Now in the church at Antioch there were prophets and teachers: Barnabas, Simeon called Niger, Lucius of Cyrene, Manaen (who had been brought up with Herod the tetrarch), and Saul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 2, 'While they were worshiping the Lord and fasting, the Holy Spirit said, “Set apart for Me Barnabas and Saul for the work to which I have called them.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 3, 'And after they had fasted and prayed, they laid their hands on them and sent them off.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 4, 'So Barnabas and Saul, sent forth by the Holy Spirit, went down to Seleucia and sailed from there to Cyprus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 5, 'When they arrived at Salamis, they proclaimed the word of God in the Jewish synagogues. And John was with them as their helper.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 6, 'They traveled through the whole island as far as Paphos, where they found a Jewish sorcerer and false prophet named Bar-Jesus,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 7, 'an attendant of the proconsul, Sergius Paulus. The proconsul, a man of intelligence, summoned Barnabas and Saul because he wanted to hear the word of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 8, 'But Elymas the sorcerer (for that is what his name means) opposed them and tried to turn the proconsul from the faith.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 9, 'Then Saul, who was also called Paul, filled with the Holy Spirit, looked directly at Elymas'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 10, 'and said, “O child of the devil and enemy of all righteousness, you are full of all kinds of deceit and trickery! Will you never stop perverting the straight ways of the Lord?'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 11, 'Now look, the hand of the Lord is against you, and for a time you will be blind and unable to see the light of the sun.” Immediately mist and darkness came over him, and he groped about, seeking someone to lead him by the hand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 12, 'When the proconsul saw what had happened, he believed, for he was astonished at the teaching about the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 13, 'After setting sail from Paphos, Paul and his companions came to Perga in Pamphylia, where John left them to return to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 14, 'And from Perga, they traveled inland to Pisidian Antioch, where they entered the synagogue on the Sabbath and sat down.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 15, 'After the reading from the Law and the Prophets, the synagogue leaders sent word to them: “Brothers, if you have a word of encouragement for the people, please speak.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 16, 'Paul stood up, motioned with his hand, and began to speak: “Men of Israel and you Gentiles who fear God, listen to me!'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 17, 'The God of the people of Israel chose our fathers. He made them into a great people during their stay in Egypt, and with an uplifted arm He led them out of that land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 18, 'He endured their conduct for about forty years in the wilderness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 19, 'And having vanquished seven nations in Canaan, He gave their land to His people as an inheritance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 20, 'All this took about 450 years. After this, God gave them judges until the time of Samuel the prophet.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 21, 'Then the people asked for a king, and God gave them forty years under Saul son of Kish, from the tribe of Benjamin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 22, 'After removing Saul, He raised up David as their king and testified about him: ‘I have found David son of Jesse a man after My own heart; he will carry out My will in its entirety.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 23, 'From the descendants of this man, God has brought to Israel the Savior Jesus, as He promised.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 24, 'Before the arrival of Jesus, John preached a baptism of repentance to all the people of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 25, 'As John was completing his course, he said, ‘Who do you suppose I am? I am not that One. But He is coming after me whose sandals I am not worthy to untie.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 26, 'Brothers, children of Abraham, and you Gentiles who fear God, it is to us that this message of salvation has been sent.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 27, 'The people of Jerusalem and their rulers did not recognize Jesus, yet in condemning Him they fulfilled the words of the prophets that are read every Sabbath.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 28, 'And though they found no ground for a death sentence, they asked Pilate to have Him executed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 29, 'When they had carried out all that was written about Him, they took Him down from the tree and laid Him in a tomb.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 30, 'But God raised Him from the dead,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 31, 'and for many days He was seen by those who had accompanied Him from Galilee to Jerusalem. They are now His witnesses to our people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 32, 'And now we proclaim to you the good news: What God promised our fathers'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 33, 'He has fulfilled for us, their children, by raising up Jesus. As it is written in the second Psalm: ‘You are My Son; today I have become Your Father.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 34, 'In fact, God raised Him from the dead, never to see decay. As He has said: ‘I will give you the holy and sure blessings promised to David.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 35, 'So also, He says in another Psalm: ‘You will not let Your Holy One see decay.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 36, 'For when David had served God’s purpose in his own generation, he fell asleep. His body was buried with his fathers and saw decay.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 37, 'But the One whom God raised from the dead did not see decay.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 38, 'Therefore let it be known to you, brothers, that through Jesus the forgiveness of sins is proclaimed to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 39, 'Through Him everyone who believes is justified from everything you could not be justified from by the law of Moses.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 40, 'Watch out, then, that what was spoken by the prophets does not happen to you:'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 41, '‘Look, you scoffers, wonder and perish! For I am doing a work in your days that you would never believe, even if someone told you.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 42, 'As Paul and Barnabas were leaving the synagogue, the people urged them to continue this message on the next Sabbath.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 43, 'After the synagogue was dismissed, many of the Jews and devout converts to Judaism followed Paul and Barnabas, who spoke to them and urged them to continue in the grace of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 44, 'On the following Sabbath, nearly the whole city gathered to hear the word of the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 45, 'But when the Jews saw the crowds, they were filled with jealousy, and they blasphemously contradicted what Paul was saying.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 46, 'Then Paul and Barnabas answered them boldly: “It was necessary to speak the word of God to you first. But since you reject it and do not consider yourselves worthy of eternal life, we now turn to the Gentiles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 47, 'For this is what the Lord has commanded us: ‘I have made you a light for the Gentiles, to bring salvation to the ends of the earth.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 48, 'When the Gentiles heard this, they rejoiced and glorified the word of the Lord, and all who were appointed for eternal life believed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 49, 'And the word of the Lord spread throughout that region.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 50, 'The Jews, however, incited the religious women of prominence and the leading men of the city. They stirred up persecution against Paul and Barnabas and drove them out of their district.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 51, 'So they shook the dust off their feet in protest against them and went to Iconium.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 13, 52, 'And the disciples were filled with joy and with the Holy Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 1, 'At Iconium, Paul and Barnabas went as usual into the Jewish synagogue, where they spoke so well that a great number of Jews and Greeks believed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 2, 'But the unbelieving Jews stirred up the Gentiles and poisoned their minds against the brothers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 3, 'So Paul and Barnabas spent considerable time there, speaking boldly for the Lord, who affirmed the message of His grace by enabling them to perform signs and wonders.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 4, 'The people of the city were divided. Some sided with the Jews, and others with the apostles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 5, 'But when the Gentiles and Jews, together with their rulers, set out to mistreat and stone them,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 6, 'they found out about it and fled to the Lycaonian cities of Lystra and Derbe and to the surrounding region,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 7, 'where they continued to preach the gospel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 8, 'In Lystra there sat a man crippled in his feet, who was lame from birth and had never walked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 9, 'This man was listening to the words of Paul, who looked intently at him and saw that he had faith to be healed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 10, 'In a loud voice Paul called out, “Stand up on your feet!” And the man jumped up and began to walk.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 11, 'When the crowds saw what Paul had done, they lifted up their voices in the Lycaonian language: “The gods have come down to us in human form!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 12, 'Barnabas they called Zeus, and Paul they called Hermes, because he was the chief speaker.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 13, 'The priest of Zeus, whose temple was just outside the city, brought bulls and wreaths to the city gates, hoping to offer a sacrifice along with the crowds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 14, 'But when the apostles Barnabas and Paul found out about this, they tore their clothes and rushed into the crowd, shouting,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 15, '“Men, why are you doing this? We too are only men, human like you. We are bringing you good news that you should turn from these worthless things to the living God, who made heaven and earth and sea and everything in them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 16, 'In past generations, He let all nations go their own way.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 17, 'Yet He has not left Himself without testimony to His goodness: He gives you rain from heaven and fruitful seasons, filling your hearts with food and gladness.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 18, 'Even with these words, Paul and Barnabas could hardly stop the crowds from sacrificing to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 19, 'Then some Jews arrived from Antioch and Iconium and won over the crowds. They stoned Paul and dragged him outside the city, presuming he was dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 20, 'But after the disciples had gathered around him, he got up and went back into the city. And the next day he left with Barnabas for Derbe.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 21, 'They preached the gospel to that city and made many disciples. Then they returned to Lystra, Iconium, and Antioch,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 22, 'strengthening the souls of the disciples and encouraging them to continue in the faith. “We must endure many hardships to enter the kingdom of God,” they said.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 23, 'Paul and Barnabas appointed elders for them in each church, praying and fasting as they entrusted them to the Lord, in whom they had believed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 24, 'After passing through Pisidia, they came to Pamphylia.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 25, 'And when they had spoken the word in Perga, they went down to Attalia.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 26, 'From Attalia they sailed to Antioch, where they had been commended to the grace of God for the work they had just completed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 27, 'When they arrived, they gathered the church together and reported all that God had done through them, and how He had opened the door of faith to the Gentiles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 14, 28, 'And they spent a long time there with the disciples.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 1, 'Then some men came down from Judea and were teaching the brothers, “Unless you are circumcised according to the custom of Moses, you cannot be saved.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 2, 'And after engaging these men in sharp debate, Paul and Barnabas were appointed, along with some other believers, to go up to Jerusalem to see the apostles and elders about this question.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 3, 'Sent on their way by the church, they passed through Phoenicia and Samaria, recounting the conversion of the Gentiles and bringing great joy to all the brothers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 4, 'On their arrival in Jerusalem, they were welcomed by the church and apostles and elders, to whom they reported all that God had done through them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 5, 'But some believers from the party of the Pharisees stood up and declared, “The Gentiles must be circumcised and required to obey the law of Moses.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 6, 'So the apostles and elders met to look into this matter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 7, 'After much discussion, Peter got up and said to them, “Brothers, you know that in the early days God made a choice among you that the Gentiles would hear from my lips the message of the gospel and believe.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 8, 'And God, who knows the heart, showed His approval by giving the Holy Spirit to them, just as He did to us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 9, 'He made no distinction between us and them, for He cleansed their hearts by faith.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 10, 'Now then, why do you test God by placing on the necks of the disciples a yoke that neither we nor our fathers have been able to bear?'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 11, 'On the contrary, we believe it is through the grace of the Lord Jesus that we are saved, just as they are.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 12, 'The whole assembly fell silent as they listened to Barnabas and Paul describing the signs and wonders God had done among the Gentiles through them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 13, 'When they had finished speaking, James declared, “Brothers, listen to me!'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 14, 'Simon has told us how God first visited the Gentiles to take from them a people to be His own.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 15, 'The words of the prophets agree with this, as it is written:'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 16, '‘After this I will return and rebuild the fallen tent of David. Its ruins I will rebuild, and I will restore it,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 17, 'so that the remnant of men may seek the Lord, and all the Gentiles who are called by My name, says the Lord who does these things'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 18, 'that have been known for ages.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 19, 'It is my judgment, therefore, that we should not cause trouble for the Gentiles who are turning to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 20, 'Instead, we should write and tell them to abstain from food polluted by idols, from sexual immorality, from the meat of strangled animals, and from blood.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 21, 'For Moses has been proclaimed in every city from ancient times and is read in the synagogues on every Sabbath.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 22, 'Then the apostles and elders, with the whole church, decided to select men from among them to send to Antioch with Paul and Barnabas. They chose Judas called Barsabbas and Silas, two leaders among the brothers,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 23, 'and sent them with this letter: The apostles and the elders, your brothers, To the brothers among the Gentiles in Antioch, Syria, and Cilicia: Greetings.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 24, 'It has come to our attention that some went out from us without our authorization and unsettled you, troubling your minds by what they said.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 25, 'So we all agreed to choose men to send to you along with our beloved Barnabas and Paul,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 26, 'men who have risked their lives for the name of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 27, 'Therefore we are sending Judas and Silas to tell you in person the same things we are writing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 28, 'It seemed good to the Holy Spirit and to us not to burden you with anything beyond these essential requirements:'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 29, 'You must abstain from food sacrificed to idols, from blood, from the meat of strangled animals, and from sexual immorality. You will do well to avoid these things. Farewell.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 30, 'So the men were sent off and went down to Antioch, where they assembled the congregation and delivered the letter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 31, 'When the people read it, they rejoiced at its encouraging message.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 32, 'Judas and Silas, who themselves were prophets, said much to encourage and strengthen the brothers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 33, 'After spending some time there, they were sent off by the brothers in peace to return to those who had sent them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 34, ''),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 35, 'But Paul and Barnabas remained at Antioch, along with many others, teaching and preaching the word of the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 36, 'Some time later Paul said to Barnabas, “Let us go back and visit the brothers in every town where we proclaimed the word of the Lord, to see how they are doing.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 37, 'Barnabas wanted to take John, also called Mark.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 38, 'But Paul thought it best not to take him, because he had deserted them in Pamphylia and had not accompanied them in the work.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 39, 'Their disagreement was so sharp that they parted company. Barnabas took Mark and sailed for Cyprus,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 40, 'but Paul chose Silas and left, commended by the brothers to the grace of the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 15, 41, 'And he traveled through Syria and Cilicia, strengthening the churches.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 1, 'Paul came to Derbe and then to Lystra, where he found a disciple named Timothy, the son of a believing Jewish woman and a Greek father.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 2, 'The brothers in Lystra and Iconium spoke well of him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 3, 'Paul wanted Timothy to accompany him, so he took him and circumcised him on account of the Jews in that area, for they all knew that his father was a Greek.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 4, 'As they went from town to town, they delivered the decisions handed down by the apostles and elders in Jerusalem for the people to obey.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 5, 'So the churches were strengthened in the faith and grew daily in numbers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 6, 'After the Holy Spirit had prevented them from speaking the word in the province of Asia, they traveled through the region of Phrygia and Galatia.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 7, 'And when they came to the border of Mysia, they tried to enter Bithynia, but the Spirit of Jesus would not permit them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 8, 'So they passed by Mysia and went down to Troas.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 9, 'During the night, Paul had a vision of a man of Macedonia standing and pleading with him, “Come over to Macedonia and help us.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 10, 'As soon as Paul had seen the vision, we got ready to leave for Macedonia, concluding that God had called us to preach the gospel to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 11, 'We sailed from Troas straight to Samothrace, and the following day on to Neapolis.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 12, 'From there we went to the Roman colony of Philippi, the leading city of that district of Macedonia. And we stayed there several days.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 13, 'On the Sabbath we went outside the city gate along the river, where it was customary to find a place of prayer. After sitting down, we spoke to the women who had gathered there.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 14, 'Among those listening was a woman named Lydia, a dealer in purple cloth from the city of Thyatira, who was a worshiper of God. The Lord opened her heart to respond to Paul’s message.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 15, 'And when she and her household had been baptized, she urged us, “If you consider me a believer in the Lord, come and stay at my house.” And she persuaded us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 16, 'One day as we were going to the place of prayer, we were met by a slave girl with a spirit of divination, who earned a large income for her masters by fortune-telling.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 17, 'This girl followed Paul and the rest of us, shouting, “These men are servants of the Most High God, who are proclaiming to you the way of salvation!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 18, 'She continued this for many days. Eventually Paul grew so aggravated that he turned and said to the spirit, “In the name of Jesus Christ I command you to come out of her!” And the spirit left her at that very moment.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 19, 'When the girl’s owners saw that their hope of making money was gone, they seized Paul and Silas and dragged them before the authorities in the marketplace.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 20, 'They brought them to the magistrates and said, “These men are Jews and are throwing our city into turmoil'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 21, 'by promoting customs that are unlawful for us Romans to adopt or practice.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 22, 'The crowd joined in the attack against Paul and Silas, and the magistrates ordered that they be stripped and beaten with rods.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 23, 'And after striking them with many blows, they threw them into prison and ordered the jailer to guard them securely.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 24, 'On receiving this order, he placed them in the inner cell and fastened their feet in the stocks.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 25, 'About midnight Paul and Silas were praying and singing hymns to God, and the other prisoners were listening to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 26, 'Suddenly a strong earthquake shook the foundations of the prison. At once all the doors flew open and everyone’s chains came loose.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 27, 'When the jailer woke up and saw the prison doors open, he drew his sword and was about to kill himself, presuming that the prisoners had escaped.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 28, 'But Paul called out in a loud voice, “Do not harm yourself! We are all here!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 29, 'Calling for lights, the jailer rushed in and fell trembling before Paul and Silas.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 30, 'Then he brought them out and asked, “Sirs, what must I do to be saved?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 31, 'They replied, “Believe in the Lord Jesus and you will be saved, you and your household.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 32, 'Then Paul and Silas spoke the word of the Lord to him and to everyone in his house.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 33, 'At that hour of the night, the jailer took them and washed their wounds. And without delay, he and all his household were baptized.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 34, 'Then he brought them into his home and set a meal before them. So he and all his household rejoiced that they had come to believe in God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 35, 'When daylight came, the magistrates sent their officers with the order: “Release those men.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 36, 'The jailer informed Paul: “The magistrates have sent orders to release you. Now you may go on your way in peace.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 37, 'But Paul said to the officers, “They beat us publicly without a trial and threw us into prison, even though we are Roman citizens. And now do they want to send us away secretly? Absolutely not! Let them come themselves and escort us out!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 38, 'So the officers relayed this message to the magistrates, who were alarmed to hear that Paul and Silas were Roman citizens.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 39, 'They came to appease them and led them out, requesting that they leave the city.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 16, 40, 'After Paul and Silas came out of the prison, they went to Lydia’s house to see the brothers and encourage them. Then they left the city.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 1, 'When they had passed through Amphipolis and Apollonia, they came to Thessalonica, where there was a Jewish synagogue.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 2, 'As was his custom, Paul went into the synagogue, and on three Sabbaths he reasoned with them from the Scriptures,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 3, 'explaining and proving that the Christ had to suffer and rise from the dead. “This Jesus I am proclaiming to you is the Christ,” he declared.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 4, 'Some of the Jews were persuaded and joined Paul and Silas, along with a large number of God-fearing Greeks and quite a few leading women.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 5, 'The Jews, however, became jealous. So they brought in some troublemakers from the marketplace, formed a mob, and sent the city into an uproar. They raided Jason’s house in search of Paul and Silas, hoping to bring them out to the people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 6, 'But when they could not find them, they dragged Jason and some other brothers before the city officials, shouting, “These men who have turned the world upside down have now come here,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 7, 'and Jason has welcomed them into his home. They are all defying Caesar’s decrees, saying that there is another king, named Jesus!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 8, 'On hearing this, the crowd and city officials were greatly disturbed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 9, 'And they collected bond from Jason and the others, and then released them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 10, 'As soon as night had fallen, the brothers sent Paul and Silas away to Berea. On arriving there, they went into the Jewish synagogue.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 11, 'Now the Bereans were more noble-minded than the Thessalonians, for they received the message with great eagerness and examined the Scriptures every day to see if these teachings were true.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 12, 'As a result, many of them believed, along with quite a few prominent Greek women and men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 13, 'But when the Jews from Thessalonica learned that Paul was also proclaiming the word of God in Berea, they went there themselves to incite and agitate the crowds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 14, 'The brothers immediately sent Paul to the coast, but Silas and Timothy remained in Berea.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 15, 'Those who escorted Paul brought him to Athens and then returned with instructions for Silas and Timothy to join him as soon as possible.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 16, 'While Paul was waiting for them in Athens, he was deeply disturbed in his spirit to see that the city was full of idols.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 17, 'So he reasoned in the synagogue with the Jews and God-fearing Gentiles, and in the marketplace with those he met each day.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 18, 'Some Epicurean and Stoic philosophers also began to debate with him. Some of them asked, “What is this babbler trying to say?” Others said, “He seems to be advocating foreign gods.” They said this because Paul was proclaiming the good news of Jesus and the resurrection.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 19, 'So they took Paul and brought him to the Areopagus, where they asked him, “May we know what this new teaching is that you are presenting?'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 20, 'For you are bringing some strange notions to our ears, and we want to know what they mean.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 21, 'Now all the Athenians and foreigners who lived there spent their time doing nothing more than hearing and articulating new ideas.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 22, 'Then Paul stood up in the meeting of the Areopagus and said, “Men of Athens, I see that in every way you are very religious.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 23, 'For as I walked around and examined your objects of worship, I even found an altar with this inscription: TO AN UNKNOWN GOD. Therefore what you worship as something unknown, I now proclaim to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 24, 'The God who made the world and everything in it is the Lord of heaven and earth and does not live in temples made by human hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 25, 'Nor is He served by human hands, as if He needed anything, because He Himself gives everyone life and breath and everything else.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 26, 'From one man He made every nation of men, that they should inhabit the whole earth; and He determined their appointed times and the boundaries of their lands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 27, 'God intended that they would seek Him and perhaps reach out for Him and find Him, though He is not far from each one of us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 28, '‘For in Him we live and move and have our being.’ As some of your own poets have said, ‘We are His offspring.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 29, 'Therefore, being offspring of God, we should not think that the Divine Being is like gold or silver or stone, an image formed by man’s skill and imagination.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 30, 'Although God overlooked the ignorance of earlier times, He now commands all people everywhere to repent.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 31, 'For He has set a day when He will judge the world with justice by the Man He has appointed. He has given proof of this to everyone by raising Him from the dead.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 32, 'When they heard about the resurrection of the dead, some began to mock him, but others said, “We want to hear you again on this topic.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 33, 'At that, Paul left the Areopagus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 17, 34, 'But some joined him and believed, including Dionysius the Areopagite, a woman named Damaris, and others who were with them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 1, 'After this, Paul left Athens and went to Corinth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 2, 'There he found a Jew named Aquila, a native of Pontus, who had recently come from Italy with his wife Priscilla because Claudius had ordered all the Jews to leave Rome. Paul went to visit them,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 3, 'and he stayed and worked with them because they were tentmakers by trade, just as he was.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 4, 'Every Sabbath he reasoned in the synagogue, trying to persuade Jews and Greeks alike.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 5, 'And when Silas and Timothy came down from Macedonia, Paul devoted himself fully to the word, testifying to the Jews that Jesus is the Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 6, 'But when they opposed and insulted him, he shook out his garments and told them, “Your blood be on your own heads! I am innocent of it. From now on I will go to the Gentiles.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 7, 'So Paul left the synagogue and went next door to the house of Titus Justus, a worshiper of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 8, 'Crispus, the synagogue leader, and his whole household believed in the Lord. And many of the Corinthians who heard the message believed and were baptized.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 9, 'One night the Lord spoke to Paul in a vision: “Do not be afraid; keep on speaking; do not be silent.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 10, 'For I am with you and no one will lay a hand on you, because I have many people in this city.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 11, 'So Paul stayed for a year and a half, teaching the word of God among the Corinthians.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 12, 'While Gallio was proconsul of Achaia, the Jews coordinated an attack on Paul and brought him before the judgment seat.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 13, '“This man is persuading the people to worship God in ways contrary to the law,” they said.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 14, 'But just as Paul was about to speak, Gallio told the Jews, “If this matter involved a wrongdoing or vicious crime, O Jews, it would be reasonable for me to hear your complaint.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 15, 'But since it is a dispute about words and names and your own law, settle it yourselves. I refuse to be a judge of such things.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 16, 'And he drove them away from the judgment seat.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 17, 'At this, the crowd seized Sosthenes the synagogue leader and beat him in front of the judgment seat. But none of this was of concern to Gallio.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 18, 'Paul remained in Corinth for quite some time before saying goodbye to the brothers. He had his head shaved in Cenchrea to keep a vow he had made, and then he sailed for Syria, accompanied by Priscilla and Aquila.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 19, 'When they reached Ephesus, Paul parted ways with Priscilla and Aquila. He himself went into the synagogue there and reasoned with the Jews.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 20, 'When they asked him to stay for a while longer, he declined.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 21, 'But as he left, he said, “I will come back to you if God is willing.” And he set sail from Ephesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 22, 'When Paul had landed at Caesarea, he went up and greeted the church at Jerusalem. Then he went down to Antioch.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 23, 'After Paul had spent some time in Antioch, he traveled from place to place throughout the region of Galatia and Phrygia, strengthening all the disciples.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 24, 'Meanwhile a Jew named Apollos, a native of Alexandria, came to Ephesus. He was an eloquent man, well versed in the Scriptures.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 25, 'He had been instructed in the way of the Lord and was fervent in spirit. He spoke and taught accurately about Jesus, though he knew only the baptism of John.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 26, 'And he began to speak boldly in the synagogue. When Priscilla and Aquila heard him, they took him in and explained to him the way of God more accurately.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 27, 'When Apollos resolved to cross over to Achaia, the brothers encouraged him and wrote to the disciples there to welcome him. On his arrival, he was a great help to those who by grace had believed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 18, 28, 'For he powerfully refuted the Jews in public debate, proving from the Scriptures that Jesus is the Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 1, 'While Apollos was at Corinth, Paul passed through the interior and came to Ephesus. There he found some disciples'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 2, 'and asked them, “Did you receive the Holy Spirit when you became believers?” “No,” they answered, “we have not even heard that there is a Holy Spirit.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 3, '“Into what, then, were you baptized?” Paul asked. “The baptism of John,” they replied.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 4, 'Paul explained: “John’s baptism was a baptism of repentance. He told the people to believe in the One coming after him, that is, in Jesus.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 5, 'On hearing this, they were baptized into the name of the Lord Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 6, 'And when Paul laid his hands on them, the Holy Spirit came upon them, and they spoke in tongues and prophesied.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 7, 'There were about twelve men in all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 8, 'Then Paul went into the synagogue and spoke boldly there for three months, arguing persuasively about the kingdom of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 9, 'But when some of them stubbornly refused to believe and publicly maligned the Way, Paul took his disciples and left the synagogue to conduct daily discussions in the lecture hall of Tyrannus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 10, 'This continued for two years, so that everyone who lived in the province of Asia, Jews and Greeks alike, heard the word of the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 11, 'God did extraordinary miracles through the hands of Paul,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 12, 'so that even handkerchiefs and aprons that had touched him were taken to the sick, and the diseases and evil spirits left them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 13, 'Now there were some itinerant Jewish exorcists who tried to invoke the name of the Lord Jesus over those with evil spirits. They would say, “I bind you by Jesus, whom Paul proclaims.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 14, 'Seven sons of Sceva, a Jewish chief priest, were doing this.');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 15, 'Eventually, one of the evil spirits answered them, “Jesus I know, and I know about Paul, but who are you?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 16, 'Then the man with the evil spirit jumped on them and overpowered them all. The attack was so violent that they ran out of the house naked and wounded.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 17, 'This became known to all the Jews and Greeks living in Ephesus, and fear came over all of them. So the name of the Lord Jesus was held in high honor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 18, 'Many who had believed now came forward, confessing and disclosing their deeds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 19, 'And a number of those who had practiced magic arts brought their books and burned them in front of everyone. When the value of the books was calculated, the total came to fifty thousand drachmas.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 20, 'So the word of the Lord powerfully continued to spread and prevail.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 21, 'After these things had happened, Paul resolved in the Spirit to go to Jerusalem after he had passed through Macedonia and Achaia. “After I have been there,” he said, “I must see Rome as well.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 22, 'He sent two of his helpers, Timothy and Erastus, to Macedonia, while he stayed for a time in the province of Asia.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 23, 'About that time there arose a great disturbance about the Way.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 24, 'It began with a silversmith named Demetrius who made silver shrines of Artemis, bringing much business to the craftsmen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 25, 'Demetrius assembled the craftsmen, along with the workmen in related trades. “Men,” he said, “you know that this business is our source of prosperity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 26, 'And you can see and hear that not only in Ephesus, but in nearly the whole province of Asia, Paul has persuaded a great number of people to turn away. He says that man-made gods are no gods at all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 27, 'There is danger not only that our business will fall into disrepute, but also that the temple of the great goddess Artemis will be discredited and her majesty deposed—she who is worshiped by all the province of Asia and the whole world.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 28, 'When the men heard this, they were enraged and began shouting, “Great is Artemis of the Ephesians!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 29, 'Soon the whole city was in disarray. They rushed together into the theatre, dragging with them Gaius and Aristarchus, Paul’s traveling companions from Macedonia.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 30, 'Paul wanted to go before the assembly, but the disciples would not allow him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 31, 'Even some of Paul’s friends who were officials of the province of Asia sent word to him, begging him not to venture into the theatre.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 32, 'Meanwhile the assembly was in turmoil. Some were shouting one thing and some another, and most of them did not even know why they were there.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 33, 'The Jews in the crowd pushed Alexander forward to explain himself, and he motioned for silence so he could make his defense to the people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 34, 'But when they realized that he was a Jew, they all shouted in unison for about two hours: “Great is Artemis of the Ephesians!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 35, 'Finally the city clerk quieted the crowd and declared, “Men of Ephesus, doesn’t everyone know that the city of Ephesus is guardian of the temple of the great Artemis and of her image, which fell from heaven?'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 36, 'Since these things are undeniable, you ought to be calm and not do anything rash.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 37, 'For you have brought these men here, though they have neither robbed our temple nor blasphemed our goddess.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 38, 'So if Demetrius and his fellow craftsmen have a complaint against anyone, the courts are open and proconsuls are available. Let them bring charges against one another there.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 39, 'But if you are seeking anything beyond this, it must be settled in a legal assembly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 40, 'For we are in jeopardy of being charged with rioting for today’s events, and we have no justification to account for this commotion.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 19, 41, 'After he had said this, he dismissed the assembly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 1, 'When the uproar had ended, Paul sent for the disciples. And after encouraging them, he said goodbye to them and left for Macedonia.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 2, 'After traveling through that area and speaking many words of encouragement, he arrived in Greece,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 3, 'where he stayed three months. And when the Jews formed a plot against him as he was about to sail for Syria, he decided to go back through Macedonia.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 4, 'Paul was accompanied by Sopater son of Pyrrhus from Berea, Aristarchus and Secundus from Thessalonica, Gaius from Derbe, Timothy, and Tychicus and Trophimus from the province of Asia.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 5, 'These men went on ahead and waited for us in Troas.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 6, 'And after the Feast of Unleavened Bread, we sailed from Philippi, and five days later we rejoined them in Troas, where we stayed seven days.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 7, 'On the first day of the week we came together to break bread. Since Paul was ready to leave the next day, he talked to them and kept on speaking until midnight.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 8, 'Now there were many lamps in the upper room where we were gathered.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 9, 'And a certain young man named Eutychus, seated in the window, was sinking into a deep sleep as Paul talked on and on. When he was sound asleep, he fell from the third story and was picked up dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 10, 'But Paul went down, threw himself on the young man, and embraced him. “Do not be alarmed!” he said. “He is still alive!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 11, 'Then Paul went back upstairs, broke bread, and ate. And after speaking until daybreak, he departed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 12, 'And the people were greatly relieved to take the boy home alive.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 13, 'We went on ahead to the ship and sailed to Assos, where we were to take Paul aboard. He had arranged this because he was going there on foot.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 14, 'And when he met us at Assos, we took him aboard and went on to Mitylene.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 15, 'Sailing on from there, we arrived the next day opposite Chios. The day after that we arrived at Samos, and on the following day we came to Miletus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 16, 'Paul had decided to sail past Ephesus to avoid spending time in the province of Asia, because he was in a hurry to reach Jerusalem, if possible, by the day of Pentecost.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 17, 'From Miletus, Paul sent to Ephesus for the elders of the church.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 18, 'When they came to him, he said, “You know how I lived the whole time I was with you, from the first day I arrived in the province of Asia.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 19, 'I served the Lord with great humility and with tears, especially in the trials that came upon me through the plots of the Jews.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 20, 'I did not shrink back from declaring anything that was helpful to you as I taught you publicly and from house to house,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 21, 'testifying to Jews and Greeks alike about repentance to God and faith in our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 22, 'And now, compelled by the Spirit, I am going to Jerusalem, not knowing what will happen to me there.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 23, 'I only know that in town after town the Holy Spirit warns me that chains and afflictions await me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 24, 'But I consider my life of no value to me, if only I may finish my course and complete the ministry I have received from the Lord Jesus—the ministry of testifying to the good news of God’s grace.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 25, 'Now I know that none of you among whom I have preached the kingdom will see my face again.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 26, 'Therefore I testify to you this day that I am innocent of the blood of all men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 27, 'For I did not shrink back from declaring to you the whole will of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 28, 'Keep watch over yourselves and the entire flock of which the Holy Spirit has made you overseers. Be shepherds of the church of God, which He purchased with His own blood.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 29, 'I know that after my departure, savage wolves will come in among you and will not spare the flock.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 30, 'Even from your own number, men will rise up and distort the truth to draw away disciples after them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 31, 'Therefore be alert and remember that for three years I never stopped warning each of you night and day with tears.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 32, 'And now I commit you to God and to the word of His grace, which can build you up and give you an inheritance among all who are sanctified.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 33, 'I have not coveted anyone’s silver or gold or clothing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 34, 'You yourselves know that these hands of mine have ministered to my own needs and those of my companions.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 35, 'In everything, I showed you that by this kind of hard work we must help the weak, remembering the words of the Lord Jesus Himself: ‘It is more blessed to give than to receive.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 36, 'When Paul had said this, he knelt down with all of them and prayed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 37, 'They all wept openly as they embraced Paul and kissed him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 20, 38, 'They were especially grieved by his statement that they would never see his face again. Then they accompanied him to the ship.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 1, 'After we had torn ourselves away from them, we sailed directly to Cos, and the next day on to Rhodes, and from there to Patara.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 2, 'Finding a ship crossing over to Phoenicia, we boarded it and set sail.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 3, 'After sighting Cyprus and passing south of it, we sailed on to Syria and landed at Tyre, where the ship was to unload its cargo.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 4, 'We sought out the disciples in Tyre and stayed with them seven days. Through the Spirit they kept telling Paul not to go up to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 5, 'But when our time there had ended, we set out on our journey. All the disciples, with their wives and children, accompanied us out of the city and knelt down on the beach to pray with us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 6, 'And after we had said our farewells, we went aboard the ship, and they returned home.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 7, 'When we had finished our voyage from Tyre, we landed at Ptolemais, where we greeted the brothers and stayed with them for a day.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 8, 'Leaving the next day, we went on to Caesarea and stayed at the home of Philip the evangelist, who was one of the Seven.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 9, 'He had four unmarried daughters who prophesied.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 10, 'After we had been there several days, a prophet named Agabus came down from Judea.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 11, 'Coming over to us, he took Paul’s belt, bound his own feet and hands, and said, “The Holy Spirit says: ‘In this way the Jews of Jerusalem will bind the owner of this belt and hand him over to the Gentiles.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 12, 'When we heard this, we and the people there pleaded with Paul not to go up to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 13, 'Then Paul answered, “Why are you weeping and breaking my heart? I am ready not only to be bound, but also to die in Jerusalem for the name of the Lord Jesus.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 14, 'When he would not be dissuaded, we fell silent and said, “The Lord’s will be done.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 15, 'After these days, we packed up and went on to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 16, 'Some of the disciples from Caesarea accompanied us, and they took us to stay at the home of Mnason the Cypriot, an early disciple.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 17, 'When we arrived in Jerusalem, the brothers welcomed us joyfully.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 18, 'The next day Paul went in with us to see James, and all the elders were present.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 19, 'Paul greeted them and recounted one by one the things that God had done among the Gentiles through his ministry.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 20, 'When they heard this, they glorified God. Then they said to Paul, “You see, brother, how many thousands of Jews have believed, and all of them are zealous for the law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 21, 'But they are under the impression that you teach all the Jews who live among the Gentiles to forsake Moses, telling them not to circumcise their children or observe our customs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 22, 'What then should we do? They will certainly hear that you have come.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 23, 'Therefore do what we advise you. There are four men with us who have taken a vow.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 24, 'Take these men, purify yourself along with them, and pay their expenses so they can have their heads shaved. Then everyone will know that there is no truth to these rumors about you, but that you also live in obedience to the law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 25, 'As for the Gentile believers, we have written to them our decision that they must abstain from food sacrificed to idols, from blood, from the meat of strangled animals, and from sexual immorality.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 26, 'So the next day Paul took the men and purified himself along with them. Then he entered the temple to give notice of the date when their purification would be complete and the offering would be made for each of them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 27, 'When the seven days were almost over, some Jews from the province of Asia saw Paul at the temple. They stirred up the whole crowd and seized him,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 28, 'crying out, “Men of Israel, help us! This is the man who teaches everywhere against our people and against our law and against this place. Furthermore, he has brought Greeks into the temple and defiled this holy place.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 29, 'For they had previously seen Trophimus the Ephesian with him in the city, and they assumed that Paul had brought him into the temple.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 30, 'The whole city was stirred up, and the people rushed together. They seized Paul and dragged him out of the temple, and at once the gates were shut.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 31, 'While they were trying to kill him, the commander of the Roman regiment received a report that all Jerusalem was in turmoil.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 32, 'Immediately he took some soldiers and centurions and ran down to the crowd. When the people saw the commander and the soldiers, they stopped beating Paul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 33, 'The commander came up and arrested Paul, ordering that he be bound with two chains. Then he asked who he was and what he had done.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 34, 'Some in the crowd were shouting one thing, and some another. And since the commander could not get at the truth because of the uproar, he ordered that Paul be brought into the barracks.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 35, 'When Paul reached the steps, he had to be carried by the soldiers because of the violence of the mob.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 36, 'For the crowd that followed him kept shouting, “Away with him!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 37, 'As they were about to take Paul into the barracks, he asked the commander, “May I say something to you?” “Do you speak Greek?” he replied.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 38, '“Aren’t you the Egyptian who incited a rebellion some time ago and led four thousand members of the ‘Assassins’ into the wilderness?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 39, 'But Paul answered, “I am a Jew from Tarsus in Cilicia, a citizen of no ordinary city. Now I beg you to allow me to speak to the people.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 21, 40, 'Having received permission, Paul stood on the steps and motioned to the crowd. A great hush came over the crowd, and he addressed them in Hebrew:'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 1, '“Brothers and fathers, listen now to my defense before you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 2, 'When they heard him speak to them in Hebrew, they became even more silent. Then Paul declared,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 3, '“I am a Jew, born in Tarsus of Cilicia, but raised in this city. I was educated at the feet of Gamaliel in strict conformity to the law of our fathers. I am just as zealous for God as any of you here today.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 4, 'I persecuted this Way even to the death, detaining both men and women and throwing them into prison,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 5, 'as the high priest and the whole Council can testify about me. I even obtained letters from them to their brothers in Damascus, and I was on my way to apprehend these people and bring them to Jerusalem to be punished.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 6, 'About noon as I was approaching Damascus, suddenly a bright light from heaven flashed around me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 7, 'I fell to the ground and heard a voice say to me, ‘Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me?’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 8, '‘Who are You, Lord?’ I asked. ‘I am Jesus of Nazareth, whom you are persecuting,’ He replied.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 9, 'My companions saw the light, but they could not understand the voice of the One speaking to me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 10, 'Then I asked, ‘What should I do, Lord?’ ‘Get up and go into Damascus,’ He told me. ‘There you will be told all that you have been appointed to do.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 11, 'Because the brilliance of the light had blinded me, my companions led me by the hand into Damascus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 12, 'There a man named Ananias, a devout observer of the law who was highly regarded by all the Jews living there,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 13, 'came and stood beside me. ‘Brother Saul,’ he said, ‘receive your sight.’ And at that moment I could see him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 14, 'Then he said, ‘The God of our fathers has appointed you to know His will, and to see the Righteous One, and to hear His voice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 15, 'You will be His witness to everyone of what you have seen and heard.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 16, 'And now what are you waiting for? Get up, be baptized, and wash your sins away, calling on His name.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 17, 'Later, when I had returned to Jerusalem and was praying at the temple, I fell into a trance'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 18, 'and saw the Lord saying to me, ‘Hurry! Leave Jerusalem quickly, because the people here will not accept your testimony about Me.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 19, '‘Lord,’ I answered, ‘they know very well that in one synagogue after another I imprisoned and beat those who believed in You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 20, 'And when the blood of Your witness Stephen was shed, I stood there giving my approval and watching over the garments of those who killed him.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 21, 'Then He said to me, ‘Go! I will send you far away to the Gentiles.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 22, 'The crowd listened to Paul until he made this statement. Then they lifted up their voices and shouted, “Rid the earth of him! He is not fit to live!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 23, 'As they were shouting and throwing off their cloaks and tossing dust into the air,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 24, 'the commander ordered that Paul be brought into the barracks. He directed that Paul be flogged and interrogated to determine the reason for this outcry against him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 25, 'But as they stretched him out to strap him down, Paul said to the centurion standing there, “Is it lawful for you to flog a Roman citizen without a trial?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 26, 'On hearing this, the centurion went and reported it to the commander. “What are you going to do?” he said. “This man is a Roman citizen.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 27, 'The commander went to Paul and asked, “Tell me, are you a Roman citizen?” “Yes,” he answered.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 28, '“I paid a high price for my citizenship,” said the commander. “But I was born a citizen,” Paul replied.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 29, 'Then those who were about to interrogate Paul stepped back, and the commander himself was alarmed when he realized that he had put a Roman citizen in chains.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 22, 30, 'The next day the commander, wanting to learn the real reason Paul was accused by the Jews, released him and ordered the chief priests and the whole Sanhedrin to assemble. Then he brought Paul down and had him stand before them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 1, 'Paul looked directly at the Sanhedrin and said, “Brothers, I have conducted myself before God in all good conscience to this day.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 2, 'At this, the high priest Ananias ordered those standing near Paul to strike him on the mouth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 3, 'Then Paul said to him, “God will strike you, you whitewashed wall! You sit here to judge me according to the law, yet you yourself violate the law by commanding that I be struck.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 4, 'But those standing nearby said, “How dare you insult the high priest of God!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 5, '“Brothers,” Paul replied, “I was not aware that he was the high priest, for it is written: ‘Do not speak evil about the ruler of your people.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 6, 'Then Paul, knowing that some of them were Sadducees and others Pharisees, called out in the Sanhedrin, “Brothers, I am a Pharisee, the son of a Pharisee. It is because of my hope in the resurrection of the dead that I am on trial.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 7, 'As soon as he had said this, a dispute broke out between the Pharisees and Sadducees, and the assembly was divided.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 8, 'For the Sadducees say that there is neither a resurrection, nor angels, nor spirits, but the Pharisees acknowledge them all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 9, 'A great clamor arose, and some scribes from the party of the Pharisees got up and contended sharply, “We find nothing wrong with this man. What if a spirit or an angel has spoken to him?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 10, 'The dispute grew so violent that the commander was afraid they would tear Paul to pieces. He ordered the soldiers to go down and remove him by force and bring him into the barracks.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 11, 'The following night the Lord stood near Paul and said, “Take courage! As you have testified about Me in Jerusalem, so also you must testify in Rome.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 12, 'When daylight came, the Jews formed a conspiracy and bound themselves with an oath not to eat or drink until they had killed Paul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 13, 'More than forty of them were involved in this plot.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 14, 'They went to the chief priests and elders and said, “We have bound ourselves with a solemn oath not to eat anything until we have killed Paul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 15, 'Now then, you and the Sanhedrin petition the commander to bring him down to you on the pretext of examining his case more carefully. We are ready to kill him on the way.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 16, 'But when the son of Paul’s sister heard about the plot, he went into the barracks and told Paul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 17, 'Then Paul called one of the centurions and said, “Take this young man to the commander; he has something to tell him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 18, 'So the centurion took him to the commander and said, “Paul the prisoner sent and asked me to bring this young man to you. He has something to tell you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 19, 'The commander took the young man by the hand, drew him aside, and asked, “What do you need to tell me?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 20, 'He answered, “The Jews have agreed to ask you to bring Paul to the Sanhedrin tomorrow on the pretext of acquiring more information about him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 21, 'Do not let them persuade you, because more than forty men are waiting to ambush him. They have bound themselves with an oath not to eat or drink until they have killed him; they are ready now, awaiting your consent.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 22, 'So the commander dismissed the young man and instructed him, “Do not tell anyone that you have reported this to me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 23, 'Then he called two of his centurions and said, “Prepare two hundred soldiers, seventy horsemen, and two hundred spearmen to go to Caesarea in the third hour of the night.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 24, 'Provide mounts for Paul to take him safely to Governor Felix.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 25, 'And he wrote the following letter:'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 26, 'Claudius Lysias, To His Excellency, Governor Felix: Greetings.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 27, 'This man was seized by the Jews, and they were about to kill him when I came with my troops to rescue him. For I had learned that he is a Roman citizen,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 28, 'and since I wanted to understand their charges against him, I brought him down to their Sanhedrin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 29, 'I found that the accusation involved questions about their own law, but there was no charge worthy of death or imprisonment.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 30, 'When I was informed that there was a plot against the man, I sent him to you at once. I also instructed his accusers to present their case against him before you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 31, 'So the soldiers followed their orders and brought Paul by night to Antipatris.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 32, 'The next day they returned to the barracks and let the horsemen go on with him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 33, 'When the horsemen arrived in Caesarea, they delivered the letter to the governor and presented Paul to him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 34, 'The governor read the letter and asked what province Paul was from. Learning that he was from Cilicia,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 23, 35, 'he said, “I will hear your case when your accusers arrive.” Then he ordered that Paul be kept under guard in Herod’s Praetorium.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 1, 'Five days later the high priest Ananias came down with some elders and a lawyer named Tertullus, who presented to the governor their case against Paul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 2, 'When Paul had been called in, Tertullus opened the prosecution: “Because of you, we have enjoyed a lasting peace, and your foresight has brought improvements to this nation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 3, 'In every way and everywhere, most excellent Felix, we acknowledge this with all gratitude.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 4, 'But in order not to burden you any further, I beg your indulgence to hear us briefly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 5, 'We have found this man to be a pestilence, stirring up dissension among the Jews all over the world. He is a ringleader of the sect of the Nazarenes,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 6, 'and he even tried to desecrate the temple; so we seized him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 7, ''),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 8, 'By examining him yourself, you will be able to learn the truth about all our charges against him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 9, 'The Jews concurred, asserting that these charges were true.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 10, 'When the governor motioned for Paul to speak, he began his response: “Knowing that you have been a judge over this nation for many years, I gladly make my defense.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 11, 'You can verify for yourself that no more than twelve days ago I went up to Jerusalem to worship.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 12, 'Yet my accusers did not find me debating with anyone in the temple or riling up a crowd in the synagogues or in the city.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 13, 'Nor can they prove to you any of their charges against me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 14, 'I do confess to you, however, that I worship the God of our fathers according to the Way, which they call a sect. I believe everything that is laid down by the Law and written in the Prophets,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 15, 'and I have the same hope in God that they themselves cherish, that there will be a resurrection of both the righteous and the wicked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 16, 'In this hope, I strive always to maintain a clear conscience before God and man.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 17, 'After several years, then, I returned to Jerusalem to bring alms to my people and to present offerings.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 18, 'At the time they found me in the temple, I was ceremonially clean and was not inciting a crowd or an uproar. But there are some Jews from the province of Asia'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 19, 'who ought to appear before you and bring charges, if they have anything against me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 20, 'Otherwise, let these men state for themselves any crime they found in me when I stood before the Sanhedrin,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 21, 'unless it was this one thing I called out as I stood in their presence: ‘It is concerning the resurrection of the dead that I am on trial before you today.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 22, 'Then Felix, who was well informed about the Way, adjourned the hearing and said, “When Lysias the commander comes, I will decide your case.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 23, 'He ordered the centurion to keep Paul under guard, but to allow him some freedom and permit his friends to minister to his needs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 24, 'After several days, Felix returned with his wife Drusilla, who was a Jewess. He sent for Paul and listened to him speak about faith in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 25, 'As Paul expounded on righteousness, self-control, and the coming judgment, Felix became frightened and said, “You may go for now. When I find the time, I will call for you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 26, 'At the same time, he was hoping that Paul would offer him a bribe. So he sent for Paul frequently and talked with him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 24, 27, 'After two years had passed, Felix was succeeded by Porcius Festus. And wishing to do the Jews a favor, Felix left Paul in prison.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 1, 'Three days after his arrival in the province, Festus went up from Caesarea to Jerusalem,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 2, 'where the chief priests and Jewish leaders presented their case against Paul. They urged Festus'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 3, 'to grant them a concession against Paul by summoning him to Jerusalem, because they were preparing an ambush to kill him along the way.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 4, 'But Festus replied, “Paul is being held in Caesarea, and I myself am going there soon.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 5, 'So if this man has done anything wrong, let some of your leaders come down with me and accuse him there.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 6, 'After spending no more than eight or ten days with them, Festus went down to Caesarea. The next day he sat on the judgment seat and ordered that Paul be brought in.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 7, 'When Paul arrived, the Jews who had come down from Jerusalem stood around him, bringing many serious charges that they could not prove.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 8, 'Then Paul made his defense: “I have committed no offense against the law of the Jews or against the temple or against Caesar.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 9, 'But Festus, wishing to do the Jews a favor, said to Paul, “Are you willing to go up to Jerusalem to stand trial before me on these charges?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 10, 'Paul replied, “I am standing before the judgment seat of Caesar, where I ought to be tried. I have done nothing wrong to the Jews, as you yourself know very well.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 11, 'If, however, I am guilty of anything worthy of death, I do not refuse to die. But if there is no truth to their accusations against me, no one has the right to hand me over to them. I appeal to Caesar!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 12, 'Then Festus conferred with his council and replied, “You have appealed to Caesar. To Caesar you will go!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 13, 'After several days had passed, King Agrippa and Bernice came down to Caesarea to pay their respects to Festus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 14, 'Since they were staying several days, Festus laid out Paul’s case before the king: “There is a certain man whom Felix left in prison.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 15, 'While I was in Jerusalem, the chief priests and elders of the Jews presented their case and requested a judgment against him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 16, 'I told them that it is not the Roman custom to hand a man over before he has had an opportunity to face his accusers and defend himself against their charges.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 17, 'So when they came here with me, I did not delay. The next day I sat on the judgment seat and ordered that the man be brought in.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 18, 'But when his accusers rose to speak, they did not charge him with any of the crimes I had expected.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 19, 'They only had some contentions with him regarding their own religion and a certain Jesus who had died, but whom Paul affirmed to be alive.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 20, 'Since I was at a loss as to how to investigate these matters, I asked if he was willing to go to Jerusalem and be tried there on these charges.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 21, 'But when Paul appealed to be held over for the decision of the Emperor, I ordered that he be held until I could send him to Caesar.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 22, 'Then Agrippa said to Festus, “I would like to hear this man myself.” “Tomorrow you will hear him,” Festus declared.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 23, 'The next day Agrippa and Bernice came with great pomp and entered the auditorium, along with the commanders and leading men of the city. And Festus ordered that Paul be brought in.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 24, 'Then Festus said, “King Agrippa and all who are present with us, you see this man. The whole Jewish community has petitioned me about him, both here and in Jerusalem, crying out that he ought not to live any longer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 25, 'But I found he had done nothing worthy of death, and since he has now appealed to the Emperor, I decided to send him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 26, 'I have nothing definite to write to our sovereign one about him. Therefore I have brought him before all of you, and especially before you, King Agrippa, so that after this inquiry I may have something to write.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 25, 27, 'For it seems unreasonable to me to send on a prisoner without specifying the charges against him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 1, 'Agrippa said to Paul, “You have permission to speak for yourself.” Then Paul stretched out his hand and began his defense:'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 2, '“King Agrippa, I consider myself fortunate to stand before you today to defend myself against all the accusations of the Jews,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 3, 'especially since you are acquainted with all the Jewish customs and controversies. I beg you, therefore, to listen to me patiently.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 4, 'Surely all the Jews know how I have lived from the earliest days of my youth, among my own people and in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 5, 'They have known me for a long time and can testify, if they are willing, that I lived as a Pharisee, adhering to the strictest sect of our religion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 6, 'And now I stand on trial because of my hope in the promise that God made to our fathers,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 7, 'the promise our twelve tribes are hoping to realize as they earnestly serve God day and night. It is because of this hope, O king, that I am accused by the Jews.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 8, 'Why would any of you consider it incredible that God raises the dead?'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 9, 'So then, I too was convinced that I ought to do all I could to oppose the name of Jesus of Nazareth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 10, 'And that is what I did in Jerusalem. With authority from the chief priests I put many of the saints in prison, and when they were condemned to death, I cast my vote against them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 11, 'I frequently had them punished in the synagogues, and I tried to make them blaspheme. In my raging fury against them, I even went to foreign cities to persecute them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 12, 'In this pursuit I was on my way to Damascus with the authority and commission of the chief priests.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 13, 'About noon, O king, as I was on the road, I saw a light from heaven, brighter than the sun, shining around me and my companions.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 14, 'We all fell to the ground, and I heard a voice say to me in Hebrew, ‘Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me? It is hard for you to kick against the goads.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 15, '‘Who are You, Lord?’ I asked. ‘I am Jesus, whom you are persecuting,’ the Lord replied.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 16, '‘But get up and stand on your feet. For I have appeared to you to appoint you as a servant and as a witness of what you have seen from Me and what I will show you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 17, 'I will rescue you from your own people and from the Gentiles. I am sending you to them'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 18, 'to open their eyes, so that they may turn from darkness to light and from the power of Satan to God, that they may receive forgiveness of sins and an inheritance among those sanctified by faith in Me.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 19, 'So then, King Agrippa, I was not disobedient to the heavenly vision.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 20, 'First to those in Damascus and Jerusalem, then to everyone in the region of Judea, and then to the Gentiles, I declared that they should repent and turn to God, performing deeds worthy of their repentance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 21, 'For this reason the Jews seized me in the temple courts and tried to kill me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 22, 'But I have had God’s help to this day, and I stand here to testify to small and great alike. I am saying nothing beyond what the prophets and Moses said would happen:'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 23, 'that the Christ would suffer, and as the first to rise from the dead, would proclaim light to our people and to the Gentiles.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 24, 'At this stage of Paul’s defense, Festus exclaimed in a loud voice, “You are insane, Paul! Your great learning is driving you to madness!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 25, 'But Paul answered, “I am not insane, most excellent Festus; I am speaking words of truth and sobriety.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 26, 'For the king knows about these matters, and I can speak freely to him. I am confident that none of this has escaped his notice, because it was not done in a corner.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 27, 'King Agrippa, do you believe the prophets? I know you do.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 28, 'Then Agrippa said to Paul, “Can you persuade me in such a short time to become a Christian?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 29, '“Short time or long,” Paul replied, “I wish to God that not only you but all who hear me this day may become what I am, except for these chains.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 30, 'Then the king and the governor rose, along with Bernice and those seated with them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 31, 'On their way out, they said to one another, “This man has done nothing worthy of death or imprisonment.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 26, 32, 'And Agrippa said to Festus, “This man could have been released if he had not appealed to Caesar.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 1, 'When it was decided that we would sail for Italy, Paul and some other prisoners were handed over to a centurion named Julius, who belonged to the Imperial Regiment.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 2, 'We boarded an Adramyttian ship about to sail for ports along the coast of Asia, and we put out to sea. Aristarchus, a Macedonian from Thessalonica, was with us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 3, 'The next day we landed at Sidon, and Julius treated Paul with consideration, allowing him to visit his friends and receive their care.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 4, 'After putting out from there, we sailed to the lee of Cyprus because the winds were against us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 5, 'And when we had sailed across the open sea off the coast of Cilicia and Pamphylia, we came to Myra in Lycia.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 6, 'There the centurion found an Alexandrian ship sailing for Italy and put us on board.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 7, 'After sailing slowly for many days, we arrived off Cnidus. When the wind impeded us, we sailed to the lee of Crete, opposite Salmone.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 8, 'After we had moved along the coast with difficulty, we came to a place called Fair Havens, near the town of Lasea.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 9, 'By now much time had passed, and the voyage had already become dangerous because it was after the Fast. So Paul advised them,'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 10, '“Men, I can see that our voyage will be filled with disaster and great loss, not only to ship and cargo, but to our own lives as well.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 11, 'But contrary to Paul’s advice, the centurion was persuaded by the pilot and by the owner of the ship.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 12, 'Since the harbor was unsuitable to winter in, the majority decided to sail on, if somehow they could reach Phoenix to winter there. Phoenix was a harbor in Crete facing both southwest and northwest.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 13, 'When a gentle south wind began to blow, they thought they had their opportunity. So they weighed anchor and sailed along, hugging the coast of Crete.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 14, 'But it was not long before a cyclone called the Northeaster swept down across the island.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 15, 'Unable to head into the wind, the ship was caught up. So we gave way and let ourselves be driven along.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 16, 'Passing to the lee of a small island called Cauda, we barely managed to secure the lifeboat.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 17, 'After hoisting it up, the crew used ropes to undergird the ship. And fearing that they would run aground on the sandbars of Syrtis, they lowered the sea anchor and were driven along.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 18, 'We were tossed so violently that the next day the men began to jettison the cargo.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 19, 'On the third day, they threw the ship’s tackle overboard with their own hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 20, 'When neither sun nor stars appeared for many days and the great storm continued to batter us, we abandoned all hope of being saved.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 21, 'After the men had gone a long time without food, Paul stood up among them and said, “Men, you should have followed my advice not to sail from Crete. Then you would have averted this disaster and loss.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 22, 'But now I urge you to keep up your courage, because you will not experience any loss of life, but only of the ship.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 23, 'For just last night an angel of God, whose I am and whom I serve, stood beside me'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 24, 'and said, ‘Do not be afraid, Paul; you must stand before Caesar. And look, God has granted you the lives of all who sail with you.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 25, 'So take courage, men, for I believe God that it will happen just as He told me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 26, 'However, we must run aground on some island.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 27, 'On the fourteenth night we were still being driven across the Adriatic Sea. About midnight the sailors sensed they were approaching land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 28, 'They took soundings and found that the water was twenty fathoms deep. Going a little farther, they took another set of soundings that read fifteen fathoms.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 29, 'Fearing that we would run aground on the rocks, they dropped four anchors from the stern and prayed for daybreak.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 30, 'Meanwhile, the sailors attempted to escape from the ship. Pretending to lower anchors from the bow, they let the lifeboat down into the sea.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 31, 'But Paul said to the centurion and the soldiers, “Unless these men remain with the ship, you cannot be saved.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 32, 'So the soldiers cut the ropes to the lifeboat and set it adrift.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 33, 'Right up to daybreak, Paul kept urging them all to eat: “Today is your fourteenth day in constant suspense, without taking any food.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 34, 'So for your own preservation, I urge you to eat something, because not a single hair of your head will be lost.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 35, 'After he had said this, Paul took bread and gave thanks to God in front of them all. Then he broke it and began to eat.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 36, 'They were all encouraged and took some food themselves.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 37, 'In all, there were 276 of us on board.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 38, 'After the men had eaten their fill, they lightened the ship by throwing the grain into the sea.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 39, 'When daylight came, they did not recognize the land, but they sighted a bay with a sandy beach, where they decided to run the ship aground if they could.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 40, 'Cutting away the anchors, they left them in the sea as they loosened the ropes that held the rudders. Then they hoisted the foresail to the wind and made for the beach.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 41, 'But the vessel struck a sandbar and ran aground. The bow stuck fast and would not move, and the stern was being broken up by the pounding of the waves.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 42, 'The soldiers planned to kill the prisoners so none of them could swim to freedom.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 43, 'But the centurion, wanting to spare Paul’s life, thwarted their plan. He commanded those who could swim to jump overboard first and get to land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 27, 44, 'The rest were to follow on planks and various parts of the ship. In this way everyone was brought safely to land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 1, 'Once we were safely ashore, we learned that the island was called Malta.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 2, 'The islanders showed us extraordinary kindness. They kindled a fire and welcomed all of us because it was raining and cold.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 3, 'Paul gathered a bundle of sticks, and as he laid them on the fire, a viper, driven out by the heat, fastened itself to his hand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 4, 'When the islanders saw the creature hanging from his hand, they said to one another, “Surely this man is a murderer. Although he was saved from the sea, Justice has not allowed him to live.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 5, 'But Paul shook the creature off into the fire and suffered no ill effects.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 6, 'The islanders were expecting him to swell up or suddenly drop dead. But after waiting a long time and seeing nothing unusual happen to him, they changed their minds and said he was a god.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 7, 'Nearby stood an estate belonging to Publius, the chief official of the island. He welcomed us and entertained us hospitably for three days.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 8, 'The father of Publius was sick in bed, suffering from fever and dysentery. Paul went in to see him, and after praying and placing his hands on him, he healed the man.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 9, 'After this had happened, the rest of the sick on the island came and were cured as well.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 10, 'The islanders honored us in many ways and supplied our needs when we were ready to sail.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 11, 'After three months we set sail in an Alexandrian ship that had wintered in the island. It had the Twin Brothers as a figurehead.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 12, 'Putting in at Syracuse, we stayed there three days.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 13, 'From there we weighed anchor and came to Rhegium. After one day, a south wind came up, and on the second day we arrived at Puteoli.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 14, 'There we found some brothers who invited us to spend the week with them. And so we came to Rome.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 15, 'The brothers there had heard about us and traveled as far as the Forum of Appius and the Three Taverns to meet us. When Paul saw them, he was encouraged and gave thanks to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 16, 'When we arrived in Rome, Paul was permitted to stay by himself, with a soldier to guard him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 17, 'After three days, he called together the leaders of the Jews. When they had gathered, he said to them, “Brothers, although I have done nothing against our people or the customs of our fathers, I was taken prisoner in Jerusalem and handed over to the Romans.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 18, 'They examined me and wanted to release me, because there was no basis for a death sentence against me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 19, 'But when the Jews objected, I was compelled to appeal to Caesar, even though I have no charge to bring against my nation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 20, 'So for this reason I have called to see you and speak with you. It is because of the hope of Israel that I am bound with this chain.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 21, 'The leaders replied, “We have not received any letters about you from Judea, nor have any of the brothers from there reported or even mentioned anything bad about you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 22, 'But we consider your views worth hearing, because we know that people everywhere are speaking against this sect.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 23, 'So they set a day to meet with Paul, and many people came to the place he was staying. He expounded to them from morning to evening, testifying about the kingdom of God and persuading them about Jesus from the Law of Moses and the Prophets.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 24, 'Some of them were convinced by what he said, but others refused to believe.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 25, 'They disagreed among themselves and began to leave after Paul had made this final statement: “The Holy Spirit was right when He spoke to your fathers through Isaiah the prophet:'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 26, '‘Go to this people and say, “You will be ever hearing but never understanding; you will be ever seeing but never perceiving.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 27, 'For this people’s heart has grown callous; they hardly hear with their ears, and they have closed their eyes. Otherwise they might see with their eyes, hear with their ears, understand with their hearts, and turn, and I would heal them.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 28, 'Be advised, therefore, that God’s salvation has been sent to the Gentiles, and they will listen!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 29, ''),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 30, 'Paul stayed there two full years in his own rented house, welcoming all who came to visit him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Acts', 44, 28, 31, 'Boldly and freely he proclaimed the kingdom of God and taught about the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 1, 'Paul, a servant of Christ Jesus, called to be an apostle, and set apart for the gospel of God—'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 2, 'the gospel He promised beforehand through His prophets in the Holy Scriptures,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 3, 'regarding His Son, who was a descendant of David according to the flesh,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 4, 'and who through the Spirit of holiness was declared with power to be the Son of God by His resurrection from the dead: Jesus Christ our Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 5, 'Through Him and on behalf of His name, we received grace and apostleship to call all those among the Gentiles to the obedience that comes from faith.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 6, 'And you also are among those who are called to belong to Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 7, 'To all in Rome who are loved by God and called to be saints: Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 8, 'First, I thank my God through Jesus Christ for all of you, because your faith is being proclaimed all over the world.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 9, 'God, whom I serve with my spirit in preaching the gospel of His Son, is my witness how constantly I remember you'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 10, 'in my prayers at all times, asking that now at last by God’s will I may succeed in coming to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 11, 'For I long to see you so that I may impart to you some spiritual gift to strengthen you,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 12, 'that is, that you and I may be mutually encouraged by each other’s faith.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 13, 'I do not want you to be unaware, brothers, how often I planned to come to you (but have been prevented from visiting until now), in order that I might have a harvest among you, just as I have had among the other Gentiles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 14, 'I am obligated both to Greeks and non-Greeks, both to the wise and the foolish.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 15, 'That is why I am so eager to preach the gospel also to you who are in Rome.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 16, 'I am not ashamed of the gospel, because it is the power of God for salvation to everyone who believes, first to the Jew, then to the Greek.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 17, 'For the gospel reveals the righteousness of God that comes by faith from start to finish, just as it is written: “The righteous will live by faith.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 18, 'The wrath of God is being revealed from heaven against all the godlessness and wickedness of men who suppress the truth by their wickedness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 19, 'For what may be known about God is plain to them, because God has made it plain to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 20, 'For since the creation of the world God’s invisible qualities, His eternal power and divine nature, have been clearly seen, being understood from His workmanship, so that men are without excuse.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 21, 'For although they knew God, they neither glorified Him as God nor gave thanks to Him, but they became futile in their thinking and darkened in their foolish hearts.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 22, 'Although they claimed to be wise, they became fools,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 23, 'and exchanged the glory of the immortal God for images of mortal man and birds and animals and reptiles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 24, 'Therefore God gave them over in the desires of their hearts to impurity for the dishonoring of their bodies with one another.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 25, 'They exchanged the truth of God for a lie, and worshiped and served the creature rather than the Creator, who is forever worthy of praise! Amen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 26, 'For this reason God gave them over to dishonorable passions. Even their women exchanged natural relations for unnatural ones.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 27, 'Likewise, the men abandoned natural relations with women and burned with lust for one another. Men committed indecent acts with other men, and received in themselves the due penalty for their error.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 28, 'Furthermore, since they did not see fit to acknowledge God, He gave them up to a depraved mind, to do what ought not to be done.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 29, 'They have become filled with every kind of wickedness, evil, greed, and depravity. They are full of envy, murder, strife, deceit, and malice. They are gossips,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 30, 'slanderers, God-haters, insolent, arrogant, and boastful. They invent new forms of evil; they disobey their parents.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 31, 'They are senseless, faithless, heartless, merciless.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 1, 32, 'Although they know God’s righteous decree that those who do such things are worthy of death, they not only continue to do these things, but also approve of those who practice them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 1, 'You, therefore, have no excuse, you who pass judgment on another. For on whatever grounds you judge the other, you are condemning yourself, because you who pass judgment do the same things.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 2, 'And we know that God’s judgment against those who do such things is based on truth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 3, 'So when you, O man, pass judgment on others, yet do the same things, do you think you will escape God’s judgment?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 4, 'Or do you disregard the riches of His kindness, tolerance, and patience, not realizing that God’s kindness leads you to repentance?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 5, 'But because of your hard and unrepentant heart, you are storing up wrath against yourself for the day of wrath, when God’s righteous judgment will be revealed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 6, 'God “will repay each one according to his deeds.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 7, 'To those who by perseverance in doing good seek glory, honor, and immortality, He will give eternal life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 8, 'But for those who are self-seeking and who reject the truth and follow wickedness, there will be wrath and anger.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 9, 'There will be trouble and distress for every human being who does evil, first for the Jew, then for the Greek;'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 10, 'but glory, honor, and peace for everyone who does good, first for the Jew, then for the Greek.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 11, 'For God does not show favoritism.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 12, 'All who sin apart from the law will also perish apart from the law, and all who sin under the law will be judged by the law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 13, 'For it is not the hearers of the law who are righteous before God, but it is the doers of the law who will be declared righteous.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 14, 'Indeed, when Gentiles, who do not have the law, do by nature what the law requires, they are a law to themselves, even though they do not have the law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 15, 'So they show that the work of the law is written on their hearts, their consciences also bearing witness, and their thoughts either accusing or defending them'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 16, 'on the day when God will judge men’s secrets through Christ Jesus, as proclaimed by my gospel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 17, 'Now you, if you call yourself a Jew; if you rely on the law and boast in God;'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 18, 'if you know His will and approve of what is superior because you are instructed by the law;'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 19, 'if you are convinced that you are a guide for the blind, a light for those in darkness,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 20, 'an instructor of the foolish, a teacher of infants, because you have in the law the embodiment of knowledge and truth—'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 21, 'you, then, who teach others, do you not teach yourself? You who preach against stealing, do you steal?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 22, 'You who forbid adultery, do you commit adultery? You who abhor idols, do you rob temples?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 23, 'You who boast in the law, do you dishonor God by breaking the law?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 24, 'As it is written: “God’s name is blasphemed among the Gentiles because of you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 25, 'Circumcision has value if you observe the law, but if you break the law, your circumcision has become uncircumcision.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 26, 'If a man who is not circumcised keeps the requirements of the law, will not his uncircumcision be regarded as circumcision?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 27, 'The one who is physically uncircumcised yet keeps the law will condemn you who, even though you have the written code and circumcision, are a lawbreaker.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 28, 'A man is not a Jew because he is one outwardly, nor is circumcision only outward and physical.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 2, 29, 'No, a man is a Jew because he is one inwardly, and circumcision is a matter of the heart, by the Spirit, not by the written code. Such a man’s praise does not come from men, but from God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 1, 'What, then, is the advantage of being a Jew? Or what is the value of circumcision?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 2, 'Much in every way. First of all, they have been entrusted with the very words of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 3, 'What if some did not have faith? Will their lack of faith nullify God’s faithfulness?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 4, 'Certainly not! Let God be true and every man a liar. As it is written: “So that You may be proved right when You speak and victorious when You judge.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 5, 'But if our unrighteousness highlights the righteousness of God, what shall we say? That God is unjust to inflict His wrath on us? I am speaking in human terms.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 6, 'Certainly not! In that case, how could God judge the world?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 7, 'However, if my falsehood accentuates God’s truthfulness, to the increase of His glory, why am I still condemned as a sinner?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 8, 'Why not say, as some slanderously claim that we say, “Let us do evil that good may result”? Their condemnation is deserved!');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 9, 'What then? Are we any better? Not at all. For we have already made the charge that Jews and Greeks alike are all under sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 10, 'As it is written: “There is no one righteous, not even one.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 11, 'There is no one who understands, no one who seeks God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 12, 'All have turned away, they have together become worthless; there is no one who does good, not even one.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 13, '“Their throats are open graves; their tongues practice deceit.” “The venom of vipers is on their lips.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 14, '“Their mouths are full of cursing and bitterness.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 15, '“Their feet are swift to shed blood;'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 16, 'ruin and misery lie in their wake,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 17, 'and the way of peace they have not known.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 18, '“There is no fear of God before their eyes.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 19, 'Now we know that whatever the law says, it says to those who are under the law, so that every mouth may be silenced and the whole world held accountable to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 20, 'Therefore no one will be justified in His sight by works of the law. For the law merely brings awareness of sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 21, 'But now, apart from the law, the righteousness of God has been revealed, as attested by the Law and the Prophets.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 22, 'And this righteousness from God comes through faith in Jesus Christ to all who believe. There is no distinction,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 23, 'for all have sinned and fall short of the glory of God,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 24, 'and are justified freely by His grace through the redemption that is in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 25, 'God presented Him as the atoning sacrifice through faith in His blood, in order to demonstrate His righteousness, because in His forbearance He had passed over the sins committed beforehand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 26, 'He did this to demonstrate His righteousness at the present time, so as to be just and to justify the one who has faith in Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 27, 'Where, then, is boasting? It is excluded. On what principle? On that of works? No, but on that of faith.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 28, 'For we maintain that a man is justified by faith apart from works of the law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 29, 'Is God the God of Jews only? Is He not the God of Gentiles too? Yes, of Gentiles too,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 30, 'since there is only one God, who will justify the circumcised by faith and the uncircumcised through that same faith.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 3, 31, 'Do we, then, nullify the law by this faith? Certainly not! Instead, we uphold the law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 1, 'What then shall we say that Abraham, our forefather, has discovered?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 2, 'If Abraham was indeed justified by works, he had something to boast about, but not before God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 3, 'For what does the Scripture say? “Abraham believed God, and it was credited to him as righteousness.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 4, 'Now the wages of the worker are not credited as a gift, but as an obligation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 5, 'However, to the one who does not work, but believes in Him who justifies the wicked, his faith is credited as righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 6, 'And David speaks likewise of the blessedness of the man to whom God credits righteousness apart from works:'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 7, '“Blessed are they whose lawless acts are forgiven, whose sins are covered.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 8, 'Blessed is the man whose sin the Lord will never count against him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 9, 'Is this blessing only on the circumcised, or also on the uncircumcised? We have been saying that Abraham’s faith was credited to him as righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 10, 'In what context was it credited? Was it after his circumcision, or before? It was not after, but before.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 11, 'And he received the sign of circumcision as a seal of the righteousness that he had by faith while he was still uncircumcised. So then, he is the father of all who believe but are not circumcised, in order that righteousness might be credited to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 12, 'And he is also the father of the circumcised who not only are circumcised, but who also walk in the footsteps of the faith that our father Abraham had before he was circumcised.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 13, 'For the promise to Abraham and his offspring that he would be heir of the world was not given through the law, but through the righteousness that comes by faith.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 14, 'For if those who live by the law are heirs, faith is useless and the promise is worthless,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 15, 'because the law brings wrath. And where there is no law, there is no transgression.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 16, 'Therefore, the promise comes by faith, so that it may rest on grace and may be guaranteed to all Abraham’s offspring—not only to those who are of the law, but also to those who are of the faith of Abraham. He is the father of us all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 17, 'As it is written: “I have made you a father of many nations.” He is our father in the presence of God, in whom he believed, the God who gives life to the dead and calls into being what does not yet exist.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 18, 'Against all hope, Abraham in hope believed and so became the father of many nations, just as he had been told, “So shall your offspring be.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 19, 'Without weakening in his faith, he acknowledged the decrepitness of his body (since he was about a hundred years old) and the lifelessness of Sarah’s womb.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 20, 'Yet he did not waver through disbelief in the promise of God, but was strengthened in his faith and gave glory to God,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 21, 'being fully persuaded that God was able to do what He had promised.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 22, 'This is why “it was credited to him as righteousness.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 23, 'Now the words “it was credited to him” were written not only for Abraham,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 24, 'but also for us, to whom righteousness will be credited—for us who believe in Him who raised Jesus our Lord from the dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 4, 25, 'He was delivered over to death for our trespasses and was raised to life for our justification.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 1, 'Therefore, since we have been justified through faith, we have peace with God through our Lord Jesus Christ,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 2, 'through whom we have gained access by faith into this grace in which we stand. And we rejoice in the hope of the glory of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 3, 'Not only that, but we also rejoice in our sufferings, because we know that suffering produces perseverance;'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 4, 'perseverance, character; and character, hope.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 5, 'And hope does not disappoint us, because God has poured out His love into our hearts through the Holy Spirit, whom He has given us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 6, 'For at just the right time, while we were still powerless, Christ died for the ungodly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 7, 'Very rarely will anyone die for a righteous man, though for a good man someone might possibly dare to die.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 8, 'But God proves His love for us in this: While we were still sinners, Christ died for us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 9, 'Therefore, since we have now been justified by His blood, how much more shall we be saved from wrath through Him!'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 10, 'For if, when we were enemies of God, we were reconciled to Him through the death of His Son, how much more, having been reconciled, shall we be saved through His life!'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 11, 'Not only that, but we also rejoice in God through our Lord Jesus Christ, through whom we have now received reconciliation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 12, 'Therefore, just as sin entered the world through one man, and death through sin, so also death was passed on to all men, because all sinned.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 13, 'For sin was in the world before the law was given; but sin is not taken into account when there is no law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 14, 'Nevertheless, death reigned from Adam until Moses, even over those who did not sin in the way that Adam transgressed. He is a pattern of the One to come.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 15, 'But the gift is not like the trespass. For if the many died by the trespass of the one man, how much more did God’s grace and the gift that came by the grace of the one man, Jesus Christ, abound to the many!'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 16, 'Again, the gift is not like the result of the one man’s sin: The judgment that followed one sin brought condemnation, but the gift that followed many trespasses brought justification.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 17, 'For if, by the trespass of the one man, death reigned through that one man, how much more will those who receive an abundance of grace and of the gift of righteousness reign in life through the one man, Jesus Christ!'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 18, 'So then, just as one trespass brought condemnation for all men, so also one act of righteousness brought justification and life for all men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 19, 'For just as through the disobedience of the one man the many were made sinners, so also through the obedience of the one man the many will be made righteous.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 20, 'The law came in so that the trespass would increase; but where sin increased, grace increased all the more,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 5, 21, 'so that, just as sin reigned in death, so also grace might reign through righteousness to bring eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 1, 'What then shall we say? Shall we continue in sin so that grace may increase?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 2, 'Certainly not! How can we who died to sin live in it any longer?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 3, 'Or aren’t you aware that all of us who were baptized into Christ Jesus were baptized into His death?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 4, 'We were therefore buried with Him through baptism into death, in order that, just as Christ was raised from the dead through the glory of the Father, we too may walk in newness of life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 5, 'For if we have been united with Him like this in His death, we will certainly also be united with Him in His resurrection.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 6, 'We know that our old self was crucified with Him so that the body of sin might be rendered powerless, that we should no longer be slaves to sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 7, 'For anyone who has died has been freed from sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 8, 'Now if we died with Christ, we believe that we will also live with Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 9, 'For we know that since Christ was raised from the dead, He cannot die again; death no longer has dominion over Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 10, 'The death He died, He died to sin once for all; but the life He lives, He lives to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 11, 'So you too must count yourselves dead to sin, but alive to God in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 12, 'Therefore do not let sin reign in your mortal body so that you obey its desires.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 13, 'Do not present the parts of your body to sin as instruments of wickedness, but present yourselves to God as those who have been brought from death to life; and present the parts of your body to Him as instruments of righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 14, 'For sin shall not be your master, because you are not under law, but under grace.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 15, 'What then? Shall we sin because we are not under law, but under grace? Certainly not!'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 16, 'Do you not know that when you offer yourselves as obedient slaves, you are slaves to the one you obey, whether you are slaves to sin leading to death, or to obedience leading to righteousness?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 17, 'But thanks be to God that, though you once were slaves to sin, you wholeheartedly obeyed the form of teaching to which you were committed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 18, 'You have been set free from sin and have become slaves to righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 19, 'I am speaking in human terms because of the weakness of your flesh. Just as you used to offer the parts of your body in slavery to impurity and to escalating wickedness, so now offer them in slavery to righteousness leading to holiness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 20, 'For when you were slaves to sin, you were free of obligation to righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 21, 'What fruit did you reap at that time from the things of which you are now ashamed? The outcome of those things is death.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 22, 'But now that you have been set free from sin and have become slaves to God, the fruit you reap leads to holiness, and the outcome is eternal life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 6, 23, 'For the wages of sin is death, but the gift of God is eternal life in Christ Jesus our Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 1, 'Do you not know, brothers (for I am speaking to those who know the law), that the law has authority over a man only as long as he lives?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 2, 'For instance, a married woman is bound by law to her husband as long as he lives. But if her husband dies, she is released from the law of marriage.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 3, 'So then, if she is joined to another man while her husband is still alive, she is called an adulteress; but if her husband dies, she is free from that law and is not an adulteress, even if she marries another man.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 4, 'Therefore, my brothers, you also died to the law through the body of Christ, that you might belong to another, to Him who was raised from the dead, in order that we might bear fruit to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 5, 'For when we lived according to the flesh, the sinful passions aroused by the law were at work in our bodies, bearing fruit for death.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 6, 'But now, having died to what bound us, we have been released from the law, so that we serve in the new way of the Spirit, and not in the old way of the written code.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 7, 'What then shall we say? Is the law sin? Certainly not! Indeed, I would not have been mindful of sin if not for the law. For I would not have been aware of coveting if the law had not said, “Do not covet.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 8, 'But sin, seizing its opportunity through the commandment, produced in me every kind of covetous desire. For apart from the law, sin is dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 9, 'Once I was alive apart from the law; but when the commandment came, sin sprang to life and I died.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 10, 'So I discovered that the very commandment that was meant to bring life actually brought death.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 11, 'For sin, seizing its opportunity through the commandment, deceived me and through the commandment put me to death.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 12, 'So then, the law is holy, and the commandment is holy, righteous, and good.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 13, 'Did that which is good, then, become death to me? Certainly not! But in order that sin might be exposed as sin, it produced death in me through what was good, so that through the commandment sin might become utterly sinful.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 14, 'We know that the law is spiritual; but I am unspiritual, sold as a slave to sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 15, 'I do not understand what I do. For what I want to do, I do not do. But what I hate, I do.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 16, 'And if I do what I do not want to do, I admit that the law is good.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 17, 'In that case, it is no longer I who do it, but it is sin living in me that does it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 18, 'I know that nothing good lives in me, that is, in my flesh; for I have the desire to do what is good, but I cannot carry it out.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 19, 'For I do not do the good I want to do. Instead, I keep on doing the evil I do not want to do.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 20, 'And if I do what I do not want, it is no longer I who do it, but it is sin living in me that does it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 21, 'So this is the principle I have discovered: When I want to do good, evil is right there with me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 22, 'For in my inner being I delight in God’s law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 23, 'But I see another law at work in my body, warring against the law of my mind and holding me captive to the law of sin that dwells within me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 24, 'What a wretched man I am! Who will rescue me from this body of death?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 7, 25, 'Thanks be to God, through Jesus Christ our Lord! So then, with my mind I serve the law of God, but with my flesh I serve the law of sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 1, 'Therefore, there is now no condemnation for those who are in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 2, 'For in Christ Jesus the law of the Spirit of life set you free from the law of sin and death.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 3, 'For what the law was powerless to do in that it was weakened by the flesh, God did by sending His own Son in the likeness of sinful man, as an offering for sin. He thus condemned sin in the flesh,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 4, 'so that the righteous standard of the law might be fulfilled in us, who do not walk according to the flesh but according to the Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 5, 'Those who live according to the flesh set their minds on the things of the flesh; but those who live according to the Spirit set their minds on the things of the Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 6, 'The mind of the flesh is death, but the mind of the Spirit is life and peace,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 7, 'because the mind of the flesh is hostile to God: It does not submit to God’s law, nor can it do so.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 8, 'Those controlled by the flesh cannot please God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 9, 'You, however, are controlled not by the flesh, but by the Spirit, if the Spirit of God lives in you. And if anyone does not have the Spirit of Christ, he does not belong to Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 10, 'But if Christ is in you, your body is dead because of sin, yet your spirit is alive because of righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 11, 'And if the Spirit of Him who raised Jesus from the dead is living in you, He who raised Christ Jesus from the dead will also give life to your mortal bodies through His Spirit, who lives in you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 12, 'Therefore, brothers, we have an obligation, but it is not to the flesh, to live according to it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 13, 'For if you live according to the flesh, you will die; but if by the Spirit you put to death the deeds of the body, you will live.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 14, 'For all who are led by the Spirit of God are sons of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 15, 'For you did not receive a spirit of slavery that returns you to fear, but you received the Spirit of sonship, by whom we cry, “Abba! Father!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 16, 'The Spirit Himself testifies with our spirit that we are God’s children.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 17, 'And if we are children, then we are heirs: heirs of God and co-heirs with Christ—if indeed we suffer with Him, so that we may also be glorified with Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 18, 'I consider that our present sufferings are not comparable to the glory that will be revealed in us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 19, 'The creation waits in eager expectation for the revelation of the sons of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 20, 'For the creation was subjected to futility, not by its own will, but because of the One who subjected it, in hope'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 21, 'that the creation itself will be set free from its bondage to decay and brought into the glorious freedom of the children of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 22, 'We know that the whole creation has been groaning together in the pains of childbirth until the present time.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 23, 'Not only that, but we ourselves, who have the firstfruits of the Spirit, groan inwardly as we wait eagerly for our adoption as sons, the redemption of our bodies.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 24, 'For in this hope we were saved; but hope that is seen is no hope at all. Who hopes for what he can already see?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 25, 'But if we hope for what we do not yet see, we wait for it patiently.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 26, 'In the same way, the Spirit helps us in our weakness. For we do not know how we ought to pray, but the Spirit Himself intercedes for us with groans too deep for words.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 27, 'And He who searches our hearts knows the mind of the Spirit, because the Spirit intercedes for the saints according to the will of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 28, 'And we know that God works all things together for the good of those who love Him, who are called according to His purpose.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 29, 'For those God foreknew, He also predestined to be conformed to the image of His Son, so that He would be the firstborn among many brothers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 30, 'And those He predestined, He also called; those He called, He also justified; those He justified, He also glorified.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 31, 'What then shall we say in response to these things? If God is for us, who can be against us?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 32, 'He who did not spare His own Son but gave Him up for us all, how will He not also, along with Him, freely give us all things?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 33, 'Who will bring any charge against God’s elect? It is God who justifies.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 34, 'Who is there to condemn us? For Christ Jesus, who died, and more than that was raised to life, is at the right hand of God—and He is interceding for us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 35, 'Who shall separate us from the love of Christ? Shall trouble or distress or persecution or famine or nakedness or danger or sword?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 36, 'As it is written: “For Your sake we face death all day long; we are considered as sheep to be slaughtered.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 37, 'No, in all these things we are more than conquerors through Him who loved us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 38, 'For I am convinced that neither death nor life, neither angels nor principalities, neither the present nor the future, nor any powers,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 8, 39, 'neither height nor depth, nor anything else in all creation, will be able to separate us from the love of God that is in Christ Jesus our Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 1, 'I speak the truth in Christ; I am not lying, as confirmed by my conscience in the Holy Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 2, 'I have deep sorrow and unceasing anguish in my heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 3, 'For I could wish that I myself were cursed and cut off from Christ for the sake of my brothers, my own flesh and blood,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 4, 'the people of Israel. Theirs is the adoption as sons; theirs the divine glory and the covenants; theirs the giving of the law, the temple worship, and the promises.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 5, 'Theirs are the patriarchs, and from them proceeds the human descent of Christ, who is God over all, forever worthy of praise! Amen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 6, 'It is not as though God’s word has failed. For not all who are descended from Israel are Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 7, 'Nor because they are Abraham’s descendants are they all his children. On the contrary, “Through Isaac your offspring will be reckoned.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 8, 'So it is not the children of the flesh who are God’s children, but it is the children of the promise who are regarded as offspring.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 9, 'For this is what the promise stated: “At the appointed time I will return, and Sarah will have a son.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 10, 'Not only that, but Rebecca’s children were conceived by one man, our father Isaac.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 11, 'Yet before the twins were born or had done anything good or bad, in order that God’s plan of election might stand,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 12, 'not by works but by Him who calls, she was told, “The older will serve the younger.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 13, 'So it is written: “Jacob I loved, but Esau I hated.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 14, 'What then shall we say? Is God unjust? Certainly not!'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 15, 'For He says to Moses: “I will have mercy on whom I have mercy, and I will have compassion on whom I have compassion.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 16, 'So then, it does not depend on man’s desire or effort, but on God’s mercy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 17, 'For the Scripture says to Pharaoh: “I raised you up for this very purpose, that I might display My power in you, and that My name might be proclaimed in all the earth.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 18, 'Therefore God has mercy on whom He wants to have mercy, and He hardens whom He wants to harden.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 19, 'One of you will say to me, “Then why does God still find fault? For who can resist His will?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 20, 'But who are you, O man, to talk back to God? Shall what is formed say to Him who formed it, “Why did You make me like this?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 21, 'Does not the potter have the right to make from the same lump of clay one vessel for special occasions and another for common use?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 22, 'What if God, intending to show His wrath and make His power known, bore with great patience the vessels of His wrath, prepared for destruction?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 23, 'What if He did this to make the riches of His glory known to the vessels of His mercy, whom He prepared in advance for glory—'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 24, 'including us, whom He has called not only from the Jews, but also from the Gentiles?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 25, 'As He says in Hosea: “I will call them ‘My People’ who are not My people, and I will call her ‘My Beloved’ who is not My beloved,”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 26, 'and, “It will happen that in the very place where it was said to them, ‘You are not My people,’ they will be called ‘sons of the living God.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 27, 'Isaiah cries out concerning Israel: “Though the number of the Israelites is like the sand of the sea, only the remnant will be saved.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 28, 'For the Lord will carry out His sentence on the earth thoroughly and decisively.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 29, 'It is just as Isaiah foretold: “Unless the Lord of Hosts had left us descendants, we would have become like Sodom, we would have resembled Gomorrah.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 30, 'What then will we say? That the Gentiles, who did not pursue righteousness, have obtained it, a righteousness that is by faith;'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 31, 'but Israel, who pursued a law of righteousness, has not attained it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 32, 'Why not? Because their pursuit was not by faith, but as if it were by works. They stumbled over the stumbling stone,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 9, 33, 'as it is written: “See, I lay in Zion a stone of stumbling and a rock of offense; and the one who believes in Him will never be put to shame.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 1, 'Brothers, my heart’s desire and prayer to God for the Israelites is for their salvation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 2, 'For I testify about them that they are zealous for God, but not on the basis of knowledge.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 3, 'Because they were ignorant of God’s righteousness and sought to establish their own, they did not submit to God’s righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 4, 'For Christ is the end of the law, to bring righteousness to everyone who believes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 5, 'For concerning the righteousness that is by the law, Moses writes: “The man who does these things will live by them.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 6, 'But the righteousness that is by faith says: “Do not say in your heart, ‘Who will ascend into heaven?’ (that is, to bring Christ down)'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 7, 'or, ‘Who will descend into the Abyss?’ (that is, to bring Christ up from the dead).”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 8, 'But what does it say? “The word is near you; it is in your mouth and in your heart,” that is, the word of faith we are proclaiming:'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 9, 'that if you confess with your mouth, “Jesus is Lord,” and believe in your heart that God raised Him from the dead, you will be saved.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 10, 'For with your heart you believe and are justified, and with your mouth you confess and are saved.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 11, 'It is just as the Scripture says: “Anyone who believes in Him will never be put to shame.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 12, 'For there is no difference between Jew and Greek: The same Lord is Lord of all, and gives richly to all who call on Him,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 13, 'for, “Everyone who calls on the name of the Lord will be saved.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 14, 'How then can they call on the One in whom they have not believed? And how can they believe in the One of whom they have not heard? And how can they hear without someone to preach?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 15, 'And how can they preach unless they are sent? As it is written: “How beautiful are the feet of those who bring good news!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 16, 'But not all of them welcomed the good news. For Isaiah says, “Lord, who has believed our message?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 17, 'Consequently, faith comes by hearing, and hearing by the word of Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 18, 'But I ask, did they not hear? Indeed they did: “Their voice has gone out into all the earth, their words to the ends of the world.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 19, 'I ask instead, did Israel not understand? First, Moses says: “I will make you jealous by those who are not a nation; I will make you angry by a nation without understanding.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 20, 'And Isaiah boldly says: “I was found by those who did not seek Me; I revealed Myself to those who did not ask for Me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 10, 21, 'But as for Israel he says: “All day long I have held out My hands to a disobedient and obstinate people.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 1, 'I ask then, did God reject His people? Certainly not! I am an Israelite myself, a descendant of Abraham, from the tribe of Benjamin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 2, 'God did not reject His people, whom He foreknew. Do you not know what the Scripture says about Elijah, how he appealed to God against Israel:'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 3, '“Lord, they have killed Your prophets and torn down Your altars. I am the only one left, and they are seeking my life as well”?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 4, 'And what was the divine reply to him? “I have reserved for Myself seven thousand men who have not bowed the knee to Baal.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 5, 'In the same way, at the present time there is a remnant chosen by grace.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 6, 'And if it is by grace, then it is no longer by works. Otherwise, grace would no longer be grace.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 7, 'What then? What Israel was seeking, it failed to obtain, but the elect did. The others were hardened,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 8, 'as it is written: “God gave them a spirit of stupor, eyes that could not see, and ears that could not hear, to this very day.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 9, 'And David says: “May their table become a snare and a trap, a stumbling block and a retribution to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 10, 'May their eyes be darkened so they cannot see, and their backs be bent forever.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 11, 'I ask then, did they stumble so as to fall beyond recovery? Certainly not! However, because of their trespass, salvation has come to the Gentiles to make Israel jealous.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 12, 'But if their trespass means riches for the world, and their failure means riches for the Gentiles, how much greater riches will their fullness bring!'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 13, 'I am speaking to you Gentiles. Inasmuch as I am the apostle to the Gentiles, I magnify my ministry'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 14, 'in the hope that I may provoke my own people to jealousy and save some of them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 15, 'For if their rejection is the reconciliation of the world, what will their acceptance be but life from the dead?'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 16, 'If the first part of the dough is holy, so is the whole batch; if the root is holy, so are the branches.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 17, 'Now if some branches have been broken off, and you, a wild olive shoot, have been grafted in among the others to share in the nourishment of the olive root,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 18, 'do not boast over those branches. If you do, remember this: You do not support the root, but the root supports you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 19, 'You will say then, “Branches were broken off so that I could be grafted in.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 20, 'That is correct: They were broken off because of unbelief, but you stand by faith. Do not be arrogant, but be afraid.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 21, 'For if God did not spare the natural branches, He will certainly not spare you either.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 22, 'Take notice, therefore, of the kindness and severity of God: severity to those who fell, but kindness to you, if you continue in His kindness. Otherwise you also will be cut off.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 23, 'And if they do not persist in unbelief, they will be grafted in, for God is able to graft them in again.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 24, 'For if you were cut from a wild olive tree, and contrary to nature were grafted into one that is cultivated, how much more readily will these, the natural branches, be grafted into their own olive tree!'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 25, 'I do not want you to be ignorant of this mystery, brothers, so that you will not be conceited: A hardening in part has come to Israel, until the full number of the Gentiles has come in.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 26, 'And so all Israel will be saved, as it is written: “The Deliverer will come from Zion; He will remove godlessness from Jacob.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 27, 'And this is My covenant with them when I take away their sins.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 28, 'Regarding the gospel, they are enemies on your account; but regarding election, they are loved on account of the patriarchs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 29, 'For God’s gifts and His call are irrevocable.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 30, 'Just as you who formerly disobeyed God have now received mercy through their disobedience,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 31, 'so they too have now disobeyed, in order that they too may now receive mercy through the mercy shown to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 32, 'For God has consigned everyone to disobedience so that He may have mercy on everyone.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 33, 'O, the depth of the riches of the wisdom and knowledge of God! How unsearchable are His judgments, and untraceable His ways!'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 34, '“Who has known the mind of the Lord? Or who has been His counselor?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 35, '“Who has first given to God, that God should repay him?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 11, 36, 'For from Him and through Him and to Him are all things. To Him be the glory forever! Amen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 1, 'Therefore I urge you, brothers, on account of God’s mercy, to offer your bodies as living sacrifices, holy and pleasing to God, which is your spiritual service of worship.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 2, 'Do not be conformed to this world, but be transformed by the renewing of your mind. Then you will be able to test and approve what is the good, pleasing, and perfect will of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 3, 'For by the grace given me I say to every one of you: Do not think of yourself more highly than you ought, but think of yourself with sober judgment, according to the measure of faith God has given you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 4, 'Just as each of us has one body with many members, and not all members have the same function,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 5, 'so in Christ we who are many are one body, and each member belongs to one another.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 6, 'We have different gifts according to the grace given us. If one’s gift is prophecy, let him use it in proportion to his faith;'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 7, 'if it is serving, let him serve; if it is teaching, let him teach;'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 8, 'if it is encouraging, let him encourage; if it is giving, let him give generously; if it is leading, let him lead with diligence; if it is showing mercy, let him do it cheerfully.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 9, 'Love must be sincere. Detest what is evil; cling to what is good.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 10, 'Be devoted to one another in brotherly love. Outdo yourselves in honoring one another.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 11, 'Do not let your zeal subside; keep your spiritual fervor, serving the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 12, 'Be joyful in hope, patient in affliction, persistent in prayer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 13, 'Share with the saints who are in need. Practice hospitality.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 14, 'Bless those who persecute you. Bless and do not curse.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 15, 'Rejoice with those who rejoice; weep with those who weep.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 16, 'Live in harmony with one another. Do not be proud, but enjoy the company of the lowly. Do not be conceited.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 17, 'Do not repay anyone evil for evil. Carefully consider what is right in the eyes of everybody.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 18, 'If it is possible on your part, live at peace with everyone.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 19, 'Do not avenge yourselves, beloved, but leave room for God’s wrath. For it is written: “Vengeance is Mine; I will repay, says the Lord.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 20, 'On the contrary, “If your enemy is hungry, feed him; if he is thirsty, give him a drink. For in so doing, you will heap burning coals on his head.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 12, 21, 'Do not be overcome by evil, but overcome evil with good.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 13, 1, 'Everyone must submit himself to the governing authorities, for there is no authority except that which is from God. The authorities that exist have been appointed by God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 13, 2, 'Consequently, whoever resists authority is opposing what God has set in place, and those who do so will bring judgment on themselves.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 13, 3, 'For rulers are not a terror to good conduct, but to bad. Do you want to be unafraid of the one in authority? Then do what is right, and you will have his approval.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 13, 4, 'For he is God’s servant for your good. But if you do wrong, be afraid, for he does not carry the sword in vain. He is God’s servant, an agent of retribution to the wrongdoer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 13, 5, 'Therefore it is necessary to submit to authority, not only to avoid punishment, but also as a matter of conscience.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 13, 6, 'This is also why you pay taxes. For the authorities are God’s servants, who devote themselves to their work.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 13, 7, 'Pay everyone what you owe him: taxes to whom taxes are due, revenue to whom revenue is due, respect to whom respect is due, honor to whom honor is due.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 13, 8, 'Be indebted to no one, except to one another in love. For he who loves his neighbor has fulfilled the law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 13, 9, 'The commandments “Do not commit adultery,” “Do not murder,” “Do not steal,” “Do not covet,” and any other commandments, are summed up in this one decree: “Love your neighbor as yourself.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 13, 10, 'Love does no wrong to its neighbor. Therefore love is the fulfillment of the law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 13, 11, 'And do this, understanding the occasion. The hour has come for you to wake up from your slumber, for our salvation is nearer now than when we first believed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 13, 12, 'The night is nearly over; the day has drawn near. So let us lay aside the deeds of darkness and put on the armor of light.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 13, 13, 'Let us behave decently, as in the daytime, not in carousing and drunkenness, not in sexual immorality and debauchery, not in dissension and jealousy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 13, 14, 'Instead, clothe yourselves with the Lord Jesus Christ, and make no provision for the desires of the flesh.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 1, 'Accept him whose faith is weak, without passing judgment on his opinions.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 2, 'For one person has faith to eat all things, while another, who is weak, eats only vegetables.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 3, 'The one who eats everything must not belittle the one who does not, and the one who does not eat everything must not judge the one who does, for God has accepted him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 4, 'Who are you to judge someone else’s servant? To his own master he stands or falls. And he will stand, for the Lord is able to make him stand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 5, 'One person regards a certain day above the others, while someone else considers every day alike. Each one should be fully convinced in his own mind.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 6, 'He who observes a special day does so to the Lord; he who eats does so to the Lord, for he gives thanks to God; and he who abstains does so to the Lord and gives thanks to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 7, 'For none of us lives to himself alone, and none of us dies to himself alone.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 8, 'If we live, we live to the Lord, and if we die, we die to the Lord. So whether we live or die, we belong to the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 9, 'For this reason Christ died and returned to life, that He might be the Lord of both the dead and the living.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 10, 'Why, then, do you judge your brother? Or why do you belittle your brother? For we will all stand before God’s judgment seat.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 11, 'It is written: “As surely as I live, says the Lord, every knee will bow before Me; every tongue will confess to God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 12, 'So then, each of us will give an account of himself to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 13, 'Therefore let us stop judging one another. Instead, make up your mind not to put any stumbling block or obstacle in your brother’s way.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 14, 'I am convinced and fully persuaded in the Lord Jesus that nothing is unclean in itself. But if anyone regards something as unclean, then for him it is unclean.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 15, 'If your brother is distressed by what you eat, you are no longer acting in love. Do not by your eating destroy your brother, for whom Christ died.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 16, 'Do not allow what you consider good, then, to be spoken of as evil.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 17, 'For the kingdom of God is not a matter of eating and drinking, but of righteousness, peace, and joy in the Holy Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 18, 'For whoever serves Christ in this way is pleasing to God and approved by men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 19, 'So then, let us pursue what leads to peace and to mutual edification.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 20, 'Do not destroy the work of God for the sake of food. All food is clean, but it is wrong for a man to let his eating be a stumbling block.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 21, 'It is better not to eat meat or drink wine or to do anything to cause your brother to stumble.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 22, 'Keep your belief about such matters between yourself and God. Blessed is the one who does not condemn himself by what he approves.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 14, 23, 'But the one who has doubts is condemned if he eats, because his eating is not from faith; and everything that is not from faith is sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 1, 'We who are strong ought to bear with the shortcomings of the weak and not to please ourselves.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 2, 'Each of us should please his neighbor for his good, to build him up.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 3, 'For even Christ did not please Himself, but as it is written: “The insults of those who insult You have fallen on Me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 4, 'For everything that was written in the past was written for our instruction, so that through endurance and the encouragement of the Scriptures, we might have hope.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 5, 'Now may the God who gives endurance and encouragement grant you harmony with one another in Christ Jesus,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 6, 'so that with one mind and one voice you may glorify the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 7, 'Accept one another, then, just as Christ accepted you, in order to bring glory to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 8, 'For I tell you that Christ has become a servant of the circumcised on behalf of God’s truth, to confirm the promises made to the patriarchs,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 9, 'so that the Gentiles may glorify God for His mercy. As it is written: “Therefore I will praise You among the Gentiles; I will sing hymns to Your name.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 10, 'Again, it says: “Rejoice, O Gentiles, with His people.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 11, 'And again: “Praise the Lord, all you Gentiles, and extol Him, all you peoples.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 12, 'And once more, Isaiah says: “The Root of Jesse will appear, One who will arise to rule over the Gentiles; in Him the Gentiles will put their hope.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 13, 'Now may the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace as you believe in Him, so that you may overflow with hope by the power of the Holy Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 14, 'I myself am convinced, my brothers, that you yourselves are full of goodness, brimming with knowledge, and able to instruct one another.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 15, 'However, I have written you a bold reminder on some points, because of the grace God has given me'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 16, 'to be a minister of Christ Jesus to the Gentiles in the priestly service of the gospel of God, so that the Gentiles might become an offering acceptable to God, sanctified by the Holy Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 17, 'Therefore I exult in Christ Jesus in my service to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 18, 'I will not presume to speak of anything except what Christ has accomplished through me in leading the Gentiles to obedience by word and deed,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 19, 'by the power of signs and wonders, and by the power of the Spirit of God. So from Jerusalem all the way around to Illyricum, I have fully proclaimed the gospel of Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 20, 'In this way I have aspired to preach the gospel where Christ was not known, so that I would not be building on someone else’s foundation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 21, 'Rather, as it is written: “Those who were not told about Him will see, and those who have not heard will understand.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 22, 'That is why I have often been hindered from coming to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 23, 'But now that there are no further opportunities for me in these regions, and since I have longed for many years to visit you,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 24, 'I hope to see you on my way to Spain. And after I have enjoyed your company for a while, you can equip me for my journey.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 25, 'Now, however, I am on my way to Jerusalem to serve the saints there.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 26, 'For Macedonia and Achaia were pleased to make a contribution for the poor among the saints in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 27, 'They were pleased to do it, and indeed they owe it to them. For if the Gentiles have shared in their spiritual blessings, they are obligated to minister to them with material blessings.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 28, 'So after I have completed this service and have safely delivered this bounty to them, I will set off to Spain by way of you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 29, 'I know that when I come to you, I will come in the fullness of the blessing of Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 30, 'Now I urge you, brothers, by our Lord Jesus Christ and by the love of the Spirit, to join me in my struggle by praying to God for me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 31, 'Pray that I may be delivered from the unbelievers in Judea, and that my service in Jerusalem may be acceptable to the saints there,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 32, 'so that by God’s will I may come to you with joy and together with you be refreshed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 15, 33, 'The God of peace be with all of you. Amen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 1, 'I commend to you our sister Phoebe, a servant of the church in Cenchrea.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 2, 'Welcome her in the Lord in a manner worthy of the saints, and assist her with anything she may need from you. For she has been a great help to many people, including me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 3, 'Greet Prisca and Aquila, my fellow workers in Christ Jesus,'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 4, 'who have risked their lives for me. Not only I but all the churches of the Gentiles are grateful to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 5, 'Greet also the church that meets at their house. Greet my beloved Epenetus, who was the first convert to Christ in the province of Asia.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 6, 'Greet Mary, who has worked very hard for you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 7, 'Greet Andronicus and Junia, my fellow countrymen and fellow prisoners. They are outstanding among the apostles, and they were in Christ before I was.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 8, 'Greet Ampliatus, my beloved in the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 9, 'Greet Urbanus, our fellow worker in Christ, and my beloved Stachys.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 10, 'Greet Apelles, who is approved in Christ. Greet those who belong to the household of Aristobulus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 11, 'Greet Herodion, my fellow countryman. Greet those from the household of Narcissus who are in the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 12, 'Greet Tryphena and Tryphosa, women who have worked hard in the Lord. Greet my beloved Persis, who has worked very hard in the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 13, 'Greet Rufus, chosen in the Lord, and his mother, who has been a mother to me as well.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 14, 'Greet Asyncritus, Phlegon, Hermes, Patrobas, Hermas, and the brothers with them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 15, 'Greet Philologus and Julia, Nereus and his sister, and Olympas and all the saints with them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 16, 'Greet one another with a holy kiss. All the churches of Christ send you greetings.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 17, 'Now I urge you, brothers, to watch out for those who create divisions and obstacles that are contrary to the teaching you have learned. Turn away from them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 18, 'For such people are not serving our Lord Christ, but their own appetites. By smooth talk and flattery they deceive the hearts of the naive.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 19, 'Everyone has heard about your obedience, so I rejoice over you. But I want you to be wise about what is good and innocent about what is evil.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 20, 'The God of peace will soon crush Satan under your feet. The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 21, 'Timothy, my fellow worker, sends you greetings, as do Lucius, Jason, and Sosipater, my fellow countrymen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 22, 'I, Tertius, who wrote down this letter, greet you in the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 23, 'Gaius, who has hosted me and all the church, sends you greetings. Erastus, the city treasurer, sends you greetings, as does our brother Quartus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 24, ''),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 25, 'Now to Him who is able to strengthen you by my gospel and by the proclamation of Jesus Christ, according to the revelation of the mystery concealed for ages past'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 26, 'but now revealed and made known through the writings of the prophets by the command of the eternal God, in order to lead all nations to the obedience that comes from faith—'),
  ('BSB', 'Romans', 45, 16, 27, 'to the only wise God be glory forever through Jesus Christ! Amen.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 1, 'Paul, called to be an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, and our brother Sosthenes,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 2, 'To the church of God in Corinth, to those sanctified in Christ Jesus and called to be holy, together with all those everywhere who call on the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, their Lord and ours:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 3, 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 4, 'I always thank my God for you because of the grace He has given you in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 5, 'For in Him you have been enriched in every way, in all speech and all knowledge,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 6, 'because our testimony about Christ was confirmed in you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 7, 'Therefore you do not lack any spiritual gift as you eagerly await the revelation of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 8, 'He will sustain you to the end, so that you will be blameless on the day of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 9, 'God, who has called you into fellowship with His Son Jesus Christ our Lord, is faithful.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 10, 'I appeal to you, brothers, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, that all of you agree together, so that there may be no divisions among you and that you may be united in mind and conviction.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 11, 'My brothers, some from Chloe’s household have informed me that there are quarrels among you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 12, 'What I mean is this: Individuals among you are saying, “I follow Paul,” “I follow Apollos,” “I follow Cephas,” or “I follow Christ.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 13, 'Is Christ divided? Was Paul crucified for you? Were you baptized into the name of Paul?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 14, 'I thank God that I did not baptize any of you except Crispus and Gaius,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 15, 'so no one can say that you were baptized into my name.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 16, 'Yes, I also baptized the household of Stephanas; beyond that I do not remember if I baptized anyone else.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 17, 'For Christ did not send me to baptize, but to preach the gospel, not with words of wisdom, lest the cross of Christ be emptied of its power.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 18, 'For the message of the cross is foolishness to those who are perishing, but to us who are being saved it is the power of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 19, 'For it is written: “I will destroy the wisdom of the wise; the intelligence of the intelligent I will frustrate.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 20, 'Where is the wise man? Where is the scribe? Where is the philosopher of this age? Has not God made foolish the wisdom of the world?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 21, 'For since in the wisdom of God the world through its wisdom did not know Him, God was pleased through the foolishness of what was preached to save those who believe.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 22, 'Jews demand signs and Greeks search for wisdom,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 23, 'but we preach Christ crucified, a stumbling block to Jews and foolishness to Gentiles,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 24, 'but to those who are called, both Jews and Greeks, Christ the power of God and the wisdom of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 25, 'For the foolishness of God is wiser than man’s wisdom, and the weakness of God is stronger than man’s strength.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 26, 'Brothers, consider the time of your calling: Not many of you were wise by human standards; not many were powerful; not many were of noble birth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 27, 'But God chose the foolish things of the world to shame the wise; God chose the weak things of the world to shame the strong.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 28, 'He chose the lowly and despised things of the world, and the things that are not, to nullify the things that are,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 29, 'so that no one may boast in His presence.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 30, 'It is because of Him that you are in Christ Jesus, who has become for us wisdom from God: our righteousness, holiness, and redemption.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 1, 31, 'Therefore, as it is written: “Let him who boasts boast in the Lord.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 2, 1, 'When I came to you, brothers, I did not come with eloquence or wisdom as I proclaimed to you the testimony about God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 2, 2, 'For I resolved to know nothing while I was with you except Jesus Christ and Him crucified.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 2, 3, 'I came to you in weakness and fear, and with much trembling.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 2, 4, 'My message and my preaching were not with persuasive words of wisdom, but with a demonstration of the Spirit’s power,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 2, 5, 'so that your faith would not rest on men’s wisdom, but on God’s power.');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 2, 6, 'Among the mature, however, we speak a message of wisdom—but not the wisdom of this age or of the rulers of this age, who are coming to nothing.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 2, 7, 'No, we speak of the mysterious and hidden wisdom of God, which He destined for our glory before time began.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 2, 8, 'None of the rulers of this age understood it. For if they had, they would not have crucified the Lord of glory.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 2, 9, 'Rather, as it is written: “No eye has seen, no ear has heard, no heart has imagined, what God has prepared for those who love Him.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 2, 10, 'But God has revealed it to us by the Spirit. The Spirit searches all things, even the deep things of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 2, 11, 'For who among men knows the thoughts of man except his own spirit within him? So too, no one knows the thoughts of God except the Spirit of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 2, 12, 'We have not received the spirit of the world, but the Spirit who is from God, that we may understand what God has freely given us.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 2, 13, 'And this is what we speak, not in words taught us by human wisdom, but in words taught by the Spirit, expressing spiritual truths in spiritual words.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 2, 14, 'The natural man does not accept the things that come from the Spirit of God. For they are foolishness to him, and he cannot understand them, because they are spiritually discerned.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 2, 15, 'The spiritual man judges all things, but he himself is not subject to anyone’s judgment.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 2, 16, '“For who has known the mind of the Lord, so as to instruct Him?” But we have the mind of Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 1, 'Brothers, I could not address you as spiritual, but as worldly—as infants in Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 2, 'I gave you milk, not solid food, for you were not yet ready for solid food. In fact, you are still not ready,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 3, 'for you are still worldly. For since there is jealousy and dissension among you, are you not worldly? Are you not walking in the way of man?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 4, 'For when one of you says, “I follow Paul,” and another, “I follow Apollos,” are you not mere men?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 5, 'What then is Apollos? And what is Paul? They are servants through whom you believed, as the Lord has assigned to each his role.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 6, 'I planted the seed and Apollos watered it, but God made it grow.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 7, 'So neither he who plants nor he who waters is anything, but only God, who makes things grow.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 8, 'He who plants and he who waters are one in purpose, and each will be rewarded according to his own labor.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 9, 'For we are God’s fellow workers; you are God’s field, God’s building.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 10, 'By the grace God has given me, I laid a foundation as an expert builder, and someone else is building on it. But each one must be careful how he builds.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 11, 'For no one can lay a foundation other than the one already laid, which is Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 12, 'If anyone builds on this foundation using gold, silver, precious stones, wood, hay, or straw,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 13, 'his workmanship will be evident, because the Day will bring it to light. It will be revealed with fire, and the fire will prove the quality of each man’s work.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 14, 'If what he has built survives, he will receive a reward.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 15, 'If it is burned up, he will suffer loss. He himself will be saved, but only as if through the flames.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 16, 'Do you not know that you yourselves are God’s temple, and that God’s Spirit dwells in you?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 17, 'If anyone destroys God’s temple, God will destroy him; for God’s temple is holy, and you are that temple.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 18, 'Let no one deceive himself. If any of you thinks he is wise in this age, he should become a fool, so that he may become wise.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 19, 'For the wisdom of this world is foolishness in God’s sight. As it is written: “He catches the wise in their craftiness.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 20, 'And again, “The Lord knows that the thoughts of the wise are futile.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 21, 'Therefore, stop boasting in men. All things are yours,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 22, 'whether Paul or Apollos or Cephas or the world or life or death or the present or the future. All of them belong to you,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 3, 23, 'and you belong to Christ, and Christ belongs to God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 1, 'So then, men ought to regard us as servants of Christ and stewards of the mysteries of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 2, 'Now it is required of stewards that they be found faithful.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 3, 'I care very little, however, if I am judged by you or by any human court. In fact, I do not even judge myself.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 4, 'My conscience is clear, but that does not vindicate me. It is the Lord who judges me.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 5, 'Therefore judge nothing before the appointed time; wait until the Lord comes. He will bring to light what is hidden in darkness and will expose the motives of men’s hearts. At that time each will receive his praise from God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 6, 'Brothers, I have applied these things to myself and Apollos for your benefit, so that you may learn from us not to go beyond what is written. Then you will not take pride in one man over another.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 7, 'For who makes you so superior? What do you have that you did not receive? And if you did receive it, why do you boast as though you did not?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 8, 'Already you have all you want. Already you have become rich. Without us, you have become kings. How I wish you really were kings, so that we might be kings with you!'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 9, 'For it seems to me that God has displayed us apostles at the end of the procession, like prisoners appointed for death. We have become a spectacle to the whole world, to angels as well as to men.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 10, 'We are fools for Christ, but you are wise in Christ. We are weak, but you are strong. You are honored, but we are dishonored.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 11, 'To this very hour we are hungry and thirsty, we are poorly clothed, we are brutally treated, we are homeless.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 12, 'We work hard with our own hands. When we are vilified, we bless; when we are persecuted, we endure it;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 13, 'when we are slandered, we answer gently. Up to this moment we have become the scum of the earth, the refuse of the world.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 14, 'I am not writing this to shame you, but to warn you as my beloved children.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 15, 'Even if you have ten thousand guardians in Christ, you do not have many fathers; for in Christ Jesus I became your father through the gospel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 16, 'Therefore I urge you to imitate me.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 17, 'That is why I have sent you Timothy, my beloved and faithful child in the Lord. He will remind you of my way of life in Christ Jesus, which is exactly what I teach everywhere in every church.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 18, 'Some of you have become arrogant, as if I were not coming to you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 19, 'But I will come to you shortly, if the Lord is willing, and then I will find out not only what these arrogant people are saying, but what power they have.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 20, 'For the kingdom of God is not a matter of talk but of power.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 4, 21, 'Which do you prefer? Shall I come to you with a rod, or in love and with a gentle spirit?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 5, 1, 'It is actually reported that there is sexual immorality among you, and of a kind that is intolerable even among pagans: A man has his father’s wife.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 5, 2, 'And you are proud! Shouldn’t you rather have been stricken with grief and have removed from your fellowship the man who did this?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 5, 3, 'Although I am absent from you in body, I am present with you in spirit, and I have already pronounced judgment on the one who did this, just as if I were present.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 5, 4, 'When you are assembled in the name of our Lord Jesus and I am with you in spirit, along with the power of the Lord Jesus,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 5, 5, 'hand this man over to Satan for the destruction of the flesh, so that his spirit may be saved on the Day of the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 5, 6, 'Your boasting is not good. Do you not know that a little leaven works through the whole batch of dough?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 5, 7, 'Get rid of the old leaven, that you may be a new unleavened batch, as you really are. For Christ, our Passover lamb, has been sacrificed.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 5, 8, 'Therefore let us keep the feast, not with the old bread, leavened with malice and wickedness, but with the unleavened bread of sincerity and of truth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 5, 9, 'I wrote you in my letter not to associate with sexually immoral people.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 5, 10, 'I was not including the sexually immoral of this world, or the greedy and swindlers, or idolaters. In that case you would have to leave this world.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 5, 11, 'But now I am writing you not to associate with anyone who claims to be a brother but is sexually immoral or greedy, an idolater or a verbal abuser, a drunkard or a swindler. With such a man do not even eat.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 5, 12, 'What business of mine is it to judge those outside the church? Are you not to judge those inside?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 5, 13, 'God will judge those outside. “Expel the wicked man from among you.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 1, 'If any of you has a grievance against another, how dare he go to law before the unrighteous instead of before the saints!'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 2, 'Do you not know that the saints will judge the world? And if you are to judge the world, are you not competent to judge trivial cases?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 3, 'Do you not know that we will judge angels? How much more the things of this life!'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 4, 'So if you need to settle everyday matters, do you appoint as judges those of no standing in the church?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 5, 'I say this to your shame. Is there really no one among you wise enough to arbitrate between his brothers?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 6, 'Instead, one brother goes to law against another, and this in front of unbelievers!'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 7, 'The very fact that you have lawsuits among you means that you are thoroughly defeated already. Why not rather be wronged? Why not rather be cheated?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 8, 'Instead, you yourselves cheat and do wrong, even against your own brothers!'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 9, 'Do you not know that the wicked will not inherit the kingdom of God? Do not be deceived: Neither the sexually immoral, nor idolaters, nor adulterers, nor men who submit to or perform homosexual acts,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 10, 'nor thieves, nor the greedy, nor drunkards, nor verbal abusers, nor swindlers, will inherit the kingdom of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 11, 'And that is what some of you were. But you were washed, you were sanctified, you were justified, in the name of the Lord Jesus Christ and by the Spirit of our God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 12, '“Everything is permissible for me,” but not everything is beneficial. “Everything is permissible for me,” but I will not be mastered by anything.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 13, '“Food for the stomach and the stomach for food,” but God will destroy them both. The body is not intended for sexual immorality, but for the Lord, and the Lord for the body.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 14, 'By His power God raised the Lord from the dead, and He will raise us also.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 15, 'Do you not know that your bodies are members of Christ? Shall I then take the members of Christ and unite them with a prostitute? Never!'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 16, 'Or don’t you know that he who unites himself with a prostitute is one with her in body? For it is said, “The two will become one flesh.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 17, 'But he who unites himself with the Lord is one with Him in spirit.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 18, 'Flee from sexual immorality. Every other sin a man can commit is outside his body, but he who sins sexually sins against his own body.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 19, 'Do you not know that your body is a temple of the Holy Spirit who is in you, whom you have received from God? You are not your own;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 6, 20, 'you were bought at a price. Therefore glorify God with your body.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 1, 'Now for the matters you wrote about: It is good to abstain from sexual relations.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 2, 'But because there is so much sexual immorality, each man should have his own wife, and each woman her own husband.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 3, 'The husband should fulfill his marital duty to his wife, and likewise the wife to her husband.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 4, 'The wife does not have authority over her own body, but the husband. Likewise the husband does not have authority over his own body, but the wife.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 5, 'Do not deprive each other, except by mutual consent and for a time, so you may devote yourselves to prayer. Then come together again, so that Satan will not tempt you through your lack of self-control.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 6, 'I say this as a concession, not as a command.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 7, 'I wish that all men were as I am. But each man has his own gift from God; one has this gift, another has that.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 8, 'Now to the unmarried and widows I say this: It is good for them to remain unmarried, as I am.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 9, 'But if they cannot control themselves, let them marry. For it is better to marry than to burn with passion.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 10, 'To the married I give this command (not I, but the Lord): A wife must not separate from her husband.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 11, 'But if she does, she must remain unmarried or else be reconciled to her husband. And a husband must not divorce his wife.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 12, 'To the rest I say this (I, not the Lord): If a brother has an unbelieving wife and she is willing to live with him, he must not divorce her.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 13, 'And if a woman has an unbelieving husband and he is willing to live with her, she must not divorce him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 14, 'For the unbelieving husband is sanctified through his believing wife, and the unbelieving wife is sanctified through her believing husband. Otherwise your children would be unclean, but now they are holy.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 15, 'But if the unbeliever leaves, let him go. The believing brother or sister is not bound in such cases. God has called you to live in peace.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 16, 'How do you know, wife, whether you will save your husband? Or how do you know, husband, whether you will save your wife?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 17, 'Regardless, each one should lead the life that the Lord has assigned to him and to which God has called him. This is what I prescribe in all the churches.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 18, 'Was a man already circumcised when he was called? He should not become uncircumcised. Was a man still uncircumcised when called? He should not be circumcised.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 19, 'Circumcision is nothing and uncircumcision is nothing. Keeping God’s commandments is what counts.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 20, 'Each one should remain in the situation he was in when he was called.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 21, 'Were you a slave when you were called? Do not let it concern you—but if you can gain your freedom, take the opportunity.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 22, 'For he who was a slave when he was called by the Lord is the Lord’s freedman. Conversely, he who was a free man when he was called is Christ’s slave.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 23, 'You were bought at a price; do not become slaves of men.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 24, 'Brothers, each one should remain in the situation he was in when God called him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 25, 'Now about virgins, I have no command from the Lord, but I give a judgment as one who by the Lord’s mercy is trustworthy.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 26, 'Because of the present crisis, I think it is good for a man to remain as he is.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 27, 'Are you committed to a wife? Do not seek to be released. Are you free of commitment? Do not look for a wife.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 28, 'But if you do marry, you have not sinned. And if a virgin marries, she has not sinned. But those who marry will face troubles in this life, and I want to spare you this.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 29, 'What I am saying, brothers, is that the time is short. From now on those who have wives should live as if they had none;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 30, 'those who weep, as if they did not; those who are joyful, as if they were not; those who make a purchase, as if they had nothing;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 31, 'and those who use the things of this world, as if not dependent on them. For this world in its present form is passing away.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 32, 'I want you to be free from concern. The unmarried man is concerned about the work of the Lord, how he can please the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 33, 'But the married man is concerned about the affairs of this world, how he can please his wife,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 34, 'and his interests are divided. The unmarried woman or virgin is concerned about the work of the Lord, how she can be holy in both body and spirit. But the married woman is concerned about the affairs of this world, how she can please her husband.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 35, 'I am saying this for your own good, not to restrict you, but in order to promote proper decorum and undivided devotion to the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 36, 'However, if someone thinks he is acting inappropriately toward his betrothed, and if she is beyond her youth and they ought to marry, let him do as he wishes; he is not sinning; they should get married.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 37, 'But the man who is firmly established in his heart and under no constraint, with control over his will and resolve in his heart not to marry the virgin, he will do well.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 38, 'So then, he who marries the virgin does well, but he who does not marry her does even better.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 39, 'A wife is bound to her husband as long as he lives. But if her husband dies, she is free to marry anyone she wishes, as long as he belongs to the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 7, 40, 'In my judgment, however, she is happier if she remains as she is. And I think that I too have the Spirit of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 8, 1, 'Now about food sacrificed to idols: We know that we all have knowledge. Knowledge puffs up, but love builds up.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 8, 2, 'The one who thinks he knows something does not yet know as he ought to know.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 8, 3, 'But the one who loves God is known by God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 8, 4, 'So about eating food sacrificed to idols: We know that an idol is nothing at all in the world, and that there is no God but one.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 8, 5, 'For even if there are so-called gods, whether in heaven or on earth (as there are many so-called gods and lords),'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 8, 6, 'yet for us there is but one God, the Father, from whom all things came and for whom we exist. And there is but one Lord, Jesus Christ, through whom all things came and through whom we exist.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 8, 7, 'But not everyone has this knowledge. Some people are still so accustomed to idols that they eat such food as if it were sacrificed to an idol. And since their conscience is weak, it is defiled.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 8, 8, 'But food does not bring us closer to God: We are no worse if we do not eat, and no better if we do.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 8, 9, 'Be careful, however, that your freedom does not become a stumbling block to the weak.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 8, 10, 'For if someone with a weak conscience sees you who are well informed eating in an idol’s temple, will he not be encouraged to eat food sacrificed to idols?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 8, 11, 'So this weak brother, for whom Christ died, is destroyed by your knowledge.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 8, 12, 'By sinning against your brothers in this way and wounding their weak conscience, you sin against Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 8, 13, 'Therefore, if what I eat causes my brother to stumble, I will never eat meat again, so that I will not cause him to stumble.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 1, 'Am I not free? Am I not an apostle? Have I not seen Jesus our Lord? Are you yourselves not my workmanship in the Lord?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 2, 'Even if I am not an apostle to others, surely I am to you. For you are the seal of my apostleship in the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 3, 'This is my defense to those who scrutinize me:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 4, 'Have we no right to food and to drink?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 5, 'Have we no right to take along a believing wife, as do the other apostles and the Lord’s brothers and Cephas?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 6, 'Or are Barnabas and I the only apostles who must work for a living?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 7, 'Who serves as a soldier at his own expense? Who plants a vineyard and does not eat of its fruit? Who tends a flock and does not drink of its milk?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 8, 'Do I say this from a human perspective? Doesn’t the Law say the same thing?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 9, 'For it is written in the Law of Moses: “Do not muzzle an ox while it is treading out the grain.” Is it about oxen that God is concerned?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 10, 'Isn’t He actually speaking on our behalf? Indeed, this was written for us, because when the plowman plows and the thresher threshes, they should also expect to share in the harvest.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 11, 'If we have sown spiritual seed among you, is it too much for us to reap a material harvest from you?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 12, 'If others have this right to your support, shouldn’t we have it all the more? But we did not exercise this right. Instead, we put up with anything rather than hinder the gospel of Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 13, 'Do you not know that those who work in the temple eat of its food, and those who serve at the altar partake of its offerings?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 14, 'In the same way, the Lord has prescribed that those who preach the gospel should receive their living from the gospel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 15, 'But I have not used any of these rights. And I am not writing this to suggest that something be done for me. Indeed, I would rather die than let anyone nullify my boast.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 16, 'Yet when I preach the gospel, I have no reason to boast, because I am obligated to preach. Woe to me if I do not preach the gospel!'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 17, 'If my preaching is voluntary, I have a reward. But if it is not voluntary, I am still entrusted with a responsibility.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 18, 'What then is my reward? That in preaching the gospel I may offer it free of charge, and so not use up my rights in preaching it.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 19, 'Though I am free of obligation to anyone, I make myself a slave to everyone, to win as many as possible.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 20, 'To the Jews I became like a Jew, to win the Jews. To those under the law I became like one under the law (though I myself am not under the law), to win those under the law.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 21, 'To those without the law I became like one without the law (though I am not outside the law of God but am under the law of Christ), to win those without the law.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 22, 'To the weak I became weak, to win the weak. I have become all things to all people so that by all possible means I might save some.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 23, 'I do all this for the sake of the gospel, so that I may share in its blessings.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 24, 'Do you not know that in a race all the runners run, but only one receives the prize? Run in such a way as to take the prize.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 25, 'Everyone who competes in the games trains with strict discipline. They do it for a crown that is perishable, but we do it for a crown that is imperishable.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 26, 'Therefore I do not run aimlessly; I do not fight like I am beating the air.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 9, 27, 'No, I discipline my body and make it my slave, so that after I have preached to others, I myself will not be disqualified.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 1, 'I do not want you to be unaware, brothers, that our forefathers were all under the cloud, and that they all passed through the sea.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 2, 'They were all baptized into Moses in the cloud and in the sea.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 3, 'They all ate the same spiritual food'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 4, 'and drank the same spiritual drink; for they drank from the spiritual rock that accompanied them, and that rock was Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 5, 'Nevertheless, God was not pleased with most of them, for they were struck down in the wilderness.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 6, 'These things took place as examples to keep us from craving evil things as they did.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 7, 'Do not be idolaters, as some of them were. As it is written: “The people sat down to eat and to drink, and got up to indulge in revelry.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 8, 'We should not commit sexual immorality, as some of them did, and in one day twenty-three thousand of them died.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 9, 'We should not test Christ, as some of them did, and were killed by snakes.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 10, 'And do not complain, as some of them did, and were killed by the destroying angel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 11, 'Now these things happened to them as examples and were written down as warnings for us, on whom the fulfillment of the ages has come.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 12, 'So the one who thinks he is standing firm should be careful not to fall.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 13, 'No temptation has seized you except what is common to man. And God is faithful; He will not let you be tempted beyond what you can bear. But when you are tempted, He will also provide an escape, so that you can stand up under it.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 14, 'Therefore, my beloved, flee from idolatry.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 15, 'I speak to reasonable people; judge for yourselves what I say.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 16, 'Is not the cup of blessing that we bless a participation in the blood of Christ? And is not the bread that we break a participation in the body of Christ?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 17, 'Because there is one loaf, we who are many are one body; for we all partake of the one loaf.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 18, 'Consider the people of Israel: Are not those who eat the sacrifices fellow partakers in the altar?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 19, 'Am I suggesting, then, that food sacrificed to an idol is anything, or that an idol is anything?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 20, 'No, but the sacrifices of pagans are offered to demons, not to God. And I do not want you to be participants with demons.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 21, 'You cannot drink the cup of the Lord and the cup of demons too; you cannot partake in the table of the Lord and the table of demons too.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 22, 'Are we trying to provoke the Lord to jealousy? Are we stronger than He?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 23, '“Everything is permissible,” but not everything is beneficial. “Everything is permissible,” but not everything is edifying.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 24, 'No one should seek his own good, but the good of others.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 25, 'Eat anything sold in the meat market without raising questions of conscience,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 26, 'for, “The earth is the Lord’s, and the fullness thereof.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 27, 'If an unbeliever invites you to a meal and you want to go, eat anything set before you without raising questions of conscience.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 28, 'But if someone tells you, “This food was offered to idols,” then do not eat it, for the sake of the one who told you and for the sake of conscience—'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 29, 'the other one’s conscience, I mean, not your own. For why should my freedom be determined by someone else’s conscience?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 30, 'If I partake in the meal with thankfulness, why am I denounced because of that for which I give thanks?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 31, 'So whether you eat or drink or whatever you do, do it all to the glory of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 32, 'Do not become a stumbling block, whether to Jews or Greeks or the church of God—'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 10, 33, 'as I also try to please everyone in all I do. For I am not seeking my own good, but the good of many, that they may be saved.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 1, 'You are to imitate me, just as I imitate Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 2, 'Now I commend you for remembering me in everything and for maintaining the traditions, just as I passed them on to you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 3, 'But I want you to understand that the head of every man is Christ, and the head of the woman is man, and the head of Christ is God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 4, 'Every man who prays or prophesies with his head covered dishonors his head.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 5, 'And every woman who prays or prophesies with her head uncovered dishonors her head, for it is just as if her head were shaved.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 6, 'If a woman does not cover her head, she should have her hair cut off. And if it is shameful for a woman to have her hair cut or shaved off, she should cover her head.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 7, 'A man ought not to cover his head, since he is the image and glory of God; but the woman is the glory of man.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 8, 'For man did not come from woman, but woman from man.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 9, 'Neither was man created for woman, but woman for man.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 10, 'For this reason a woman ought to have a sign of authority on her head, because of the angels.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 11, 'In the Lord, however, woman is not independent of man, nor is man independent of woman.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 12, 'For just as woman came from man, so also man is born of woman. But everything comes from God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 13, 'Judge for yourselves: Is it proper for a woman to pray to God with her head uncovered?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 14, 'Doesn’t nature itself teach you that if a man has long hair, it is a disgrace to him,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 15, 'but that if a woman has long hair, it is her glory? For long hair is given to her as a covering.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 16, 'If anyone is inclined to dispute this, we have no other practice, nor do the churches of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 17, 'In the following instructions I have no praise to offer, because your gatherings do more harm than good.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 18, 'First of all, I hear that when you come together as a church, there are divisions among you, and in part I believe it.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 19, 'And indeed, there must be differences among you to show which of you are approved.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 20, 'Now then, when you come together, it is not the Lord’s Supper you eat.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 21, 'For as you eat, each of you goes ahead without sharing his meal. While one remains hungry, another gets drunk.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 22, 'Don’t you have your own homes in which to eat and drink? Or do you despise the church of God and humiliate those who have nothing? What can I say to you? Shall I praise you for this? No, I will not!'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 23, 'For I received from the Lord what I also passed on to you: The Lord Jesus, on the night He was betrayed, took bread,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 24, 'and when He had given thanks, He broke it and said, “This is My body, which is for you; do this in remembrance of Me.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 25, 'In the same way, after supper He took the cup, saying, “This cup is the new covenant in My blood; do this, as often as you drink it, in remembrance of Me.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 26, 'For as often as you eat this bread and drink this cup, you proclaim the Lord’s death until He comes.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 27, 'Therefore, whoever eats the bread or drinks the cup of the Lord in an unworthy manner will be guilty of sinning against the body and blood of the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 28, 'Each one must examine himself before he eats of the bread and drinks of the cup.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 29, 'For anyone who eats and drinks without recognizing the body eats and drinks judgment on himself.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 30, 'That is why many among you are weak and sick, and a number of you have fallen asleep.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 31, 'Now if we judged ourselves properly, we would not come under judgment.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 32, 'But when we are judged by the Lord, we are being disciplined so that we will not be condemned with the world.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 33, 'So, my brothers, when you come together to eat, wait for one another.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 11, 34, 'If anyone is hungry, he should eat at home, so that when you come together it will not result in judgment. And when I come, I will give instructions about the remaining matters.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 1, 'Now about spiritual gifts, brothers, I do not want you to be uninformed.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 2, 'You know that when you were pagans, you were influenced and led astray to mute idols.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 3, 'Therefore I inform you that no one who is speaking by the Spirit of God says, “Jesus be cursed,” and no one can say, “Jesus is Lord,” except by the Holy Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 4, 'There are different gifts, but the same Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 5, 'There are different ministries, but the same Lord.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 6, 'There are different ways of working, but the same God works all things in all people.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 7, 'Now to each one the manifestation of the Spirit is given for the common good.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 8, 'To one there is given through the Spirit the message of wisdom, to another the message of knowledge by the same Spirit,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 9, 'to another faith by the same Spirit, to another gifts of healing by that one Spirit,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 10, 'to another the working of miracles, to another prophecy, to another distinguishing between spirits, to another speaking in various tongues, and to still another the interpretation of tongues.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 11, 'All these are the work of one and the same Spirit, who apportions them to each one as He determines.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 12, 'The body is a unit, though it is composed of many parts. And although its parts are many, they all form one body. So it is with Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 13, 'For in one Spirit we were all baptized into one body, whether Jews or Greeks, slave or free, and we were all given one Spirit to drink.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 14, 'For the body does not consist of one part, but of many.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 15, 'If the foot should say, “Because I am not a hand, I do not belong to the body,” that would not make it any less a part of the body.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 16, 'And if the ear should say, “Because I am not an eye, I do not belong to the body,” that would not make it any less a part of the body.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 17, 'If the whole body were an eye, where would the sense of hearing be? If the whole body were an ear, where would the sense of smell be?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 18, 'But in fact, God has arranged the members of the body, every one of them, according to His design.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 19, 'If they were all one part, where would the body be?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 20, 'As it is, there are many parts, but one body.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 21, 'The eye cannot say to the hand, “I do not need you.” Nor can the head say to the feet, “I do not need you.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 22, 'On the contrary, the parts of the body that seem to be weaker are indispensable,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 23, 'and the parts we consider less honorable, we treat with greater honor. And our unpresentable parts are treated with special modesty,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 24, 'whereas our presentable parts have no such need. But God has composed the body and has given greater honor to the parts that lacked it,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 25, 'so that there should be no division in the body, but that its members should have mutual concern for one another.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 26, 'If one part suffers, every part suffers with it; if one part is honored, every part rejoices with it.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 27, 'Now you are the body of Christ, and each of you is a member of it.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 28, 'And in the church God has appointed first of all apostles, second prophets, third teachers, then workers of miracles, and those with gifts of healing, helping, administration, and various tongues.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 29, 'Are all apostles? Are all prophets? Are all teachers? Do all work miracles?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 30, 'Do all have gifts of healing? Do all speak in tongues? Do all interpret?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 12, 31, 'But eagerly desire the greater gifts. And now I will show you the most excellent way.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 13, 1, 'If I speak in the tongues of men and of angels, but have not love, I am only a ringing gong or a clanging cymbal.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 13, 2, 'If I have the gift of prophecy and can fathom all mysteries and all knowledge, and if I have absolute faith so as to move mountains, but have not love, I am nothing.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 13, 3, 'If I give all I possess to the poor and exult in the surrender of my body, but have not love, I gain nothing.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 13, 4, 'Love is patient, love is kind. It does not envy, it does not boast, it is not proud.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 13, 5, 'It is not rude, it is not self-seeking, it is not easily angered, it keeps no account of wrongs.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 13, 6, 'Love takes no pleasure in evil, but rejoices in the truth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 13, 7, 'It bears all things, believes all things, hopes all things, endures all things.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 13, 8, 'Love never fails. But where there are prophecies, they will cease; where there are tongues, they will be restrained; where there is knowledge, it will be dismissed.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 13, 9, 'For we know in part and we prophesy in part,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 13, 10, 'but when the perfect comes, the partial passes away.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 13, 11, 'When I was a child, I talked like a child, I thought like a child, I reasoned like a child. When I became a man, I set aside childish ways.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 13, 12, 'Now we see but a dim reflection as in a mirror; then we shall see face to face. Now I know in part; then I shall know fully, even as I am fully known.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 13, 13, 'And now these three remain: faith, hope, and love; but the greatest of these is love.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 1, 'Earnestly pursue love and eagerly desire spiritual gifts, especially the gift of prophecy.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 2, 'For he who speaks in a tongue does not speak to men, but to God. Indeed, no one understands him; he utters mysteries in the Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 3, 'But he who prophesies speaks to men for their edification, encouragement, and comfort.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 4, 'The one who speaks in a tongue edifies himself, but the one who prophesies edifies the church.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 5, 'I wish that all of you could speak in tongues, but I would rather have you prophesy. He who prophesies is greater than one who speaks in tongues, unless he interprets so that the church may be edified.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 6, 'Now, brothers, if I come to you speaking in tongues, how will I benefit you, unless I bring you some revelation or knowledge or prophecy or teaching?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 7, 'Even in the case of lifeless instruments, such as the flute or harp, how will anyone recognize the tune they are playing unless the notes are distinct?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 8, 'Again, if the trumpet sounds a muffled call, who will prepare for battle?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 9, 'So it is with you. Unless you speak intelligible words with your tongue, how will anyone know what you are saying? You will just be speaking into the air.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 10, 'Assuredly, there are many different languages in the world, yet none of them is without meaning.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 11, 'If, then, I do not know the meaning of someone’s language, I am a foreigner to the speaker, and he is a foreigner to me.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 12, 'It is the same with you. Since you are eager to have spiritual gifts, strive to excel in gifts that build up the church.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 13, 'Therefore, the one who speaks in a tongue should pray that he may interpret.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 14, 'For if I pray in a tongue, my spirit prays, but my mind is unfruitful.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 15, 'What then shall I do? I will pray with my spirit, but I will also pray with my mind. I will sing with my spirit, but I will also sing with my mind.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 16, 'Otherwise, if you speak a blessing in spirit, how can someone who is uninstructed say “Amen” to your thanksgiving, since he does not know what you are saying?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 17, 'You may be giving thanks well enough, but the other one is not edified.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 18, 'I thank God that I speak in tongues more than all of you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 19, 'But in the church, I would rather speak five coherent words to instruct others than ten thousand words in a tongue.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 20, 'Brothers, stop thinking like children. In regard to evil be infants, but in your thinking be mature.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 21, 'It is written in the Law: “By strange tongues and foreign lips I will speak to this people, but even then they will not listen to Me, says the Lord.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 22, 'Tongues, then, are a sign, not for believers, but for unbelievers. Prophecy, however, is for believers, not for unbelievers.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 23, 'So if the whole church comes together and everyone speaks in tongues, and some who are uninstructed or some unbelievers come in, will they not say that you are out of your minds?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 24, 'But if an unbeliever or uninstructed person comes in while everyone is prophesying, he will be convicted and called to account by all,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 25, 'and the secrets of his heart will be made known. So he will fall facedown and worship God, proclaiming, “God is truly among you!”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 26, 'What then shall we say, brothers? When you come together, everyone has a psalm or a teaching, a revelation, a tongue, or an interpretation. All of these must be done to build up the church.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 27, 'If anyone speaks in a tongue, two, or at most three, should speak in turn, and someone must interpret.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 28, 'But if there is no interpreter, he should remain silent in the church and speak only to himself and God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 29, 'Two or three prophets should speak, and the others should weigh carefully what is said.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 30, 'And if a revelation comes to someone who is seated, the first speaker should stop.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 31, 'For you can all prophesy in turn so that everyone may be instructed and encouraged.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 32, 'The spirits of prophets are subject to prophets.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 33, 'For God is not a God of disorder, but of peace—as in all the churches of the saints.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 34, 'Women are to be silent in the churches. They are not permitted to speak, but must be in submission, as the law says.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 35, 'If they wish to inquire about something, they are to ask their own husbands at home; for it is dishonorable for a woman to speak in the church.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 36, 'Did the word of God originate with you? Or are you the only ones it has reached?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 37, 'If anyone considers himself a prophet or spiritual person, let him acknowledge that what I am writing you is the Lord’s command.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 38, 'But if anyone ignores this, he himself will be ignored.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 39, 'So, my brothers, be eager to prophesy, and do not forbid speaking in tongues.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 14, 40, 'But everything must be done in a proper and orderly manner.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 1, 'Now, brothers, I want to remind you of the gospel I preached to you, which you received, and in which you stand firm.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 2, 'By this gospel you are saved, if you hold firmly to the word I preached to you. Otherwise, you have believed in vain.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 3, 'For what I received I passed on to you as of first importance: that Christ died for our sins according to the Scriptures,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 4, 'that He was buried, that He was raised on the third day according to the Scriptures,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 5, 'and that He appeared to Cephas and then to the Twelve.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 6, 'After that, He appeared to more than five hundred brothers at once, most of whom are still living, though some have fallen asleep.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 7, 'Then He appeared to James, then to all the apostles.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 8, 'And last of all He appeared to me also, as to one of untimely birth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 9, 'For I am the least of the apostles and am unworthy to be called an apostle, because I persecuted the church of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 10, 'But by the grace of God I am what I am, and His grace to me was not in vain. No, I worked harder than all of them—yet not I, but the grace of God that was with me.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 11, 'Whether, then, it was I or they, this is what we preach, and this is what you believed.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 12, 'But if it is preached that Christ has been raised from the dead, how can some of you say that there is no resurrection of the dead?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 13, 'If there is no resurrection of the dead, then not even Christ has been raised.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 14, 'And if Christ has not been raised, our preaching is worthless, and so is your faith.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 15, 'In that case, we are also exposed as false witnesses about God. For we have testified about God that He raised Christ from the dead, but He did not raise Him if in fact the dead are not raised.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 16, 'For if the dead are not raised, then not even Christ has been raised.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 17, 'And if Christ has not been raised, your faith is futile; you are still in your sins.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 18, 'Then those also who have fallen asleep in Christ have perished.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 19, 'If our hope in Christ is for this life alone, we are to be pitied more than all men.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 20, 'But Christ has indeed been raised from the dead, the firstfruits of those who have fallen asleep.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 21, 'For since death came through a man, the resurrection of the dead comes also through a man.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 22, 'For as in Adam all die, so in Christ all will be made alive.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 23, 'But each in his own turn: Christ the firstfruits; then at His coming, those who belong to Him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 24, 'Then the end will come, when He hands over the kingdom to God the Father after He has destroyed all dominion, authority, and power.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 25, 'For He must reign until He has put all His enemies under His feet.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 26, 'The last enemy to be destroyed is death.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 27, 'For “God has put everything under His feet.” Now when it says that everything has been put under Him, this clearly does not include the One who put everything under Him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 28, 'And when all things have been subjected to Him, then the Son Himself will be made subject to Him who put all things under Him, so that God may be all in all.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 29, 'If these things are not so, what will those do who are baptized for the dead? If the dead are not raised at all, why are people baptized for them?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 30, 'And why do we endanger ourselves every hour?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 31, 'I face death every day, brothers, as surely as I boast about you in Christ Jesus our Lord.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 32, 'If I fought wild beasts in Ephesus for human motives, what did I gain? If the dead are not raised, “Let us eat and drink, for tomorrow we die.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 33, 'Do not be deceived: “Bad company corrupts good character.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 34, 'Sober up as you ought, and stop sinning; for some of you are ignorant of God. I say this to your shame.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 35, 'But someone will ask, “How are the dead raised? With what kind of body will they come?”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 36, 'You fool! What you sow does not come to life unless it dies.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 37, 'And what you sow is not the body that will be, but just a seed, perhaps of wheat or something else.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 38, 'But God gives it a body as He has designed, and to each kind of seed He gives its own body.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 39, 'Not all flesh is the same: Men have one kind of flesh, animals have another, birds another, and fish another.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 40, 'There are also heavenly bodies and earthly bodies. But the splendor of the heavenly bodies is of one degree, and the splendor of the earthly bodies is of another.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 41, 'The sun has one degree of splendor, the moon another, and the stars another; and star differs from star in splendor.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 42, 'So will it be with the resurrection of the dead: What is sown is perishable; it is raised imperishable.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 43, 'It is sown in dishonor; it is raised in glory. It is sown in weakness; it is raised in power.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 44, 'It is sown a natural body; it is raised a spiritual body. If there is a natural body, there is also a spiritual body.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 45, 'So it is written: “The first man Adam became a living being;” the last Adam a life-giving spirit.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 46, 'The spiritual, however, was not first, but the natural, and then the spiritual.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 47, 'The first man was of the dust of the earth, the second man from heaven.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 48, 'As was the earthly man, so also are those who are of the earth; and as is the heavenly man, so also are those who are of heaven.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 49, 'And just as we have borne the likeness of the earthly man, so also shall we bear the likeness of the heavenly man.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 50, 'Now I declare to you, brothers, that flesh and blood cannot inherit the kingdom of God, nor does the perishable inherit the imperishable.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 51, 'Listen, I tell you a mystery: We will not all sleep, but we will all be changed—'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 52, 'in an instant, in the twinkling of an eye, at the last trumpet. For the trumpet will sound, the dead will be raised imperishable, and we will be changed.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 53, 'For the perishable must be clothed with the imperishable, and the mortal with immortality.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 54, 'When the perishable has been clothed with the imperishable and the mortal with immortality, then the saying that is written will come to pass: “Death has been swallowed up in victory.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 55, '“Where, O Death, is your victory? Where, O Death, is your sting?”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 56, 'The sting of death is sin, and the power of sin is the law.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 57, 'But thanks be to God, who gives us the victory through our Lord Jesus Christ!'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 15, 58, 'Therefore, my beloved brothers, be steadfast and immovable. Always excel in the work of the Lord, because you know that your labor in the Lord is not in vain.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 1, 'Now about the collection for the saints, you are to do as I directed the churches of Galatia:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 2, 'On the first day of every week, each of you should set aside a portion of his income, saving it up, so that when I come no collections will be needed.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 3, 'Then, on my arrival, I will send letters with those you recommend to carry your gift to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 4, 'And if it is advisable for me to go also, they can travel with me.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 5, 'After I go through Macedonia, however, I will come to you; for I will be going through Macedonia.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 6, 'Perhaps I will stay with you awhile, or even spend the winter, so that you can help me on my journey, wherever I go.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 7, 'For I do not want to see you now only in passing; I hope to spend some time with you, if the Lord permits.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 8, 'But I will stay in Ephesus until Pentecost,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 9, 'because a great door for effective work has opened to me, even though many oppose me.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 10, 'If Timothy comes, see to it that he has nothing to fear while he is with you, for he is doing the work of the Lord, just as I am.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 11, 'No one, then, should treat him with contempt. Send him on his way in peace so that he can return to me, for I am expecting him along with the brothers.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 12, 'Now about our brother Apollos: I strongly urged him to go to you with the brothers. He was not at all inclined to go now, but he will go when he has the opportunity.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 13, 'Be on the alert. Stand firm in the faith. Be men of courage. Be strong.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 14, 'Do everything in love.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 15, 'You know that Stephanas and his household were the first converts in Achaia, and they have devoted themselves to the service of the saints. Now I urge you, brothers,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 16, 'to submit to such as these, and to every fellow worker and laborer.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 17, 'I am glad that Stephanas, Fortunatus, and Achaicus have arrived, because they have supplied what was lacking from you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 18, 'For they refreshed my spirit and yours as well. Show your appreciation, therefore, to such men.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 19, 'The churches in the province of Asia send you greetings. Aquila and Prisca greet you warmly in the Lord, and so does the church that meets at their house.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 20, 'All the brothers here send you greetings. Greet one another with a holy kiss.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 21, 'This greeting is in my own hand—Paul.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 22, 'If anyone does not love the Lord, let him be under a curse. Come, O Lord!'),
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 23, 'The grace of the Lord Jesus be with you.');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', '1 Corinthians', 46, 16, 24, 'My love be with all of you in Christ Jesus. Amen.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 1, 'Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, and Timothy our brother, To the church of God in Corinth, together with all the saints throughout Achaia:'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 2, 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 3, 'Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of compassion and the God of all comfort,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 4, 'who comforts us in all our troubles, so that we can comfort those in any trouble with the comfort we ourselves have received from God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 5, 'For just as the sufferings of Christ overflow to us, so also through Christ our comfort overflows.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 6, 'If we are afflicted, it is for your comfort and salvation; if we are comforted, it is for your comfort, which accomplishes in you patient endurance of the same sufferings we experience.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 7, 'And our hope for you is sure, because we know that just as you share in our sufferings, so also you will share in our comfort.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 8, 'We do not want you to be unaware, brothers, of the hardships we encountered in the province of Asia. We were under a burden far beyond our ability to endure, so that we despaired even of life.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 9, 'Indeed, we felt we were under the sentence of death, in order that we would not trust in ourselves, but in God, who raises the dead.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 10, 'He has delivered us from such a deadly peril, and He will deliver us. In Him we have placed our hope that He will yet again deliver us,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 11, 'as you help us by your prayers. Then many will give thanks on our behalf for the favor shown us in answer to their prayers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 12, 'And this is our boast: Our conscience testifies that we have conducted ourselves in the world, and especially in relation to you, in the holiness and sincerity that are from God—not in worldly wisdom, but in the grace of God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 13, 'For we do not write you anything that is beyond your ability to read and understand. And I hope that you will understand us completely,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 14, 'as you have already understood us in part, so that you may boast of us just as we will boast of you in the day of our Lord Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 15, 'Confident of this, I planned to visit you first, so that you might receive a double blessing.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 16, 'I wanted to visit you on my way to Macedonia, and to return to you from Macedonia, and then to have you help me on my way to Judea.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 17, 'When I planned this, did I do it carelessly? Or do I make my plans by human standards, so as to say “Yes, yes” when I really mean “No, no”?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 18, 'But as surely as God is faithful, our message to you is not “Yes” and “No.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 19, 'For the Son of God, Jesus Christ, who was proclaimed among you by me and Silvanus and Timothy, was not “Yes” and “No,” but in Him it has always been “Yes.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 20, 'For all the promises of God are “Yes” in Christ. And so through Him, our “Amen” is spoken to the glory of God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 21, 'Now it is God who establishes both us and you in Christ. He anointed us,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 22, 'placed His seal on us, and put His Spirit in our hearts as a pledge of what is to come.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 23, 'I call God as my witness that it was in order to spare you that I did not return to Corinth.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 1, 24, 'Not that we lord it over your faith, but we are fellow workers with you for your joy, because it is by faith that you stand firm.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 2, 1, 'So I made up my mind not to make another painful visit to you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 2, 2, 'For if I grieve you, who is left to cheer me but those whom I have grieved?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 2, 3, 'I wrote as I did so that on my arrival I would not be saddened by those who ought to make me rejoice. I had confidence in all of you, that you would share my joy.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 2, 4, 'For through many tears I wrote you out of great distress and anguish of heart, not to grieve you but to let you know how much I love you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 2, 5, 'Now if anyone has caused grief, he has not grieved me but all of you—to some degree, not to overstate it.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 2, 6, 'The punishment imposed on him by the majority is sufficient for him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 2, 7, 'So instead, you ought to forgive and comfort him, so that he will not be overwhelmed by excessive sorrow.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 2, 8, 'Therefore I urge you to reaffirm your love for him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 2, 9, 'My purpose in writing you was to see if you would stand the test and be obedient in everything.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 2, 10, 'If you forgive anyone, I also forgive him. And if I have forgiven anything, I have forgiven it in the presence of Christ for your sake,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 2, 11, 'in order that Satan should not outwit us. For we are not unaware of his schemes.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 2, 12, 'Now when I went to Troas to preach the gospel of Christ and a door stood open for me in the Lord,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 2, 13, 'I had no peace in my spirit, because I did not find my brother Titus there. So I said goodbye to them and went on to Macedonia.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 2, 14, 'But thanks be to God, who always leads us triumphantly as captives in Christ and through us spreads everywhere the fragrance of the knowledge of Him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 2, 15, 'For we are to God the sweet aroma of Christ among those who are being saved and those who are perishing.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 2, 16, 'To the one, we are an odor of death and demise; to the other, a fragrance that brings life. And who is qualified for such a task?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 2, 17, 'For we are not like so many others, who peddle the word of God for profit. On the contrary, in Christ we speak before God with sincerity, as men sent from God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 1, 'Are we beginning to commend ourselves again? Or do we need, like some people, letters of recommendation to you or from you?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 2, 'You yourselves are our letter, inscribed on our hearts, known and read by everyone.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 3, 'It is clear that you are a letter from Christ, the result of our ministry, written not with ink but with the Spirit of the living God, not on tablets of stone but on tablets of human hearts.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 4, 'Such confidence before God is ours through Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 5, 'Not that we are competent in ourselves to claim that anything comes from us, but our competence comes from God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 6, 'And He has qualified us as ministers of a new covenant, not of the letter but of the Spirit; for the letter kills, but the Spirit gives life.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 7, 'Now if the ministry of death, which was engraved in letters on stone, came with such glory that the Israelites could not gaze at the face of Moses because of its fleeting glory,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 8, 'will not the ministry of the Spirit be even more glorious?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 9, 'For if the ministry of condemnation was glorious, how much more glorious is the ministry of righteousness!'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 10, 'Indeed, what was once glorious has no glory now in comparison to the glory that surpasses it.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 11, 'For if what was fading away came with glory, how much greater is the glory of that which endures!'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 12, 'Therefore, since we have such a hope, we are very bold.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 13, 'We are not like Moses, who would put a veil over his face to keep the Israelites from gazing at the end of what was fading away.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 14, 'But their minds were closed. For to this day the same veil remains at the reading of the old covenant. It has not been lifted, because only in Christ can it be removed.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 15, 'And even to this day when Moses is read, a veil covers their hearts.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 16, 'But whenever anyone turns to the Lord, the veil is taken away.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 17, 'Now the Lord is the Spirit, and where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is freedom.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 3, 18, 'And we, who with unveiled faces all reflect the glory of the Lord, are being transformed into His image with intensifying glory, which comes from the Lord, who is the Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 1, 'Therefore, since God in His mercy has given us this ministry, we do not lose heart.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 2, 'Instead, we have renounced secret and shameful ways. We do not practice deceit, nor do we distort the word of God. On the contrary, by open proclamation of the truth, we commend ourselves to every man’s conscience in the sight of God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 3, 'And even if our gospel is veiled, it is veiled to those who are perishing.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 4, 'The god of this age has blinded the minds of unbelievers so they cannot see the light of the gospel of the glory of Christ, who is the image of God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 5, 'For we do not proclaim ourselves, but Jesus Christ as Lord, and ourselves as your servants for Jesus’ sake.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 6, 'For God, who said, “Let light shine out of darkness,” made His light shine in our hearts to give us the light of the knowledge of the glory of God in the face of Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 7, 'Now we have this treasure in jars of clay to show that this surpassingly great power is from God and not from us.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 8, 'We are hard pressed on all sides, but not crushed; perplexed, but not in despair;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 9, 'persecuted, but not forsaken; struck down, but not destroyed.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 10, 'We always carry around in our body the death of Jesus, so that the life of Jesus may also be revealed in our body.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 11, 'For we who are alive are always consigned to death for Jesus’ sake, so that the life of Jesus may also be revealed in our mortal body.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 12, 'So then, death is at work in us, but life is at work in you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 13, 'And in keeping with what is written: “I believed, therefore I have spoken,” we who have the same spirit of faith also believe and therefore speak,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 14, 'knowing that the One who raised the Lord Jesus will also raise us with Jesus and present us with you in His presence.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 15, 'All this is for your benefit, so that the grace that is extending to more and more people may overflow in thanksgiving, to the glory of God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 16, 'Therefore we do not lose heart. Though our outer self is wasting away, yet our inner self is being renewed day by day.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 17, 'For our light and momentary affliction is producing for us an eternal weight of glory that is far beyond comparison.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 4, 18, 'So we fix our eyes not on what is seen, but on what is unseen. For what is seen is temporary, but what is unseen is eternal.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 1, 'Now we know that if the earthly tent we live in is dismantled, we have a building from God, an eternal house in heaven, not built by human hands.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 2, 'For in this tent we groan, longing to be clothed with our heavenly dwelling,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 3, 'because when we are clothed, we will not be found naked.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 4, 'So while we are in this tent, we groan under our burdens, because we do not wish to be unclothed but clothed, so that our mortality may be swallowed up by life.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 5, 'And God has prepared us for this very purpose and has given us the Spirit as a pledge of what is to come.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 6, 'Therefore we are always confident, although we know that while we are at home in the body, we are away from the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 7, 'For we walk by faith, not by sight.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 8, 'We are confident, then, and would prefer to be away from the body and at home with the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 9, 'So we aspire to please Him, whether we are here in this body or away from it.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 10, 'For we must all appear before the judgment seat of Christ, that each one may receive his due for the things done in the body, whether good or bad.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 11, 'Therefore, since we know what it means to fear the Lord, we try to persuade men. What we are is clear to God, and I hope it is clear to your conscience as well.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 12, 'We are not commending ourselves to you again. Instead, we are giving you an occasion to be proud of us, so that you can answer those who take pride in appearances rather than in the heart.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 13, 'If we are out of our mind, it is for God; if we are of sound mind, it is for you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 14, 'For Christ’s love compels us, because we are convinced that One died for all, therefore all died.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 15, 'And He died for all, that those who live should no longer live for themselves, but for Him who died for them and was raised again.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 16, 'So from now on we regard no one according to the flesh. Although we once regarded Christ in this way, we do so no longer.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 17, 'Therefore if anyone is in Christ, he is a new creation. The old has passed away. Behold, the new has come!'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 18, 'All this is from God, who reconciled us to Himself through Christ and gave us the ministry of reconciliation:'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 19, 'that God was reconciling the world to Himself in Christ, not counting men’s trespasses against them. And He has committed to us the message of reconciliation.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 20, 'Therefore we are ambassadors for Christ, as though God were making His appeal through us. We implore you on behalf of Christ: Be reconciled to God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 5, 21, 'God made Him who knew no sin to be sin on our behalf, so that in Him we might become the righteousness of God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 1, 'As God’s fellow workers, then, we urge you not to receive God’s grace in vain.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 2, 'For He says: “In the time of favor I heard you, and in the day of salvation I helped you.” Behold, now is the time of favor; now is the day of salvation!'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 3, 'We put no obstacle in anyone’s way, so that no one can discredit our ministry.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 4, 'Rather, as servants of God we commend ourselves in every way: in great endurance; in troubles, hardships, and calamities;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 5, 'in beatings, imprisonments, and riots; in labor, sleepless nights, and hunger;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 6, 'in purity, knowledge, patience, and kindness; in the Holy Spirit and in sincere love;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 7, 'in truthful speech and in the power of God; with the weapons of righteousness in the right hand and in the left;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 8, 'through glory and dishonor, slander and praise; viewed as imposters, yet genuine;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 9, 'as unknown, yet well-known; dying, and yet we live on; punished, yet not killed;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 10, 'sorrowful, yet always rejoicing; poor, yet making many rich; having nothing, and yet possessing everything.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 11, 'We have spoken freely to you, Corinthians. Our hearts are open wide.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 12, 'It is not our affection, but yours, that is restrained.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 13, 'As a fair exchange, I ask you as my children: Open wide your hearts also.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 14, 'Do not be unequally yoked with unbelievers. For what partnership can righteousness have with wickedness? Or what fellowship does light have with darkness?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 15, 'What harmony is there between Christ and Belial? Or what does a believer have in common with an unbeliever?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 16, 'What agreement can exist between the temple of God and idols? For we are the temple of the living God. As God has said: “I will dwell with them and walk among them, and I will be their God, and they will be My people.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 17, '“Therefore come out from among them and be separate, says the Lord. Touch no unclean thing, and I will receive you.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 6, 18, 'And: “I will be a Father to you, and you will be My sons and daughters, says the Lord Almighty.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 7, 1, 'Therefore, beloved, since we have these promises, let us cleanse ourselves from everything that defiles body and spirit, perfecting holiness in the fear of God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 7, 2, 'Make room for us in your hearts. We have wronged no one, we have corrupted no one, we have exploited no one.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 7, 3, 'I do not say this to condemn you. I have said before that you so occupy our hearts that we live and die together with you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 7, 4, 'Great is my confidence in you; great is my pride in you; I am filled with encouragement; in all our troubles my joy overflows.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 7, 5, 'For when we arrived in Macedonia, our bodies had no rest, but we were pressed from every direction—conflicts on the outside, fears within.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 7, 6, 'But God, who comforts the downcast, comforted us by the arrival of Titus,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 7, 7, 'and not only by his arrival, but also by the comfort he had received from you. He told us about your longing, your mourning, and your zeal for me, so that I rejoiced all the more.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 7, 8, 'Even if I caused you sorrow by my letter, I do not regret it. Although I did regret it, I now see that my letter caused you sorrow, but only for a short time.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 7, 9, 'And now I rejoice, not because you were made sorrowful, but because your sorrow led you to repentance. For you felt the sorrow that God had intended, and so were not harmed in any way by us.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 7, 10, 'Godly sorrow brings repentance that leads to salvation without regret, but worldly sorrow brings death.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 7, 11, 'Consider what this godly sorrow has produced in you: what earnestness, what eagerness to clear yourselves, what indignation, what alarm, what longing, what zeal, what vindication! In every way you have proved yourselves to be innocent in this matter.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 7, 12, 'So even though I wrote to you, it was not on account of the one who did wrong or the one who was harmed, but rather that your earnestness on our behalf would be made clear to you in the sight of God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 7, 13, 'On account of this, we are encouraged. In addition to our own encouragement, we were even more delighted by the joy of Titus. For his spirit has been refreshed by all of you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 7, 14, 'Indeed, I was not embarrassed by anything I had boasted to him about you. But just as everything we said to you was true, so our boasting to Titus has proved to be true as well.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 7, 15, 'And his affection for you is even greater when he remembers that you were all obedient as you welcomed him with fear and trembling.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 7, 16, 'I rejoice that I can have complete confidence in you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 1, 'Now, brothers, we want you to know about the grace that God has given the churches of Macedonia.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 2, 'In the terrible ordeal they suffered, their abundant joy and deep poverty overflowed into rich generosity.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 3, 'For I testify that they gave according to their ability and even beyond it. Of their own accord,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 4, 'they earnestly pleaded with us for the privilege of sharing in this service to the saints.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 5, 'And not only did they do as we expected, but they gave themselves first to the Lord and then to us, because it was the will of God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 6, 'So we urged Titus to help complete your act of grace, just as he had started it.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 7, 'But just as you excel in everything—in faith, in speech, in knowledge, in complete earnestness, and in the love we inspired in you—see that you also excel in this grace of giving.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 8, 'I am not making a demand, but I am testing the sincerity of your love in comparison to the earnestness of others.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 9, 'For you know the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ, that though He was rich, yet for your sakes He became poor, so that you through His poverty might become rich.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 10, 'And this is my opinion about what is helpful for you in this matter: Last year you were the first not only to give, but even to have such a desire.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 11, 'Now finish the work, so that you may complete it just as eagerly as you began, according to your means.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 12, 'For if the eagerness is there, the gift is acceptable according to what one has, not according to what he does not have.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 13, 'It is not our intention that others may be relieved while you are burdened, but that there may be equality.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 14, 'At the present time, your surplus will meet their need, so that in turn their surplus will meet your need. Then there will be equality.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 15, 'As it is written: “He who gathered much had no excess, and he who gathered little had no shortfall.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 16, 'But thanks be to God, who put into the heart of Titus the same devotion I have for you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 17, 'For not only did he welcome our appeal, but he is eagerly coming to you of his own volition.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 18, 'Along with Titus we are sending the brother who is praised by all the churches for his work in the gospel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 19, 'More than that, this brother was chosen by the churches to accompany us with the offering—the gracious gift we administer to honor the Lord Himself and to show our eagerness to help.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 20, 'We hope to avoid any criticism of the way we administer this generous gift.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 21, 'For we are taking great care to do what is right, not only in the eyes of the Lord, but also in the eyes of men.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 22, 'And we are sending along with them our brother whose earnestness has been proven many times and in many ways, and now even more so by his great confidence in you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 23, 'As for Titus, he is my partner and fellow worker among you. As for our brothers, they are messengers of the churches, to the glory of Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 8, 24, 'In full view of the churches, then, show these men the proof of your love and the reason for our boasting about you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 9, 1, 'Now about the service to the saints, there is no need for me to write to you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 9, 2, 'For I know your eagerness to help, and I have been boasting to the Macedonians that since last year you in Achaia were prepared to give. And your zeal has stirred most of them to do likewise.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 9, 3, 'But I am sending the brothers in order that our boasting about you in this matter should not prove empty, but that you will be prepared, just as I said.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 9, 4, 'Otherwise, if any Macedonians come with me and find you unprepared, we—to say nothing of you—would be ashamed of having been so confident.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 9, 5, 'So I thought it necessary to urge the brothers to visit you beforehand and make arrangements for the bountiful gift you had promised. This way, your gift will be prepared generously and not begrudgingly.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 9, 6, 'Remember this: Whoever sows sparingly will also reap sparingly, and whoever sows generously will also reap generously.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 9, 7, 'Each one should give what he has decided in his heart to give, not out of regret or compulsion. For God loves a cheerful giver.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 9, 8, 'And God is able to make all grace abound to you, so that in all things, at all times, having all that you need, you will abound in every good work.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 9, 9, 'As it is written: “He has scattered abroad His gifts to the poor; His righteousness endures forever.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 9, 10, 'Now He who supplies seed to the sower and bread for food will supply and multiply your store of seed and will increase the harvest of your righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 9, 11, 'You will be enriched in every way to be generous on every occasion, so that through us your giving will produce thanksgiving to God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 9, 12, 'For this ministry of service is not only supplying the needs of the saints, but is also overflowing in many expressions of thanksgiving to God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 9, 13, 'Because of the proof this ministry provides, the saints will glorify God for your obedient confession of the gospel of Christ, and for the generosity of your contribution to them and to all the others.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 9, 14, 'And their prayers for you will express their affection for you, because of the surpassing grace God has given you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 9, 15, 'Thanks be to God for His indescribable gift!'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 1, 'Now by the mildness and gentleness of Christ, I appeal to you—I, Paul, who am humble when face to face with you, but bold when away.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 2, 'I beg you that when I come I may not need to be as bold as I expect toward those who presume that we live according to the flesh.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 3, 'For though we live in the flesh, we do not wage war according to the flesh.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 4, 'The weapons of our warfare are not the weapons of the world. Instead, they have divine power to demolish strongholds.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 5, 'We tear down arguments and every presumption set up against the knowledge of God; and we take captive every thought to make it obedient to Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 6, 'And we will be ready to punish every act of disobedience, as soon as your obedience is complete.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 7, 'You are looking at outward appearances. If anyone is confident that he belongs to Christ, he should remind himself that we belong to Christ just as much as he does.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 8, 'For even if I boast somewhat excessively about the authority the Lord gave us for building you up rather than tearing you down, I will not be ashamed.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 9, 'I do not want to seem to be trying to frighten you by my letters.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 10, 'For some say, “His letters are weighty and forceful, but his physical presence is unimpressive, and his speaking is of no account.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 11, 'Such people should consider that what we are in our letters when absent, we will be in our actions when present.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 12, 'We do not dare to classify or compare ourselves with some who commend themselves. When they measure themselves by themselves and compare themselves with themselves, they show their ignorance.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 13, 'We, however, will not boast beyond our limits, but only within the field of influence that God has assigned to us—a field that reaches even to you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 14, 'We are not overstepping our bounds, as if we had not come to you. Indeed, we were the first to reach you with the gospel of Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 15, 'Neither do we boast beyond our limits in the labors of others. But we hope that as your faith increases, our area of influence among you will greatly increase as well,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 16, 'so that we can preach the gospel in the regions beyond you. Then we will not be boasting in the work already done in another man’s territory.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 17, 'Rather, “Let him who boasts boast in the Lord.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 10, 18, 'For it is not the one who commends himself who is approved, but the one whom the Lord commends.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 1, 'I hope you will bear with a little of my foolishness, but you are already doing that.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 2, 'I am jealous for you with a godly jealousy. For I promised you to one husband, to present you as a pure virgin to Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 3, 'I am afraid, however, that just as Eve was deceived by the serpent’s cunning, your minds may be led astray from your simple and pure devotion to Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 4, 'For if someone comes and proclaims a Jesus other than the One we proclaimed, or if you receive a different spirit than the One you received, or a different gospel than the one you accepted, you put up with it way too easily.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 5, 'I consider myself in no way inferior to those “super-apostles.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 6, 'Although I am not a polished speaker, I am certainly not lacking in knowledge. We have made this clear to you in every way possible.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 7, 'Was it a sin for me to humble myself in order to exalt you, because I preached the gospel of God to you free of charge?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 8, 'I robbed other churches by accepting their support in order to serve you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 9, 'And when I was with you and in need, I was not a burden to anyone; for the brothers who came from Macedonia supplied my needs. I have refrained from being a burden to you in any way, and I will continue to do so.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 10, 'As surely as the truth of Christ is in me, this boasting of mine will not be silenced in the regions of Achaia.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 11, 'Why? Because I do not love you? God knows I do!'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 12, 'But I will keep on doing what I am doing, in order to undercut those who want an opportunity to be regarded as our equals in the things of which they boast.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 13, 'For such men are false apostles, deceitful workers, masquerading as apostles of Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 14, 'And no wonder, for Satan himself masquerades as an angel of light.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 15, 'It is not surprising, then, if his servants masquerade as servants of righteousness. Their end will correspond to their actions.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 16, 'I repeat: Let no one take me for a fool. But if you do, then receive me as a fool, so that I too may boast a little.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 17, 'In this confident boasting of mine, I am not speaking as the Lord would, but as a fool.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 18, 'Since many are boasting according to the flesh, I too will boast.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 19, 'For you gladly tolerate fools, since you are so wise.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 20, 'In fact, you even put up with anyone who enslaves you or exploits you or takes advantage of you or exalts himself or strikes you in the face.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 21, 'To my shame I concede that we were too weak for that! Speaking as a fool, however, I can match what anyone else dares to boast about.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 22, 'Are they Hebrews? So am I. Are they Israelites? So am I. Are they descendants of Abraham? So am I.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 23, 'Are they servants of Christ? I am speaking like I am out of my mind, but I am so much more: in harder labor, in more imprisonments, in worse beatings, in frequent danger of death.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 24, 'Five times I received from the Jews the forty lashes minus one.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 25, 'Three times I was beaten with rods, once I was stoned, three times I was shipwrecked. I spent a night and a day in the open sea.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 26, 'In my frequent journeys, I have been in danger from rivers and from bandits, in danger from my countrymen and from the Gentiles, in danger in the city and in the country, in danger on the sea and among false brothers,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 27, 'in labor and toil and often without sleep, in hunger and thirst and often without food, in cold and exposure.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 28, 'Apart from these external trials, I face daily the pressure of my concern for all the churches.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 29, 'Who is weak, and I am not weak? Who is led into sin, and I do not burn with grief?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 30, 'If I must boast, I will boast of the things that show my weakness.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 31, 'The God and Father of the Lord Jesus, who is forever worthy of praise, knows that I am not lying.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 32, 'In Damascus, the governor under King Aretas secured the city of the Damascenes in order to arrest me.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 11, 33, 'But I was lowered in a basket through a window in the wall and escaped his grasp.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 1, 'I must go on boasting. Although there is nothing to gain, I will go on to visions and revelations from the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 2, 'I know a man in Christ who fourteen years ago was caught up to the third heaven. Whether it was in the body or out of it I do not know, but God knows.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 3, 'And I know that this man—whether in the body or out of it I do not know, but God knows—'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 4, 'was caught up to Paradise. The things he heard were too sacred for words, things that man is not permitted to tell.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 5, 'I will boast about such a man, but I will not boast about myself, except in my weaknesses.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 6, 'Even if I wanted to boast, I would not be a fool, because I would be speaking the truth. But I refrain, so no one will credit me with more than he sees in me or hears from me,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 7, 'or because of these surpassingly great revelations. So to keep me from becoming conceited, I was given a thorn in my flesh, a messenger of Satan, to torment me.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 8, 'Three times I pleaded with the Lord to take it away from me.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 9, 'But He said to me, “My grace is sufficient for you, for My power is perfected in weakness.” Therefore I will boast all the more gladly in my weaknesses, so that the power of Christ may rest on me.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 10, 'That is why, for the sake of Christ, I delight in weaknesses, in insults, in hardships, in persecutions, in difficulties. For when I am weak, then I am strong.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 11, 'I have become a fool, but you drove me to it. In fact, you should have commended me, since I am in no way inferior to those “super-apostles,” even though I am nothing.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 12, 'The true marks of an apostle—signs, wonders, and miracles—were performed among you with great perseverance.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 13, 'In what way were you inferior to the other churches, except that I was not a burden to you? Forgive me this wrong!'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 14, 'See, I am ready to come to you a third time, and I will not be a burden, because I am not seeking your possessions, but you. For children should not have to save up for their parents, but parents for their children.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 15, 'And for the sake of your souls, I will most gladly spend my money and myself. If I love you more, will you love me less?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 16, 'Be that as it may, I was not a burden to you; but crafty as I am, I caught you by trickery.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 17, 'Did I exploit you by anyone I sent you?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 18, 'I urged Titus to visit you, and I sent our brother with him. Did Titus exploit you in any way? Did we not walk in the same Spirit and follow in the same footsteps?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 19, 'Have you been thinking all along that we were making a defense to you? We speak before God in Christ, and all of this, beloved, is to build you up.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 20, 'For I am afraid that when I come, I may not find you as I wish, and you may not find me as you wish. I fear that there may be quarreling, jealousy, rage, rivalry, slander, gossip, arrogance, and disorder.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 12, 21, 'I am afraid that when I come again, my God will humble me before you, and I will be grieved over many who have sinned earlier and have not repented of their acts of impurity, sexual immorality, and debauchery.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 13, 1, 'This is the third time I am coming to you. “Every matter must be established by the testimony of two or three witnesses.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 13, 2, 'I already warned you the second time I was with you. So now in my absence I warn those who sinned earlier and everyone else: If I return, I will not spare anyone,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 13, 3, 'since you are demanding proof that Christ is speaking through me. He is not weak in dealing with you, but is powerful among you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 13, 4, 'For He was indeed crucified in weakness, yet He lives by God’s power. And though we are weak in Him, yet by God’s power we will live with Him to serve you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 13, 5, 'Examine yourselves to see whether you are in the faith; test yourselves. Can’t you see for yourselves that Jesus Christ is in you—unless you actually fail the test?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 13, 6, 'And I hope you will realize that we have not failed the test.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 13, 7, 'Now we pray to God that you will not do anything wrong—not that we will appear to have stood the test, but that you will do what is right, even if we appear to have failed.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 13, 8, 'For we cannot do anything against the truth, but only for the truth.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 13, 9, 'In fact, we rejoice when we are weak but you are strong, and our prayer is for your perfection.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 13, 10, 'This is why I write these things while absent, so that when I am present I will not need to be severe in my use of the authority that the Lord gave me for building you up, not for tearing you down.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 13, 11, 'Finally, brothers, rejoice! Aim for perfect harmony, encourage one another, be of one mind, live in peace. And the God of love and peace will be with you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 13, 12, 'Greet one another with a holy kiss.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 13, 13, 'All the saints send you greetings.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Corinthians', 47, 13, 14, 'The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ, and the love of God, and the fellowship of the Holy Spirit be with all of you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 1, 'Paul, an apostle—sent not from men nor by man, but by Jesus Christ and God the Father, who raised Him from the dead—'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 2, 'and all the brothers with me, To the churches of Galatia:'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 3, 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ,'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 4, 'who gave Himself for our sins to rescue us from the present evil age, according to the will of our God and Father,'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 5, 'to whom be glory forever and ever. Amen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 6, 'I am amazed how quickly you are deserting the One who called you by the grace of Christ and are turning to a different gospel—'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 7, 'which is not even a gospel. Evidently some people are troubling you and trying to distort the gospel of Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 8, 'But even if we or an angel from heaven should preach a gospel contrary to the one we preached to you, let him be under a curse!'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 9, 'As we have said before, so now I say again: If anyone is preaching to you a gospel contrary to the one you received, let him be under a curse!'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 10, 'Am I now seeking the approval of men, or of God? Or am I striving to please men? If I were still trying to please men, I would not be a servant of Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 11, 'For I certify to you, brothers, that the gospel I preached was not devised by man.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 12, 'I did not receive it from any man, nor was I taught it; rather, I received it by revelation from Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 13, 'For you have heard of my former way of life in Judaism, how severely I persecuted the church of God and tried to destroy it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 14, 'I was advancing in Judaism beyond many of my contemporaries and was extremely zealous for the traditions of my fathers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 15, 'But when God, who set me apart from my mother’s womb and called me by His grace, was pleased'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 16, 'to reveal His Son in me so that I might preach Him among the Gentiles, I did not rush to consult with flesh and blood,'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 17, 'nor did I go up to Jerusalem to the apostles who came before me, but I went into Arabia and later returned to Damascus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 18, 'Only after three years did I go up to Jerusalem to confer with Cephas, and I stayed with him fifteen days.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 19, 'But I saw none of the other apostles except James, the Lord’s brother.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 20, 'I assure you before God that what I am writing to you is no lie.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 21, 'Later I went to the regions of Syria and Cilicia.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 22, 'I was personally unknown, however, to the churches of Judea that are in Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 23, 'They only heard the account: “The man who formerly persecuted us is now preaching the faith he once tried to destroy.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 1, 24, 'And they glorified God because of me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 1, 'Fourteen years later I went up again to Jerusalem, accompanied by Barnabas. I took Titus along also.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 2, 'I went in response to a revelation and set before them the gospel that I preach among the Gentiles. But I spoke privately to those recognized as leaders, for fear that I was running or had already run in vain.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 3, 'Yet not even Titus, who was with me, was compelled to be circumcised, even though he was a Greek.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 4, 'This issue arose because some false brothers had come in under false pretenses to spy on our freedom in Christ Jesus, in order to enslave us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 5, 'We did not give in to them for a moment, so that the truth of the gospel would remain with you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 6, 'But as for the highly esteemed—whatever they were makes no difference to me; God does not show favoritism—those leaders added nothing to me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 7, 'On the contrary, they saw that I had been entrusted to preach the gospel to the uncircumcised, just as Peter had been to the circumcised.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 8, 'For the One who was at work in Peter’s apostleship to the circumcised was also at work in my apostleship to the Gentiles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 9, 'And recognizing the grace that I had been given, James, Cephas, and John—those reputed to be pillars—gave me and Barnabas the right hand of fellowship, so that we should go to the Gentiles, and they to the circumcised.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 10, 'They only asked us to remember the poor, the very thing I was eager to do.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 11, 'When Cephas came to Antioch, however, I opposed him to his face, because he stood to be condemned.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 12, 'For before certain men came from James, he used to eat with the Gentiles. But when they arrived, he began to draw back and separate himself, for fear of those in the circumcision group.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 13, 'The other Jews joined him in his hypocrisy, so that by their hypocrisy even Barnabas was led astray.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 14, 'When I saw that they were not walking in line with the truth of the gospel, I said to Cephas in front of them all, “If you, who are a Jew, live like a Gentile and not like a Jew, how can you compel the Gentiles to live like Jews?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 15, 'We who are Jews by birth and not Gentile “sinners”'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 16, 'know that a man is not justified by works of the law, but by faith in Jesus Christ. So we, too, have believed in Christ Jesus, that we may be justified by faith in Christ and not by works of the law, because by works of the law no one will be justified.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 17, 'But if, while we seek to be justified in Christ, we ourselves are found to be sinners, does that make Christ a minister of sin? Certainly not!'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 18, 'If I rebuild what I have already torn down, I prove myself to be a lawbreaker.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 19, 'For through the law I died to the law so that I might live to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 20, 'I have been crucified with Christ, and I no longer live, but Christ lives in me. The life I live in the body, I live by faith in the Son of God, who loved me and gave Himself up for me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 2, 21, 'I do not set aside the grace of God. For if righteousness comes through the law, Christ died for nothing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 1, 'O foolish Galatians! Who has bewitched you? Before your very eyes Jesus Christ was clearly portrayed as crucified.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 2, 'I would like to learn just one thing from you: Did you receive the Spirit by works of the law, or by hearing with faith?'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 3, 'Are you so foolish? After starting in the Spirit, are you now finishing in the flesh?'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 4, 'Have you suffered so much for nothing, if it really was for nothing?'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 5, 'Does God lavish His Spirit on you and work miracles among you because you practice the law, or because you hear and believe?'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 6, 'So also, “Abraham believed God, and it was credited to him as righteousness.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 7, 'Understand, then, that those who have faith are sons of Abraham.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 8, 'The Scripture foresaw that God would justify the Gentiles by faith, and foretold the gospel to Abraham: “All nations will be blessed through you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 9, 'So those who have faith are blessed along with Abraham, the man of faith.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 10, 'All who rely on works of the law are under a curse. For it is written: “Cursed is everyone who does not continue to do everything written in the Book of the Law.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 11, 'Now it is clear that no one is justified before God by the law, because, “The righteous will live by faith.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 12, 'The law, however, is not based on faith; on the contrary, “The man who does these things will live by them.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 13, 'Christ redeemed us from the curse of the law by becoming a curse for us. For it is written: “Cursed is everyone who is hung on a tree.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 14, 'He redeemed us in order that the blessing promised to Abraham would come to the Gentiles in Christ Jesus, so that by faith we might receive the promise of the Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 15, 'Brothers, let me put this in human terms. Even a human covenant, once it is ratified, cannot be canceled or amended.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 16, 'The promises were spoken to Abraham and to his seed. The Scripture does not say, “and to seeds,” meaning many, but “and to your seed,” meaning One, who is Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 17, 'What I mean is this: The law that came 430 years later does not revoke the covenant previously established by God, so as to nullify the promise.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 18, 'For if the inheritance depends on the law, then it no longer depends on a promise; but God freely granted it to Abraham through a promise.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 19, 'Why then was the law given? It was added because of transgressions, until the arrival of the seed to whom the promise referred. It was administered through angels by a mediator.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 20, 'A mediator is unnecessary, however, for only one party; but God is one.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 21, 'Is the law, then, opposed to the promises of God? Certainly not! For if a law had been given that could impart life, then righteousness would certainly have come from the law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 22, 'But the Scripture pronounces all things confined by sin, so that by faith in Jesus Christ the promise might be given to those who believe.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 23, 'Before this faith came, we were held in custody under the law, locked up until faith should be revealed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 24, 'So the law became our guardian to lead us to Christ, that we might be justified by faith.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 25, 'Now that faith has come, we are no longer under a guardian.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 26, 'You are all sons of God through faith in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 27, 'For all of you who were baptized into Christ have clothed yourselves with Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 28, 'There is neither Jew nor Greek, slave nor free, male nor female, for you are all one in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 3, 29, 'And if you belong to Christ, then you are Abraham’s seed and heirs according to the promise.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 1, 'What I am saying is that as long as the heir is a child, he is no different from a slave, although he is the owner of everything.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 2, 'He is subject to guardians and trustees until the date set by his father.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 3, 'So also, when we were children, we were enslaved under the basic principles of the world.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 4, 'But when the time had fully come, God sent His Son, born of a woman, born under the law,'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 5, 'to redeem those under the law, that we might receive our adoption as sons.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 6, 'And because you are sons, God sent the Spirit of His Son into our hearts, crying out, “Abba, Father!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 7, 'So you are no longer a slave, but a son; and since you are a son, you are also an heir through God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 8, 'Formerly, when you did not know God, you were slaves to those who by nature are not gods.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 9, 'But now that you know God, or rather are known by God, how is it that you are turning back to those weak and worthless principles? Do you wish to be enslaved by them all over again?'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 10, 'You are observing special days and months and seasons and years!'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 11, 'I fear for you, that my efforts for you may have been in vain.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 12, 'I beg you, brothers, become like me, for I became like you. You have done me no wrong.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 13, 'You know that it was because of an illness that I first preached the gospel to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 14, 'And although my illness was a trial to you, you did not despise or reject me. Instead, you welcomed me as if I were an angel of God, as if I were Christ Jesus Himself.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 15, 'What then has become of your blessing? For I can testify that, if it were possible, you would have torn out your eyes and given them to me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 16, 'Have I now become your enemy by telling you the truth?'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 17, 'Those people are zealous for you, but not in a good way. Instead, they want to isolate you from us, so that you may be zealous for them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 18, 'Nevertheless, it is good to be zealous if it serves a noble purpose—at any time, and not only when I am with you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 19, 'My children, for whom I am again in the pains of childbirth until Christ is formed in you,'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 20, 'how I wish I could be with you now and change my tone, because I am perplexed about you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 21, 'Tell me, you who want to be under the law, do you not understand what the law says?'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 22, 'For it is written that Abraham had two sons, one by the slave woman and the other by the free woman.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 23, 'His son by the slave woman was born according to the flesh, but his son by the free woman was born through the promise.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 24, 'These things serve as illustrations, for the women represent two covenants. One covenant is from Mount Sinai and bears children into slavery: This is Hagar.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 25, 'Now Hagar stands for Mount Sinai in Arabia and corresponds to the present-day Jerusalem, because she is in slavery with her children.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 26, 'But the Jerusalem above is free, and she is our mother.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 27, 'For it is written: “Rejoice, O barren woman, who bears no children; break forth and cry aloud, you who have never travailed; because more are the children of the desolate woman than of her who has a husband.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 28, 'Now you, brothers, like Isaac, are children of promise.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 29, 'At that time, however, the son born by the flesh persecuted the son born by the Spirit. It is the same now.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 30, 'But what does the Scripture say? “Expel the slave woman and her son, for the slave woman’s son will never share in the inheritance with the free woman’s son.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 4, 31, 'Therefore, brothers, we are not children of the slave woman, but of the free woman.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 1, 'It is for freedom that Christ has set us free. Stand firm, then, and do not be encumbered once more by a yoke of slavery.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 2, 'Take notice: I, Paul, tell you that if you let yourselves be circumcised, Christ will be of no value to you at all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 3, 'Again I testify to every man who gets himself circumcised that he is obligated to obey the whole law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 4, 'You who are trying to be justified by the law have been severed from Christ; you have fallen away from grace.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 5, 'But by faith we eagerly await through the Spirit the hope of righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 6, 'For in Christ Jesus neither circumcision nor uncircumcision has any value. All that matters is faith, expressed through love.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 7, 'You were running so well. Who has obstructed you from obeying the truth?'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 8, 'Such persuasion does not come from the One who calls you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 9, 'A little leaven works through the whole batch of dough.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 10, 'I am confident in the Lord that you will take no other view. The one who is troubling you will bear the judgment, whoever he may be.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 11, 'Now, brothers, if I am still preaching circumcision, why am I still being persecuted? In that case the offense of the cross has been abolished.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 12, 'As for those who are agitating you, I wish they would proceed to emasculate themselves!'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 13, 'For you, brothers, were called to freedom; but do not use your freedom as an opportunity for the flesh. Rather, serve one another in love.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 14, 'The entire law is fulfilled in a single decree: “Love your neighbor as yourself.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 15, 'But if you keep on biting and devouring one another, watch out, or you will be consumed by one another.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 16, 'So I say, walk by the Spirit, and you will not gratify the desires of the flesh.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 17, 'For the flesh craves what is contrary to the Spirit, and the Spirit what is contrary to the flesh. They are opposed to each other, so that you do not do what you want.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 18, 'But if you are led by the Spirit, you are not under the law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 19, 'The acts of the flesh are obvious: sexual immorality, impurity, and debauchery;'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 20, 'idolatry and sorcery; hatred, discord, jealousy, and rage; rivalries, divisions, factions,'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 21, 'and envy; drunkenness, orgies, and the like. I warn you, as I did before, that those who practice such things will not inherit the kingdom of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 22, 'But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness,'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 23, 'gentleness, and self-control. Against such things there is no law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 24, 'Those who belong to Christ Jesus have crucified the flesh with its passions and desires.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 25, 'Since we live by the Spirit, let us walk in step with the Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 5, 26, 'Let us not become conceited, provoking and envying one another.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 1, 'Brothers, if someone is caught in a trespass, you who are spiritual should restore him with a spirit of gentleness. But watch yourself, or you also may be tempted.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 2, 'Carry one another’s burdens, and in this way you will fulfill the law of Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 3, 'If anyone thinks he is something when he is nothing, he deceives himself.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 4, 'Each one should test his own work. Then he will have reason to boast in himself alone, and not in someone else.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 5, 'For each one should carry his own load.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 6, 'Nevertheless, the one who receives instruction in the word must share in all good things with his instructor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 7, 'Do not be deceived: God is not to be mocked. Whatever a man sows, he will reap in return.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 8, 'The one who sows to please his flesh, from the flesh will reap destruction; but the one who sows to please the Spirit, from the Spirit will reap eternal life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 9, 'Let us not grow weary in well-doing, for in due time we will reap a harvest if we do not give up.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 10, 'Therefore, as we have opportunity, let us do good to everyone, and especially to the family of faith.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 11, 'See what large letters I am using to write to you with my own hand!');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 12, 'Those who want to make a good impression outwardly are trying to compel you to be circumcised. They only do this to avoid persecution for the cross of Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 13, 'For the circumcised do not even keep the law themselves, yet they want you to be circumcised that they may boast in your flesh.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 14, 'But as for me, may I never boast, except in the cross of our Lord Jesus Christ, through which the world has been crucified to me, and I to the world.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 15, 'For neither circumcision nor uncircumcision means anything. What counts is a new creation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 16, 'Peace and mercy to all who walk by this rule, even to the Israel of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 17, 'From now on let no one cause me trouble, for I bear on my body the marks of Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Galatians', 48, 6, 18, 'The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit, brothers. Amen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 1, 'Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, To the saints in Ephesus, the faithful in Christ Jesus:'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 2, 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 3, 'Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who has blessed us in Christ with every spiritual blessing in the heavenly realms.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 4, 'For He chose us in Him before the foundation of the world to be holy and blameless in His presence. In love'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 5, 'He predestined us for adoption as His sons through Jesus Christ, according to the good pleasure of His will,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 6, 'to the praise of His glorious grace, which He has freely given us in the Beloved One.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 7, 'In Him we have redemption through His blood, the forgiveness of our trespasses, according to the riches of His grace'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 8, 'that He lavished on us with all wisdom and understanding.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 9, 'And He has made known to us the mystery of His will according to His good pleasure, which He purposed in Christ'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 10, 'as a plan for the fullness of time, to bring all things in heaven and on earth together in Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 11, 'In Him we were also chosen as God’s own, having been predestined according to the plan of Him who works out everything by the counsel of His will,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 12, 'in order that we, who were the first to hope in Christ, would be for the praise of His glory.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 13, 'And in Him, having heard and believed the word of truth—the gospel of your salvation—you were sealed with the promised Holy Spirit,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 14, 'who is the pledge of our inheritance until the redemption of those who are God’s possession, to the praise of His glory.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 15, 'For this reason, ever since I heard about your faith in the Lord Jesus and your love for all the saints,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 16, 'I have not stopped giving thanks for you, remembering you in my prayers,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 17, 'that the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the glorious Father, may give you a spirit of wisdom and revelation in your knowledge of Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 18, 'I ask that the eyes of your heart may be enlightened, so that you may know the hope of His calling, the riches of His glorious inheritance in the saints,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 19, 'and the surpassing greatness of His power to us who believe. These are in accordance with the working of His mighty strength,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 20, 'which He exerted in Christ when He raised Him from the dead and seated Him at His right hand in the heavenly realms,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 21, 'far above all rule and authority, power and dominion, and every name that is named, not only in the present age but also in the one to come.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 22, 'And God put everything under His feet and made Him head over everything for the church,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 1, 23, 'which is His body, the fullness of Him who fills all in all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 1, 'And you were dead in your trespasses and sins,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 2, 'in which you used to walk when you conformed to the ways of this world and of the ruler of the power of the air, the spirit who is now at work in the sons of disobedience.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 3, 'All of us also lived among them at one time, fulfilling the cravings of our flesh and indulging its desires and thoughts. Like the rest, we were by nature children of wrath.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 4, 'But because of His great love for us, God, who is rich in mercy,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 5, 'made us alive with Christ even when we were dead in our trespasses. It is by grace you have been saved!'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 6, 'And God raised us up with Christ and seated us with Him in the heavenly realms in Christ Jesus,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 7, 'in order that in the coming ages He might display the surpassing riches of His grace, demonstrated by His kindness to us in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 8, 'For it is by grace you have been saved through faith, and this not from yourselves; it is the gift of God,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 9, 'not by works, so that no one can boast.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 10, 'For we are God’s workmanship, created in Christ Jesus to do good works, which God prepared in advance as our way of life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 11, 'Therefore remember that formerly you who are Gentiles in the flesh and called uncircumcised by the so-called circumcision (that done in the body by human hands)—'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 12, 'remember that at that time you were separate from Christ, alienated from the commonwealth of Israel, and strangers to the covenants of the promise, without hope and without God in the world.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 13, 'But now in Christ Jesus you who once were far away have been brought near through the blood of Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 14, 'For He Himself is our peace, who has made the two one and has torn down the dividing wall of hostility'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 15, 'by abolishing in His flesh the law of commandments and decrees. He did this to create in Himself one new man out of the two, thus making peace'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 16, 'and reconciling both of them to God in one body through the cross, by which He extinguished their hostility.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 17, 'He came and preached peace to you who were far away and peace to those who were near.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 18, 'For through Him we both have access to the Father by one Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 19, 'Therefore you are no longer strangers and foreigners, but fellow citizens with the saints and members of God’s household,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 20, 'built on the foundation of the apostles and prophets, with Christ Jesus Himself as the cornerstone.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 21, 'In Him the whole building is fitted together and grows into a holy temple in the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 2, 22, 'And in Him you too are being built together into a dwelling place for God in His Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 1, 'For this reason I, Paul, the prisoner of Christ Jesus for the sake of you Gentiles...'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 2, 'Surely you have heard about the stewardship of God’s grace that was given to me for you,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 3, 'that is, the mystery made known to me by revelation, as I have already written briefly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 4, 'In reading this, then, you will be able to understand my insight into the mystery of Christ,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 5, 'which was not made known to men in other generations as it has now been revealed by the Spirit to God’s holy apostles and prophets.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 6, 'This mystery is that through the gospel the Gentiles are fellow heirs, fellow members of the body, and fellow partakers of the promise in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 7, 'I became a servant of this gospel by the gift of God’s grace, given me through the working of His power.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 8, 'Though I am less than the least of all the saints, this grace was given me: to preach to the Gentiles the unsearchable riches of Christ,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 9, 'and to illuminate for everyone the stewardship of this mystery, which for ages past was kept hidden in God, who created all things.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 10, 'His purpose was that now, through the church, the manifold wisdom of God should be made known to the rulers and authorities in the heavenly realms,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 11, 'according to the eternal purpose that He accomplished in Christ Jesus our Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 12, 'In Him and through faith in Him we may enter God’s presence with boldness and confidence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 13, 'So I ask you not to be discouraged because of my sufferings for you, which are your glory.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 14, '... for this reason I bow my knees before the Father,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 15, 'from whom every family in heaven and on earth derives its name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 16, 'I ask that out of the riches of His glory He may strengthen you with power through His Spirit in your inner being,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 17, 'so that Christ may dwell in your hearts through faith. Then you, being rooted and grounded in love,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 18, 'will have power, together with all the saints, to comprehend the length and width and height and depth'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 19, 'of the love of Christ, and to know this love that surpasses knowledge, that you may be filled with all the fullness of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 20, 'Now to Him who is able to do immeasurably more than all we ask or imagine, according to His power that is at work within us,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 3, 21, 'to Him be the glory in the church and in Christ Jesus throughout all generations, forever and ever. Amen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 1, 'As a prisoner in the Lord, then, I urge you to walk in a manner worthy of the calling you have received:'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 2, 'with all humility and gentleness, with patience, bearing with one another in love,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 3, 'and with diligence to preserve the unity of the Spirit through the bond of peace.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 4, 'There is one body and one Spirit, just as you were called to one hope when you were called;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 5, 'one Lord, one faith, one baptism;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 6, 'one God and Father of all, who is over all and through all and in all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 7, 'Now to each one of us grace has been given according to the measure of the gift of Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 8, 'This is why it says: “When He ascended on high, He led captives away, and gave gifts to men.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 9, 'What does “He ascended” mean, except that He also descended to the lower parts of the earth?'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 10, 'He who descended is the very One who ascended above all the heavens, in order to fill all things.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 11, 'And it was He who gave some to be apostles, some to be prophets, some to be evangelists, and some to be pastors and teachers,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 12, 'to equip the saints for works of ministry and to build up the body of Christ,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 13, 'until we all reach unity in the faith and in the knowledge of the Son of God, as we mature to the full measure of the stature of Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 14, 'Then we will no longer be infants, tossed about by the waves and carried around by every wind of teaching and by the clever cunning of men in their deceitful scheming.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 15, 'Instead, speaking the truth in love, we will in all things grow up into Christ Himself, who is the head.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 16, 'From Him the whole body, fitted and held together by every supporting ligament, grows and builds itself up in love through the work of each individual part.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 17, 'So I tell you this, and insist on it in the Lord, that you must no longer walk as the Gentiles do, in the futility of their thinking.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 18, 'They are darkened in their understanding and alienated from the life of God because of the ignorance that is in them due to the hardness of their hearts.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 19, 'Having lost all sense of shame, they have given themselves over to sensuality for the practice of every kind of impurity, with a craving for more.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 20, 'But this is not the way you came to know Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 21, 'Surely you heard of Him and were taught in Him—in keeping with the truth that is in Jesus—'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 22, 'to put off your former way of life, your old self, which is being corrupted by its deceitful desires;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 23, 'to be renewed in the spirit of your minds;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 24, 'and to put on the new self, created to be like God in true righteousness and holiness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 25, 'Therefore each of you must put off falsehood and speak truthfully to his neighbor, for we are all members of one another.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 26, '“Be angry, yet do not sin.” Do not let the sun set upon your anger,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 27, 'and do not give the devil a foothold.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 28, 'He who has been stealing must steal no longer, but must work, doing good with his own hands, that he may have something to share with the one in need.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 29, 'Let no unwholesome talk come out of your mouths, but only what is helpful for building up the one in need and bringing grace to those who listen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 30, 'And do not grieve the Holy Spirit of God, in whom you were sealed for the day of redemption.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 31, 'Get rid of all bitterness, rage and anger, outcry and slander, along with every form of malice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 4, 32, 'Be kind and tenderhearted to one another, forgiving each other just as in Christ God forgave you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 1, 'Be imitators of God, therefore, as beloved children,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 2, 'and walk in love, just as Christ loved us and gave Himself up for us as a fragrant sacrificial offering to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 3, 'But among you, as is proper among the saints, there must not be even a hint of sexual immorality, or of any kind of impurity, or of greed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 4, 'Nor should there be obscenity, foolish talk, or crude joking, which are out of character, but rather thanksgiving.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 5, 'For of this you can be sure: No immoral, impure, or greedy person (that is, an idolater), has any inheritance in the kingdom of Christ and of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 6, 'Let no one deceive you with empty words, for because of such things the wrath of God is coming on the sons of disobedience.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 7, 'Therefore do not be partakers with them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 8, 'For you were once darkness, but now you are light in the Lord. Walk as children of light,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 9, 'for the fruit of the light consists in all goodness, righteousness, and truth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 10, 'Test and prove what pleases the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 11, 'Have no fellowship with the fruitless deeds of darkness, but rather expose them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 12, 'For it is shameful even to mention what the disobedient do in secret.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 13, 'But everything exposed by the light becomes visible, for everything that is illuminated becomes a light itself.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 14, 'So it is said: “Wake up, O sleeper, rise up from the dead, and Christ will shine on you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 15, 'Pay careful attention, then, to how you walk, not as unwise but as wise,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 16, 'redeeming the time, because the days are evil.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 17, 'Therefore do not be foolish, but understand what the Lord’s will is.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 18, 'Do not get drunk on wine, which leads to reckless indiscretion. Instead, be filled with the Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 19, 'Speak to one another with psalms, hymns, and spiritual songs. Sing and make music in your hearts to the Lord,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 20, 'always giving thanks to God the Father for everything in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 21, 'Submit to one another out of reverence for Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 22, 'Wives, submit to your husbands as to the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 23, 'For the husband is the head of the wife as Christ is the head of the church, His body, of which He is the Savior.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 24, 'Now as the church submits to Christ, so also wives should submit to their husbands in everything.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 25, 'Husbands, love your wives, just as Christ loved the church and gave Himself up for her'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 26, 'to sanctify her, cleansing her by the washing with water through the word,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 27, 'and to present her to Himself as a glorious church, without stain or wrinkle or any such blemish, but holy and blameless.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 28, 'In the same way, husbands ought to love their wives as their own bodies. He who loves his wife loves himself.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 29, 'Indeed, no one ever hated his own body, but he nourishes and cherishes it, just as Christ does the church.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 30, 'For we are members of His body.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 31, '“For this reason a man will leave his father and mother and be united to his wife, and the two will become one flesh.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 32, 'This mystery is profound, but I am speaking about Christ and the church.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 5, 33, 'Nevertheless, each one of you also must love his wife as he loves himself, and the wife must respect her husband.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 1, 'Children, obey your parents in the Lord, for this is right.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 2, '“Honor your father and mother” (which is the first commandment with a promise),'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 3, '“that it may go well with you and that you may have a long life on the earth.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 4, 'Fathers, do not provoke your children to wrath; instead, bring them up in the discipline and instruction of the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 5, 'Slaves, obey your earthly masters with respect and fear and sincerity of heart, just as you would obey Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 6, 'And do this not only to please them while they are watching, but as servants of Christ, doing the will of God from your heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 7, 'Serve with good will, as to the Lord and not to men,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 8, 'because you know that the Lord will reward each one for whatever good he does, whether he is slave or free.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 9, 'And masters, do the same for your slaves. Give up your use of threats, because you know that He who is both their Master and yours is in heaven, and there is no favoritism with Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 10, 'Finally, be strong in the Lord and in His mighty power.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 11, 'Put on the full armor of God, so that you can make your stand against the devil’s schemes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 12, 'For our struggle is not against flesh and blood, but against the rulers, against the authorities, against the powers of this world’s darkness, and against the spiritual forces of evil in the heavenly realms.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 13, 'Therefore take up the full armor of God, so that when the day of evil comes, you will be able to stand your ground, and having done everything, to stand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 14, 'Stand firm then, with the belt of truth buckled around your waist, with the breastplate of righteousness arrayed,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 15, 'and with your feet fitted with the readiness of the gospel of peace.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 16, 'In addition to all this, take up the shield of faith, with which you can extinguish all the flaming arrows of the evil one.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 17, 'And take the helmet of salvation and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 18, 'Pray in the Spirit at all times, with every kind of prayer and petition. To this end, stay alert with all perseverance in your prayers for all the saints.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 19, 'Pray also for me, that whenever I open my mouth, words may be given me so that I will boldly make known the mystery of the gospel,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 20, 'for which I am an ambassador in chains. Pray that I may proclaim it fearlessly, as I should.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 21, 'Tychicus, the beloved brother and faithful servant in the Lord, will tell you everything, so that you also may know about me and what I am doing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 22, 'I have sent him to you for this very purpose, that you may know about us, and that he may encourage your hearts.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 23, 'Peace to the brothers and love with faith from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ephesians', 49, 6, 24, 'Grace to all who love our Lord Jesus Christ with an undying love.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 1, 'Paul and Timothy, servants of Christ Jesus, To all the saints in Christ Jesus at Philippi, together with the overseers and deacons:'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 2, 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 3, 'I thank my God every time I remember you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 4, 'In every prayer for all of you, I always pray with joy,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 5, 'because of your partnership in the gospel from the first day until now,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 6, 'being confident of this, that He who began a good work in you will carry it on to completion until the day of Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 7, 'It is right for me to feel this way about all of you, since I have you in my heart. For in my chains and in my defense and confirmation of the gospel, you are all partners in grace with me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 8, 'God is my witness how I long for all of you with the affection of Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 9, 'And this is my prayer: that your love may abound more and more in knowledge and depth of insight,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 10, 'so that you may be able to test and prove what is best and may be pure and blameless for the day of Christ,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 11, 'filled with the fruit of righteousness that comes through Jesus Christ, to the glory and praise of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 12, 'Now I want you to know, brothers, that my circumstances have actually served to advance the gospel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 13, 'As a result, it has become clear throughout the whole palace guard and to everyone else that I am in chains for Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 14, 'And most of the brothers, confident in the Lord by my chains, now dare more greatly to speak the word without fear.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 15, 'It is true that some preach Christ out of envy and rivalry, but others out of goodwill.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 16, 'The latter do so in love, knowing that I am appointed for the defense of the gospel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 17, 'The former, however, preach Christ out of selfish ambition, not sincerely, supposing that they can add to the distress of my chains.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 18, 'What then is the issue? Just this: that in every way, whether by false motives or true, Christ is preached. And in this I rejoice. Yes, and I will continue to rejoice,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 19, 'because I know that through your prayers and the provision of the Spirit of Jesus Christ, my distress will turn out for my deliverance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 20, 'I eagerly expect and hope that I will in no way be ashamed, but will have complete boldness so that now as always Christ will be exalted in my body, whether by life or by death.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 21, 'For to me, to live is Christ, and to die is gain.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 22, 'But if I go on living in the body, this will mean fruitful labor for me. So what shall I choose? I do not know.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 23, 'I am torn between the two. I desire to depart and be with Christ, which is far better indeed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 24, 'But it is more necessary for you that I remain in the body.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 25, 'Convinced of this, I know that I will remain and will continue with all of you for your progress and joy in the faith,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 26, 'so that through my coming to you again your exultation in Christ Jesus will resound on account of me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 27, 'Nevertheless, conduct yourselves in a manner worthy of the gospel of Christ. Then, whether I come and see you or only hear about you in my absence, I will know that you stand firm in one spirit, contending side by side for the faith of the gospel,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 28, 'without being frightened in any way by those who oppose you. This is a clear sign of their destruction but of your salvation, and it is from God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 29, 'For it has been granted to you on behalf of Christ not only to believe in Him, but also to suffer for Him,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 1, 30, 'since you are encountering the same struggle you saw I had, and now hear that I still have.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 1, 'Therefore if you have any encouragement in Christ, if any comfort from His love, if any fellowship with the Spirit, if any affection and compassion,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 2, 'then make my joy complete by being like-minded, having the same love, being united in spirit and purpose.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 3, 'Do nothing out of selfish ambition or empty pride, but in humility consider others more important than yourselves.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 4, 'Each of you should look not only to your own interests, but also to the interests of others.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 5, 'Let this mind be in you which was also in Christ Jesus:'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 6, 'Who, existing in the form of God, did not consider equality with God something to be grasped,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 7, 'but emptied Himself, taking the form of a servant, being made in human likeness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 8, 'And being found in appearance as a man, He humbled Himself and became obedient to death— even death on a cross.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 9, 'Therefore God exalted Him to the highest place and gave Him the name above all names,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 10, 'that at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, in heaven and on earth and under the earth,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 11, 'and every tongue confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 12, 'Therefore, my beloved, just as you have always obeyed, not only in my presence, but now even more in my absence, continue to work out your salvation with fear and trembling.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 13, 'For it is God who works in you to will and to act on behalf of His good purpose.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 14, 'Do everything without complaining or arguing,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 15, 'so that you may be blameless and pure, children of God without fault in a crooked and perverse generation, in which you shine as lights in the world'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 16, 'as you hold forth the word of life, in order that I may boast on the day of Christ that I did not run or labor in vain.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 17, 'But even if I am being poured out like a drink offering on the sacrifice and service of your faith, I am glad and rejoice with all of you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 18, 'So you too should be glad and rejoice with me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 19, 'Now I hope in the Lord Jesus to send Timothy to you soon, that I also may be cheered when I learn how you are doing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 20, 'I have nobody else like him who will genuinely care for your needs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 21, 'For all the others look after their own interests, not those of Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 22, 'But you know Timothy’s proven worth, that as a child with his father he has served with me to advance the gospel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 23, 'So I hope to send him as soon as I see what happens with me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 24, 'And I trust in the Lord that I myself will come soon.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 25, 'But I thought it necessary to send back to you Epaphroditus, my brother, fellow worker, and fellow soldier, who is also your messenger and minister to my needs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 26, 'For he has been longing for all of you and is distressed because you heard he was ill.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 27, 'He was sick indeed, nearly unto death. But God had mercy on him, and not only on him but also on me, to spare me sorrow upon sorrow.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 28, 'Therefore I am all the more eager to send him, so that when you see him again you may rejoice, and I may be less anxious.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 29, 'Welcome him in the Lord with great joy, and honor men like him,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 2, 30, 'because he nearly died for the work of Christ, risking his life to make up for your deficit of service to me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 1, 'Finally, my brothers, rejoice in the Lord. It is no trouble for me to write the same things to you again, and it is a safeguard for you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 2, 'Watch out for those dogs, those workers of evil, those mutilators of the flesh!'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 3, 'For it is we who are the circumcision, we who worship by the Spirit of God, who glory in Christ Jesus, and who put no confidence in the flesh—'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 4, 'though I myself could have such confidence. If anyone else thinks he has grounds for confidence in the flesh, I have more:'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 5, 'circumcised on the eighth day, of the people of Israel, of the tribe of Benjamin; a Hebrew of Hebrews; as to the law, a Pharisee;'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 6, 'as to zeal, persecuting the church; as to righteousness in the law, faultless.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 7, 'But whatever was gain to me I count as loss for the sake of Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 8, 'More than that, I count all things as loss compared to the surpassing excellence of knowing Christ Jesus my Lord, for whom I have lost all things. I consider them rubbish, that I may gain Christ'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 9, 'and be found in Him, not having my own righteousness from the law, but that which is through faith in Christ, the righteousness from God on the basis of faith.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 10, 'I want to know Christ and the power of His resurrection and the fellowship of His sufferings, being conformed to Him in His death,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 11, 'and so, somehow, to attain to the resurrection from the dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 12, 'Not that I have already obtained all this, or have already been made perfect, but I press on to take hold of that for which Christ Jesus took hold of me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 13, 'Brothers, I do not consider myself yet to have taken hold of it. But one thing I do: Forgetting what is behind and straining toward what is ahead,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 14, 'I press on toward the goal to win the prize of God’s heavenly calling in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 15, 'All of us who are mature should embrace this point of view. And if you think differently about some issue, God will reveal this to you as well.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 16, 'Nevertheless, we must live up to what we have already attained.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 17, 'Join one another in following my example, brothers, and carefully observe those who walk according to the pattern we set for you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 18, 'For as I have often told you before, and now say again even with tears: Many live as enemies of the cross of Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 19, 'Their end is destruction, their god is their belly, and their glory is in their shame. Their minds are set on earthly things.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 20, 'But our citizenship is in heaven, and we eagerly await a Savior from there, the Lord Jesus Christ,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 3, 21, 'who, by the power that enables Him to subject all things to Himself, will transform our lowly bodies to be like His glorious body.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 1, 'Therefore, my brothers, whom I love and long for, my joy and crown, that is how you must stand firm in the Lord, my beloved.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 2, 'I urge Euodia and Syntyche to agree with each other in the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 3, 'Yes, and I ask you, my true yokefellow, to help these women who have labored with me for the gospel, along with Clement and the rest of my fellow workers, whose names are in the Book of Life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 4, 'Rejoice in the Lord always. I will say it again: Rejoice!'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 5, 'Let your gentleness be apparent to all. The Lord is near.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 6, 'Be anxious for nothing, but in everything, by prayer and petition, with thanksgiving, present your requests to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 7, 'And the peace of God, which surpasses all understanding, will guard your hearts and your minds in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 8, 'Finally, brothers, whatever is true, whatever is honorable, whatever is right, whatever is pure, whatever is lovely, whatever is admirable—if anything is excellent or praiseworthy—think on these things.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 9, 'Whatever you have learned or received or heard from me, or seen in me, put it into practice. And the God of peace will be with you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 10, 'Now I rejoice greatly in the Lord that at last you have revived your concern for me. You were indeed concerned, but you had no opportunity to show it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 11, 'I am not saying this out of need, for I have learned to be content regardless of my circumstances.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 12, 'I know how to live humbly, and I know how to abound. I am accustomed to any and every situation—to being filled and being hungry, to having plenty and having need.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 13, 'I can do all things through Christ who gives me strength.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 14, 'Nevertheless, you have done well to share in my affliction.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 15, 'And as you Philippians know, in the early days of the gospel, when I left Macedonia, no church but you partnered with me in the matter of giving and receiving.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 16, 'For even while I was in Thessalonica, you provided for my needs again and again.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 17, 'Not that I am seeking a gift, but I am looking for the fruit that may be credited to your account.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 18, 'I have all I need and more, now that I have received your gifts from Epaphroditus. They are a fragrant offering, an acceptable sacrifice, well-pleasing to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 19, 'And my God will supply all your needs according to His glorious riches in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 20, 'To our God and Father be glory forever and ever. Amen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 21, 'Greet all the saints in Christ Jesus. The brothers who are with me send you greetings.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 22, 'All the saints send you greetings, especially those from the household of Caesar.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philippians', 50, 4, 23, 'The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 1, 'Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, and Timothy our brother,'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 2, 'To the saints and faithful brothers in Christ at Colossae: Grace and peace to you from God our Father.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 3, 'We always thank God, the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, when we pray for you,'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 4, 'because we have heard about your faith in Christ Jesus and your love for all the saints—'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 5, 'the faith and love proceeding from the hope stored up for you in heaven, of which you have already heard in the word of truth, the gospel'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 6, 'that has come to you. All over the world this gospel is bearing fruit and growing, just as it has been doing among you since the day you heard it and truly understood the grace of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 7, 'You learned it from Epaphras, our beloved fellow servant, who is a faithful minister of Christ on our behalf,'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 8, 'and who also informed us of your love in the Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 9, 'For this reason, since the day we heard about you, we have not stopped praying for you and asking God to fill you with the knowledge of His will in all spiritual wisdom and understanding,'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 10, 'so that you may walk in a manner worthy of the Lord and may please Him in every way: bearing fruit in every good work, growing in the knowledge of God,'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 11, 'being strengthened with all power according to His glorious might so that you may have full endurance and patience, and joyfully'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 12, 'giving thanks to the Father, who has qualified you to share in the inheritance of the saints in the light.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 13, 'He has rescued us from the dominion of darkness and brought us into the kingdom of His beloved Son,'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 14, 'in whom we have redemption, the forgiveness of sins.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 15, 'The Son is the image of the invisible God, the firstborn over all creation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 16, 'For in Him all things were created, things in heaven and on earth, visible and invisible, whether thrones or dominions or rulers or authorities. All things were created through Him and for Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 17, 'He is before all things, and in Him all things hold together.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 18, 'And He is the head of the body, the church; He is the beginning and firstborn from among the dead, so that in all things He may have preeminence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 19, 'For God was pleased to have all His fullness dwell in Him,'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 20, 'and through Him to reconcile to Himself all things, whether things on earth or things in heaven, by making peace through the blood of His cross.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 21, 'Once you were alienated from God and were hostile in your minds, engaging in evil deeds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 22, 'But now He has reconciled you by Christ’s physical body through death to present you holy, unblemished, and blameless in His presence—'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 23, 'if indeed you continue in your faith, established and firm, not moved from the hope of the gospel you heard, which has been proclaimed to every creature under heaven, and of which I, Paul, have become a servant.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 24, 'Now I rejoice in my sufferings for you, and I fill up in my flesh what is lacking in regard to Christ’s afflictions for the sake of His body, which is the church.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 25, 'I became its servant by the commission God gave me to fully proclaim to you the word of God,'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 26, 'the mystery that was hidden for ages and generations but is now revealed to His saints.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 27, 'To them God has chosen to make known among the Gentiles the glorious riches of this mystery, which is Christ in you, the hope of glory.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 28, 'We proclaim Him, admonishing and teaching everyone with all wisdom, so that we may present everyone perfect in Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 1, 29, 'To this end I also labor, striving with all His energy working powerfully within me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 1, 'For I want you to know how much I am struggling for you and for those at Laodicea, and for all who have not met me face to face,'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 2, 'that they may be encouraged in heart, knit together in love, and filled with the full riches of complete understanding, so that they may know the mystery of God, namely Christ,'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 3, 'in whom are hidden all the treasures of wisdom and knowledge.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 4, 'I say this so that no one will deceive you by smooth rhetoric.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 5, 'For although I am absent from you in body, I am present with you in spirit, and I delight to see your orderly condition and firm faith in Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 6, 'Therefore, just as you have received Christ Jesus as Lord, continue to walk in Him,'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 7, 'rooted and built up in Him, established in the faith as you were taught, and overflowing with thankfulness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 8, 'See to it that no one takes you captive through philosophy and empty deception, which are based on human tradition and the spiritual forces of the world rather than on Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 9, 'For in Christ all the fullness of the Deity dwells in bodily form.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 10, 'And you have been made complete in Christ, who is the head over every ruler and authority.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 11, 'In Him you were also circumcised, in the putting off of your sinful nature, with the circumcision performed by Christ and not by human hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 12, 'And having been buried with Him in baptism, you were raised with Him through your faith in the power of God, who raised Him from the dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 13, 'When you were dead in your trespasses and in the uncircumcision of your sinful nature, God made you alive with Christ. He forgave us all our trespasses,'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 14, 'having canceled the debt ascribed to us in the decrees that stood against us. He took it away, nailing it to the cross!'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 15, 'And having disarmed the powers and authorities, He made a public spectacle of them, triumphing over them by the cross.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 16, 'Therefore let no one judge you by what you eat or drink, or with regard to a feast, a New Moon, or a Sabbath.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 17, 'These are a shadow of the things to come, but the body that casts it belongs to Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 18, 'Do not let anyone who delights in false humility and the worship of angels disqualify you with speculation about what he has seen. Such a person is puffed up without basis by his unspiritual mind.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 19, 'He has lost connection to the head, from whom the whole body, supported and knit together by its joints and ligaments, grows as God causes it to grow.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 20, 'If you have died with Christ to the spiritual forces of the world, why, as though you still belonged to the world, do you submit to its regulations:'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 21, '“Do not handle, do not taste, do not touch!”?'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 22, 'These will all perish with use, because they are based on human commands and teachings.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 2, 23, 'Such restrictions indeed have an appearance of wisdom, with their self-prescribed worship, their false humility, and their harsh treatment of the body; but they are of no value against the indulgence of the flesh.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 1, 'Therefore, since you have been raised with Christ, strive for the things above, where Christ is seated at the right hand of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 2, 'Set your minds on things above, not on earthly things.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 3, 'For you died, and your life is now hidden with Christ in God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 4, 'When Christ, who is your life, appears, then you also will appear with Him in glory.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 5, 'Put to death, therefore, the components of your earthly nature: sexual immorality, impurity, lust, evil desires, and greed, which is idolatry.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 6, 'Because of these, the wrath of God is coming on the sons of disobedience.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 7, 'When you lived among them, you also used to walk in these ways.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 8, 'But now you must put aside all such things as these: anger, rage, malice, slander, and filthy language from your lips.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 9, 'Do not lie to one another, since you have taken off the old self with its practices,'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 10, 'and have put on the new self, which is being renewed in knowledge in the image of its Creator.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 11, 'Here there is no Greek or Jew, circumcised or uncircumcised, barbarian, Scythian, slave, or free, but Christ is all and is in all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 12, 'Therefore, as the elect of God, holy and beloved, clothe yourselves with hearts of compassion, kindness, humility, gentleness, and patience.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 13, 'Bear with one another and forgive any complaint you may have against someone else. Forgive as the Lord forgave you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 14, 'And over all these virtues put on love, which is the bond of perfect unity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 15, 'Let the peace of Christ rule in your hearts, for to this you were called as members of one body. And be thankful.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 16, 'Let the word of Christ richly dwell within you as you teach and admonish one another with all wisdom, and as you sing psalms, hymns, and spiritual songs with gratitude in your hearts to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 17, 'And whatever you do, in word or deed, do it all in the name of the Lord Jesus, giving thanks to God the Father through Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 18, 'Wives, submit to your husbands, as is fitting in the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 19, 'Husbands, love your wives and do not be harsh with them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 20, 'Children, obey your parents in everything, for this is pleasing to the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 21, 'Fathers, do not provoke your children, so they will not become discouraged.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 22, 'Slaves, obey your earthly masters in everything, not only to please them while they are watching, but with sincerity of heart and fear of the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 23, 'Whatever you do, work at it with your whole being, for the Lord and not for men,'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 24, 'because you know that you will receive an inheritance from the Lord as your reward. It is the Lord Christ you are serving.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 3, 25, 'Whoever does wrong will be repaid for his wrong, and there is no favoritism.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 1, 'Masters, supply your slaves with what is right and fair, since you know that you also have a Master in heaven.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 2, 'Devote yourselves to prayer, being watchful and thankful,'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 3, 'as you pray also for us, that God may open to us a door for the word, so that we may proclaim the mystery of Christ, for which I am in chains.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 4, 'Pray that I may declare it clearly, as I should.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 5, 'Act wisely toward outsiders, redeeming the time.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 6, 'Let your speech always be gracious, seasoned with salt, so that you may know how to answer everyone.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 7, 'Tychicus will tell you all the news about me. He is a beloved brother, a faithful minister, and a fellow servant in the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 8, 'I have sent him to you for this very purpose, that you may know about us, and that he may encourage your hearts.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 9, 'With him I am sending Onesimus, our faithful and beloved brother, who is one of you. They will tell you about everything here.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 10, 'My fellow prisoner Aristarchus sends you greetings, as does Mark the cousin of Barnabas. You have already received instructions about him: If he comes to you, welcome him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 11, 'Jesus, who is called Justus, also sends greetings. These are the only Jews among my fellow workers for the kingdom of God, and they have been a comfort to me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 12, 'Epaphras, who is one of you and a servant of Christ Jesus, sends you greetings. He is always wrestling in prayer for you, so that you may stand mature and fully assured in the full will of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 13, 'For I testify about him that he goes to great pains for you and for those at Laodicea and Hierapolis.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 14, 'Luke, the beloved physician, and Demas send you greetings.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 15, 'Greet the brothers in Laodicea, as well as Nympha and the church that meets at her house.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 16, 'After this letter has been read among you, make sure that it is also read in the church of the Laodiceans, and that you in turn read the letter from Laodicea.'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 17, 'Tell Archippus: “See to it that you complete the ministry you have received in the Lord.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Colossians', 51, 4, 18, 'This greeting is in my own hand—Paul. Remember my chains. Grace be with you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 1, 1, 'Paul, Silvanus, and Timothy, To the church of the Thessalonians in God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ: Grace and peace to you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 1, 2, 'We always thank God for all of you, remembering you in our prayers'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 1, 3, 'and continually recalling before our God and Father your work of faith, your labor of love, and your enduring hope in our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 1, 4, 'Brothers who are beloved by God, we know that He has chosen you,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 1, 5, 'because our gospel came to you not only in word, but also in power, in the Holy Spirit, and with great conviction—just as you know we lived among you for your sake.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 1, 6, 'And you became imitators of us and of the Lord when you welcomed the message with the joy of the Holy Spirit, in spite of your great suffering.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 1, 7, 'As a result, you have become an example to all the believers in Macedonia and Achaia.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 1, 8, 'For not only did the message of the Lord ring out from you to Macedonia and Achaia, but your faith in God has gone out to every place, so that we have no need to say anything more.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 1, 9, 'For they themselves report what kind of welcome you gave us, and how you turned to God from idols to serve the living and true God'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 1, 10, 'and to await His Son from heaven, whom He raised from the dead—Jesus our deliverer from the coming wrath.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 1, 'You yourselves know, brothers, that our visit to you was not in vain.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 2, 'As you are aware, we had already endured suffering and shameful treatment in Philippi. But in the face of strong opposition, we were bold in our God to speak to you the gospel of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 3, 'For our appeal does not arise from deceit or ulterior motives or trickery.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 4, 'Instead, we speak as those approved by God to be entrusted with the gospel, not in order to please men but God, who examines our hearts.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 5, 'As you know, we never used words of flattery or any pretext for greed. God is our witness!'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 6, 'Nor did we seek praise from you or from anyone else, although as apostles of Christ we had authority to demand it.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 7, 'On the contrary, we were gentle among you, like a nursing mother caring for her children.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 8, 'We cared so deeply that we were delighted to share with you not only the gospel of God, but our own lives as well. That is how beloved you have become to us.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 9, 'Surely you recall, brothers, our labor and toil. We worked night and day so that we would not be a burden to anyone while we proclaimed to you the gospel of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 10, 'You are witnesses, and so is God, of how holy, righteous, and blameless our conduct was among you who believed.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 11, 'For you know that we treated each of you as a father treats his own children—'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 12, 'encouraging you, comforting you, and urging you to walk in a manner worthy of God, who calls you into His own kingdom and glory.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 13, 'And we continually thank God because, when you received the word of God that you heard from us, you accepted it not as the word of men, but as the true word of God—the word which is now at work in you who believe.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 14, 'For you, brothers, became imitators of the churches of God in Judea that are in Christ Jesus. You suffered from your own countrymen the very things they suffered from the Jews,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 15, 'who killed both the Lord Jesus and their own prophets, and drove us out as well. They are displeasing to God and hostile to all men,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 16, 'hindering us from telling the Gentiles how they may be saved. As a result, they continue to heap up their sins to full capacity; the utmost wrath has come upon them.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 17, 'Brothers, although we were torn away from you for a short time (in person, not in heart), our desire to see you face to face was even more intense.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 18, 'For we wanted to come to you—indeed I, Paul, tried again and again—but Satan obstructed us.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 19, 'After all, who is our hope, our joy, our crown of boasting, if it is not you yourselves in the presence of our Lord Jesus at His coming?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 2, 20, 'You are indeed our glory and our joy.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 3, 1, 'So when we could bear it no longer, we were willing to be left on our own in Athens.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 3, 2, 'We sent Timothy, our brother and fellow worker for God in the gospel of Christ, to strengthen and encourage you in your faith,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 3, 3, 'so that none of you would be shaken by these trials. For you know that we are destined for this.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 3, 4, 'Indeed, when we were with you, we kept warning you that we would suffer persecution; and as you know, it has come to pass.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 3, 5, 'For this reason, when I could bear it no longer, I sent to find out about your faith, for fear that the tempter had somehow tempted you and caused our labor to be in vain.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 3, 6, 'But just now, Timothy has returned from his visit with the good news about your faith, your love, and the fond memories you have preserved, longing to see us just as we long to see you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 3, 7, 'For this reason, brothers, in all our distress and persecution, we have been reassured about you, because of your faith.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 3, 8, 'For now we can go on living, as long as you are standing firm in the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 3, 9, 'How can we adequately thank God for you in return for our great joy over you in His presence?');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 3, 10, 'Night and day we pray most earnestly that we may see you face to face and supply what is lacking from your faith.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 3, 11, 'Now may our God and Father Himself, and our Lord Jesus, direct our way to you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 3, 12, 'And may the Lord cause you to increase and overflow with love for one another and for everyone else, just as our love for you overflows,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 3, 13, 'so that He may establish your hearts in blamelessness and holiness before our God and Father at the coming of our Lord Jesus with all His saints. Amen.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 1, 'Finally, brothers, we ask and encourage you in the Lord Jesus to live in a way that is pleasing to God, just as you have received from us. This is how you already live, so you should do so all the more.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 2, 'For you know the instructions we gave you by the authority of the Lord Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 3, 'For it is God’s will that you should be holy: You must abstain from sexual immorality;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 4, 'each of you must know how to control his own body in holiness and honor,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 5, 'not in lustful passion like the Gentiles who do not know God;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 6, 'and no one should ever violate or exploit his brother in this regard, because the Lord will avenge all such acts, as we have already told you and solemnly warned you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 7, 'For God has not called us to impurity, but to holiness.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 8, 'Anyone, then, who rejects this command does not reject man but God, the very One who gives you His Holy Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 9, 'Now about brotherly love, you do not need anyone to write to you, because you yourselves have been taught by God to love one another.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 10, 'And you are indeed showing this love to all the brothers throughout Macedonia. But we urge you, brothers, to excel more and more'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 11, 'and to aspire to live quietly, to attend to your own matters, and to work with your own hands, as we instructed you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 12, 'Then you will behave properly toward outsiders, without being dependent on anyone.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 13, 'Brothers, we do not want you to be uninformed about those who sleep in death, so that you will not grieve like the rest, who are without hope.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 14, 'For since we believe that Jesus died and rose again, we also believe that God will bring with Jesus those who have fallen asleep in Him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 15, 'By the word of the Lord, we declare to you that we who are alive and remain until the coming of the Lord will by no means precede those who have fallen asleep.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 16, 'For the Lord Himself will descend from heaven with a loud command, with the voice of an archangel, and with the trumpet of God, and the dead in Christ will be the first to rise.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 17, 'After that, we who are alive and remain will be caught up together with them in the clouds to meet the Lord in the air. And so we will always be with the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 4, 18, 'Therefore encourage one another with these words.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 1, 'Now about the times and seasons, brothers, we do not need to write to you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 2, 'For you are fully aware that the Day of the Lord will come like a thief in the night.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 3, 'While people are saying, “Peace and security,” destruction will come upon them suddenly, like labor pains on a pregnant woman, and they will not escape.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 4, 'But you, brothers, are not in the darkness so that this day should overtake you like a thief.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 5, 'For you are all sons of the light and sons of the day; we do not belong to the night or to the darkness.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 6, 'So then, let us not sleep as the others do, but let us remain awake and sober.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 7, 'For those who sleep, sleep at night; and those who get drunk, get drunk at night.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 8, 'But since we belong to the day, let us be sober, putting on the breastplate of faith and love, and the helmet of our hope of salvation.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 9, 'For God has not appointed us to suffer wrath, but to obtain salvation through our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 10, 'He died for us so that, whether we are awake or asleep, we may live together with Him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 11, 'Therefore encourage and build one another up, just as you are already doing.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 12, 'But we ask you, brothers, to acknowledge those who work diligently among you, who preside over you in the Lord and give you instruction.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 13, 'In love, hold them in highest regard because of their work. Live in peace with one another.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 14, 'And we urge you, brothers, to admonish the unruly, encourage the fainthearted, help the weak, and be patient with everyone.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 15, 'Make sure that no one repays evil for evil. Always pursue what is good for one another and for all people.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 16, 'Rejoice at all times.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 17, 'Pray without ceasing.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 18, 'Give thanks in every circumstance, for this is God’s will for you in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 19, 'Do not extinguish the Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 20, 'Do not treat prophecies with contempt,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 21, 'but test all things. Hold fast to what is good.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 22, 'Abstain from every form of evil.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 23, 'Now may the God of peace Himself sanctify you completely, and may your entire spirit, soul, and body be kept blameless at the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 24, 'The One who calls you is faithful, and He will do it.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 25, 'Brothers, pray for us as well.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 26, 'Greet all the brothers with a holy kiss.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 27, 'I charge you before the Lord to have this letter read to all the brothers.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Thessalonians', 52, 5, 28, 'The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 1, 1, 'Paul, Silvanus, and Timothy, To the church of the Thessalonians in God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ:'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 1, 2, 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 1, 3, 'We are obligated to thank God for you all the time, brothers, as is fitting, because your faith is growing more and more, and your love for one another is increasing.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 1, 4, 'That is why we boast among God’s churches about your perseverance and faith in the face of all the persecution and affliction you are enduring.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 1, 5, 'All this is clear evidence of God’s righteous judgment. And so you will be counted worthy of the kingdom of God, for which you are suffering.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 1, 6, 'After all, it is only right for God to repay with affliction those who afflict you,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 1, 7, 'and to grant relief to you who are oppressed and to us as well. This will take place when the Lord Jesus is revealed from heaven with His mighty angels'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 1, 8, 'in blazing fire, inflicting vengeance on those who do not know God and do not obey the gospel of our Lord Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 1, 9, 'They will suffer the penalty of eternal destruction, separated from the presence of the Lord and the glory of His might,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 1, 10, 'on the day He comes to be glorified in His saints and regarded with wonder by all who have believed, including you who have believed our testimony.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 1, 11, 'To this end, we always pray for you, that our God will count you worthy of His calling, and that He will powerfully fulfill your every good desire and work of faith,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 1, 12, 'so that the name of our Lord Jesus will be glorified in you, and you in Him, according to the grace of our God and of the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 2, 1, 'Now concerning the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ and our being gathered together to Him, we ask you, brothers,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 2, 2, 'not to be easily disconcerted or alarmed by any spirit or message or letter seeming to be from us, alleging that the Day of the Lord has already come.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 2, 3, 'Let no one deceive you in any way, for it will not come until the rebellion occurs and the man of lawlessness—the son of destruction—is revealed.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 2, 4, 'He will oppose and exalt himself above every so-called god or object of worship. So he will seat himself in the temple of God, proclaiming himself to be God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 2, 5, 'Do you not remember that I told you these things while I was still with you?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 2, 6, 'And you know what is now restraining him, so that he may be revealed at the proper time.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 2, 7, 'For the mystery of lawlessness is already at work, but the one who now restrains it will continue until he is taken out of the way.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 2, 8, 'And then the lawless one will be revealed, whom the Lord Jesus will slay with the breath of His mouth and annihilate by the majesty of His arrival.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 2, 9, 'The coming of the lawless one will be accompanied by the working of Satan, with every kind of power, sign, and false wonder,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 2, 10, 'and with every wicked deception directed against those who are perishing, because they refused the love of the truth that would have saved them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 2, 11, 'For this reason God will send them a powerful delusion so that they believe the lie,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 2, 12, 'in order that judgment may come upon all who have disbelieved the truth and delighted in wickedness.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 2, 13, 'But we should always thank God for you, brothers who are loved by the Lord, because God has chosen you from the beginning to be saved by the sanctification of the Spirit and by faith in the truth.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 2, 14, 'To this He called you through our gospel, so that you may share in the glory of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 2, 15, 'Therefore, brothers, stand firm and cling to the traditions we taught you, whether by speech or by letter.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 2, 16, 'Now may our Lord Jesus Christ Himself and God our Father, who by grace has loved us and given us eternal comfort and good hope,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 2, 17, 'encourage your hearts and strengthen you in every good word and deed.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 1, 'Finally, brothers, pray for us, that the word of the Lord may spread quickly and be held in honor, just as it was with you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 2, 'And pray that we may be delivered from wicked and evil men; for not everyone holds to the faith.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 3, 'But the Lord is faithful, and He will strengthen you and guard you from the evil one.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 4, 'And we have confidence in the Lord that you are doing and will continue to do what we command.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 5, 'May the Lord direct your hearts into God’s love and Christ’s perseverance.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 6, 'Now we command you, brothers, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, to keep away from any brother who leads an undisciplined life that is not in keeping with the tradition you received from us.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 7, 'For you yourselves know how you ought to imitate us, because we were not undisciplined among you,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 8, 'nor did we eat anyone’s food without paying for it. Instead, in labor and toil, we worked night and day so that we would not be a burden to any of you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 9, 'Not that we lack this right, but we wanted to offer ourselves as an example for you to imitate.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 10, 'For even while we were with you, we gave you this command: “If anyone is unwilling to work, he shall not eat.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 11, 'Yet we hear that some of you are leading undisciplined lives and accomplishing nothing but being busybodies.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 12, 'We command and urge such people by our Lord Jesus Christ to begin working quietly to earn their own living.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 13, 'But as for you, brothers, do not grow weary in well-doing.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 14, 'Take note of anyone who does not obey the instructions we have given in this letter. Do not associate with him, so that he may be ashamed.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 15, 'Yet do not regard him as an enemy, but warn him as a brother.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 16, 'Now may the Lord of peace Himself give you peace at all times and in every way. The Lord be with all of you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 17, 'This greeting is in my own hand—Paul. This is my mark in every letter; it is the way I write.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Thessalonians', 53, 3, 18, 'The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with all of you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 1, 'Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the command of God our Savior and of Christ Jesus our hope,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 2, 'To Timothy, my true child in the faith: Grace, mercy, and peace from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Lord.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 3, 'As I urged you on my departure to Macedonia, you should stay on at Ephesus to instruct certain men not to teach false doctrines'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 4, 'or devote themselves to myths and endless genealogies, which promote speculation rather than the stewardship of God’s work, which is by faith.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 5, 'The goal of our instruction is the love that comes from a pure heart, a clear conscience, and a sincere faith.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 6, 'Some have strayed from these ways and turned aside to empty talk.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 7, 'They want to be teachers of the law, but they do not understand what they are saying or that which they so confidently assert.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 8, 'Now we know that the law is good, if one uses it legitimately.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 9, 'We realize that law is not enacted for the righteous, but for the lawless and rebellious, for the ungodly and sinful, for the unholy and profane, for killers of father or mother, for murderers,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 10, 'for the sexually immoral, for homosexuals, for slave traders and liars and perjurers, and for anyone else who is averse to sound teaching'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 11, 'that agrees with the glorious gospel of the blessed God, with which I have been entrusted.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 12, 'I thank Christ Jesus our Lord, who has strengthened me, that He considered me faithful and appointed me to service.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 13, 'I was formerly a blasphemer, a persecutor, and a violent man; yet because I had acted in ignorance and unbelief, I was shown mercy.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 14, 'And the grace of our Lord overflowed to me, along with the faith and love that are in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 15, 'This is a trustworthy saying, worthy of full acceptance: Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners, of whom I am the worst.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 16, 'But for this very reason I was shown mercy, so that in me, the worst of sinners, Christ Jesus might display His perfect patience as an example to those who would believe in Him for eternal life.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 17, 'Now to the King eternal, immortal, and invisible, the only God, be honor and glory forever and ever. Amen.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 18, 'Timothy, my child, I entrust you with this command in keeping with the previous prophecies about you, so that by them you may fight the good fight,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 19, 'holding on to faith and a good conscience, which some have rejected and thereby shipwrecked their faith.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 1, 20, 'Among them are Hymenaeus and Alexander, whom I have handed over to Satan to be taught not to blaspheme.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 2, 1, 'First of all, then, I urge that petitions, prayers, intercessions, and thanksgiving be offered for everyone—'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 2, 2, 'for kings and all those in authority—so that we may lead tranquil and quiet lives in all godliness and dignity.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 2, 3, 'This is good and pleasing in the sight of God our Savior,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 2, 4, 'who wants everyone to be saved and to come to the knowledge of the truth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 2, 5, 'For there is one God, and there is one mediator between God and men, the man Christ Jesus,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 2, 6, 'who gave Himself as a ransom for all—the testimony that was given at just the right time.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 2, 7, 'For this reason I was appointed as a preacher, an apostle, and a faithful and true teacher of the Gentiles. I am telling the truth; I am not lying about anything.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 2, 8, 'Therefore I want the men everywhere to pray, lifting up holy hands, without anger or dissension.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 2, 9, 'Likewise, I want the women to adorn themselves with respectable apparel, with modesty, and with self-control, not with braided hair or gold or pearls or expensive clothes,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 2, 10, 'but with good deeds, as is proper for women who profess to worship God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 2, 11, 'A woman must learn in quietness and full submissiveness.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 2, 12, 'I do not permit a woman to teach or to exercise authority over a man; she is to remain quiet.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 2, 13, 'For Adam was formed first, and then Eve.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 2, 14, 'And it was not Adam who was deceived, but the woman who was deceived and fell into transgression.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 2, 15, 'Women, however, will be saved through childbearing, if they continue in faith, love, and holiness, with self-control.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 3, 1, 'This is a trustworthy saying: If anyone aspires to be an overseer, he desires a noble task.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 3, 2, 'An overseer, then, must be above reproach, the husband of but one wife, temperate, self-controlled, respectable, hospitable, able to teach,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 3, 3, 'not dependent on wine, not violent but gentle, peaceable, and free of the love of money.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 3, 4, 'An overseer must manage his own household well and keep his children under control, with complete dignity.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 3, 5, 'For if someone does not know how to manage his own household, how can he care for the church of God?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 3, 6, 'He must not be a recent convert, or he may become conceited and fall under the same condemnation as the devil.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 3, 7, 'Furthermore, he must have a good reputation with outsiders, so that he will not fall into disgrace and into the snare of the devil.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 3, 8, 'Deacons likewise must be dignified, not double-tongued or given to much wine or greedy for money.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 3, 9, 'They must hold to the mystery of the faith with a clear conscience.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 3, 10, 'Additionally, they must first be tested. Then, if they are above reproach, let them serve as deacons.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 3, 11, 'In the same way, the women must be dignified, not slanderers, but temperate and faithful in all things.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 3, 12, 'A deacon must be the husband of but one wife, a good manager of his children and of his own household.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 3, 13, 'For those who have served well as deacons acquire for themselves a high standing and great confidence in the faith that is in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 3, 14, 'Although I hope to come to you soon, I am writing you these things'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 3, 15, 'in case I am delayed, so that you will know how each one must conduct himself in God’s household, which is the church of the living God, the pillar and foundation of the truth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 3, 16, 'By common confession, the mystery of godliness is great: He appeared in the flesh, was vindicated by the Spirit, was seen by angels, was proclaimed among the nations, was believed in throughout the world, was taken up in glory.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 4, 1, 'Now the Spirit expressly states that in later times some will abandon the faith to follow deceitful spirits and the teachings of demons,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 4, 2, 'influenced by the hypocrisy of liars, whose consciences are seared with a hot iron.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 4, 3, 'They will prohibit marriage and require abstinence from certain foods that God has created to be received with thanksgiving by those who believe and know the truth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 4, 4, 'For every creation of God is good, and nothing that is received with thanksgiving should be rejected,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 4, 5, 'because it is sanctified by the word of God and prayer.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 4, 6, 'By pointing out these things to the brothers, you will be a good servant of Christ Jesus, nourished by the words of faith and sound instruction that you have followed.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 4, 7, 'But reject irreverent, silly myths. Instead, train yourself for godliness.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 4, 8, 'For physical exercise is of limited value, but godliness is valuable in every way, holding promise for the present life and for the one to come.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 4, 9, 'This is a trustworthy saying, worthy of full acceptance.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 4, 10, 'To this end we labor and strive, because we have set our hope on the living God, who is the Savior of everyone, and especially of those who believe.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 4, 11, 'Command and teach these things.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 4, 12, 'Let no one despise your youth, but set an example for the believers in speech, in conduct, in love, in faith, in purity.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 4, 13, 'Until I come, devote yourself to the public reading of Scripture, to exhortation, and to teaching.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 4, 14, 'Do not neglect the gift that is in you, which was given you through the prophecy spoken over you at the laying on of the hands of the elders.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 4, 15, 'Be diligent in these matters and absorbed in them, so that your progress will be evident to all.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 4, 16, 'Pay close attention to your life and to your teaching. Persevere in these things, for by so doing you will save both yourself and those who hear you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 1, 'Do not rebuke an older man, but appeal to him as to a father. Treat younger men as brothers,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 2, 'older women as mothers, and younger women as sisters, with absolute purity.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 3, 'Honor the widows who are truly widows.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 4, 'But if a widow has children or grandchildren, they must first learn to show godliness to their own family and repay their parents, for this is pleasing in the sight of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 5, 'The widow who is truly in need and left all alone puts her hope in God and continues night and day in her petitions and prayers.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 6, 'But she who lives for pleasure is dead even while she is still alive.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 7, 'Give these instructions to the believers, so that they will be above reproach.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 8, 'If anyone does not provide for his own, and especially his own household, he has denied the faith and is worse than an unbeliever.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 9, 'A widow should be enrolled if she is at least sixty years old, the wife of one man,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 10, 'and well known for good deeds such as bringing up children, entertaining strangers, washing the feet of the saints, imparting relief to the afflicted, and devoting herself to every good work.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 11, 'But refuse to enroll younger widows. For when their passions draw them away from Christ, they will want to marry,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 12, 'and thus will incur judgment because they are setting aside their first faith.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 13, 'At the same time they will also learn to be idle, going from house to house and being not only idle, but also gossips and busybodies, discussing things they should not mention.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 14, 'So I advise the younger widows to marry, have children, and manage their households, denying the adversary occasion for slander.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 15, 'For some have already turned aside to follow Satan.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 16, 'If any believing woman has dependent widows, she must assist them and not allow the church to be burdened, so that it can help the widows who are truly in need.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 17, 'Elders who lead effectively are worthy of double honor, especially those who work hard at preaching and teaching.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 18, 'For the Scripture says, “Do not muzzle an ox while it is treading out the grain,” and, “The worker is worthy of his wages.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 19, 'Do not entertain an accusation against an elder, except on the testimony of two or three witnesses.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 20, 'But those who persist in sin should be rebuked in front of everyone, so that the others will stand in fear of sin.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 21, 'I solemnly charge you before God and Christ Jesus and the elect angels to maintain these principles without bias, and to do nothing out of partiality.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 22, 'Do not be too quick in the laying on of hands and thereby share in the sins of others. Keep yourself pure.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 23, 'Stop drinking only water and use a little wine instead, because of your stomach and your frequent ailments.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 24, 'The sins of some men are obvious, going ahead of them to judgment; but the sins of others do not surface until later.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 5, 25, 'In the same way, good deeds are obvious, and even the ones that are inconspicuous cannot remain hidden.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 1, 'All who are under the yoke of slavery should regard their masters as fully worthy of honor, so that God’s name and our teaching will not be discredited.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 2, 'Those who have believing masters should not show disrespect because they are brothers, but should serve them all the more, since those receiving their good service are beloved believers. Teach and encourage these principles.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 3, 'If anyone teaches another doctrine and disagrees with the sound words of our Lord Jesus Christ and with godly teaching,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 4, 'he is conceited and understands nothing. Instead, he has an unhealthy interest in controversies and semantics, out of which come envy, strife, abusive talk, evil suspicions,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 5, 'and constant friction between men of depraved mind who are devoid of the truth. These men regard godliness as a means of gain.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 6, 'Of course, godliness with contentment is great gain.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 7, 'For we brought nothing into the world, so we cannot carry anything out of it.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 8, 'But if we have food and clothing, we will be content with these.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 9, 'Those who want to be rich, however, fall into temptation and become ensnared by many foolish and harmful desires that plunge them into ruin and destruction.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 10, 'For the love of money is the root of all kinds of evil. By craving it, some have wandered away from the faith and pierced themselves with many sorrows.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 11, 'But you, O man of God, flee from these things and pursue righteousness, godliness, faith, love, perseverance, and gentleness.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 12, 'Fight the good fight of the faith. Take hold of the eternal life to which you were called when you made the good confession before many witnesses.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 13, 'I charge you in the presence of God, who gives life to all things, and of Christ Jesus, who made the good confession in His testimony before Pontius Pilate:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 14, 'Keep this commandment without stain or reproach until the appearance of our Lord Jesus Christ,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 15, 'which the blessed and only Sovereign One—the King of kings and Lord of lords—will bring about in His own time.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 16, 'He alone is immortal and dwells in unapproachable light. No one has ever seen Him, nor can anyone see Him. To Him be honor and eternal dominion! Amen.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 17, 'Instruct those who are rich in the present age not to be conceited and not to put their hope in the uncertainty of wealth, but in God, who richly provides all things for us to enjoy.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 18, 'Instruct them to do good, to be rich in good works, and to be generous and ready to share,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 19, 'treasuring up for themselves a firm foundation for the future, so that they may take hold of that which is truly life.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 20, 'O Timothy, guard what has been entrusted to you. Avoid irreverent, empty chatter and the opposing arguments of so-called “knowledge,”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Timothy', 54, 6, 21, 'which some have professed and thus swerved away from the faith. Grace be with you all.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 1, 'Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, according to the promise of life in Christ Jesus,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 2, 'To Timothy, my beloved child: Grace, mercy, and peace from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Lord.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 3, 'I thank God, whom I serve with a clear conscience as did my forefathers, as I constantly remember you night and day in my prayers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 4, 'Recalling your tears, I long to see you so that I may be filled with joy.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 5, 'I am reminded of your sincere faith, which first dwelt in your grandmother Lois and your mother Eunice, and I am convinced is in you as well.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 6, 'For this reason I remind you to fan into flame the gift of God, which is in you through the laying on of my hands.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 7, 'For God has not given us a spirit of fear, but of power, love, and self-control.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 8, 'So do not be ashamed of the testimony of our Lord, or of me, His prisoner. Instead, join me in suffering for the gospel by the power of God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 9, 'He has saved us and called us to a holy calling, not because of our works, but by His own purpose and by the grace He granted us in Christ Jesus before time began.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 10, 'And now He has revealed this grace through the appearing of our Savior, Christ Jesus, who has abolished death and illuminated the way to life and immortality through the gospel,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 11, 'to which I was appointed as a preacher, an apostle, and a teacher.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 12, 'For this reason, even though I suffer as I do, I am not ashamed; for I know whom I have believed, and I am convinced that He is able to guard what I have entrusted to Him for that day.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 13, 'Hold on to the pattern of sound teaching you have heard from me, with the faith and love that are in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 14, 'Guard the treasure entrusted to you, with the help of the Holy Spirit who dwells in us.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 15, 'You know that everyone in the Province of Asia has deserted me, including Phygelus and Hermogenes.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 16, 'May the Lord grant mercy to the household of Onesiphorus, because he has often refreshed me and was unashamed of my chains.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 17, 'Indeed, when he arrived in Rome, he searched diligently until he found me.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 1, 18, 'May the Lord grant Onesiphorus His mercy on that day. You know very well how much he ministered to me in Ephesus.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 1, 'You therefore, my child, be strong in the grace that is in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 2, 'And the things that you have heard me say among many witnesses, entrust these to faithful men who will be qualified to teach others as well.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 3, 'Join me in suffering, like a good soldier of Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 4, 'A soldier refrains from entangling himself in civilian affairs, in order to please the one who enlisted him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 5, 'Likewise, a competitor does not receive the crown unless he competes according to the rules.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 6, 'The hardworking farmer should be the first to partake of the crops.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 7, 'Consider what I am saying, for the Lord will give you insight into all things.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 8, 'Remember Jesus Christ, raised from the dead, descended from David, as proclaimed by my gospel,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 9, 'for which I suffer to the extent of being chained like a criminal. But the word of God cannot be chained!'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 10, 'For this reason I endure all things for the sake of the elect, so that they too may obtain the salvation that is in Christ Jesus, with eternal glory.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 11, 'This is a trustworthy saying: If we died with Him, we will also live with Him;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 12, 'if we endure, we will also reign with Him; if we deny Him, He will also deny us;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 13, 'if we are faithless, He remains faithful, for He cannot deny Himself.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 14, 'Remind the believers of these things, charging them before God to avoid quarreling over words, which succeeds only in leading the listeners to ruin.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 15, 'Make every effort to present yourself approved to God, an unashamed workman who accurately handles the word of truth.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 16, 'But avoid irreverent, empty chatter, which will only lead to more ungodliness,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 17, 'and the talk of such men will spread like gangrene. Among them are Hymenaeus and Philetus,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 18, 'who have deviated from the truth. They say that the resurrection has already occurred, and they undermine the faith of some.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 19, 'Nevertheless, God’s firm foundation stands, bearing this seal: “The Lord knows those who are His,” and, “Everyone who calls on the name of the Lord must turn away from iniquity.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 20, 'A large house contains not only vessels of gold and silver, but also of wood and clay. Some indeed are for honorable use, but others are for common use.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 21, 'So if anyone cleanses himself of what is unfit, he will be a vessel for honor: sanctified, useful to the Master, and prepared for every good work.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 22, 'Flee from youthful passions and pursue righteousness, faith, love, and peace, together with those who call on the Lord out of a pure heart.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 23, 'But reject foolish and ignorant speculation, for you know that it breeds quarreling.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 24, 'And a servant of the Lord must not be quarrelsome, but must be kind to everyone, able to teach, and forbearing.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 25, 'He must gently reprove those who oppose him, in the hope that God may grant them repentance leading to a knowledge of the truth.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 2, 26, 'Then they will come to their senses and escape the snare of the devil, who has taken them captive to his will.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 3, 1, 'But understand this: In the last days terrible times will come.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 3, 2, 'For men will be lovers of themselves, lovers of money, boastful, arrogant, abusive, disobedient to their parents, ungrateful, unholy,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 3, 3, 'unloving, unforgiving, slanderous, without self-control, brutal, without love of good,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 3, 4, 'traitorous, reckless, conceited, lovers of pleasure rather than lovers of God,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 3, 5, 'having a form of godliness but denying its power. Turn away from such as these!'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 3, 6, 'They are the kind who worm their way into households and captivate vulnerable women who are weighed down with sins and led astray by various passions,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 3, 7, 'who are always learning but never able to come to a knowledge of the truth.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 3, 8, 'Just as Jannes and Jambres opposed Moses, so also these men oppose the truth. They are depraved in mind and disqualified from the faith.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 3, 9, 'But they will not advance much further. For just like Jannes and Jambres, their folly will be plain to everyone.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 3, 10, 'You, however, have observed my teaching, my conduct, my purpose, my faith, my patience, my love, my perseverance,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 3, 11, 'my persecutions, and the sufferings that came upon me in Antioch, Iconium, and Lystra. What persecutions I endured! Yet the Lord rescued me from all of them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 3, 12, 'Indeed, all who desire to live godly lives in Christ Jesus will be persecuted,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 3, 13, 'while evil men and imposters go from bad to worse, deceiving and being deceived.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 3, 14, 'But as for you, continue in the things you have learned and firmly believed, since you know from whom you have learned them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 3, 15, 'From infancy you have known the Holy Scriptures, which are able to make you wise for salvation through faith in Christ Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 3, 16, 'All Scripture is God-breathed and is useful for instruction, for conviction, for correction, and for training in righteousness,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 3, 17, 'so that the man of God may be complete, fully equipped for every good work.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 1, 'I charge you in the presence of God and of Christ Jesus, who will judge the living and the dead, and in view of His appearing and His kingdom:'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 2, 'Preach the word; be prepared in season and out of season; reprove, rebuke, and encourage with every form of patient instruction.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 3, 'For the time will come when men will not tolerate sound doctrine, but with itching ears they will gather around themselves teachers to suit their own desires.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 4, 'So they will turn their ears away from the truth and turn aside to myths.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 5, 'But you, be sober in all things, endure hardship, do the work of an evangelist, fulfill your ministry.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 6, 'For I am already being poured out like a drink offering, and the time of my departure is at hand.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 7, 'I have fought the good fight, I have finished the race, I have kept the faith.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 8, 'From now on there is laid up for me the crown of righteousness, which the Lord, the righteous Judge, will award to me on that day—and not only to me, but to all who crave His appearing.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 9, 'Make every effort to come to me quickly,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 10, 'because Demas, in his love of this world, has deserted me and gone to Thessalonica. Crescens has gone to Galatia, and Titus to Dalmatia.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 11, 'Only Luke is with me. Get Mark and bring him with you, because he is useful to me in the ministry.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 12, 'Tychicus, however, I have sent to Ephesus.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 13, 'When you come, bring the cloak that I left with Carpus at Troas, and my scrolls, especially the parchments.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 14, 'Alexander the coppersmith did great harm to me. The Lord will repay him according to his deeds.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 15, 'You too should beware of him, for he has vigorously opposed our message.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 16, 'At my first defense, no one stood with me, but everyone deserted me. May it not be charged against them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 17, 'But the Lord stood by me and strengthened me, so that through me the message would be fully proclaimed, and all the Gentiles would hear it. So I was delivered from the mouth of the lion.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 18, 'And the Lord will rescue me from every evil action and bring me safely into His heavenly kingdom. To Him be the glory forever and ever. Amen.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 19, 'Greet Prisca and Aquila, as well as the household of Onesiphorus.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 20, 'Erastus has remained at Corinth, and Trophimus I left sick in Miletus.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 21, 'Make every effort to come to me before winter. Eubulus sends you greetings, as do Pudens, Linus, Claudia, and all the brothers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Timothy', 55, 4, 22, 'The Lord be with your spirit. Grace be with you all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 1, 1, 'Paul, a servant of God and an apostle of Jesus Christ for the faith of God’s elect and their knowledge of the truth that leads to godliness,'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 1, 2, 'in the hope of eternal life, which God, who cannot lie, promised before time began.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 1, 3, 'In His own time He has made His word evident in the proclamation entrusted to me by the command of God our Savior.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 1, 4, 'To Titus, my true child in our common faith: Grace and peace from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Savior.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 1, 5, 'The reason I left you in Crete was that you would set in order what was unfinished and appoint elders in every town, as I directed you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 1, 6, 'An elder must be blameless, the husband of but one wife, having children who are believers and who are not open to accusation of indiscretion or insubordination.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 1, 7, 'As God’s steward, an overseer must be above reproach—not self-absorbed, not quick-tempered, not given to drunkenness, not violent, not greedy for money.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 1, 8, 'Instead, he must be hospitable, a lover of good, self-controlled, upright, holy, and disciplined.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 1, 9, 'He must hold firmly to the faithful word as it was taught, so that he can encourage others by sound teaching and refute those who contradict it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 1, 10, 'For many are rebellious and full of empty talk and deception, especially those of the circumcision,'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 1, 11, 'who must be silenced. For the sake of dishonorable gain, they undermine entire households and teach things they should not.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 1, 12, 'As one of their own prophets has said, “Cretans are always liars, evil beasts, lazy gluttons.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 1, 13, 'This testimony is true. Therefore rebuke them sternly, so that they will be sound in the faith'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 1, 14, 'and will pay no attention to Jewish myths or to the commands of men who have rejected the truth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 1, 15, 'To the pure, all things are pure; but to the defiled and unbelieving, nothing is pure. Indeed, both their minds and their consciences are defiled.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 1, 16, 'They profess to know God, but by their actions they deny Him. They are detestable, disobedient, and unfit for any good deed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 2, 1, 'But as for you, speak the things that are consistent with sound doctrine.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 2, 2, 'Older men are to be temperate, dignified, self-controlled, and sound in faith, love, and perseverance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 2, 3, 'Older women, likewise, are to be reverent in their behavior, not slanderers or addicted to much wine, but teachers of good.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 2, 4, 'In this way they can train the young women to love their husbands and children,'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 2, 5, 'to be self-controlled, pure, managers of their households, kind, and submissive to their own husbands, so that the word of God will not be discredited.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 2, 6, 'In the same way, urge the younger men to be self-controlled.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 2, 7, 'In everything, show yourself to be an example by doing good works. In your teaching show integrity, dignity,'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 2, 8, 'and wholesome speech that is above reproach, so that anyone who opposes us will be ashamed, having nothing bad to say about us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 2, 9, 'Slaves are to submit to their own masters in everything, to be well-pleasing, not argumentative,'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 2, 10, 'not stealing from them, but showing all good faith, so that in every respect they will adorn the teaching about God our Savior.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 2, 11, 'For the grace of God has appeared, bringing salvation to everyone.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 2, 12, 'It instructs us to renounce ungodliness and worldly passions, and to live sensible, upright, and godly lives in the present age,'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 2, 13, 'as we await the blessed hope and glorious appearance of our great God and Savior Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 2, 14, 'He gave Himself for us to redeem us from all lawlessness and to purify for Himself a people for His own possession, zealous for good deeds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 2, 15, 'Speak these things as you encourage and rebuke with all authority. Let no one despise you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 3, 1, 'Remind the believers to submit to rulers and authorities, to be obedient and ready for every good work,'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 3, 2, 'to malign no one, and to be peaceable and gentle, showing full consideration to everyone.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 3, 3, 'For at one time we too were foolish, disobedient, misled, and enslaved to all sorts of desires and pleasures—living in malice and envy, being hated and hating one another.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 3, 4, 'But when the kindness of God our Savior and His love for mankind appeared,'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 3, 5, 'He saved us, not by the righteous deeds we had done, but according to His mercy, through the washing of new birth and renewal by the Holy Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 3, 6, 'This is the Spirit He poured out on us abundantly through Jesus Christ our Savior,'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 3, 7, 'so that, having been justified by His grace, we would become heirs with the hope of eternal life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 3, 8, 'This saying is trustworthy. And I want you to emphasize these things, so that those who have believed God will take care to devote themselves to good deeds. These things are excellent and profitable for the people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 3, 9, 'But avoid foolish controversies, genealogies, arguments, and quarrels about the law, because these things are pointless and worthless.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 3, 10, 'Reject a divisive man after a first and second admonition,'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 3, 11, 'knowing that such a man is corrupt and sinful; he is self-condemned.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 3, 12, 'As soon as I send Artemas or Tychicus to you, make every effort to come to me at Nicopolis, because I have decided to winter there.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 3, 13, 'Do your best to equip Zenas the lawyer and Apollos, so that they will have everything they need.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 3, 14, 'And our people must also learn to devote themselves to good works in order to meet the pressing needs of others, so that they will not be unfruitful.'),
  ('BSB', 'Titus', 56, 3, 15, 'All who are with me send you greetings. Greet those who love us in the faith. Grace be with all of you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 1, 'Paul, a prisoner of Christ Jesus, and Timothy our brother, To Philemon our beloved fellow worker,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 2, 'to Apphia our sister, to Archippus our fellow soldier, and to the church that meets at your house:'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 3, 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 4, 'I always thank my God, remembering you in my prayers,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 5, 'because I hear about your faith in the Lord Jesus and your love for all the saints.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 6, 'I pray that your partnership in the faith may become effective as you fully acknowledge every good thing that is ours in Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 7, 'I take great joy and encouragement in your love, because you, brother, have refreshed the hearts of the saints.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 8, 'So although in Christ I am bold enough to order you to do what is proper,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 9, 'I prefer to appeal on the basis of love. For I, Paul, am now aged, and a prisoner of Christ Jesus as well.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 10, 'I appeal to you for my child Onesimus, whose father I became while I was in chains.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 11, 'Formerly he was useless to you, but now he has become useful both to you and to me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 12, 'I am sending back to you him who is my very heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 13, 'I would have liked to keep him with me, so that on your behalf he could minister to me in my chains for the gospel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 14, 'But I did not want to do anything without your consent, so that your goodness will not be out of compulsion, but by your own free will.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 15, 'For perhaps this is why he was separated from you for a while, so that you might have him back for good—'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 16, 'no longer as a slave, but better than a slave, as a beloved brother. He is especially beloved to me, but even more so to you, both in person and in the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 17, 'So if you consider me a partner, receive him as you would receive me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 18, 'But if he has wronged you in any way or owes you anything, charge it to my account.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 19, 'I, Paul, write this with my own hand. I will repay it—not to mention that you owe me your very self.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 20, 'Yes, brother, let me have some benefit from you in the Lord. Refresh my heart in Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 21, 'Confident of your obedience, I write to you, knowing that you will do even more than I ask.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 22, 'In the meantime, prepare a guest room for me, because I hope that through your prayers I will be restored to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 23, 'Epaphras, my fellow prisoner in Christ Jesus, sends you greetings,'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 24, 'as do Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke, my fellow workers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Philemon', 57, 1, 25, 'The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 1, 1, 'On many past occasions and in many different ways, God spoke to our fathers through the prophets.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 1, 2, 'But in these last days He has spoken to us by His Son, whom He appointed heir of all things, and through whom He made the universe.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 1, 3, 'The Son is the radiance of God’s glory and the exact representation of His nature, upholding all things by His powerful word. After He had provided purification for sins, He sat down at the right hand of the Majesty on high.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 1, 4, 'So He became as far superior to the angels as the name He has inherited is excellent beyond theirs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 1, 5, 'For to which of the angels did God ever say: “You are My Son; today I have become Your Father”? Or again: “I will be His Father, and He will be My Son”?'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 1, 6, 'And again, when God brings His firstborn into the world, He says: “Let all God’s angels worship Him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 1, 7, 'Now about the angels He says: “He makes His angels winds, His servants flames of fire.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 1, 8, 'But about the Son He says: “Your throne, O God, endures forever and ever, and justice is the scepter of Your kingdom.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 1, 9, 'You have loved righteousness and hated wickedness; therefore God, Your God, has anointed You above Your companions with the oil of joy.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 1, 10, 'And: “In the beginning, O Lord, You laid the foundations of the earth, and the heavens are the work of Your hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 1, 11, 'They will perish, but You remain; they will all wear out like a garment.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 1, 12, 'You will roll them up like a robe; like a garment they will be changed; but You remain the same, and Your years will never end.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 1, 13, 'Yet to which of the angels did God ever say: “Sit at My right hand until I make Your enemies a footstool for Your feet”?'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 1, 14, 'Are not the angels ministering spirits sent to serve those who will inherit salvation?'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 1, 'We must pay closer attention, therefore, to what we have heard, so that we do not drift away.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 2, 'For if the message spoken by angels was binding, and every transgression and disobedience received its just punishment,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 3, 'how shall we escape if we neglect such a great salvation? This salvation was first announced by the Lord, was confirmed to us by those who heard Him,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 4, 'and was affirmed by God through signs, wonders, various miracles, and gifts of the Holy Spirit distributed according to His will.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 5, 'For it is not to angels that He has subjected the world to come, about which we are speaking.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 6, 'But somewhere it is testified in these words: “What is man that You are mindful of him, or the son of man that You care for him?'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 7, 'You made him a little lower than the angels; You crowned him with glory and honor'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 8, 'and placed everything under his feet.” When God subjected all things to him, He left nothing outside of his control. Yet at present we do not see everything subject to him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 9, 'But we see Jesus, who was made a little lower than the angels, now crowned with glory and honor because He suffered death, so that by the grace of God He might taste death for everyone.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 10, 'In bringing many sons to glory, it was fitting for God, for whom and through whom all things exist, to make the author of their salvation perfect through suffering.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 11, 'For both the One who sanctifies and those who are sanctified are of the same family. So Jesus is not ashamed to call them brothers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 12, 'He says: “I will proclaim Your name to My brothers; I will sing Your praises in the assembly.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 13, 'And again: “I will put My trust in Him.” And once again: “Here am I, and the children God has given Me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 14, 'Now since the children have flesh and blood, He too shared in their humanity, so that by His death He might destroy him who holds the power of death, that is, the devil,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 15, 'and free those who all their lives were held in slavery by their fear of death.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 16, 'For surely it is not the angels He helps, but the descendants of Abraham.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 17, 'For this reason He had to be made like His brothers in every way, so that He might become a merciful and faithful high priest in service to God, in order to make atonement for the sins of the people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 2, 18, 'Because He Himself suffered when He was tempted, He is able to help those who are being tempted.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 1, 'Therefore, holy brothers, who share in the heavenly calling, set your focus on Jesus, the apostle and high priest whom we confess.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 2, 'He was faithful to the One who appointed Him, just as Moses was faithful in all God’s house.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 3, 'For Jesus has been counted worthy of greater glory than Moses, just as the builder of a house has greater honor than the house itself.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 4, 'And every house is built by someone, but God is the builder of everything.');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 5, 'Now Moses was faithful as a servant in all God’s house, testifying to what would be spoken later.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 6, 'But Christ is faithful as the Son over God’s house. And we are His house, if we hold firmly to our confidence and the hope of which we boast.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 7, 'Therefore, as the Holy Spirit says: “Today, if you hear His voice,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 8, 'do not harden your hearts, as you did in the rebellion, in the day of testing in the wilderness,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 9, 'where your fathers tested and tried Me, and for forty years saw My works.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 10, 'Therefore I was angry with that generation, and I said, ‘Their hearts are always going astray, and they have not known My ways.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 11, 'So I swore on oath in My anger, ‘They shall never enter My rest.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 12, 'See to it, brothers, that none of you has a wicked heart of unbelief that turns away from the living God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 13, 'But exhort one another daily, as long as it is called today, so that none of you may be hardened by sin’s deceitfulness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 14, 'We have come to share in Christ if we hold firmly to the end the assurance we had at first.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 15, 'As it has been said: “Today, if you hear His voice, do not harden your hearts, as you did in the rebellion.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 16, 'For who were the ones who heard and rebelled? Were they not all those Moses led out of Egypt?'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 17, 'And with whom was God angry for forty years? Was it not with those who sinned, whose bodies fell in the wilderness?'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 18, 'And to whom did He swear that they would never enter His rest? Was it not to those who disobeyed?'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 3, 19, 'So we see that it was because of their unbelief that they were unable to enter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 4, 1, 'Therefore, while the promise of entering His rest still stands, let us be careful that none of you be deemed to have fallen short of it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 4, 2, 'For we also received the good news just as they did; but the message they heard was of no value to them, since they did not share the faith of those who comprehended it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 4, 3, 'Now we who have believed enter that rest. As for the others, it is just as God has said: “So I swore on oath in My anger, ‘They shall never enter My rest.’” And yet His works have been finished since the foundation of the world.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 4, 4, 'For somewhere He has spoken about the seventh day in this manner: “And on the seventh day God rested from all His works.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 4, 5, 'And again, as He says in the passage above: “They shall never enter My rest.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 4, 6, 'Since, then, it remains for some to enter His rest, and since those who formerly heard the good news did not enter because of their disobedience,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 4, 7, 'God again designated a certain day as “Today,” when a long time later He spoke through David as was just stated: “Today, if you hear His voice, do not harden your hearts.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 4, 8, 'For if Joshua had given them rest, God would not have spoken later about another day.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 4, 9, 'There remains, then, a Sabbath rest for the people of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 4, 10, 'For whoever enters God’s rest also rests from his own work, just as God did from His.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 4, 11, 'Let us, therefore, make every effort to enter that rest, so that no one will fall by following the same pattern of disobedience.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 4, 12, 'For the word of God is living and active. Sharper than any double-edged sword, it pierces even to dividing soul and spirit, joints and marrow. It judges the thoughts and intentions of the heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 4, 13, 'Nothing in all creation is hidden from God’s sight; everything is uncovered and exposed before the eyes of Him to whom we must give account.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 4, 14, 'Therefore, since we have a great high priest who has passed through the heavens, Jesus the Son of God, let us hold firmly to what we profess.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 4, 15, 'For we do not have a high priest who is unable to sympathize with our weaknesses, but we have one who was tempted in every way that we are, yet was without sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 4, 16, 'Let us then approach the throne of grace with confidence, so that we may receive mercy and find grace to help us in our time of need.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 5, 1, 'Every high priest is appointed from among men to represent them in matters relating to God, to offer gifts and sacrifices for sins.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 5, 2, 'He is able to deal gently with those who are ignorant and misguided, since he himself is beset by weakness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 5, 3, 'That is why he is obligated to offer sacrifices for his own sins, as well as for the sins of the people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 5, 4, 'No one takes this honor upon himself; he must be called by God, just as Aaron was.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 5, 5, 'So also Christ did not take upon Himself the glory of becoming a high priest, but He was called by the One who said to Him: “You are My Son; today I have become Your Father.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 5, 6, 'And in another passage God says: “You are a priest forever in the order of Melchizedek.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 5, 7, 'During the days of Jesus’ earthly life, He offered up prayers and petitions with loud cries and tears to the One who could save Him from death, and He was heard because of His reverence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 5, 8, 'Although He was a Son, He learned obedience from what He suffered.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 5, 9, 'And having been made perfect, He became the source of eternal salvation to all who obey Him'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 5, 10, 'and was designated by God as high priest in the order of Melchizedek.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 5, 11, 'We have much to say about this, but it is hard to explain, because you are dull of hearing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 5, 12, 'Although by this time you ought to be teachers, you need someone to reteach you the basic principles of God’s word. You need milk, not solid food!'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 5, 13, 'For everyone who lives on milk is still an infant, inexperienced in the message of righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 5, 14, 'But solid food is for the mature, who by constant use have trained their senses to distinguish good from evil.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 1, 'Therefore let us leave the elementary teachings about Christ and go on to maturity, not laying again the foundation of repentance from dead works, and of faith in God,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 2, 'instruction about baptisms, the laying on of hands, the resurrection of the dead, and eternal judgment.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 3, 'And this we will do, if God permits.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 4, 'It is impossible for those who have once been enlightened, who have tasted the heavenly gift, who have shared in the Holy Spirit,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 5, 'who have tasted the goodness of the word of God and the powers of the coming age—'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 6, 'and then have fallen away—to be restored to repentance, because they themselves are crucifying the Son of God all over again and subjecting Him to open shame.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 7, 'For land that drinks in the rain often falling on it and that produces a crop useful to those for whom it is tended receives the blessing of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 8, 'But land that produces thorns and thistles is worthless, and its curse is imminent. In the end it will be burned.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 9, 'Even though we speak like this, beloved, we are convinced of better things in your case—things that accompany salvation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 10, 'For God is not unjust. He will not forget your work and the love you have shown for His name as you have ministered to the saints and continue to do so.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 11, 'We want each of you to show this same diligence to the very end, in order to make your hope sure.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 12, 'Then you will not be sluggish, but will imitate those who through faith and patience inherit what has been promised.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 13, 'When God made His promise to Abraham, since He had no one greater to swear by, He swore by Himself,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 14, 'saying, “I will surely bless you and multiply your descendants.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 15, 'And so Abraham, after waiting patiently, obtained the promise.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 16, 'Men swear by someone greater than themselves, and their oath serves as a confirmation to end all argument.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 17, 'So when God wanted to make the unchanging nature of His purpose very clear to the heirs of the promise, He guaranteed it with an oath.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 18, 'Thus by two unchangeable things in which it is impossible for God to lie, we who have fled to take hold of the hope set before us may be strongly encouraged.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 19, 'We have this hope as an anchor for the soul, firm and secure. It enters the inner sanctuary behind the curtain,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 6, 20, 'where Jesus our forerunner has entered on our behalf. He has become a high priest forever in the order of Melchizedek.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 1, 'This Melchizedek was king of Salem and priest of God Most High. He met Abraham returning from the slaughter of the kings and blessed him,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 2, 'and Abraham apportioned to him a tenth of everything. First, his name means “king of righteousness.” Then also, “king of Salem” means “king of peace.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 3, 'Without father or mother or genealogy, without beginning of days or end of life, like the Son of God, he remains a priest for all time.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 4, 'Consider how great Melchizedek was: Even the patriarch Abraham gave him a tenth of the plunder.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 5, 'Now the law commands the sons of Levi who become priests to collect a tenth from the people—that is, from their brothers—though they too are descended from Abraham.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 6, 'But Melchizedek, who did not trace his descent from Levi, collected a tenth from Abraham and blessed him who had the promises.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 7, 'And indisputably, the lesser is blessed by the greater.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 8, 'In the case of the Levites, mortal men collect the tenth; but in the case of Melchizedek, it is affirmed that he lives on.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 9, 'And so to speak, Levi, who collects the tenth, paid the tenth through Abraham.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 10, 'For when Melchizedek met Abraham, Levi was still in the loin of his ancestor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 11, 'Now if perfection could have been attained through the Levitical priesthood (for on this basis the people received the law), why was there still need for another priest to appear—one in the order of Melchizedek and not in the order of Aaron?'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 12, 'For when the priesthood is changed, the law must be changed as well.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 13, 'He of whom these things are said belonged to a different tribe, from which no one has ever served at the altar.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 14, 'For it is clear that our Lord descended from Judah, a tribe as to which Moses said nothing about priests.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 15, 'And this point is even more clear if another priest like Melchizedek appears,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 16, 'one who has become a priest not by a law of succession, but by the power of an indestructible life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 17, 'For it is testified: “You are a priest forever in the order of Melchizedek.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 18, 'So the former commandment is set aside because it was weak and useless'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 19, '(for the law made nothing perfect), and a better hope is introduced, by which we draw near to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 20, 'And none of this happened without an oath. For others became priests without an oath,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 21, 'but Jesus became a priest with an oath by the One who said to Him: “The Lord has sworn and will not change His mind: ‘You are a priest forever.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 22, 'Because of this oath, Jesus has become the guarantee of a better covenant.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 23, 'Now there have been many other priests, since death prevented them from continuing in office.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 24, 'But because Jesus lives forever, He has a permanent priesthood.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 25, 'Therefore He is able to save completely those who draw near to God through Him, since He always lives to intercede for them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 26, 'Such a high priest truly befits us—One who is holy, innocent, undefiled, set apart from sinners, and exalted above the heavens.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 27, 'Unlike the other high priests, He does not need to offer daily sacrifices, first for His own sins and then for the sins of the people; He sacrificed for sin once for all when He offered up Himself.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 7, 28, 'For the law appoints as high priests men who are weak; but the oath, which came after the law, appointed the Son, who has been made perfect forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 8, 1, 'The point of what we are saying is this: We do have such a high priest, who sat down at the right hand of the throne of the Majesty in heaven,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 8, 2, 'and who ministers in the sanctuary and true tabernacle set up by the Lord, not by man.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 8, 3, 'And since every high priest is appointed to offer both gifts and sacrifices, it was necessary for this One also to have something to offer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 8, 4, 'Now if He were on earth, He would not be a priest, since there are already priests who offer gifts according to the law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 8, 5, 'The place where they serve is a copy and shadow of what is in heaven. This is why Moses was warned when he was about to build the tabernacle: “See to it that you make everything according to the pattern shown you on the mountain.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 8, 6, 'Now, however, Jesus has received a much more excellent ministry, just as the covenant He mediates is better and is founded on better promises.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 8, 7, 'For if that first covenant had been without fault, no place would have been sought for a second.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 8, 8, 'But God found fault with the people and said: “Behold, the days are coming, declares the Lord, when I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 8, 9, 'It will not be like the covenant I made with their fathers when I took them by the hand to lead them out of the land of Egypt, because they did not abide by My covenant, and I disregarded them, declares the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 8, 10, 'For this is the covenant I will make with the house of Israel after those days, declares the Lord. I will put My laws in their minds and inscribe them on their hearts. And I will be their God, and they will be My people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 8, 11, 'No longer will each one teach his neighbor or his brother, saying, ‘Know the Lord,’ because they will all know Me, from the least of them to the greatest.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 8, 12, 'For I will forgive their iniquities and will remember their sins no more.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 8, 13, 'By speaking of a new covenant, He has made the first one obsolete; and what is obsolete and aging will soon disappear.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 1, 'Now the first covenant had regulations for worship and also an earthly sanctuary.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 2, 'A tabernacle was prepared. In its first room were the lampstand, the table, and the consecrated bread. This was called the Holy Place.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 3, 'Behind the second curtain was a room called the Most Holy Place,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 4, 'containing the golden altar of incense and the gold-covered ark of the covenant. Inside the ark were the gold jar of manna, Aaron’s staff that had budded, and the stone tablets of the covenant.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 5, 'Above the ark were the cherubim of glory, overshadowing the mercy seat. But we cannot discuss these things in detail now.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 6, 'When everything had been prepared in this way, the priests entered regularly into the first room to perform their sacred duties.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 7, 'But only the high priest entered the second room, and then only once a year, and never without blood, which he offered for himself and for the sins the people had committed in ignorance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 8, 'By this arrangement the Holy Spirit was showing that the way into the Most Holy Place had not yet been disclosed as long as the first tabernacle was still standing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 9, 'It is an illustration for the present time, because the gifts and sacrifices being offered were unable to cleanse the conscience of the worshiper.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 10, 'They consist only in food and drink and special washings—external regulations imposed until the time of reform.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 11, 'But when Christ came as high priest of the good things that have come, He went through the greater and more perfect tabernacle that is not made by hands and is not a part of this creation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 12, 'He did not enter by the blood of goats and calves, but He entered the Most Holy Place once for all by His own blood, thus securing eternal redemption.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 13, 'For if the blood of goats and bulls and the ashes of a heifer sprinkled on those who are ceremonially unclean sanctify them so that their bodies are clean,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 14, 'how much more will the blood of Christ, who through the eternal Spirit offered Himself unblemished to God, purify our consciences from works of death, so that we may serve the living God!'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 15, 'Therefore Christ is the mediator of a new covenant, so that those who are called may receive the promised eternal inheritance, now that He has died to redeem them from the transgressions committed under the first covenant.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 16, 'In the case of a will, it is necessary to establish the death of the one who made it,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 17, 'because a will does not take effect until the one who made it has died; it cannot be executed while he is still alive.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 18, 'That is why even the first covenant was not put into effect without blood.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 19, 'For when Moses had proclaimed every commandment of the law to all the people, he took the blood of calves and goats, along with water, scarlet wool, and hyssop, and sprinkled the scroll and all the people,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 20, 'saying, “This is the blood of the covenant, which God has commanded you to keep.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 21, 'In the same way, he sprinkled with blood the tabernacle and all the vessels used in worship.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 22, 'According to the law, in fact, nearly everything must be purified with blood, and without the shedding of blood there is no forgiveness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 23, 'So it was necessary for the copies of the heavenly things to be purified with these sacrifices, but the heavenly things themselves with better sacrifices than these.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 24, 'For Christ did not enter a man-made copy of the true sanctuary, but He entered heaven itself, now to appear on our behalf in the presence of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 25, 'Nor did He enter heaven to offer Himself again and again, as the high priest enters the Most Holy Place every year with blood that is not his own.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 26, 'Otherwise, Christ would have had to suffer repeatedly since the foundation of the world. But now He has appeared once for all at the end of the ages to do away with sin by the sacrifice of Himself.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 27, 'Just as man is appointed to die once, and after that to face judgment,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 9, 28, 'so also Christ was offered once to bear the sins of many; and He will appear a second time, not to bear sin, but to bring salvation to those who eagerly await Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 1, 'For the law is only a shadow of the good things to come, not the realities themselves. It can never, by the same sacrifices offered year after year, make perfect those who draw near to worship.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 2, 'If it could, would not the offerings have ceased? For the worshipers would have been cleansed once for all, and would no longer have felt the guilt of their sins.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 3, 'Instead, those sacrifices are an annual reminder of sins,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 4, 'because it is impossible for the blood of bulls and goats to take away sins.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 5, 'Therefore, when Christ came into the world, He said: “Sacrifice and offering You did not desire, but a body You prepared for Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 6, 'In burnt offerings and sin offerings You took no delight.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 7, 'Then I said, ‘Here I am, it is written about Me in the scroll: I have come to do Your will, O God.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 8, 'In the passage above He says, “Sacrifices and offerings, burnt offerings and sin offerings You did not desire, nor did You delight in them” (although they are offered according to the law).'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 9, 'Then He adds, “Here I am, I have come to do Your will.” He takes away the first to establish the second.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 10, 'And by that will, we have been sanctified through the sacrifice of the body of Jesus Christ once for all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 11, 'Day after day every priest stands to minister and to offer again and again the same sacrifices, which can never take away sins.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 12, 'But when this Priest had offered for all time one sacrifice for sins, He sat down at the right hand of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 13, 'Since that time, He waits for His enemies to be made a footstool for His feet,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 14, 'because by a single offering He has made perfect for all time those who are being sanctified.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 15, 'The Holy Spirit also testifies to us about this. First He says:'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 16, '“This is the covenant I will make with them after those days, declares the Lord. I will put My laws in their hearts and inscribe them on their minds.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 17, 'Then He adds: “Their sins and lawless acts I will remember no more.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 18, 'And where these have been forgiven, an offering for sin is no longer needed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 19, 'Therefore, brothers, since we have confidence to enter the Most Holy Place by the blood of Jesus,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 20, 'by the new and living way opened for us through the curtain of His body,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 21, 'and since we have a great priest over the house of God,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 22, 'let us draw near with a sincere heart in full assurance of faith, having our hearts sprinkled to cleanse us from a guilty conscience and our bodies washed with pure water.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 23, 'Let us hold resolutely to the hope we profess, for He who promised is faithful.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 24, 'And let us consider how to spur one another on to love and good deeds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 25, 'Let us not neglect meeting together, as some have made a habit, but let us encourage one another, and all the more as you see the Day approaching.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 26, 'If we deliberately go on sinning after we have received the knowledge of the truth, no further sacrifice for sins remains,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 27, 'but only a fearful expectation of judgment and of raging fire that will consume all adversaries.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 28, 'Anyone who rejected the law of Moses died without mercy on the testimony of two or three witnesses.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 29, 'How much more severely do you think one deserves to be punished who has trampled on the Son of God, profaned the blood of the covenant that sanctified him, and insulted the Spirit of grace?'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 30, 'For we know Him who said, “Vengeance is Mine; I will repay,” and again, “The Lord will judge His people.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 31, 'It is a fearful thing to fall into the hands of the living God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 32, 'Remember the early days that you were in the light. In those days, you endured a great conflict in the face of suffering.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 33, 'Sometimes you were publicly exposed to ridicule and persecution; at other times you were partners with those who were so treated.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 34, 'You sympathized with those in prison and joyfully accepted the confiscation of your property, knowing that you yourselves had a better and permanent possession.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 35, 'So do not throw away your confidence; it holds a great reward.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 36, 'You need to persevere, so that after you have done the will of God, you will receive what He has promised.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 37, 'For, “In just a little while, He who is coming will come and will not delay.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 38, 'But My righteous one will live by faith; and if he shrinks back, I will take no pleasure in him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 10, 39, 'But we are not of those who shrink back and are destroyed, but of those who have faith and preserve their souls.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 1, 'Now faith is the assurance of what we hope for and the certainty of what we do not see.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 2, 'This is why the ancients were commended.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 3, 'By faith we understand that the universe was formed at God’s command, so that what is seen was not made out of what was visible.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 4, 'By faith Abel offered God a better sacrifice than Cain did. By faith he was commended as righteous when God gave approval to his gifts. And by faith he still speaks, even though he is dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 5, 'By faith Enoch was taken up so that he did not see death: “He could not be found, because God had taken him away.” For before he was taken, he was commended as one who pleased God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 6, 'And without faith it is impossible to please God, because anyone who approaches Him must believe that He exists and that He rewards those who earnestly seek Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 7, 'By faith Noah, when warned about things not yet seen, in godly fear built an ark to save his family. By faith he condemned the world and became heir of the righteousness that comes by faith.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 8, 'By faith Abraham, when called to go to a place he would later receive as his inheritance, obeyed and went, without knowing where he was going.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 9, 'By faith he dwelt in the promised land as a stranger in a foreign country. He lived in tents, as did Isaac and Jacob, who were heirs with him of the same promise.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 10, 'For he was looking forward to the city with foundations, whose architect and builder is God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 11, 'By faith Sarah, even though she was barren and beyond the proper age, was enabled to conceive a child, because she considered Him faithful who had promised.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 12, 'And so from one man, and he as good as dead, came descendants as numerous as the stars in the sky and as countless as the sand on the seashore.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 13, 'All these people died in faith, without having received the things they were promised. However, they saw them and welcomed them from afar. And they acknowledged that they were strangers and exiles on the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 14, 'Now those who say such things show that they are seeking a country of their own.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 15, 'If they had been thinking of the country they had left, they would have had opportunity to return.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 16, 'Instead, they were longing for a better country, a heavenly one. Therefore God is not ashamed to be called their God, for He has prepared a city for them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 17, 'By faith Abraham, when he was tested, offered up Isaac on the altar. He who had received the promises was ready to offer his one and only son,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 18, 'even though God had said to him, “Through Isaac your offspring will be reckoned.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 19, 'Abraham reasoned that God could raise the dead, and in a sense, he did receive Isaac back from death.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 20, 'By faith Isaac blessed Jacob and Esau concerning the future.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 21, 'By faith Jacob, when he was dying, blessed each of Joseph’s sons and worshiped as he leaned on the top of his staff.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 22, 'By faith Joseph, when his end was near, spoke about the exodus of the Israelites and gave instructions about his bones.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 23, 'By faith Moses’ parents hid him for three months after his birth, because they saw that he was a beautiful child, and they were unafraid of the king’s edict.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 24, 'By faith Moses, when he was grown, refused to be called the son of Pharaoh’s daughter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 25, 'He chose to suffer oppression with God’s people rather than to experience the fleeting enjoyment of sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 26, 'He valued disgrace for Christ above the treasures of Egypt, for he was looking ahead to his reward.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 27, 'By faith Moses left Egypt, not fearing the king’s anger; he persevered because he saw Him who is invisible.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 28, 'By faith he kept the Passover and the sprinkling of blood, so that the destroyer of the firstborn would not touch Israel’s own firstborn.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 29, 'By faith the people passed through the Red Sea as on dry land; but when the Egyptians tried to follow, they were drowned.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 30, 'By faith the walls of Jericho fell, after the people had marched around them for seven days.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 31, 'By faith the prostitute Rahab, because she welcomed the spies in peace, did not perish with those who were disobedient.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 32, 'And what more shall I say? Time will not allow me to tell of Gideon, Barak, Samson, Jephthah, David, Samuel, and the prophets,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 33, 'who through faith conquered kingdoms, administered justice, and gained what was promised; who shut the mouths of lions,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 34, 'quenched the raging fire, and escaped the edge of the sword; who gained strength from weakness, became mighty in battle, and put foreign armies to flight.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 35, 'Women received back their dead, raised to life again. Others were tortured and refused their release, so that they might gain a better resurrection.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 36, 'Still others endured mocking and flogging, and even chains and imprisonment.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 37, 'They were stoned, they were sawed in two, they were put to death by the sword. They went around in sheepskins and goatskins, destitute, oppressed, and mistreated.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 38, 'The world was not worthy of them. They wandered in deserts and mountains, and hid in caves and holes in the ground.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 39, 'These were all commended for their faith, yet they did not receive what was promised.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 11, 40, 'God had planned something better for us, so that together with us they would be made perfect.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 1, 'Therefore, since we are surrounded by such a great cloud of witnesses, let us throw off every encumbrance and the sin that so easily entangles, and let us run with endurance the race set out for us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 2, 'Let us fix our eyes on Jesus, the author and perfecter of our faith, who for the joy set before Him endured the cross, scorning its shame, and sat down at the right hand of the throne of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 3, 'Consider Him who endured such hostility from sinners, so that you will not grow weary and lose heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 4, 'In your struggle against sin, you have not yet resisted to the point of shedding your blood.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 5, 'And you have forgotten the exhortation that addresses you as sons: “My son, do not take lightly the discipline of the Lord, and do not lose heart when He rebukes you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 6, 'For the Lord disciplines the one He loves, and He chastises every son He receives.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 7, 'Endure suffering as discipline; God is treating you as sons. For what son is not disciplined by his father?'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 8, 'If you do not experience discipline like everyone else, then you are illegitimate children and not true sons.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 9, 'Furthermore, we have all had earthly fathers who disciplined us, and we respected them. Should we not much more submit to the Father of our spirits and live?'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 10, 'Our fathers disciplined us for a short time as they thought best, but God disciplines us for our good, so that we may share in His holiness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 11, 'No discipline seems enjoyable at the time, but painful. Later on, however, it yields a harvest of righteousness and peace to those who have been trained by it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 12, 'Therefore strengthen your limp hands and weak knees.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 13, 'Make straight paths for your feet, so that the lame may not be disabled, but rather healed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 14, 'Pursue peace with everyone, as well as holiness, without which no one will see the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 15, 'See to it that no one falls short of the grace of God, and that no root of bitterness springs up to cause trouble and defile many.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 16, 'See to it that no one is sexually immoral, or is godless like Esau, who for a single meal sold his birthright.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 17, 'For you know that afterward, when he wanted to inherit the blessing, he was rejected. He could find no ground for repentance, though he sought the blessing with tears.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 18, 'For you have not come to a mountain that can be touched and that is burning with fire; to darkness, gloom, and storm;'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 19, 'to a trumpet blast or to a voice that made its hearers beg that no further word be spoken.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 20, 'For they could not bear what was commanded: “If even an animal touches the mountain, it must be stoned.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 21, 'The sight was so terrifying that even Moses said, “I am trembling with fear.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 22, 'Instead, you have come to Mount Zion, to the city of the living God, the heavenly Jerusalem. You have come to myriads of angels'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 23, 'in joyful assembly, to the congregation of the firstborn, enrolled in heaven. You have come to God the Judge of all, to the spirits of the righteous made perfect,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 24, 'to Jesus the mediator of a new covenant, and to the sprinkled blood that speaks a better word than the blood of Abel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 25, 'See to it that you do not refuse Him who speaks. For if the people did not escape when they refused Him who warned them on earth, how much less will we escape if we reject Him who warns us from heaven?'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 26, 'At that time His voice shook the earth, but now He has promised, “Once more I will shake not only the earth, but heaven as well.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 27, 'The words “Once more” signify the removal of what can be shaken—that is, created things—so that the unshakable may remain.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 28, 'Therefore, since we are receiving an unshakable kingdom, let us be filled with gratitude, and so worship God acceptably with reverence and awe.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 12, 29, '“For our God is a consuming fire.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 1, 'Continue in brotherly love.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 2, 'Do not neglect to show hospitality to strangers, for by so doing some people have entertained angels without knowing it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 3, 'Remember those in prison as if you were bound with them, and those who are mistreated as if you were suffering with them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 4, 'Marriage should be honored by all and the marriage bed kept undefiled, for God will judge the sexually immoral and adulterers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 5, 'Keep your lives free from the love of money and be content with what you have, for God has said: “Never will I leave you, never will I forsake you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 6, 'So we say with confidence: “The Lord is my helper; I will not be afraid. What can man do to me?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 7, 'Remember your leaders who spoke the word of God to you. Consider the outcome of their way of life and imitate their faith.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 8, 'Jesus Christ is the same yesterday and today and forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 9, 'Do not be carried away by all kinds of strange teachings, for it is good for the heart to be strengthened by grace and not by foods of no value to those devoted to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 10, 'We have an altar from which those who serve at the tabernacle have no right to eat.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 11, 'Although the high priest brings the blood of animals into the Holy Place as a sacrifice for sin, the bodies are burned outside the camp.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 12, 'And so Jesus also suffered outside the city gate, to sanctify the people by His own blood.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 13, 'Therefore let us go to Him outside the camp, bearing the disgrace He bore.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 14, 'For here we do not have a permanent city, but we are looking for the city that is to come.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 15, 'Through Jesus, therefore, let us continually offer to God a sacrifice of praise, the fruit of lips that confess His name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 16, 'And do not neglect to do good and to share with others, for with such sacrifices God is pleased.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 17, 'Obey your leaders and submit to them, for they watch over your souls as those who must give an account. To this end, allow them to lead with joy and not with grief, for that would be of no advantage to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 18, 'Pray for us; we are convinced that we have a clear conscience and desire to live honorably in every way.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 19, 'And I especially urge you to pray that I may be restored to you soon.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 20, 'Now may the God of peace, who through the blood of the eternal covenant brought back from the dead our Lord Jesus, that great Shepherd of the sheep,'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 21, 'equip you with every good thing to do His will. And may He accomplish in us what is pleasing in His sight through Jesus Christ, to whom be glory forever and ever. Amen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 22, 'I urge you, brothers, to bear with my word of exhortation, for I have only written to you briefly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 23, 'Be aware that our brother Timothy has been released. If he arrives soon, I will come with him to see you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 24, 'Greet all your leaders and all the saints. Those from Italy send you greetings.'),
  ('BSB', 'Hebrews', 58, 13, 25, 'Grace be with all of you.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 1, 'James, a servant of God and of the Lord Jesus Christ, To the twelve tribes of the Dispersion: Greetings.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 2, 'Consider it pure joy, my brothers, when you encounter trials of many kinds,'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 3, 'because you know that the testing of your faith develops perseverance.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 4, 'Allow perseverance to finish its work, so that you may be mature and complete, not lacking anything.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 5, 'Now if any of you lacks wisdom, he should ask God, who gives generously to all without finding fault, and it will be given to him.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 6, 'But he must ask in faith, without doubting, because he who doubts is like a wave of the sea, blown and tossed by the wind.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 7, 'That man should not expect to receive anything from the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 8, 'He is a double-minded man, unstable in all his ways.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 9, 'The brother in humble circumstances should exult in his high position.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 10, 'But the one who is rich should exult in his low position, because he will pass away like a flower of the field.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 11, 'For the sun rises with scorching heat and withers the plant; its flower falls and its beauty is lost. So too, the rich man will fade away in the midst of his pursuits.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 12, 'Blessed is the man who perseveres under trial, because when he has stood the test, he will receive the crown of life that God has promised to those who love Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 13, 'When tempted, no one should say, “God is tempting me.” For God cannot be tempted by evil, nor does He tempt anyone.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 14, 'But each one is tempted when by his own evil desires he is lured away and enticed.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 15, 'Then after desire has conceived, it gives birth to sin; and sin, when it is full-grown, gives birth to death.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 16, 'Do not be deceived, my beloved brothers.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 17, 'Every good and perfect gift is from above, coming down from the Father of the heavenly lights, with whom there is no change or shifting shadow.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 18, 'He chose to give us birth through the word of truth, that we would be a kind of firstfruits of His creation.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 19, 'My beloved brothers, understand this: Everyone should be quick to listen, slow to speak, and slow to anger,'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 20, 'for man’s anger does not bring about the righteousness that God desires.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 21, 'Therefore, get rid of all moral filth and every expression of evil, and humbly accept the word planted in you, which can save your souls.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 22, 'Be doers of the word, and not hearers only. Otherwise, you are deceiving yourselves.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 23, 'For anyone who hears the word but does not carry it out is like a man who looks at his face in a mirror,'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 24, 'and after observing himself goes away and immediately forgets what he looks like.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 25, 'But the one who looks intently into the perfect law of freedom, and continues to do so—not being a forgetful hearer, but an effective doer—he will be blessed in what he does.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 26, 'If anyone considers himself religious and yet does not bridle his tongue, he deceives his heart and his religion is worthless.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 1, 27, 'Pure and undefiled religion before our God and Father is this: to care for orphans and widows in their distress, and to keep oneself from being polluted by the world.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 1, 'My brothers, as you hold out your faith in our glorious Lord Jesus Christ, do not show favoritism.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 2, 'Suppose a man comes into your meeting wearing a gold ring and fine clothes, and a poor man in shabby clothes also comes in.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 3, 'If you lavish attention on the man in fine clothes and say, “Here is a seat of honor,” but say to the poor man, “You must stand” or “Sit at my feet,”'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 4, 'have you not discriminated among yourselves and become judges with evil thoughts?'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 5, 'Listen, my beloved brothers: Has not God chosen the poor of this world to be rich in faith and to inherit the kingdom He promised those who love Him?'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 6, 'But you have dishonored the poor. Is it not the rich who oppress you and drag you into court?'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 7, 'Are they not the ones who blaspheme the noble name by which you have been called?'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 8, 'If you really fulfill the royal law stated in Scripture, “Love your neighbor as yourself,” you are doing well.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 9, 'But if you show favoritism, you sin and are convicted by the law as transgressors.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 10, 'Whoever keeps the whole law but stumbles at just one point is guilty of breaking all of it.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 11, 'For He who said, “Do not commit adultery,” also said, “Do not murder.” If you do not commit adultery, but do commit murder, you have become a lawbreaker.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 12, 'Speak and act as those who are going to be judged by the law that gives freedom.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 13, 'For judgment without mercy will be shown to anyone who has not been merciful. Mercy triumphs over judgment.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 14, 'What good is it, my brothers, if someone claims to have faith, but has no deeds? Can such faith save him?'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 15, 'Suppose a brother or sister is without clothes and daily food.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 16, 'If one of you tells him, “Go in peace; stay warm and well fed,” but does not provide for his physical needs, what good is that?'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 17, 'So too, faith by itself, if it does not result in action, is dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 18, 'But someone will say, “You have faith and I have deeds.” Show me your faith without deeds, and I will show you my faith by my deeds.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 19, 'You believe that God is one. Good for you! Even the demons believe that—and shudder.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 20, 'O foolish man, do you want evidence that faith without deeds is worthless?'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 21, 'Was not our father Abraham justified by what he did when he offered his son Isaac on the altar?'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 22, 'You see that his faith was working with his actions, and his faith was perfected by what he did.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 23, 'And the Scripture was fulfilled that says, “Abraham believed God, and it was credited to him as righteousness,” and he was called a friend of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 24, 'As you can see, a man is justified by his deeds and not by faith alone.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 25, 'In the same way, was not even Rahab the prostitute justified by her actions when she welcomed the spies and sent them off on another route?'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 2, 26, 'As the body without the spirit is dead, so faith without deeds is dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 1, 'Not many of you should become teachers, my brothers, because you know that we who teach will be judged more strictly.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 2, 'We all stumble in many ways. If anyone is never at fault in what he says, he is a perfect man, able to control his whole body.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 3, 'When we put bits into the mouths of horses to make them obey us, we can guide the whole animal.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 4, 'Consider ships as well. Although they are so large and are driven by strong winds, they are steered by a very small rudder wherever the pilot is inclined.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 5, 'In the same way, the tongue is a small part of the body, but it boasts of great things. Consider how small a spark sets a great forest ablaze.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 6, 'The tongue also is a fire, a world of wickedness among the parts of the body. It pollutes the whole person, sets the course of his life on fire, and is itself set on fire by hell.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 7, 'All kinds of animals, birds, reptiles, and creatures of the sea are being tamed and have been tamed by man,'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 8, 'but no man can tame the tongue. It is a restless evil, full of deadly poison.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 9, 'With the tongue we bless our Lord and Father, and with it we curse men, who have been made in God’s likeness.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 10, 'Out of the same mouth come blessing and cursing. My brothers, this should not be!'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 11, 'Can both fresh water and salt water flow from the same spring?'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 12, 'My brothers, can a fig tree grow olives, or a grapevine bear figs? Neither can a salt spring produce fresh water.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 13, 'Who is wise and understanding among you? Let him show it by his good conduct, by deeds done in the humility that comes from wisdom.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 14, 'But if you harbor bitter jealousy and selfish ambition in your hearts, do not boast in it or deny the truth.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 15, 'Such wisdom does not come from above, but is earthly, unspiritual, demonic.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 16, 'For where jealousy and selfish ambition exist, there will be disorder and every evil practice.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 17, 'But the wisdom from above is first of all pure, then peace-loving, gentle, accommodating, full of mercy and good fruit, impartial, and sincere.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 3, 18, 'Peacemakers who sow in peace reap the fruit of righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 4, 1, 'What causes conflicts and quarrels among you? Don’t they come from the passions at war within you?'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 4, 2, 'You crave what you do not have; you kill and covet, but are unable to obtain it. You quarrel and fight. You do not have, because you do not ask.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 4, 3, 'And when you do ask, you do not receive, because you ask with wrong motives, that you may squander it on your pleasures.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 4, 4, 'You adulteresses! Do you not know that friendship with the world is hostility toward God? Therefore, whoever chooses to be a friend of the world renders himself an enemy of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 4, 5, 'Or do you think the Scripture says without reason that the Spirit He caused to dwell in us yearns with envy?'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 4, 6, 'But He gives us more grace. This is why it says: “God opposes the proud, but gives grace to the humble.”'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 4, 7, 'Submit yourselves, then, to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 4, 8, 'Draw near to God, and He will draw near to you. Cleanse your hands, you sinners, and purify your hearts, you double-minded.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 4, 9, 'Grieve, mourn, and weep. Turn your laughter to mourning, and your joy to gloom.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 4, 10, 'Humble yourselves before the Lord, and He will exalt you.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 4, 11, 'Brothers, do not slander one another. Anyone who speaks against his brother or judges him speaks against the law and judges it. And if you judge the law, you are not a practitioner of the law, but a judge of it.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 4, 12, 'There is only one Lawgiver and Judge, the One who is able to save and destroy. But who are you to judge your neighbor?'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 4, 13, 'Come now, you who say, “Today or tomorrow we will go to this or that city, spend a year there, carry on business, and make a profit.”'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 4, 14, 'You do not even know what will happen tomorrow! What is your life? You are a mist that appears for a little while and then vanishes.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 4, 15, 'Instead, you ought to say, “If the Lord is willing, we will live and do this or that.”'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 4, 16, 'As it is, you boast in your proud intentions. All such boasting is evil.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 4, 17, 'Anyone, then, who knows the right thing to do, yet fails to do it, is guilty of sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 1, 'Come now, you who are rich, weep and wail over the misery to come upon you.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 2, 'Your riches have rotted and moths have eaten your clothes.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 3, 'Your gold and silver are corroded. Their corrosion will testify against you and consume your flesh like fire. You have hoarded treasure in the last days.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 4, 'Look, the wages you withheld from the workmen who mowed your fields are crying out against you. The cries of the harvesters have reached the ears of the Lord of Hosts.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 5, 'You have lived on earth in luxury and self-indulgence. You have fattened your hearts in the day of slaughter.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 6, 'You have condemned and murdered the righteous, who did not resist you.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 7, 'Be patient, then, brothers, until the Lord’s coming. See how the farmer awaits the precious fruit of the soil—how patient he is for the fall and spring rains.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 8, 'You, too, be patient and strengthen your hearts, because the Lord’s coming is near.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 9, 'Do not complain about one another, brothers, so that you will not be judged. Look, the Judge is standing at the door!'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 10, 'Brothers, as an example of patience in affliction, take the prophets who spoke in the name of the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 11, 'See how blessed we consider those who have persevered. You have heard of Job’s perseverance and have seen the outcome from the Lord. The Lord is full of compassion and mercy.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 12, 'Above all, my brothers, do not swear, not by heaven or earth or by any other oath. Simply let your “Yes” be yes, and your “No,” no, so that you will not fall under judgment.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 13, 'Is any one of you suffering? He should pray. Is anyone cheerful? He should sing praises.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 14, 'Is any one of you sick? He should call the elders of the church to pray over him and anoint him with oil in the name of the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 15, 'And the prayer offered in faith will restore the one who is sick. The Lord will raise him up. If he has sinned, he will be forgiven.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 16, 'Therefore confess your sins to each other and pray for each other so that you may be healed. The prayer of a righteous man has great power to prevail.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 17, 'Elijah was a man just like us. He prayed earnestly that it would not rain, and it did not rain on the land for three and a half years.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 18, 'Again he prayed, and the heavens gave rain, and the earth yielded its crops.'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 19, 'My brothers, if one of you should wander from the truth and someone should bring him back,'),
  ('BSB', 'James', 59, 5, 20, 'consider this: Whoever turns a sinner from the error of his way will save his soul from death and cover over a multitude of sins.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 1, 'Peter, an apostle of Jesus Christ, To the elect who are exiles of the Dispersion throughout Pontus, Galatia, Cappadocia, Asia, and Bithynia, chosen'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 2, 'according to the foreknowledge of God the Father and sanctified by the Spirit for obedience to Jesus Christ and sprinkling by His blood: Grace and peace be yours in abundance.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 3, 'Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ! By His great mercy He has given us new birth into a living hope through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 4, 'and into an inheritance that is imperishable, undefiled, and unfading, reserved in heaven for you,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 5, 'who through faith are shielded by God’s power for the salvation that is ready to be revealed in the last time.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 6, 'In this you greatly rejoice, though now for a little while you may have had to suffer grief in various trials'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 7, 'so that the proven character of your faith—more precious than gold, which perishes even though refined by fire—may result in praise, glory, and honor at the revelation of Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 8, 'Though you have not seen Him, you love Him; and though you do not see Him now, you believe in Him and rejoice with an inexpressible and glorious joy,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 9, 'now that you are receiving the goal of your faith, the salvation of your souls.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 10, 'Concerning this salvation, the prophets who foretold the grace to come to you searched and investigated carefully,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 11, 'trying to determine the time and setting to which the Spirit of Christ in them was pointing when He predicted the sufferings of Christ and the glories to follow.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 12, 'It was revealed to them that they were not serving themselves, but you, when they foretold the things now announced by those who preached the gospel to you by the Holy Spirit sent from heaven. Even angels long to look into these things.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 13, 'Therefore prepare your minds for action. Be sober-minded. Set your hope fully on the grace to be given you at the revelation of Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 14, 'As obedient children, do not conform to the passions of your former ignorance.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 15, 'But just as He who called you is holy, so be holy in all you do,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 16, 'for it is written: “Be holy, because I am holy.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 17, 'Since you call on a Father who judges each one’s work impartially, conduct yourselves in reverent fear during your stay as foreigners.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 18, 'For you know that it was not with perishable things such as silver or gold that you were redeemed from the empty way of life you inherited from your forefathers,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 19, 'but with the precious blood of Christ, a lamb without blemish or spot.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 20, 'He was known before the foundation of the world, but was revealed in the last times for your sake.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 21, 'Through Him you believe in God, who raised Him from the dead and glorified Him; and so your faith and hope are in God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 22, 'Since you have purified your souls by obedience to the truth so that you have a genuine love for your brothers, love one another deeply, from a pure heart.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 23, 'For you have been born again, not of perishable seed, but of imperishable, through the living and enduring word of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 24, 'For, “All flesh is like grass, and all its glory like the flowers of the field; the grass withers and the flowers fall,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 1, 25, 'but the word of the Lord stands forever.” And this is the word that was proclaimed to you.');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 1, 'Rid yourselves, therefore, of all malice, deceit, hypocrisy, envy, and slander.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 2, 'Like newborn babies, crave pure spiritual milk, so that by it you may grow up in your salvation,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 3, 'now that you have tasted that the Lord is good.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 4, 'As you come to Him, the living stone, rejected by men but chosen and precious in God’s sight,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 5, 'you also, like living stones, are being built into a spiritual house to be a holy priesthood, offering spiritual sacrifices acceptable to God through Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 6, 'For it stands in Scripture: “See, I lay in Zion a stone, a chosen and precious cornerstone; and the one who believes in Him will never be put to shame.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 7, 'To you who believe, then, this stone is precious. But to those who do not believe, “The stone the builders rejected has become the cornerstone,”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 8, 'and, “A stone of stumbling and a rock of offense.” They stumble because they disobey the word—and to this they were appointed.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 9, 'But you are a chosen people, a royal priesthood, a holy nation, a people for God’s own possession, to proclaim the virtues of Him who called you out of darkness into His marvelous light.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 10, 'Once you were not a people, but now you are the people of God; once you had not received mercy, but now you have received mercy.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 11, 'Beloved, I urge you, as foreigners and exiles, to abstain from the desires of the flesh, which war against your soul.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 12, 'Conduct yourselves with such honor among the Gentiles that, though they slander you as evildoers, they may see your good deeds and glorify God on the day He visits us.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 13, 'Submit yourselves for the Lord’s sake to every human institution, whether to the king as the supreme authority,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 14, 'or to governors as those sent by him to punish those who do wrong and to praise those who do right.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 15, 'For it is God’s will that by doing good you should silence the ignorance of foolish men.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 16, 'Live in freedom, but do not use your freedom as a cover-up for evil; live as servants of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 17, 'Treat everyone with high regard: Love the brotherhood of believers, fear God, honor the king.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 18, 'Servants, submit yourselves to your masters with all respect, not only to those who are good and gentle, but even to those who are unreasonable.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 19, 'For if anyone endures the pain of unjust suffering because he is conscious of God, this is to be commended.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 20, 'How is it to your credit if you are beaten for doing wrong and you endure it? But if you suffer for doing good and you endure it, this is commendable before God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 21, 'For to this you were called, because Christ also suffered for you, leaving you an example, that you should follow in His footsteps:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 22, '“He committed no sin, and no deceit was found in His mouth.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 23, 'When they heaped abuse on Him, He did not retaliate; when He suffered, He made no threats, but entrusted Himself to Him who judges justly.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 24, 'He Himself bore our sins in His body on the tree, so that we might die to sin and live to righteousness. “By His stripes you are healed.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 2, 25, 'For “you were like sheep going astray,” but now you have returned to the Shepherd and Overseer of your souls.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 1, 'Wives, in the same way, submit yourselves to your husbands, so that even if they refuse to believe the word, they will be won over without words by the behavior of their wives'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 2, 'when they see your pure and reverent demeanor.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 3, 'Your beauty should not come from outward adornment, such as braided hair or gold jewelry or fine clothes,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 4, 'but from the inner disposition of your heart, the unfading beauty of a gentle and quiet spirit, which is precious in God’s sight.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 5, 'For this is how the holy women of the past adorned themselves. They put their hope in God and were submissive to their husbands,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 6, 'just as Sarah obeyed Abraham and called him lord. And you are her children if you do what is right and refuse to give way to fear.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 7, 'Husbands, in the same way, treat your wives with consideration as a delicate vessel, and with honor as fellow heirs of the gracious gift of life, so that your prayers will not be hindered.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 8, 'Finally, all of you, be like-minded and sympathetic, love as brothers, be tenderhearted and humble.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 9, 'Do not repay evil with evil or insult with insult, but with blessing, because to this you were called so that you may inherit a blessing.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 10, 'For, “Whoever would love life and see good days must keep his tongue from evil and his lips from deceitful speech.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 11, 'He must turn from evil and do good; he must seek peace and pursue it.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 12, 'For the eyes of the Lord are on the righteous, and His ears are inclined to their prayer. But the face of the Lord is against those who do evil.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 13, 'Who can harm you if you are zealous for what is good?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 14, 'But even if you should suffer for what is right, you are blessed. “Do not fear what they fear; do not be shaken.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 15, 'But in your hearts sanctify Christ as Lord. Always be prepared to give a defense to everyone who asks you the reason for the hope that is in you. But respond with gentleness and respect,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 16, 'keeping a clear conscience, so that those who slander you may be put to shame by your good behavior in Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 17, 'For it is better, if it is God’s will, to suffer for doing good than for doing evil.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 18, 'For Christ also suffered for sins once for all, the righteous for the unrighteous, to bring you to God. He was put to death in the body but made alive in the Spirit,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 19, 'in whom He also went and preached to the spirits in prison'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 20, 'who disobeyed long ago when God waited patiently in the days of Noah while the ark was being built. In the ark a few people, only eight souls, were saved through water.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 21, 'And this water symbolizes the baptism that now saves you also—not the removal of dirt from the body, but the pledge of a clear conscience toward God—through the resurrection of Jesus Christ,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 3, 22, 'who has gone into heaven and is at the right hand of God, with angels, authorities, and powers subject to Him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 1, 'Therefore, since Christ suffered in His body, arm yourselves with the same resolve, because anyone who has suffered in his body is done with sin.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 2, 'Consequently, he does not live out his remaining time on earth for human passions, but for the will of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 3, 'For you have spent enough time in the past carrying out the same desires as the Gentiles: living in debauchery, lust, drunkenness, orgies, carousing, and detestable idolatry.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 4, 'Because of this, they consider it strange of you not to plunge with them into the same flood of reckless indiscretion, and they heap abuse on you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 5, 'But they will have to give an account to Him who is ready to judge the living and the dead.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 6, 'That is why the gospel was preached even to those who are now dead, so that they might be judged as men in the flesh, but live according to God in the spirit.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 7, 'The end of all things is near. Therefore be clear-minded and sober, so that you can pray.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 8, 'Above all, love one another deeply, because love covers over a multitude of sins.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 9, 'Show hospitality to one another without complaining.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 10, 'As good stewards of the manifold grace of God, each of you should use whatever gift he has received to serve one another.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 11, 'If anyone speaks, he should speak as one conveying the words of God. If anyone serves, he should serve with the strength God provides, so that in all things God may be glorified through Jesus Christ, to whom be the glory and the power forever and ever. Amen.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 12, 'Beloved, do not be surprised at the fiery trial that has come upon you, as though something strange were happening to you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 13, 'But rejoice that you share in the sufferings of Christ, so that you may be overjoyed at the revelation of His glory.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 14, 'If you are insulted for the name of Christ, you are blessed, because the Spirit of glory and of God rests on you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 15, 'Indeed, none of you should suffer as a murderer or thief or wrongdoer, or even as a meddler.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 16, 'But if you suffer as a Christian, do not be ashamed, but glorify God that you bear that name.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 17, 'For it is time for judgment to begin with the family of God; and if it begins with us, what will the outcome be for those who disobey the gospel of God?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 18, 'And, “If it is hard for the righteous to be saved, what will become of the ungodly and the sinner?”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 4, 19, 'So then, those who suffer according to God’s will should entrust their souls to their faithful Creator and continue to do good.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 5, 1, 'As a fellow elder, a witness of Christ’s sufferings, and a partaker of the glory to be revealed, I appeal to the elders among you:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 5, 2, 'Be shepherds of God’s flock that is among you, watching over them not out of compulsion, but because it is God’s will; not out of greed, but out of eagerness;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 5, 3, 'not lording it over those entrusted to you, but being examples to the flock.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 5, 4, 'And when the Chief Shepherd appears, you will receive the crown of glory that will never fade away.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 5, 5, 'Young men, in the same way, submit yourselves to your elders. And all of you, clothe yourselves with humility toward one another, because, “God opposes the proud, but gives grace to the humble.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 5, 6, 'Humble yourselves, therefore, under God’s mighty hand, so that in due time He may exalt you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 5, 7, 'Cast all your anxiety on Him, because He cares for you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 5, 8, 'Be sober-minded and alert. Your adversary the devil prowls around like a roaring lion, seeking someone to devour.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 5, 9, 'Resist him, standing firm in your faith and in the knowledge that your brothers throughout the world are undergoing the same kinds of suffering.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 5, 10, 'And after you have suffered for a little while, the God of all grace, who has called you to His eternal glory in Christ, will Himself restore you, secure you, strengthen you, and establish you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 5, 11, 'To Him be the power forever and ever. Amen.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 5, 12, 'Through Silvanus, whom I regard as a faithful brother, I have written to you briefly, encouraging you and testifying that this is the true grace of God. Stand firm in it.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 5, 13, 'The church in Babylon, chosen together with you, sends you greetings, as does my son Mark.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Peter', 60, 5, 14, 'Greet one another with a kiss of love. Peace to all of you who are in Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 1, 'Simon Peter, a servant and apostle of Jesus Christ, To those who through the righteousness of our God and Savior Jesus Christ have received a faith as precious as ours:'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 2, 'Grace and peace be multiplied to you through the knowledge of God and of Jesus our Lord.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 3, 'His divine power has given us everything we need for life and godliness through the knowledge of Him who called us by His own glory and excellence.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 4, 'Through these He has given us His precious and magnificent promises, so that through them you may become partakers of the divine nature, now that you have escaped the corruption in the world caused by evil desires.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 5, 'For this very reason, make every effort to add to your faith virtue; and to virtue, knowledge;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 6, 'and to knowledge, self-control; and to self-control, perseverance; and to perseverance, godliness;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 7, 'and to godliness, brotherly kindness; and to brotherly kindness, love.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 8, 'For if you possess these qualities and continue to grow in them, they will keep you from being ineffective and unproductive in your knowledge of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 9, 'But whoever lacks these traits is nearsighted to the point of blindness, having forgotten that he has been cleansed from his past sins.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 10, 'Therefore, brothers, strive to make your calling and election sure. For if you practice these things you will never stumble,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 11, 'and you will receive a lavish reception into the eternal kingdom of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 12, 'Therefore I will always remind you of these things, even though you know them and are established in the truth you now have.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 13, 'I think it is right to refresh your memory as long as I live in the tent of my body,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 14, 'because I know that this tent will soon be laid aside, as our Lord Jesus Christ has made clear to me.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 15, 'And I will make every effort to ensure that after my departure, you will be able to recall these things at all times.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 16, 'For we did not follow cleverly devised fables when we made known to you the power and coming of our Lord Jesus Christ, but we were eyewitnesses of His majesty.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 17, 'For He received honor and glory from God the Father when the voice came to Him from the Majestic Glory, saying, “This is My beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 18, 'And we ourselves heard this voice from heaven when we were with Him on the holy mountain.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 19, 'We also have the word of the prophets as confirmed beyond doubt. And you will do well to pay attention to it, as to a lamp shining in a dark place, until the day dawns and the morning star rises in your hearts.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 20, 'Above all, you must understand that no prophecy of Scripture comes from one’s own interpretation.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 1, 21, 'For no such prophecy was ever brought forth by the will of man, but men spoke from God as they were carried along by the Holy Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 1, 'Now there were also false prophets among the people, just as there will be false teachers among you. They will secretly introduce destructive heresies, even denying the Master who bought them—bringing swift destruction on themselves.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 2, 'Many will follow in their depravity, and because of them the way of truth will be defamed.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 3, 'In their greed, these false teachers will exploit you with deceptive words. The longstanding verdict against them remains in force, and their destruction does not sleep.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 4, 'For if God did not spare the angels when they sinned, but cast them deep into hell, placing them in chains of darkness to be held for judgment;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 5, 'if He did not spare the ancient world when He brought the flood on its ungodly people, but preserved Noah, a preacher of righteousness, among the eight;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 6, 'if He condemned the cities of Sodom and Gomorrah to destruction, reducing them to ashes as an example of what is coming on the ungodly;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 7, 'and if He rescued Lot, a righteous man distressed by the depraved conduct of the lawless'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 8, '(for that righteous man, living among them day after day, was tormented in his righteous soul by the lawless deeds he saw and heard)—'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 9, 'if all this is so, then the Lord knows how to rescue the godly from trials and to hold the unrighteous for punishment on the day of judgment.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 10, 'Such punishment is specially reserved for those who indulge the corrupt desires of the flesh and despise authority. Bold and self-willed, they are unafraid to slander glorious beings.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 11, 'Yet not even angels, though greater in strength and power, dare to bring such slanderous charges against them before the Lord.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 12, 'These men are like irrational animals, creatures of instinct, born to be captured and destroyed. They blaspheme in matters they do not understand, and like such creatures, they too will be destroyed.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 13, 'The harm they will suffer is the wages of their wickedness. They consider it a pleasure to carouse in broad daylight. They are blots and blemishes, reveling in their deception as they feast with you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 14, 'Their eyes are full of adultery; their desire for sin is never satisfied; they seduce the unstable. They are accursed children with hearts trained in greed.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 15, 'They have left the straight way and wandered off to follow the way of Balaam son of Beor, who loved the wages of wickedness.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 16, 'But he was rebuked for his transgression by a donkey, otherwise without speech, that spoke with a man’s voice and restrained the prophet’s madness.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 17, 'These men are springs without water and mists driven by a storm. Blackest darkness is reserved for them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 18, 'With lofty but empty words, they appeal to the sensual passions of the flesh and entice those who are just escaping from others who live in error.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 19, 'They promise them freedom, while they themselves are slaves to depravity. For a man is a slave to whatever has mastered him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 20, 'If indeed they have escaped the corruption of the world through the knowledge of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ, only to be entangled and overcome by it again, their final condition is worse than it was at first.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 21, 'It would have been better for them not to have known the way of righteousness than to have known it and then to turn away from the holy commandment passed on to them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 2, 22, 'Of them the proverbs are true: “A dog returns to its vomit,” and, “A sow that is washed goes back to her wallowing in the mud.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 1, 'Beloved, this is now my second letter to you. Both of them are reminders to stir you to wholesome thinking'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 2, 'by recalling what was foretold by the holy prophets and commanded by our Lord and Savior through your apostles.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 3, 'Most importantly, you must understand that in the last days scoffers will come, scoffing and following their own evil desires.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 4, '“Where is the promise of His coming?” they will ask. “Ever since our fathers fell asleep, everything continues as it has from the beginning of creation.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 5, 'But they deliberately overlook the fact that long ago by God’s word the heavens existed and the earth was formed out of water and by water,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 6, 'through which the world of that time perished in the flood.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 7, 'And by that same word, the present heavens and earth are reserved for fire, being kept for the day of judgment and destruction of ungodly men.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 8, 'Beloved, do not let this one thing escape your notice: With the Lord a day is like a thousand years, and a thousand years are like a day.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 9, 'The Lord is not slow in keeping His promise as some understand slowness, but is patient with you, not wanting anyone to perish but everyone to come to repentance.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 10, 'But the Day of the Lord will come like a thief. The heavens will disappear with a roar, the elements will be destroyed by fire, and the earth and its works will be laid bare.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 11, 'Since everything will be destroyed in this way, what kind of people ought you to be? You ought to conduct yourselves in holiness and godliness'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 12, 'as you anticipate and hasten the coming of the day of God, when the heavens will be destroyed by fire and the elements will melt in the heat.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 13, 'But in keeping with God’s promise, we are looking forward to a new heaven and a new earth, where righteousness dwells.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 14, 'Therefore, beloved, as you anticipate these things, make every effort to be found at peace—spotless and blameless in His sight.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 15, 'Consider also that our Lord’s patience brings salvation, just as our beloved brother Paul also wrote you with the wisdom God gave him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 16, 'He writes this way in all his letters, speaking in them about such matters. Some parts of his letters are hard to understand, which ignorant and unstable people distort, as they do the rest of the Scriptures, to their own destruction.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 17, 'Therefore, beloved, since you already know these things, be on your guard so that you will not be carried away by the error of the lawless and fall from your secure standing.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Peter', 61, 3, 18, 'But grow in the grace and knowledge of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ. To Him be the glory both now and to the day of eternity. Amen.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 1, 1, 'That which was from the beginning, which we have heard, which we have seen with our own eyes, which we have gazed upon and touched with our own hands—this is the Word of life.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 1, 2, 'And this is the life that was revealed; we have seen it and testified to it, and we proclaim to you the eternal life that was with the Father and was revealed to us.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 1, 3, 'We proclaim to you what we have seen and heard, so that you also may have fellowship with us. And this fellowship of ours is with the Father and with His Son, Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 1, 4, 'We write these things so that our joy may be complete.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 1, 5, 'And this is the message we have heard from Him and announce to you: God is light, and in Him there is no darkness at all.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 1, 6, 'If we say we have fellowship with Him yet walk in the darkness, we lie and do not practice the truth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 1, 7, 'But if we walk in the light as He is in the light, we have fellowship with one another, and the blood of Jesus His Son cleanses us from all sin.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 1, 8, 'If we say we have no sin, we deceive ourselves, and the truth is not in us.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 1, 9, 'If we confess our sins, He is faithful and just to forgive us our sins and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 1, 10, 'If we say we have not sinned, we make Him out to be a liar, and His word is not in us.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 1, 'My little children, I am writing these things to you so that you will not sin. But if anyone does sin, we have an advocate before the Father—Jesus Christ, the Righteous One.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 2, 'He Himself is the atoning sacrifice for our sins, and not only for ours but also for the sins of the whole world.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 3, 'By this we can be sure that we have come to know Him: if we keep His commandments.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 4, 'If anyone says, “I know Him,” but does not keep His commandments, he is a liar, and the truth is not in him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 5, 'But if anyone keeps His word, the love of God has been truly perfected in him. By this we know that we are in Him:'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 6, 'Whoever claims to abide in Him must walk as Jesus walked.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 7, 'Beloved, I am not writing to you a new commandment, but an old one, which you have had from the beginning. This commandment is the message you have heard.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 8, 'Then again, I am also writing to you a new commandment, which is true in Him and also in you. For the darkness is fading and the true light is already shining.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 9, 'If anyone claims to be in the light but hates his brother, he is still in the darkness.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 10, 'Whoever loves his brother remains in the light, and there is no cause of stumbling in him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 11, 'But whoever hates his brother is in the darkness and walks in the darkness. He does not know where he is going, because the darkness has blinded his eyes.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 12, 'I am writing to you, little children, because your sins have been forgiven through His name.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 13, 'I am writing to you, fathers, because you know Him who is from the beginning. I am writing to you, young men, because you have overcome the evil one. I have written to you, children, because you know the Father.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 14, 'I have written to you, fathers, because you know Him who is from the beginning. I have written to you, young men, because you are strong, and the word of God abides in you, and you have overcome the evil one.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 15, 'Do not love the world or anything in the world. If anyone loves the world, the love of the Father is not in him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 16, 'For all that is in the world—the desires of the flesh, the desires of the eyes, and the pride of life—is not from the Father but from the world.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 17, 'The world is passing away, along with its desires; but whoever does the will of God remains forever.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 18, 'Children, it is the last hour; and just as you have heard that the antichrist is coming, so now many antichrists have appeared. This is how we know it is the last hour.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 19, 'They went out from us, but they did not belong to us. For if they had belonged to us, they would have remained with us. But their departure made it clear that none of them belonged to us.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 20, 'You, however, have an anointing from the Holy One, and all of you know the truth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 21, 'I have not written to you because you lack knowledge of the truth, but because you have it, and because no lie comes from the truth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 22, 'Who is the liar, if it is not the one who denies that Jesus is the Christ? This is the antichrist, who denies the Father and the Son.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 23, 'Whoever denies the Son does not have the Father, but whoever confesses the Son has the Father as well.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 24, 'As for you, let what you have heard from the beginning remain in you. If it does, you will also remain in the Son and in the Father.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 25, 'And this is the promise that He Himself made to us: eternal life.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 26, 'I have written these things to you about those who are trying to deceive you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 27, 'And as for you, the anointing you received from Him remains in you, and you do not need anyone to teach you. But just as His true and genuine anointing teaches you about all things, so remain in Him as you have been taught.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 28, 'And now, little children, remain in Christ, so that when He appears, we may be confident and unashamed before Him at His coming.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 2, 29, 'If you know that He is righteous, you also know that everyone who practices righteousness has been born of Him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 1, 'Behold what manner of love the Father has given to us, that we should be called children of God. And that is what we are! The reason the world does not know us is that it did not know Him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 2, 'Beloved, we are now children of God, and what we will be has not yet been revealed. We know that when Christ appears, we will be like Him, for we will see Him as He is.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 3, 'And everyone who has this hope in Him purifies himself, just as Christ is pure.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 4, 'Everyone who practices sin practices lawlessness as well. Indeed, sin is lawlessness.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 5, 'But you know that Christ appeared to take away sins, and in Him there is no sin.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 6, 'No one who remains in Him keeps on sinning. No one who continues to sin has seen Him or known Him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 7, 'Little children, let no one deceive you: The one who practices righteousness is righteous, just as Christ is righteous.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 8, 'The one who practices sin is of the devil, because the devil has been sinning from the very start. This is why the Son of God was revealed, to destroy the works of the devil.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 9, 'Anyone born of God refuses to practice sin, because God’s seed abides in him; he cannot go on sinning, because he has been born of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 10, 'By this the children of God are distinguished from the children of the devil: Anyone who does not practice righteousness is not of God, nor is anyone who does not love his brother.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 11, 'This is the message you have heard from the beginning: We should love one another.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 12, 'Do not be like Cain, who belonged to the evil one and murdered his brother. And why did Cain slay him? Because his own deeds were evil, while those of his brother were righteous.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 13, 'So do not be surprised, brothers, if the world hates you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 14, 'We know that we have passed from death to life, because we love our brothers. The one who does not love remains in death.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 15, 'Everyone who hates his brother is a murderer, and you know that eternal life does not reside in a murderer.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 16, 'By this we know what love is: Jesus laid down His life for us, and we ought to lay down our lives for our brothers.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 17, 'If anyone with earthly possessions sees his brother in need, but withholds his compassion from him, how can the love of God abide in him?'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 18, 'Little children, let us love not in word and speech, but in action and truth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 19, 'And by this we will know that we belong to the truth, and will assure our hearts in His presence:'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 20, 'Even if our hearts condemn us, God is greater than our hearts, and He knows all things.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 21, 'Beloved, if our hearts do not condemn us, we have confidence before God,'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 22, 'and we will receive from Him whatever we ask, because we keep His commandments and do what is pleasing in His sight.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 23, 'And this is His commandment: that we should believe in the name of His Son, Jesus Christ, and we should love one another just as He commanded us.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 3, 24, 'Whoever keeps His commandments remains in God, and God in him. And by this we know that He remains in us: by the Spirit He has given us.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 1, 'Beloved, do not believe every spirit, but test the spirits to see whether they are from God. For many false prophets have gone out into the world.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 2, 'By this you will know the Spirit of God: Every spirit that confesses that Jesus Christ has come in the flesh is from God,'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 3, 'and every spirit that does not confess Jesus is not from God. This is the spirit of the antichrist, which you have heard is coming and which is already in the world at this time.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 4, 'You, little children, are from God and have overcome them, because greater is He who is in you than he who is in the world.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 5, 'They are of the world. That is why they speak from the world’s perspective, and the world listens to them.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 6, 'We are from God. Whoever knows God listens to us; whoever is not from God does not listen to us. That is how we know the Spirit of truth and the spirit of deception.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 7, 'Beloved, let us love one another, because love comes from God. Everyone who loves has been born of God and knows God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 8, 'Whoever does not love does not know God, because God is love.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 9, 'This is how God’s love was revealed among us: God sent His one and only Son into the world, so that we might live through Him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 10, 'And love consists in this: not that we loved God, but that He loved us and sent His Son as the atoning sacrifice for our sins.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 11, 'Beloved, if God so loved us, we also ought to love one another.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 12, 'No one has ever seen God; but if we love one another, God remains in us, and His love is perfected in us.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 13, 'By this we know that we remain in Him, and He in us: He has given us of His Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 14, 'And we have seen and testify that the Father has sent His Son to be the Savior of the world.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 15, 'If anyone confesses that Jesus is the Son of God, God abides in him, and he in God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 16, 'And we have come to know and believe the love that God has for us. God is love; whoever abides in love abides in God, and God in him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 17, 'In this way, love has been perfected among us, so that we may have confidence on the day of judgment; for in this world we are just like Him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 18, 'There is no fear in love, but perfect love drives out fear, because fear involves punishment. The one who fears has not been perfected in love.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 19, 'We love because He first loved us.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 20, 'If anyone says, “I love God,” but hates his brother, he is a liar. For anyone who does not love his brother, whom he has seen, cannot love God, whom he has not seen.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 4, 21, 'And we have this commandment from Him: Whoever loves God must love his brother as well.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 1, 'Everyone who believes that Jesus is the Christ has been born of God, and everyone who loves the Father also loves those born of Him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 2, 'By this we know that we love the children of God: when we love God and keep His commandments.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 3, 'For this is the love of God, that we keep His commandments. And His commandments are not burdensome,'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 4, 'because everyone born of God overcomes the world. And this is the victory that has overcome the world: our faith.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 5, 'Who then overcomes the world? Only he who believes that Jesus is the Son of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 6, 'This is the One who came by water and blood, Jesus Christ—not by water alone, but by water and blood. And it is the Spirit who testifies to this, because the Spirit is the truth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 7, 'For there are three that testify:'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 8, 'the Spirit, the water, and the blood—and these three are in agreement.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 9, 'Even if we accept human testimony, the testimony of God is greater. For this is the testimony that God has given about His Son.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 10, 'Whoever believes in the Son of God has this testimony within him; whoever does not believe God has made Him out to be a liar, because he has not believed in the testimony that God has given about His Son.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 11, 'And this is that testimony: God has given us eternal life, and this life is in His Son.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 12, 'Whoever has the Son has life; whoever does not have the Son of God does not have life.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 13, 'I have written these things to you who believe in the name of the Son of God, so that you may know that you have eternal life.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 14, 'And this is the confidence that we have before Him: If we ask anything according to His will, He hears us.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 15, 'And if we know that He hears us in whatever we ask, we know that we already possess what we have asked of Him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 16, 'If anyone sees his brother committing a sin not leading to death, he should ask God, who will give life to those who commit this kind of sin. There is a sin that leads to death; I am not saying he should ask regarding that sin.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 17, 'All unrighteousness is sin, yet there is sin that does not lead to death.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 18, 'We know that anyone born of God does not keep on sinning; the One who was born of God protects him, and the evil one cannot touch him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 19, 'We know that we are of God, and that the whole world is under the power of the evil one.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 20, 'And we know that the Son of God has come and has given us understanding, so that we may know Him who is true; and we are in Him who is true—in His Son Jesus Christ. He is the true God and eternal life.'),
  ('BSB', '1 John', 62, 5, 21, 'Little children, keep yourselves from idols.'),
  ('BSB', '2 John', 63, 1, 1, 'The elder, To the chosen lady and her children, whom I love in the truth—and not I alone, but also all who know the truth—'),
  ('BSB', '2 John', 63, 1, 2, 'because of the truth that abides in us and will be with us forever:'),
  ('BSB', '2 John', 63, 1, 3, 'Grace, mercy, and peace from God the Father and from Jesus Christ, the Son of the Father, will be with us in truth and love.'),
  ('BSB', '2 John', 63, 1, 4, 'I was overjoyed to find some of your children walking in the truth, just as the Father has commanded us.'),
  ('BSB', '2 John', 63, 1, 5, 'And now I urge you, dear lady—not as a new commandment to you, but one we have had from the beginning—that we love one another.'),
  ('BSB', '2 John', 63, 1, 6, 'And this is love, that we walk according to His commandments. This is the very commandment you have heard from the beginning, that you must walk in love.'),
  ('BSB', '2 John', 63, 1, 7, 'For many deceivers have gone out into the world, refusing to confess the coming of Jesus Christ in the flesh. Any such person is the deceiver and the antichrist.'),
  ('BSB', '2 John', 63, 1, 8, 'Watch yourselves, so that you do not lose what we have worked for, but that you may be fully rewarded.'),
  ('BSB', '2 John', 63, 1, 9, 'Anyone who runs ahead without remaining in the teaching of Christ does not have God. Whoever remains in His teaching has both the Father and the Son.'),
  ('BSB', '2 John', 63, 1, 10, 'If anyone comes to you but does not bring this teaching, do not receive him into your home or even greet him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 John', 63, 1, 11, 'Whoever greets such a person shares in his evil deeds.'),
  ('BSB', '2 John', 63, 1, 12, 'I have many things to write to you, but I would prefer not to do so with paper and ink. Instead, I hope to come and speak with you face to face, so that our joy may be complete.'),
  ('BSB', '2 John', 63, 1, 13, 'The children of your elect sister send you greetings.'),
  ('BSB', '3 John', 64, 1, 1, 'The elder, To the beloved Gaius, whom I love in the truth:'),
  ('BSB', '3 John', 64, 1, 2, 'Beloved, I pray that in every way you may prosper and enjoy good health, as your soul also prospers.'),
  ('BSB', '3 John', 64, 1, 3, 'For I was overjoyed when the brothers came and testified about your devotion to the truth, in which you continue to walk.'),
  ('BSB', '3 John', 64, 1, 4, 'I have no greater joy than to hear that my children are walking in the truth.'),
  ('BSB', '3 John', 64, 1, 5, 'Beloved, you are faithful in what you are doing for the brothers, and especially since they are strangers to you.'),
  ('BSB', '3 John', 64, 1, 6, 'They have testified to the church about your love. You will do well to send them on their way in a manner worthy of God.'),
  ('BSB', '3 John', 64, 1, 7, 'For they went out on behalf of the Name, accepting nothing from the Gentiles.'),
  ('BSB', '3 John', 64, 1, 8, 'Therefore we ought to support such men, so that we may be fellow workers for the truth.'),
  ('BSB', '3 John', 64, 1, 9, 'I have written to the church about this, but Diotrephes, who loves to be first, will not accept our instruction.'),
  ('BSB', '3 John', 64, 1, 10, 'So if I come, I will call attention to his malicious slander against us. And unsatisfied with that, he refuses to welcome the brothers and forbids those who want to do so, even putting them out of the church.'),
  ('BSB', '3 John', 64, 1, 11, 'Beloved, do not imitate what is evil, but what is good. The one who does good is of God; the one who does evil has not seen God.'),
  ('BSB', '3 John', 64, 1, 12, 'Demetrius has received a good testimony from everyone, and from the truth itself. We also testify for him, and you know that our testimony is true.'),
  ('BSB', '3 John', 64, 1, 13, 'I have many things to write to you, but I would prefer not to do so with pen and ink.'),
  ('BSB', '3 John', 64, 1, 14, 'Instead, I hope to see you soon and speak with you face to face. Peace to you. The friends here send you greetings. Greet each of our friends there by name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 1, 'Jude, a servant of Jesus Christ and a brother of James, To those who are called, loved by God the Father, and kept in Jesus Christ:'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 2, 'Mercy, peace, and love be multiplied to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 3, 'Beloved, although I made every effort to write to you about the salvation we share, I felt it necessary to write and urge you to contend earnestly for the faith entrusted once for all to the saints.'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 4, 'For certain men have crept in among you unnoticed—ungodly ones who were designated long ago for condemnation. They turn the grace of our God into a license for immorality, and they deny our only Master and Lord, Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 5, 'Although you are fully aware of this, I want to remind you that after Jesus had delivered His people out of the land of Egypt, He destroyed those who did not believe.'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 6, 'And the angels who did not stay within their own domain but abandoned their proper dwelling—these He has kept in eternal chains under darkness, bound for judgment on that great day.'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 7, 'In like manner, Sodom and Gomorrah and the cities around them, who indulged in sexual immorality and pursued strange flesh, are on display as an example of those who sustain the punishment of eternal fire.'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 8, 'Yet in the same way these dreamers defile their bodies, reject authority, and slander glorious beings.'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 9, 'But even the archangel Michael, when he disputed with the devil over the body of Moses, did not presume to bring a slanderous charge against him, but said, “The Lord rebuke you!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 10, 'These men, however, slander what they do not understand, and like irrational animals, they will be destroyed by the things they do instinctively.'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 11, 'Woe to them! They have traveled the path of Cain; they have rushed headlong into the error of Balaam; they have perished in Korah’s rebellion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 12, 'These men are hidden reefs in your love feasts, shamelessly feasting with you but shepherding only themselves. They are clouds without water, carried along by the wind; fruitless trees in autumn, twice dead after being uprooted.'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 13, 'They are wild waves of the sea, foaming up their own shame; wandering stars, for whom blackest darkness has been reserved forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 14, 'Enoch, the seventh from Adam, also prophesied about them: “Behold, the Lord is coming with myriads of His holy ones'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 15, 'to execute judgment on everyone, and to convict all the ungodly of every ungodly act of wickedness and every harsh word spoken against Him by ungodly sinners.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 16, 'These men are discontented grumblers, following after their own lusts; their mouths spew arrogance; they flatter others for their own advantage.'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 17, 'But you, beloved, remember what was foretold by the apostles of our Lord Jesus Christ'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 18, 'when they said to you, “In the last times there will be scoffers who will follow after their own ungodly desires.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 19, 'These are the ones who cause divisions, who are worldly and devoid of the Spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 20, 'But you, beloved, by building yourselves up in your most holy faith and praying in the Holy Spirit,'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 21, 'keep yourselves in the love of God as you await the mercy of our Lord Jesus Christ to bring you eternal life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 22, 'And indeed, have mercy on those who doubt;'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 23, 'save others by snatching them from the fire; and to still others show mercy tempered with fear, hating even the clothing stained by the flesh.'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 24, 'Now to Him who is able to keep you from stumbling and to present you unblemished in His glorious presence, with great joy—'),
  ('BSB', 'Jude', 65, 1, 25, 'to the only God our Savior be glory, majesty, dominion, and authority through Jesus Christ our Lord before all time, and now, and for all eternity. Amen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 1, 'This is the revelation of Jesus Christ, which God gave Him to show His servants what must soon come to pass. He made it known by sending His angel to His servant John,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 2, 'who testifies to everything he saw. This is the word of God and the testimony of Jesus Christ.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 3, 'Blessed is the one who reads aloud the words of this prophecy, and blessed are those who hear and obey what is written in it, because the time is near.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 4, 'John, To the seven churches in the province of Asia: Grace and peace to you from Him who is and was and is to come, and from the seven Spirits before His throne,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 5, 'and from Jesus Christ, the faithful witness, the firstborn from the dead, and the ruler of the kings of the earth. To Him who loves us and has released us from our sins by His blood,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 6, 'who has made us to be a kingdom, priests to His God and Father—to Him be the glory and power forever and ever! Amen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 7, 'Behold, He is coming with the clouds, and every eye will see Him—even those who pierced Him. And all the tribes of the earth will mourn because of Him. So shall it be! Amen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 8, '“I am the Alpha and the Omega,” says the Lord God, who is and was and is to come—the Almighty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 9, 'I, John, your brother and partner in the tribulation and kingdom and perseverance that are in Jesus, was on the island of Patmos because of the word of God and my testimony about Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 10, 'On the Lord’s day I was in the Spirit, and I heard behind me a loud voice like a trumpet,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 11, 'saying, “Write on a scroll what you see and send it to the seven churches: to Ephesus, Smyrna, Pergamum, Thyatira, Sardis, Philadelphia, and Laodicea.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 12, 'Then I turned to see the voice that was speaking with me. And having turned, I saw seven golden lampstands,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 13, 'and among the lampstands was One like the Son of Man, dressed in a long robe, with a golden sash around His chest.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 14, 'The hair of His head was white like wool, as white as snow, and His eyes were like a blazing fire.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 15, 'His feet were like polished bronze refined in a furnace, and His voice was like the roar of many waters.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 16, 'He held in His right hand seven stars, and a sharp double-edged sword came from His mouth. His face was like the sun shining at its brightest.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 17, 'When I saw Him, I fell at His feet like a dead man. But He placed His right hand on me and said, “Do not be afraid. I am the First and the Last,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 18, 'the Living One. I was dead, and behold, now I am alive forever and ever! And I hold the keys of Death and of Hades.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 19, 'Therefore write down the things you have seen, and the things that are, and the things that will happen after this.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 1, 20, 'This is the mystery of the seven stars you saw in My right hand and of the seven golden lampstands: The seven stars are the angels of the seven churches, and the seven lampstands are the seven churches.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 1, '“To the angel of the church in Ephesus write: These are the words of Him who holds the seven stars in His right hand and walks among the seven golden lampstands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 2, 'I know your deeds, your labor, and your perseverance. I know that you cannot tolerate those who are evil, and you have tested and exposed as liars those who falsely claim to be apostles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 3, 'Without growing weary, you have persevered and endured many things for the sake of My name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 4, 'But I have this against you: You have abandoned your first love.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 5, 'Therefore, keep in mind how far you have fallen. Repent and perform the deeds you did at first. But if you do not repent, I will come to you and remove your lampstand from its place.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 6, 'But you have this to your credit: You hate the works of the Nicolaitans, which I also hate.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 7, 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches. To the one who overcomes, I will grant the right to eat from the tree of life in the Paradise of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 8, 'To the angel of the church in Smyrna write: These are the words of the First and the Last, who died and returned to life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 9, 'I know your affliction and your poverty—though you are rich! And I am aware of the slander of those who falsely claim to be Jews, but are in fact a synagogue of Satan.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 10, 'Do not fear what you are about to suffer. Look, the devil is about to throw some of you into prison to test you, and you will suffer tribulation for ten days. Be faithful even unto death, and I will give you the crown of life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 11, 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches. The one who overcomes will not be harmed by the second death.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 12, 'To the angel of the church in Pergamum write: These are the words of the One who holds the sharp, double-edged sword.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 13, 'I know where you live, where the throne of Satan sits. Yet you have held fast to My name and have not denied your faith in Me, even in the day when My faithful witness Antipas was killed among you, where Satan dwells.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 14, 'But I have a few things against you, because some of you hold to the teaching of Balaam, who taught Balak to place a stumbling block before the Israelites so they would eat food sacrificed to idols and commit sexual immorality.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 15, 'In the same way, some of you also hold to the teaching of the Nicolaitans.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 16, 'Therefore repent! Otherwise I will come to you shortly and wage war against them with the sword of My mouth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 17, 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches. To the one who overcomes, I will give the hidden manna. I will also give him a white stone inscribed with a new name, known only to the one who receives it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 18, 'To the angel of the church in Thyatira write: These are the words of the Son of God, whose eyes are like a blazing fire and whose feet are like polished bronze.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 19, 'I know your deeds—your love, your faith, your service, your perseverance—and your latter deeds are greater than your first.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 20, 'But I have this against you: You tolerate that woman Jezebel, who calls herself a prophetess. By her teaching she misleads My servants to be sexually immoral and to eat food sacrificed to idols.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 21, 'Even though I have given her time to repent of her immorality, she is unwilling.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 22, 'Behold, I will cast her onto a bed of sickness, and those who commit adultery with her will suffer great tribulation unless they repent of her deeds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 23, 'Then I will strike her children dead, and all the churches will know that I am the One who searches minds and hearts, and I will repay each of you according to your deeds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 24, 'But I say to the rest of you in Thyatira, who do not hold to her teaching and have not learned the so-called deep things of Satan: I will place no further burden upon you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 25, 'Nevertheless, hold fast to what you have until I come.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 26, 'And to the one who overcomes and continues in My work until the end, I will give authority over the nations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 27, 'He will rule them with an iron scepter and shatter them like pottery—just as I have received authority from My Father.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 28, 'And I will give him the morning star.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 2, 29, 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 1, '“To the angel of the church in Sardis write: These are the words of the One who holds the seven Spirits of God and the seven stars. I know your deeds; you have a reputation for being alive, yet you are dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 2, 'Wake up and strengthen what remains, which was about to die; for I have found your deeds incomplete in the sight of My God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 3, 'Remember, then, what you have received and heard. Keep it and repent. If you do not wake up, I will come like a thief, and you will not know the hour when I will come upon you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 4, 'But you do have a few people in Sardis who have not soiled their garments, and because they are worthy, they will walk with Me in white.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 5, 'Like them, he who overcomes will be dressed in white. And I will never blot out his name from the Book of Life, but I will confess his name before My Father and His angels.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 6, 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 7, 'To the angel of the church in Philadelphia write: These are the words of the One who is holy and true, who holds the key of David. What He opens no one can shut, and what He shuts no one can open.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 8, 'I know your deeds. See, I have placed before you an open door, which no one can shut. For you have only a little strength, yet you have kept My word and have not denied My name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 9, 'Look at those who belong to the synagogue of Satan, who claim to be Jews but are liars instead. I will make them come and bow down at your feet, and they will know that I love you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 10, 'Because you have kept My command to persevere, I will also keep you from the hour of testing that is about to come upon the whole world, to test those who dwell on the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 11, 'I am coming soon. Hold fast to what you have, so that no one will take your crown.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 12, 'The one who overcomes I will make a pillar in the temple of My God, and he will never again leave it. Upon him I will write the name of My God, and the name of the city of My God (the new Jerusalem that comes down out of heaven from My God), and My new name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 13, 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 14, 'To the angel of the church in Laodicea write: These are the words of the Amen, the faithful and true Witness, the Originator of God’s creation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 15, 'I know your deeds; you are neither cold nor hot. How I wish you were one or the other!'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 16, 'So because you are lukewarm—neither hot nor cold—I am about to vomit you out of My mouth!'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 17, 'You say, ‘I am rich; I have grown wealthy and need nothing.’ But you do not realize that you are wretched, pitiful, poor, blind, and naked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 18, 'I counsel you to buy from Me gold refined by fire so that you may become rich, white garments so that you may be clothed and your shameful nakedness not exposed, and salve to anoint your eyes so that you may see.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 19, 'Those I love, I rebuke and discipline. Therefore be earnest and repent.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 20, 'Behold, I stand at the door and knock. If anyone hears My voice and opens the door, I will come in and dine with him, and he with Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 21, 'To the one who overcomes, I will grant the right to sit with Me on My throne, just as I overcame and sat down with My Father on His throne.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 3, 22, 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 4, 1, 'After this I looked and saw a door standing open in heaven. And the voice I had previously heard speak to me like a trumpet was saying, “Come up here, and I will show you what must happen after these things.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 4, 2, 'At once I was in the Spirit, and I saw a throne standing in heaven, with someone seated on it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 4, 3, 'The One seated there looked like jasper and carnelian, and a rainbow that gleamed like an emerald encircled the throne.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 4, 4, 'Surrounding the throne were twenty-four other thrones, and on these thrones sat twenty-four elders dressed in white, with golden crowns on their heads.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 4, 5, 'From the throne came flashes of lightning, and rumblings, and peals of thunder. Before the throne burned seven torches of fire. These are the seven Spirits of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 4, 6, 'And before the throne was something like a sea of glass, as clear as crystal. In the center, around the throne, were four living creatures, covered with eyes in front and back.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 4, 7, 'The first living creature was like a lion, the second like a calf, the third had a face like a man, and the fourth was like an eagle in flight.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 4, 8, 'And each of the four living creatures had six wings and was covered with eyes all around and within. Day and night they never stop saying: “Holy, Holy, Holy, is the Lord God Almighty, who was and is and is to come!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 4, 9, 'And whenever the living creatures give glory, honor, and thanks to the One seated on the throne who lives forever and ever,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 4, 10, 'the twenty-four elders fall down before the One seated on the throne, and they worship Him who lives forever and ever. They cast their crowns before the throne, saying:'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 4, 11, '“Worthy are You, our Lord and God, to receive glory and honor and power, for You created all things; by Your will they exist and came to be.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 5, 1, 'Then I saw a scroll in the right hand of the One seated on the throne. It had writing on both sides and was sealed with seven seals.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 5, 2, 'And I saw a mighty angel proclaiming in a loud voice, “Who is worthy to break the seals and open the scroll?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 5, 3, 'But no one in heaven or on earth or under the earth was able to open the scroll or look inside it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 5, 4, 'And I began to weep bitterly, because no one was found worthy to open the scroll or look inside it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 5, 5, 'Then one of the elders said to me, “Do not weep! Behold, the Lion of the tribe of Judah, the Root of David, has triumphed to open the scroll and its seven seals.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 5, 6, 'Then I saw a Lamb who appeared to have been slain, standing in the center of the throne, encircled by the four living creatures and the elders. The Lamb had seven horns and seven eyes, which represent the seven Spirits of God sent out into all the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 5, 7, 'And He came and took the scroll from the right hand of the One seated on the throne.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 5, 8, 'When He had taken the scroll, the four living creatures and the twenty-four elders fell down before the Lamb. Each one had a harp, and they were holding golden bowls full of incense, which are the prayers of the saints.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 5, 9, 'And they sang a new song: “Worthy are You to take the scroll and open its seals, because You were slain, and by Your blood You purchased for God those from every tribe and tongue and people and nation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 5, 10, 'You have made them to be a kingdom and priests to serve our God, and they will reign upon the earth.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 5, 11, 'Then I looked, and I heard the voices of many angels and living creatures and elders encircling the throne, and their number was myriads of myriads and thousands of thousands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 5, 12, 'In a loud voice they were saying: “Worthy is the Lamb, who was slain, to receive power and riches and wisdom and strength and honor and glory and blessing!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 5, 13, 'And I heard every creature in heaven and on earth and under the earth and in the sea, and all that is in them, saying: “To Him who sits on the throne and to the Lamb be praise and honor and glory and power forever and ever!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 5, 14, 'And the four living creatures said, “Amen,” and the elders fell down and worshiped.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 6, 1, 'Then I watched as the Lamb opened one of the seven seals, and I heard one of the four living creatures say in a thunderous voice, “Come!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 6, 2, 'So I looked and saw a white horse, and its rider held a bow. And he was given a crown, and he rode out to overcome and conquer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 6, 3, 'And when the Lamb opened the second seal, I heard the second living creature say, “Come!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 6, 4, 'Then another horse went forth. It was bright red, and its rider was granted permission to take away peace from the earth and to make men slay one another. And he was given a great sword.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 6, 5, 'And when the Lamb opened the third seal, I heard the third living creature say, “Come!” Then I looked and saw a black horse, and its rider held in his hand a pair of scales.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 6, 6, 'And I heard what sounded like a voice from among the four living creatures, saying, “A quart of wheat for a denarius, and three quarts of barley for a denarius, and do not harm the oil and wine.”');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 6, 7, 'And when the Lamb opened the fourth seal, I heard the voice of the fourth living creature say, “Come!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 6, 8, 'Then I looked and saw a pale green horse. Its rider’s name was Death, and Hades followed close behind. And they were given authority over a fourth of the earth, to kill by sword, by famine, by plague, and by the beasts of the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 6, 9, 'And when the Lamb opened the fifth seal, I saw under the altar the souls of those who had been slain for the word of God and for the testimony they had upheld.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 6, 10, 'And they cried out in a loud voice, “How long, O Lord, holy and true, until You avenge our blood and judge those who dwell upon the earth?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 6, 11, 'Then each of them was given a white robe and told to rest a little while longer, until the full number of their fellow servants, their brothers, were killed, just as they had been killed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 6, 12, 'And when I saw the Lamb open the sixth seal, there was a great earthquake, and the sun became black like sackcloth of goat hair, and the whole moon turned blood red,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 6, 13, 'and the stars of the sky fell to the earth like unripe figs dropping from a tree shaken by a great wind.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 6, 14, 'The sky receded like a scroll being rolled up, and every mountain and island was moved from its place.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 6, 15, 'Then the kings of the earth, the nobles, the commanders, the rich, the mighty, and every slave and free man hid in the caves and among the rocks of the mountains.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 6, 16, 'And they said to the mountains and the rocks, “Fall on us and hide us from the face of the One seated on the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 6, 17, 'For the great day of Their wrath has come, and who is able to withstand it?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 7, 1, 'After this I saw four angels standing at the four corners of the earth, holding back its four winds so that no wind would blow on land or sea or on any tree.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 7, 2, 'And I saw another angel ascending from the east, with the seal of the living God. And he called out in a loud voice to the four angels who had been given power to harm the land and the sea:'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 7, 3, '“Do not harm the land or sea or trees until we have sealed the foreheads of the servants of our God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 7, 4, 'And I heard the number of those who were sealed, 144,000 from all the tribes of Israel:'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 7, 5, 'From the tribe of Judah 12,000 were sealed, from the tribe of Reuben 12,000, from the tribe of Gad 12,000,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 7, 6, 'from the tribe of Asher 12,000, from the tribe of Naphtali 12,000, from the tribe of Manasseh 12,000,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 7, 7, 'from the tribe of Simeon 12,000, from the tribe of Levi 12,000, from the tribe of Issachar 12,000,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 7, 8, 'from the tribe of Zebulun 12,000, from the tribe of Joseph 12,000, and from the tribe of Benjamin 12,000.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 7, 9, 'After this I looked and saw a multitude too large to count, from every nation and tribe and people and tongue, standing before the throne and before the Lamb. They were wearing white robes and holding palm branches in their hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 7, 10, 'And they cried out in a loud voice: “Salvation to our God, who sits on the throne, and to the Lamb!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 7, 11, 'And all the angels stood around the throne and around the elders and the four living creatures. And they fell facedown before the throne and worshiped God,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 7, 12, 'saying, “Amen! Blessing and glory and wisdom and thanks and honor and power and strength be to our God forever and ever! Amen.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 7, 13, 'Then one of the elders addressed me: “These in white robes,” he asked, “who are they, and where have they come from?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 7, 14, '“Sir,” I answered, “you know.” So he replied, “These are the ones who have come out of the great tribulation; they have washed their robes and made them white in the blood of the Lamb.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 7, 15, 'For this reason, they are before the throne of God and serve Him day and night in His temple; and the One seated on the throne will spread His tabernacle over them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 7, 16, '‘Never again will they hunger, and never will they thirst; nor will the sun beat down upon them, nor any scorching heat.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 7, 17, 'For the Lamb in the center of the throne will be their shepherd. ‘He will lead them to springs of living water,’ and ‘God will wipe away every tear from their eyes.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 8, 1, 'When the Lamb opened the seventh seal, there was silence in heaven for about half an hour.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 8, 2, 'And I saw the seven angels who stand before God, and they were given seven trumpets.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 8, 3, 'Then another angel, who had a golden censer, came and stood at the altar. He was given much incense to offer, along with the prayers of all the saints, on the golden altar before the throne.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 8, 4, 'And the smoke of the incense, together with the prayers of the saints, rose up before God from the hand of the angel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 8, 5, 'Then the angel took the censer, filled it with fire from the altar, and hurled it to the earth; and there were peals of thunder, and rumblings, and flashes of lightning, and an earthquake.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 8, 6, 'And the seven angels with the seven trumpets prepared to sound them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 8, 7, 'Then the first angel sounded his trumpet, and hail and fire mixed with blood were hurled down upon the earth. A third of the earth was burned up, along with a third of the trees and all the green grass.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 8, 8, 'Then the second angel sounded his trumpet, and something like a great mountain burning with fire was thrown into the sea. A third of the sea turned to blood,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 8, 9, 'a third of the living creatures in the sea died, and a third of the ships were destroyed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 8, 10, 'Then the third angel sounded his trumpet, and a great star burning like a torch fell from heaven and landed on a third of the rivers and on the springs of water.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 8, 11, 'The name of the star is Wormwood. A third of the waters turned bitter like wormwood oil, and many people died from the bitter waters.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 8, 12, 'Then the fourth angel sounded his trumpet, and a third of the sun and moon and stars were struck. A third of the stars were darkened, a third of the day was without light, and a third of the night as well.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 8, 13, 'And as I observed, I heard an eagle flying overhead, calling in a loud voice, “Woe! Woe! Woe to those who dwell on the earth, because of the trumpet blasts about to be sounded by the remaining three angels!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 1, 'Then the fifth angel sounded his trumpet, and I saw a star that had fallen from heaven to earth, and it was given the key to the pit of the Abyss.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 2, 'The star opened the pit of the Abyss, and smoke rose out of it like the smoke of a great furnace, and the sun and the air were darkened by the smoke from the pit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 3, 'And out of the smoke, locusts descended on the earth, and they were given power like that of the scorpions of the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 4, 'They were told not to harm the grass of the earth or any plant or tree, but only those who did not have the seal of God on their foreheads.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 5, 'The locusts were not given power to kill them, but only to torment them for five months, and their torment was like the stinging of a scorpion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 6, 'In those days men will seek death and will not find it; they will long to die, but death will escape them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 7, 'And the locusts looked like horses prepared for battle, with something like crowns of gold on their heads, and faces like the faces of men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 8, 'They had hair like that of women, and teeth like those of lions.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 9, 'They also had thoraxes like breastplates of iron, and the sound of their wings was like the roar of many horses and chariots rushing into battle.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 10, 'They had tails with stingers like scorpions, which had the power to injure people for five months.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 11, 'They were ruled by a king, the angel of the Abyss. His name in Hebrew is Abaddon, and in Greek it is Apollyon.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 12, 'The first woe has passed. Behold, two woes are still to follow.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 13, 'Then the sixth angel sounded his trumpet, and I heard a voice from the four horns of the golden altar before God'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 14, 'saying to the sixth angel with the trumpet, “Release the four angels who are bound at the great river Euphrates.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 15, 'So the four angels who had been prepared for this hour and day and month and year were released to kill a third of mankind.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 16, 'And the number of mounted troops was two hundred million; I heard their number.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 17, 'Now the horses and riders in my vision looked like this: The riders had breastplates the colors of fire, sapphire, and sulfur. The heads of the horses were like the heads of lions, and out of their mouths proceeded fire, smoke, and sulfur.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 18, 'A third of mankind was killed by the three plagues of fire, smoke, and sulfur that proceeded from their mouths.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 19, 'For the power of the horses was in their mouths and in their tails; indeed, their tails were like snakes, having heads with which to inflict harm.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 20, 'Now the rest of mankind who were not killed by these plagues still did not repent of the works of their hands. They did not stop worshiping demons and idols of gold, silver, bronze, stone, and wood, which cannot see or hear or walk.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 9, 21, 'Furthermore, they did not repent of their murder, sorcery, sexual immorality, and theft.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 10, 1, 'Then I saw another mighty angel coming down from heaven, wrapped in a cloud, with a rainbow above his head. His face was like the sun, and his legs were like pillars of fire.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 10, 2, 'He held in his hand a small scroll, which lay open. He placed his right foot on the sea and his left foot on the land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 10, 3, 'Then he cried out in a loud voice like the roar of a lion. And when he cried out, the seven thunders sounded their voices.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 10, 4, 'When the seven thunders had spoken, I was about to put it in writing. But I heard a voice from heaven saying, “Seal up what the seven thunders have said, and do not write it down.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 10, 5, 'Then the angel I had seen standing on the sea and on the land lifted up his right hand to heaven.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 10, 6, 'And he swore by Him who lives forever and ever, who created heaven and everything in it, the earth and everything in it, and the sea and everything in it: “There will be no more delay!'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 10, 7, 'But in the days of the voice of the seventh angel, when he is about to sound his trumpet, the mystery of God will be fulfilled, just as He proclaimed to His servants the prophets.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 10, 8, 'Then the voice that I had heard from heaven spoke to me again, saying, “Go, take the small scroll that lies open in the hand of the angel standing on the sea and on the land.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 10, 9, 'And I went to the angel and said, “Give me the small scroll.” “Take it and eat it,” he said. “It will make your stomach bitter, but in your mouth it will be as sweet as honey.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 10, 10, 'So I took the small scroll from the angel’s hand and ate it; and it was as sweet as honey in my mouth, but when I had eaten it, my stomach turned bitter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 10, 11, 'And they told me, “You must prophesy again about many peoples and nations and tongues and kings.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 1, 'Then I was given a measuring rod like a staff and was told, “Go and measure the temple of God and the altar, and count the number of worshipers there.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 2, 'But exclude the courtyard outside the temple. Do not measure it, because it has been given over to the nations, and they will trample the holy city for 42 months.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 3, 'And I will empower my two witnesses, and they will prophesy for 1,260 days, clothed in sackcloth.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 4, 'These witnesses are the two olive trees and the two lampstands that stand before the Lord of the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 5, 'If anyone wants to harm them, fire proceeds from their mouths and devours their enemies. In this way, anyone who wants to harm them must be killed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 6, 'These witnesses have power to shut the sky so that no rain will fall during the days of their prophecy, and power to turn the waters into blood and to strike the earth with every kind of plague as often as they wish.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 7, 'When the two witnesses have finished their testimony, the beast that comes up from the Abyss will wage war with them, and will overpower and kill them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 8, 'Their bodies will lie in the street of the great city—figuratively called Sodom and Egypt—where their Lord was also crucified.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 9, 'For three and a half days all peoples and tribes and tongues and nations will view their bodies and will not permit them to be laid in a tomb.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 10, 'And those who dwell on the earth will gloat over them, and will celebrate and send one another gifts, because these two prophets had tormented them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 11, 'But after the three and a half days, the breath of life from God entered the two witnesses, and they stood on their feet, and great fear fell upon those who saw them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 12, 'And the witnesses heard a loud voice from heaven saying, “Come up here.” And they went up to heaven in a cloud as their enemies watched them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 13, 'And in that hour there was a great earthquake, and a tenth of the city collapsed. Seven thousand were killed in the quake, and the rest were terrified and gave glory to the God of heaven.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 14, 'The second woe has passed. Behold, the third woe is coming shortly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 15, 'Then the seventh angel sounded his trumpet, and loud voices called out in heaven: “The kingdom of the world has become the kingdom of our Lord and of His Christ, and He will reign forever and ever.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 16, 'And the twenty-four elders who sit on their thrones before God fell on their faces and worshiped God,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 17, 'saying: “We give thanks to You, O Lord God Almighty, the One who is and who was, because You have taken Your great power and have begun to reign.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 18, 'The nations were enraged, and Your wrath has come. The time has come to judge the dead and to reward Your servants the prophets, as well as the saints and those who fear Your name, both small and great— and to destroy those who destroy the earth.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 11, 19, 'Then the temple of God in heaven was opened, and the ark of His covenant appeared in His temple. And there were flashes of lightning, and rumblings, and peals of thunder, and an earthquake, and a great hailstorm.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 12, 1, 'And a great sign appeared in heaven: a woman clothed in the sun, with the moon under her feet and a crown of twelve stars on her head.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 12, 2, 'She was pregnant and crying out in the pain and agony of giving birth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 12, 3, 'Then another sign appeared in heaven: a huge red dragon with seven heads, ten horns, and seven royal crowns on his heads.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 12, 4, 'His tail swept a third of the stars from the sky, tossing them to the earth. And the dragon stood before the woman who was about to give birth, ready to devour her child as soon as she gave birth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 12, 5, 'And she gave birth to a son, a male child, who will rule all the nations with an iron scepter. And her child was caught up to God and to His throne.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 12, 6, 'And the woman fled into the wilderness, where God had prepared a place for her to be nourished for 1,260 days.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 12, 7, 'Then a war broke out in heaven: Michael and his angels fought against the dragon, and the dragon and his angels fought back.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 12, 8, 'But the dragon was not strong enough, and no longer was any place found in heaven for him and his angels.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 12, 9, 'And the great dragon was hurled down—that ancient serpent called the devil and Satan, the deceiver of the whole world. He was hurled to the earth, and his angels with him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 12, 10, 'And I heard a loud voice in heaven saying: “Now have come the salvation and the power and the kingdom of our God, and the authority of His Christ. For the accuser of our brothers has been thrown down— he who accuses them day and night before our God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 12, 11, 'They have conquered him by the blood of the Lamb and by the word of their testimony. And they did not love their lives so as to shy away from death.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 12, 12, 'Therefore rejoice, O heavens, and you who dwell in them! But woe to the earth and the sea; with great fury the devil has come down to you, knowing he has only a short time.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 12, 13, 'And when the dragon saw that he had been thrown to the earth, he pursued the woman who had given birth to the male child.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 12, 14, 'But the woman was given two wings of a great eagle to fly from the presence of the serpent to her place in the wilderness, where she was nourished for a time, and times, and half a time.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 12, 15, 'Then from the mouth of the serpent spewed water like a river to overtake the woman and sweep her away in the torrent.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 12, 16, 'But the earth helped the woman and opened its mouth to swallow up the river that had poured from the dragon’s mouth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 12, 17, 'And the dragon was enraged at the woman, and went to make war with the rest of her children, who keep the commandments of God and hold to the testimony of Jesus. And the dragon stood on the shore of the sea.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 1, 'Then I saw a beast with ten horns and seven heads rising out of the sea. There were ten royal crowns on its horns and blasphemous names on its heads.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 2, 'The beast I saw was like a leopard, with the feet of a bear and the mouth of a lion. And the dragon gave the beast his power and his throne and great authority.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 3, 'One of the heads of the beast appeared to be mortally wounded. But the mortal wound was healed, and the whole world marveled and followed the beast.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 4, 'They worshiped the dragon who had given authority to the beast, and they worshiped the beast, saying, “Who is like the beast, and who can wage war against it?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 5, 'The beast was given a mouth to speak arrogant and blasphemous words, and authority to act for 42 months.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 6, 'And the beast opened its mouth to speak blasphemies against God and to slander His name and His tabernacle—those who dwell in heaven.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 7, 'Then the beast was permitted to wage war against the saints and to conquer them, and it was given authority over every tribe and people and tongue and nation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 8, 'And all who dwell on the earth will worship the beast—all whose names have not been written from the foundation of the world in the Book of Life belonging to the Lamb who was slain.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 9, 'He who has an ear, let him hear:'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 10, '“If anyone is destined for captivity, into captivity he will go; if anyone is to die by the sword, by the sword he must be killed.” Here is a call for the perseverance and faith of the saints.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 11, 'Then I saw another beast rising out of the earth. This beast had two horns like a lamb, but spoke like a dragon.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 12, 'And this beast exercised all the authority of the first beast and caused the earth and those who dwell in it to worship the first beast, whose mortal wound had been healed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 13, 'And the second beast performed great signs to cause even fire from heaven to come down to earth in the presence of the people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 14, 'Because of the signs it was given to perform on behalf of the first beast, it deceived those who dwell on the earth, telling them to make an image to the beast that had been wounded by the sword and yet had lived.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 15, 'The second beast was permitted to give breath to the image of the first beast, so that the image could speak and cause all who refused to worship it to be killed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 16, 'And the second beast required all people small and great, rich and poor, free and slave, to receive a mark on their right hand or on their forehead,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 17, 'so that no one could buy or sell unless he had the mark—the name of the beast or the number of its name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 13, 18, 'Here is a call for wisdom: Let the one who has insight calculate the number of the beast, for it is the number of a man, and that number is 666.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 1, 'Then I looked and saw the Lamb standing on Mount Zion, and with Him 144,000 who had His name and His Father’s name written on their foreheads.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 2, 'And I heard a sound from heaven like the roar of many waters and the loud rumbling of thunder. And the sound I heard was like harpists strumming their harps.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 3, 'And they sang a new song before the throne and before the four living creatures and the elders. And no one could learn the song except the 144,000 who had been redeemed from the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 4, 'These are the ones who have not been defiled with women, for they are virgins. They follow the Lamb wherever He goes. They have been redeemed from among men as firstfruits to God and to the Lamb.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 5, 'And no lie was found in their mouths; they are blameless.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 6, 'Then I saw another angel flying overhead, with the eternal gospel to proclaim to those who dwell on the earth—to every nation and tribe and tongue and people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 7, 'And he said in a loud voice, “Fear God and give Him glory, because the hour of His judgment has come. Worship the One who made the heavens and the earth and the sea and the springs of waters.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 8, 'Then a second angel followed, saying, “Fallen, fallen is Babylon the great, who has made all the nations drink the wine of the passion of her immorality.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 9, 'And a third angel followed them, calling out in a loud voice, “If anyone worships the beast and its image, and receives its mark on his forehead or on his hand,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 10, 'he too will drink the wine of God’s anger, poured undiluted into the cup of His wrath. And he will be tormented in fire and sulfur in the presence of the holy angels and of the Lamb.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 11, 'And the smoke of their torment rises forever and ever. Day and night there is no rest for those who worship the beast and its image, or for anyone who receives the mark of its name.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 12, 'Here is a call for the perseverance of the saints who keep the commandments of God and the faith of Jesus.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 13, 'And I heard a voice from heaven telling me to write, “Blessed are the dead—those who die in the Lord from this moment on.” “Yes,” says the Spirit, “they will rest from their labors, for their deeds will follow them.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 14, 'And I looked and saw a white cloud, and seated on the cloud was One like the Son of Man, with a golden crown on His head and a sharp sickle in His hand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 15, 'Then another angel came out of the temple, crying out in a loud voice to the One seated on the cloud, “Swing Your sickle and reap, because the time has come to harvest; for the crop of the earth is ripe.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 16, 'So the One seated on the cloud swung His sickle over the earth, and the earth was harvested.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 17, 'Then another angel came out of the temple in heaven, and he too had a sharp sickle.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 18, 'Still another angel, with authority over the fire, came from the altar and called out in a loud voice to the angel with the sharp sickle, “Swing your sharp sickle and gather the clusters of grapes from the vine of the earth, because its grapes are ripe.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 19, 'So the angel swung his sickle over the earth and gathered the grapes of the earth, and he threw them into the great winepress of God’s wrath.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 14, 20, 'And the winepress was trodden outside the city, and the blood that flowed from it rose as high as the bridles of the horses for a distance of 1,600 stadia.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 15, 1, 'Then I saw another great and marvelous sign in heaven: seven angels with the seven final plagues, with which the wrath of God is completed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 15, 2, 'And I saw something like a sea of glass mixed with fire, beside which stood those who had conquered the beast and its image and the number of its name. They were holding harps from God,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 15, 3, 'and they sang the song of God’s servant Moses and of the Lamb: “Great and wonderful are Your works, O Lord God Almighty! Just and true are Your ways, O King of the nations!'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 15, 4, 'Who will not fear You, O Lord, and glorify Your name? For You alone are holy. All nations will come and worship before You, for Your righteous acts have been revealed.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 15, 5, 'After this I looked, and the temple—the tabernacle of the Testimony—was opened in heaven.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 15, 6, 'And out of the temple came the seven angels with the seven plagues, dressed in clean and bright linen and girded with golden sashes around their chests.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 15, 7, 'Then one of the four living creatures gave the seven angels seven golden bowls full of the wrath of God, who lives forever and ever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 15, 8, 'And the temple was filled with smoke from the glory of God and from His power; and no one could enter the temple until the seven plagues of the seven angels were completed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 1, 'Then I heard a loud voice from the temple saying to the seven angels, “Go, pour out on the earth the seven bowls of God’s wrath.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 2, 'So the first angel went and poured out his bowl on the earth, and loathsome, malignant sores broke out on those who had the mark of the beast and worshiped its image.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 3, 'And the second angel poured out his bowl into the sea, and it turned to blood like that of the dead, and every living thing in the sea died.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 4, 'And the third angel poured out his bowl into the rivers and springs of water, and they turned to blood.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 5, 'And I heard the angel of the waters say: “Righteous are You, O Holy One, who is and was, because You have brought these judgments.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 6, 'For they have spilled the blood of saints and prophets, and You have given them blood to drink, as they deserve.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 7, 'And I heard the altar reply: “Yes, Lord God Almighty, true and just are Your judgments.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 8, 'Then the fourth angel poured out his bowl on the sun, and it was given power to scorch the people with fire.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 9, 'And the people were scorched by intense heat, and they cursed the name of God, who had authority over these plagues; yet they did not repent and give Him glory.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 10, 'And the fifth angel poured out his bowl on the throne of the beast, and its kingdom was plunged into darkness, and men began to gnaw their tongues in anguish'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 11, 'and curse the God of heaven for their pains and sores; yet they did not repent of their deeds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 12, 'And the sixth angel poured out his bowl on the great river Euphrates, and its water was dried up to prepare the way for the kings of the East.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 13, 'And I saw three unclean spirits that looked like frogs coming out of the mouths of the dragon, the beast, and the false prophet.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 14, 'These are demonic spirits that perform signs and go out to all the kings of the earth, to assemble them for battle on the great day of God the Almighty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 15, '“Behold, I am coming like a thief. Blessed is the one who remains awake and clothed, so that he will not go naked and let his shame be exposed.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 16, 'And they assembled the kings in the place that in Hebrew is called Armageddon.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 17, 'Then the seventh angel poured out his bowl into the air, and a loud voice came from the throne in the temple, saying, “It is done!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 18, 'And there were flashes of lightning, and rumblings, and peals of thunder, and a great earthquake the likes of which had not occurred since men were upon the earth—so mighty was the great quake.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 19, 'The great city was split into three parts, and the cities of the nations collapsed. And God remembered Babylon the great and gave her the cup of the wine of the fury of His wrath.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 20, 'Then every island fled, and no mountain could be found.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 16, 21, 'And great hailstones weighing almost a hundred pounds each rained down on them from above. And men cursed God for the plague of hail, because it was so horrendous.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 1, 'Then one of the seven angels with the seven bowls came and said to me, “Come, I will show you the punishment of the great prostitute, who sits on many waters.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 2, 'The kings of the earth were immoral with her, and those who dwell on the earth were intoxicated with the wine of her immorality.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 3, 'And the angel carried me away in the Spirit into a wilderness, where I saw a woman sitting on a scarlet beast that was covered with blasphemous names and had seven heads and ten horns.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 4, 'The woman was dressed in purple and scarlet, and adorned with gold and precious stones and pearls. She held in her hand a golden cup full of abominations and the impurities of her sexual immorality.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 5, 'And on her forehead a mysterious name was written: BABYLON THE GREAT, THE MOTHER OF PROSTITUTES AND OF THE ABOMINATIONS OF THE EARTH.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 6, 'I could see that the woman was drunk with the blood of the saints and witnesses for Jesus. And I was utterly amazed at the sight of her.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 7, '“Why are you so amazed?” said the angel. “I will tell you the mystery of the woman and of the beast that carries her, which has the seven heads and ten horns.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 8, 'The beast that you saw—it was, and now is no more, but is about to come up out of the Abyss and go to its destruction. And those who dwell on the earth whose names were not written in the Book of Life from the foundation of the world will marvel when they see the beast that was, and is not, and yet will be.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 9, 'This calls for a mind with wisdom. The seven heads are seven mountains on which the woman sits.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 10, 'There are also seven kings. Five have fallen, one is, and the other has not yet come; but when he does come, he must remain for only a little while.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 11, 'The beast that was, and now is not, is an eighth king, who belongs to the other seven and is going into destruction.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 12, 'The ten horns you saw are ten kings who have not yet received a kingdom, but will receive one hour of authority as kings, along with the beast.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 13, 'These kings have one purpose: to yield their power and authority to the beast.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 14, 'They will make war against the Lamb, and the Lamb will triumph over them, because He is Lord of lords and King of kings; and He will be accompanied by His called and chosen and faithful ones.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 15, 'Then the angel said to me, “The waters you saw, where the prostitute was seated, are peoples and multitudes and nations and tongues.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 16, 'And the ten horns and the beast that you saw will hate the prostitute. They will leave her desolate and naked, and will eat her flesh and burn her with fire.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 17, 'For God has put it into their hearts to carry out His purpose by uniting to give their kingdom to the beast, until the words of God are fulfilled.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 17, 18, 'And the woman you saw is the great city that rules over the kings of the earth.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 1, 'After this I saw another angel descending from heaven with great authority, and the earth was illuminated by his glory.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 2, 'And he cried out in a mighty voice: “Fallen, fallen is Babylon the great! She has become a lair for demons and a haunt for every unclean spirit, every unclean bird, and every detestable beast.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 3, 'All the nations have drunk the wine of the passion of her immorality. The kings of the earth were immoral with her, and the merchants of the earth have grown wealthy from the extravagance of her luxury.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 4, 'Then I heard another voice from heaven say: “Come out of her, My people, so that you will not share in her sins or contract any of her plagues.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 5, 'For her sins are piled up to heaven, and God has remembered her iniquities.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 6, 'Give back to her as she has done to others; pay her back double for what she has done; mix her a double portion in her own cup.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 7, 'As much as she has glorified herself and lived in luxury, give her the same measure of torment and grief. In her heart she says, ‘I sit as queen; I am not a widow and will never see grief.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 8, 'Therefore her plagues will come in one day— death and grief and famine— and she will be consumed by fire, for mighty is the Lord God who judges her.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 9, 'Then the kings of the earth who committed sexual immorality and lived in luxury with her will weep and wail at the sight of the smoke rising from the fire that consumes her.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 10, 'In fear of her torment, they will stand at a distance and cry out: “Woe, woe to the great city, the mighty city of Babylon! For in a single hour your judgment has come.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 11, 'And the merchants of the earth will weep and mourn over her, because there is no one left to buy their cargo—'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 12, 'cargo of gold, silver, precious stones, and pearls; of fine linen, purple, silk, and scarlet; of all kinds of citron wood and every article of ivory, precious wood, bronze, iron, and marble;'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 13, 'of cinnamon, spice, incense, myrrh, and frankincense; of wine, olive oil, fine flour, and wheat; of cattle, sheep, horses, and chariots; of slaves and souls of men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 14, 'And they will say: “The fruit of your soul’s desire has departed from you; all your luxury and splendor have vanished, never to be seen again.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 15, 'The merchants who sold these things and grew their wealth from her will stand at a distance, in fear of her torment. They will weep and mourn,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 16, 'saying: “Woe, woe to the great city, clothed in fine linen and purple and scarlet, adorned with gold and precious stones and pearls!'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 17, 'For in a single hour such fabulous wealth has been destroyed!” Every shipmaster, passenger, and sailor, and all who make their living from the sea, will stand at a distance'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 18, 'and cry out at the sight of the smoke rising from the fire that consumes her. “What city was ever like this great city?” they will exclaim.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 19, 'Then they will throw dust on their heads as they weep and mourn and cry out: “Woe, woe to the great city, where all who had ships on the sea were enriched by her wealth! For in a single hour she has been destroyed.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 20, 'Rejoice over her, O heaven, O saints and apostles and prophets, because God has pronounced for you His judgment against her.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 21, 'Then a mighty angel picked up a stone the size of a great millstone and cast it into the sea, saying: “With such violence the great city of Babylon will be cast down, never to be seen again.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 22, 'And the sound of harpists and musicians, of flute players and trumpeters, will never ring out in you again. Nor will any craftsmen of any trade be found in you again, nor the sound of a millstone be heard in you again.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 23, 'The light of a lamp will never shine in you again, and the voices of a bride and bridegroom will never call out in you again. For your merchants were the great ones of the earth, because all the nations were deceived by your sorcery.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 18, 24, 'And there was found in her the blood of prophets and saints, and of all who had been slain on the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 1, 'After this I heard a sound like the roar of a great multitude in heaven, shouting: “Hallelujah! Salvation and glory and power belong to our God!'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 2, 'For His judgments are true and just. He has judged the great prostitute who corrupted the earth with her immorality. He has avenged the blood of His servants that was poured out by her hand.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 3, 'And a second time they called out: “Hallelujah! Her smoke rises forever and ever.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 4, 'And the twenty-four elders and the four living creatures fell down and worshiped God who sits on the throne, saying: “Amen, Hallelujah!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 5, 'Then a voice came from the throne, saying: “Praise our God, all you who serve Him, and those who fear Him, small and great alike!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 6, 'And I heard a sound like the roar of a great multitude, like the rushing of many waters, and like a mighty rumbling of thunder, crying out: “Hallelujah! For the Lord our God the Almighty reigns.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 7, 'Let us rejoice and be glad and give Him the glory. For the marriage of the Lamb has come, and His bride has made herself ready.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 8, 'She was given clothing of fine linen, bright and pure.” For the fine linen she wears is the righteous acts of the saints.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 9, 'Then the angel told me to write, “Blessed are those who are invited to the marriage supper of the Lamb.” And he said to me, “These are the true words of God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 10, 'So I fell at his feet to worship him. But he told me, “Do not do that! I am a fellow servant with you and your brothers who rely on the testimony of Jesus. Worship God! For the testimony of Jesus is the spirit of prophecy.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 11, 'Then I saw heaven standing open, and there before me was a white horse. And its rider is called Faithful and True. With righteousness He judges and wages war.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 12, 'He has eyes like blazing fire, and many royal crowns on His head. He has a name written on Him that only He Himself knows.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 13, 'He is dressed in a robe dipped in blood, and His name is The Word of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 14, 'The armies of heaven, dressed in fine linen, white and pure, follow Him on white horses.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 15, 'And from His mouth proceeds a sharp sword with which to strike down the nations, and He will rule them with an iron scepter. He treads the winepress of the fury of the wrath of God the Almighty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 16, 'And He has a name written on His robe and on His thigh: KING OF KINGS AND LORD OF LORDS.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 17, 'Then I saw an angel standing in the sun, and he cried out in a loud voice to all the birds flying overhead, “Come, gather together for the great supper of God,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 18, 'so that you may eat the flesh of kings and commanders and mighty men, of horses and riders, of everyone slave and free, small and great.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 19, 'Then I saw the beast and the kings of the earth with their armies assembled to wage war against the One seated on the horse, and against His army.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 20, 'But the beast was captured along with the false prophet, who on its behalf had performed signs deceiving those who had the mark of the beast and worshiped its image. Both the beast and the false prophet were thrown alive into the fiery lake of burning sulfur.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 19, 21, 'And the rest were killed with the sword that proceeded from the mouth of the One seated on the horse. And all the birds gorged themselves on their flesh.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 20, 1, 'Then I saw an angel coming down from heaven with the key to the Abyss, holding in his hand a great chain.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 20, 2, 'He seized the dragon, that ancient serpent who is the devil and Satan, and bound him for a thousand years.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 20, 3, 'And he threw him into the Abyss, shut it, and sealed it over him, so that he could not deceive the nations until the thousand years were complete. After that, he must be released for a brief period of time.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 20, 4, 'Then I saw the thrones, and those seated on them had been given authority to judge. And I saw the souls of those who had been beheaded for their testimony of Jesus and for the word of God, and those who had not worshiped the beast or its image, and had not received its mark on their foreheads or hands. And they came to life and reigned with Christ for a thousand years.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 20, 5, 'The rest of the dead did not come back to life until the thousand years were complete. This is the first resurrection.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 20, 6, 'Blessed and holy are those who share in the first resurrection! The second death has no power over them, but they will be priests of God and of Christ, and will reign with Him for a thousand years.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 20, 7, 'When the thousand years are complete, Satan will be released from his prison,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 20, 8, 'and will go out to deceive the nations in the four corners of the earth—Gog and Magog—to assemble them for battle. Their number is like the sand of the seashore.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 20, 9, 'And they marched across the broad expanse of the earth and surrounded the camp of the saints and the beloved city. But fire came down from heaven and consumed them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 20, 10, 'And the devil who had deceived them was thrown into the lake of fire and sulfur, into which the beast and the false prophet had already been thrown. There they will be tormented day and night forever and ever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 20, 11, 'Then I saw a great white throne and the One seated on it. Earth and heaven fled from His presence, and no place was found for them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 20, 12, 'And I saw the dead, great and small, standing before the throne. And there were open books, and one of them was the Book of Life. And the dead were judged according to their deeds, as recorded in the books.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 20, 13, 'The sea gave up its dead, and Death and Hades gave up their dead, and each one was judged according to his deeds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 20, 14, 'Then Death and Hades were thrown into the lake of fire. This is the second death—the lake of fire.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 20, 15, 'And if anyone was found whose name was not written in the Book of Life, he was thrown into the lake of fire.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 1, 'Then I saw a new heaven and a new earth, for the first heaven and earth had passed away, and the sea was no more.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 2, 'I saw the holy city, the new Jerusalem, coming down out of heaven from God, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 3, 'And I heard a loud voice from the throne saying: “Behold, the dwelling place of God is with man, and He will dwell with them. They will be His people, and God Himself will be with them as their God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 4, '‘He will wipe away every tear from their eyes,’ and there will be no more death or mourning or crying or pain, for the former things have passed away.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 5, 'And the One seated on the throne said, “Behold, I make all things new.” Then He said, “Write this down, for these words are faithful and true.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 6, 'And He told me, “It is done! I am the Alpha and the Omega, the Beginning and the End. To the thirsty I will give freely from the spring of the water of life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 7, 'The one who overcomes will inherit all things, and I will be his God, and he will be My son.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 8, 'But to the cowardly and unbelieving and abominable and murderers and sexually immoral and sorcerers and idolaters and all liars, their place will be in the lake that burns with fire and sulfur. This is the second death.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 9, 'Then one of the seven angels with the seven bowls full of the seven final plagues came and said to me, “Come, I will show you the bride, the wife of the Lamb.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 10, 'And he carried me away in the Spirit to a mountain great and high, and showed me the holy city of Jerusalem coming down out of heaven from God,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 11, 'shining with the glory of God. Its radiance was like a most precious jewel, like a jasper, as clear as crystal.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 12, 'The city had a great and high wall with twelve gates inscribed with the names of the twelve tribes of Israel, and twelve angels at the gates.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 13, 'There were three gates on the east, three on the north, three on the south, and three on the west.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 14, 'The wall of the city had twelve foundations bearing the names of the twelve apostles of the Lamb.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 15, 'The angel who spoke with me had a golden measuring rod to measure the city and its gates and walls.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 16, 'The city lies foursquare, with its width the same as its length. And he measured the city with the rod, and all its dimensions were equal—12,000 stadia in length and width and height.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 17, 'And he measured its wall to be 144 cubits, by the human measure the angel was using.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 18, 'The wall was made of jasper, and the city itself of pure gold, as pure as glass.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 19, 'The foundations of the city walls were adorned with every kind of precious stone: The first foundation was jasper, the second sapphire, the third chalcedony, the fourth emerald,'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 20, 'the fifth sardonyx, the sixth carnelian, the seventh chrysolite, the eighth beryl, the ninth topaz, the tenth chrysoprase, the eleventh jacinth, and the twelfth amethyst.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 21, 'And the twelve gates were twelve pearls, with each gate consisting of a single pearl. The main street of the city was pure gold, as clear as glass.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 22, 'But I saw no temple in the city, because the Lord God Almighty and the Lamb are its temple.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 23, 'And the city has no need of sun or moon to shine on it, because the glory of God illuminates the city, and the Lamb is its lamp.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 24, 'By its light the nations will walk, and into it the kings of the earth will bring their glory.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 25, 'Its gates will never be shut at the end of the day, because there will be no night there.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 26, 'And into the city will be brought the glory and honor of the nations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 21, 27, 'But nothing unclean will ever enter it, nor anyone who practices an abomination or a lie, but only those whose names are written in the Lamb’s Book of Life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 1, 'Then the angel showed me a river of the water of life, as clear as crystal, flowing from the throne of God and of the Lamb'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 2, 'down the middle of the main street of the city. On either side of the river stood a tree of life, bearing twelve kinds of fruit and yielding a fresh crop for each month. And the leaves of the tree are for the healing of the nations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 3, 'No longer will there be any curse. The throne of God and of the Lamb will be within the city, and His servants will worship Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 4, 'They will see His face, and His name will be on their foreheads.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 5, 'There will be no more night in the city, and they will have no need for the light of a lamp or of the sun. For the Lord God will shine on them, and they will reign forever and ever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 6, 'Then the angel said to me, “These words are faithful and true. The Lord, the God of the spirits of the prophets, has sent His angel to show His servants what must soon take place.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 7, '“Behold, I am coming soon. Blessed is the one who keeps the words of prophecy in this book.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 8, 'And I am John, who heard and saw these things. And when I had heard and seen them, I fell down to worship at the feet of the angel who had shown me these things.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 9, 'But he said to me, “Do not do that! I am a fellow servant with you and your brothers the prophets, and with those who keep the words of this book. Worship God!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 10, 'Then he told me, “Do not seal up the words of prophecy in this book, because the time is near.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 11, 'Let the unrighteous continue to be unrighteous, and the vile continue to be vile; let the righteous continue to practice righteousness, and the holy continue to be holy.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 12, '“Behold, I am coming soon, and My reward is with Me, to give to each one according to what he has done.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 13, 'I am the Alpha and the Omega, the First and the Last, the Beginning and the End.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 14, 'Blessed are those who wash their robes, so that they may have the right to the tree of life and may enter the city by its gates.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 15, 'But outside are the dogs, the sorcerers, the sexually immoral, the murderers, the idolaters, and everyone who loves and practices falsehood.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 16, '“I, Jesus, have sent My angel to give you this testimony for the churches. I am the Root and the Offspring of David, the bright Morning Star.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 17, 'The Spirit and the bride say, “Come!” Let the one who hears say, “Come!” And let the one who is thirsty come, and the one who desires the water of life drink freely.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 18, 'I testify to everyone who hears the words of prophecy in this book: If anyone adds to them, God will add to him the plagues described in this book.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 19, 'And if anyone takes away from the words of this book of prophecy, God will take away his share in the tree of life and the holy city, which are described in this book.'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 20, 'He who testifies to these things says, “Yes, I am coming soon.” Amen. Come, Lord Jesus!'),
  ('BSB', 'Revelation', 66, 22, 21, 'The grace of the Lord Jesus be with all the saints. Amen.');
